ID   1.1.1.41
DE   Isocitrate dehydrogenase (NAD(+)).
AN   Beta-ketoglutaric-isocitric carboxylase.
AN   IDH.
AN   Isocitrate dehydrogenase (NAD).
AN   Isocitric acid dehydrogenase.
AN   Isocitric dehydrogenase.
AN   NAD dependent isocitrate dehydrogenase.
AN   NAD isocitrate dehydrogenase.
AN   NAD isocitric dehydrogenase.
AN   NAD-linked isocitrate dehydrogenase.
AN   NAD-specific isocitrate dehydrogenase.
AN   Nicotinamide adenine dinucleotide isocitrate dehydrogenase.
CA   Isocitrate + NAD(+) = 2-oxoglutarate + CO(2) + NADH.
CF   Mn(2+) or Mg(2+).
CC   -!- Unlike EC 1.1.1.42, oxalosuccinate cannot be used as a substrate.
CC   -!- In eukaryotes, isocitrate dehydrogenase exists in two forms: an
CC       NAD(+)-linked enzyme found only in mitochondria and displaying
CC       allosteric properties, and a non-allosteric, NADP(+)-linked enzyme
CC       that is found in both mitochondria and cytoplasm.
CC   -!- The enzyme from some species can also use NADP(+) but much more
CC       slowly.
