//
ID   1.1.1.263
DE   1,5-anhydro-D-fructose reductase.
AN   AF reductase.
CA   1,5-anhydro-D-glucitol + NADP(+) = 1,5-anhydro-D-fructose + NADPH.
CC   -!- Also reduces pyridine-3-aldehyde and 2,3-butanedione.
CC   -!- Acetaldehyde, 2-dehydroglucose (glucosone) and glucuronate are poor
CC       substrates, but there is no detectable action on glucose, mannose and
CC       fructose.
DR   Q96JD6, AKCL2_HUMAN;  Q4R802, AKCL2_MACFA;  Q9DCT1, AKCL2_MOUSE;
DR   P82125, AKCL2_PIG  ;  Q5U1Y4, AKCL2_RAT  ;
//
ID   1.1.1.264
DE   L-idonate 5-dehydrogenase (NAD(P)(+)).
AN   L-idonate 5-dehydrogenase.
CA   L-idonate + NAD(P)(+) = 5-dehydrogluconate + NAD(P)H.
CF   Zn(2+).
CC   -!- The enzyme from the bacterium Escherichia coli is specific for
CC       5-dehydro-D-gluconate.
CC   -!- Cf. EC  1.1.1.366.
PR   PROSITE; PDOC00058;
DR   P39346, IDND_ECOLI ;
//
ID   1.1.1.265
DE   3-methylbutanal reductase.
CA   3-methylbutanol + NAD(P)(+) = 3-methylbutanal + NAD(P)H.
CC   -!- The enzyme purified from Saccharomyces cerevisiae catalyzes the
CC       reduction of a number of straight-chain and branched aldehydes,
CC       as well as some aromatic aldehydes.
DR   Q12068, GRE2_YEAST ;
//
ID   1.1.1.266
DE   dTDP-4-dehydro-6-deoxyglucose reductase.
AN   dTDP-4-keto-6-deoxyglucose reductase.
CA   dTDP-alpha-D-fucopyranose + NAD(P)(+) = dTDP-4-dehydro-6-deoxy-alpha-D-
CA   glucose + NAD(P)H.
CC   -!- The enzymes from the Gram-negative bacteria Actinobacillus
CC       actinomycetemcomitans and Escherichia coli O52 are involved in
CC       activation of fucose for incorporation into capsular polysaccharide
CC       O-antigens.
CC   -!- The enzyme from the Gram-positive bacterium Anoxybacillus tepidamans
CC       (Geobacillus tepidamans) is involved in activation of fucose for
CC       incorporation into the organism's S-layer.
CC   -!- The enzyme from E.coli O52 has a higher catalytic efficiency with
CC       NADH than with NADPH.
DR   Q6E7F2, FCF1_ECOLX ;
//
ID   1.1.1.267
DE   1-deoxy-D-xylulose-5-phosphate reductoisomerase.
AN   1-deoxyxylulose-5-phosphate reductoisomerase.
AN   DXP-reductoisomerase.
CA   2-C-methyl-D-erythritol 4-phosphate + NADP(+) = 1-deoxy-D-xylulose
CA   5-phosphate + NADPH.
CF   Mg(2+) or cobalt cation or Mn(2+).
CC   -!- The enzyme from several eubacteria, including Escherichia coli, forms
CC       part of an alternative nonmevalonate pathway for terpenoid
CC       biosynthesis.
CC   -!- The mechanism has been shown to be a retroaldol/aldol reaction.
