ID   1.1.1.292
DE   1,5-anhydro-D-fructose reductase (1,5-anhydro-D-mannitol-forming).
AN   1,5-anhydro-D-fructose reductase.
AN   AFR.
CA   1,5-anhydro-D-mannitol + NADP(+) = 1,5-anhydro-D-fructose + NADPH.
CC   -!- Present in some but not all Rhizobium species.
CC   -!- Differs from hepatic 1,5-anhydro-D-fructose reductase, which yields
CC       1,5-anhydro-D-glucitol as the product (see EC 1.1.1.263).
CC   -!- In Sinorhizobium morelense, the product of the reaction, 1,5-anhydro-
CC       D-mannitol, can be further metabolized to D-mannose.
CC   -!- Also reduces 1,5-anhydro-D-erythro-hexo-2,3-diulose and 2-ketoaldoses
CC       (called osones), such as D-glucosone (D-arabino-hexos-2-ulose) and
CC       6-deoxy-D-glucosone.
CC   -!- Does not reduce common aldoses and ketoses, or non-sugar aldehydes
CC       and ketones.
DR   Q2I8V6, AFR_ENSAD  ;  Q92KZ3, AFR_RHIME  ;
