ID   1.1.1.298
DE   3-hydroxypropionate dehydrogenase (NADP(+)).
AN   3-hydroxypropanoate dehydrogenase (NADP(+)).
CA   3-hydroxypropanoate + NADP(+) = 3-oxopropanoate + NADPH.
CC   -!- Catalyzes the reduction of 3-oxopropanoate to 3-hydroxypropanoate,
CC       a key step in the 3-hydroxypropanoate and the
CC       3-hydroxypropanoate/4-hydroxybutyrate cycles, autotrophic CO(2)
CC       fixation pathways found in some green non-sulfur phototrophic
CC       bacteria and archaea, respectively.
CC   -!- The enzyme from Chloroflexus aurantiacus is bifunctional, and also
CC       catalyzes the upstream reaction in the pathway, EC 1.2.1.75.
CC   -!- Different from EC 1.1.1.59 by cofactor preference.
