//
ID   1.1.99.37
DE   Methanol dehydrogenase (nicotinoprotein).
AN   NDMA-dependent methanol dehydrogenase.
AN   Nicotinoprotein methanol dehydrogenase.
CA   Methanol + acceptor = formaldehyde + reduced acceptor.
CF   Mg(2+); Zn(2+).
CC   -!- Nicotinoprotein methanol dehydrogenases have a tightly bound
CC       NADP+/NADPH cofactor that does not dissociate during the catalytic
CC       process.
CC   -!- Instead, the cofactor is regenerated by a second substrate or
CC       electron carrier.
CC   -!- While the in vivo electron acceptor is not known, N,N-dimethyl-4-
CC       nitrosoaniline (NDMA) can serve this function in vitro.
CC   -!- The enzyme has been detected in several Gram-positive methylotrophic
CC       bacteria, including Amycolatopsis methanolica, Rhodococcus
CC       rhodochrous and Rhodococcus erythropolis.
CC   -!- These enzymes are decameric, and possess a 5-fold symmetry.
CC   -!- Some of the enzymes can also dismutate formaldehyde to methanol and
CC       formate.
DR   Q9RCG0, MNO_AMYME  ;  C5MRT8, MNO_MYCS8  ;  Q53062, MNO_RHOER  ;
//
ID   1.1.99.38
DE   2-deoxy-scyllo-inosamine dehydrogenase (AdoMet-dependent).
CA   2-deoxy-scyllo-inosamine + S-adenosyl-L-methionine = 3-amino-2,3-dideoxy-
CA   scyllo-inosose + 5'-deoxyadenosine + L-methionine.
CF   Iron-sulfur.
CC   -!- Involved in the biosynthetic pathway of the aminoglycoside
CC       antibiotics of the butirosin family.
CC   -!- The enzyme from Bacillus circulans was shown to be a radical
CC       S-adenosyl-L-methionine (SAM) enzyme.
CC   -!- Cf. EC 1.1.1.329.
DR   Q8G907, BTRN_BACCI ;
//
ID   1.1.99.39
DE   D-2-hydroxyglutarate dehydrogenase.
CA   (R)-2-hydroxyglutarate + acceptor = 2-oxoglutarate + reduced acceptor.
CF   FAD.
CC   -!- The enzyme has no activity with NAD(+) or NADP(+), and was assayed in
CC       vitro using artificial electron acceptors.
CC   -!- It has lower activity with (R)-lactate, (R)-2-hydroxybutyrate and
CC       meso-tartrate, and no activity with the (S) isomers.
DR   O23240, D2HDH_ARATH;  B8B7X6, D2HDH_ORYSI;  Q7XI14, D2HDH_ORYSJ;
//
ID   1.1.99.40
DE   (R)-2-hydroxyglutarate--pyruvate transhydrogenase.
CA   (R)-2-hydroxyglutarate + pyruvate = 2-oxoglutarate + (R)-lactate.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized in the yeast Saccharomyces cerevisiae, also
CC       functions as EC 1.1.2.4 and is active with oxaloacetate as electron
CC       acceptor forming (R)-malate.
DR   P46681, DLD2_YEAST ;  P39976, DLD3_YEAST ;
//
ID   1.1.99.41
DE   3-hydroxy-1,2-didehydro-2,3-dihydrotabersonine reductase.
AN   T3R.
AN   Tabersonine 3-reductase.
CA   (1) (3R)-3-hydroxy-16-methoxy-2,3-dihydrotabersonine + acceptor = (3R)-3-
CA   hydroxy-16-methoxy-1,2-didehydro-2,3-dihydrotabersonine + reduced
CA   acceptor.
CA   (2) (3R)-3-hydroxy-2,3-dihydrotabersonine + acceptor = (3R)-3-hydroxy-
CA   1,2-didehydro-2,3-dihydrotabersonine + reduced acceptor.
CC   -!- This enzyme is involved in the biosynthesis of vindoline and
CC       vindorosine in the plant Catharanthus roseus (Madagascar periwinkle).
CC   -!- In vivo, it functions in the direction of reduction.
CC   -!- It has no activity with 3-epoxylated compounds, which can form
CC       spontaneously from its unstable substrates.
DR   A0A161CAI1, T3R_CATRO  ;
//
ID   1.1.99.42
DE   4-pyridoxate dehydrogenase.
CA   4-pyridoxate + acceptor = 5-formyl-3-hydroxy-2-methylpyridine-4-
CA   carboxylate + reduced acceptor.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacteria Pseudomonas sp. MA-1 and
CC       Mesorhizobium loti, participates in the degradation of pyridoxine
CC       (vitamin B(6)).
CC   -!- It is membrane bound and contains FAD.
CC   -!- The enzyme has been assayed in vitro in the presence of the
CC       artificial electron acceptor dichloroindophenol (DCPIP).
//
ID   1.2.1.1
DE   Transferred entry: 1.1.1.284 and 4.4.1.22.
//
ID   1.2.1.2
DE   Transferred entry: 1.17.1.9.
