CC       fluoroacetate and glycolaldehyde but not for acetaldehyde.
DR   F8JX40, FLUDE_STREN;
//
ID   1.2.1.70
DE   Glutamyl-tRNA reductase.
CA   L-glutamate 1-semialdehyde + NADP(+) + tRNA(Glu) = L-glutamyl-tRNA(Glu) +
CA   NADPH.
CC   -!- Forms part of the pathway for the biosynthesis of 5-aminolevulinate
CC       from glutamate, known as the C5 pathway, which is used in most
CC       eubacteria, and in all archaebacteria, algae and plants.
CC   -!- However, in the alpha-proteobacteria EC 2.3.1.37 is used in an
CC       alternative route to produce the product 5-aminolevulinate from
CC       succinyl-CoA and glycine.
CC   -!- This route is found in the mitochondria of fungi and animals,
CC       organelles that are considered to be derived from an endosymbiotic
CC       alpha-proteobacterium.
CC   -!- Although higher plants do not possess EC 2.3.1.37, the protistan
CC       Euglena gracilis possesses both the C5 pathway and EC 2.3.1.37.
PR   PROSITE; PDOC00608;
