ID   1.2.1.74
DE   Abieta-7,13-dien-18-al dehydrogenase.
AN   Abietadienal dehydrogenase.
CA   Abieta-7,13-diene-18-al + H(2)O + NAD(+) = abieta-7,13-diene-18-oate +
CA   NADH.
CC   -!- Abietic acid is the principle component of conifer resin.
CC   -!- This enzyme catalyzes the last step of the pathway of abietic acid
CC       biosynthesis in Abies grandis (grand fir).
CC   -!- The activity has been demonstrated in cell-free stem extracts of
CC       A.grandis, was present in the cytoplasm, and required NAD(+) as
CC       cofactor.
CC   -!- The enzyme is expressed constitutively at a high level, and is not
CC       inducible by wounding of the plant tissue.
//
ID   1.2.1.75
DE   Malonyl CoA reductase (malonate semialdehyde-forming).
AN   Malonyl CoA reductase (NADP).
AN   NADP-dependent malonyl CoA reductase.
CA   Malonate semialdehyde + CoA + NADP(+) = malonyl-CoA + NADPH.
CF   Mg(2+).
CC   -!- Catalyzes the reduction of malonyl-CoA to malonate semialdehyde,
CC       a key step in the 3-hydroxypropanoate and the
CC       3-hydroxypropanoate/4-hydroxybutyrate cycles, autotrophic CO(2)
CC       fixation pathways found in some green non-sulfur phototrophic
CC       bacteria and some thermoacidophilic archaea, respectively.
CC   -!- The enzyme from Sulfolobus tokodaii has been purified, and found to
CC       contain one RNA molecule per two subunits.
CC   -!- The enzyme from Chloroflexus aurantiacus is bifunctional, and also
CC       catalyzes the next reaction in the pathway, EC 1.1.1.298.
DR   A4YEN2, MCR_METS5  ;  Q96YK1, MCR_SULTO  ;
//
ID   1.2.1.76
