ID   1.2.1.88
DE   L-glutamate gamma-semialdehyde dehydrogenase.
AN   1-pyrroline-5-carboxylate dehydrogenase.
AN   Delta(1)-pyrroline-5-carboxylate dehydrogenase.
AN   Pyrroline-5-carboxylate dehydrogenase.
CA   L-glutamate 5-semialdehyde + NAD(+) + H(2)O = L-glutamate + NADH.
CC   -!- This enzyme catalyzes the irreversible oxidation of glutamate-gamma-
CC       semialdehyde to glutamate as part of the proline degradation pathway.
CC   -!- (S)-1-pyrroline-5-carboxylate, the product of the first enzyme of the
CC       pathway (EC 1.5.5.2) is in spontaneous equilibrium with its tautomer
CC       L-glutamate gamma-semialdehyde.
CC   -!- In many bacterial species, both activities are carried out by a
CC       single bifunctional enzyme.
CC   -!- The enzyme can also oxidize other 1-pyrrolines, e.g. 3-hydroxy-1-
CC       pyrroline-5-carboxylate is converted into 4-hydroxyglutamate and (R)-
