ID   1.2.5.3
DE   Aerobic carbon monoxide dehydrogenase.
AN   Molybdoenzyme carbon monoxide dehydrogenase.
CA   CO + a quinone + H(2)O = CO(2) + a quinol.
CF   Cu cation; FAD; Iron-sulfur; Molybdenum atom; Molybdopterin.
CC   -!- This enzyme, found in carboxydotrophic bacteria, catalyzes the
CC       oxidation of CO to CO(2) under aerobic conditions.
CC   -!- The enzyme belongs to the xanthine oxidoreductase family.
CC   -!- The CO(2) that is produced is assimilated by the Calvin-Benson-Basham
CC       cycle, while the electrons are transferred to a quinone via the FAD
CC       site, and continue through the electron transfer chain to a dioxygen
CC       terminal acceptor.
CC   -!- Cf. EC 1.2.7.4.
