ID   1.2.7.4
DE   Anaerobic carbon-monoxide dehydrogenase.
AN   Carbon-monoxide dehydrogenase (ferredoxin).
AN   Ni-CODH.
CA   CO + H(2)O + 2 oxidized ferredoxin = CO(2) + 2 reduced ferredoxin +
CA   2 H(+).
CF   Fe cation; Ni(2+); Zn(2+).
CC   -!- This prokaryotic enzyme catalyzes the reversible reduction of CO(2)
CC       to CO.
CC   -!- The electrons are transferred to redox proteins such as ferredoxin.
CC   -!- In purple sulfur bacteria and methanogenic archaea it catalyzes the
CC       oxidation of CO to CO(2), which is incorporated by the Calvin-Benson-
CC       Basham cycle or released, respectively.
CC   -!- In acetogenic and sulfate-reducing microbes it catalyzes the
CC       reduction of CO(2) to CO, which is incorporated into acetyl CoA by
CC       EC 2.3.1.169, with which the enzyme forms a tight complex in those
CC       organisms.
CC   -!- In purple sulfur bacteria the enzyme forms complexes with the Ni-Fe-S
CC       protein EC 1.12.7.2 which catalyze the overall reaction: CO + H(2)O =
CC       CO(2) + H(2).
CC   -!- Cf. EC 1.2.5.3.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.2.99.2.
