DE   Precorrin-2 dehydrogenase.
AN   Precorrin-2 oxidase.
CA   Precorrin-2 + NAD(+) = sirohydrochlorin + NADH.
CC   -!- Catalyzes the second of three steps leading to the formation of
CC       siroheme from uroporphyrinogen III.
CC   -!- The first step involves the donation of two S-adenosyl-L-methionine-
CC       derived methyl groups to carbons 2 and 7 of uroporphyrinogen III to
CC       form precorrin-2 (EC 2.1.1.107) and the third step involves the
CC       chelation of ferrous iron to sirohydrochlorin to form siroheme
CC       (EC 4.99.1.4).
CC   -!- In Saccharomyces cerevisiae, the last two steps are carried out by a
CC       single bifunctional enzyme, Met8p.
CC   -!- In some bacteria, steps 1-3 are catalyzed by a single multifunctional
CC       protein called CysG, whereas in Bacillus megaterium, three separate
CC       enzymes carry out each of the steps, with SirC being responsible for
