ID   1.3.1.81
DE   (+)-pulegone reductase.
CA   (1) (-)-menthone + NADP(+) = (+)-pulegone + NADPH.
CA   (2) (+)-isomenthone + NADP(+) = (+)-pulegone + NADPH.
CC   -!- NADH cannot replace NADPH as reductant.
CC   -!- The Delta(8,9)-double bond of (+)-cis-isopulegone and the Delta(1,2)-
CC       double bond of (+-)-piperitone are not substrates.
CC   -!- The enzyme from peppermint (Mentha x piperita) converts (+)-pulegone
CC       into both (-)-menthone and (+)-isomenthone at a ratio of 70:30 for
CC       native enzyme but it does not catalyze the reverse reaction.
DR   Q6WAU0, PULR_MENPI ;
//
ID   1.3.1.82
DE   (-)-isopiperitenone reductase.
CA   (+)-cis-isopulegone + NADP(+) = (-)-isopiperitenone + NADPH.
CC   -!- The reaction occurs in the opposite direction to that shown above.
CC   -!- Participates in the menthol-biosynthesis pathway of Mentha plants.
CC   -!- (+)-pulegone, (+)-cis-isopulegone and (-)-menthone are not
CC       substrates.
CC   -!- Has a preference for NADPH as the reductant, with NADH being a poor
CC       substitute.
CC   -!- Highly regioselective for the reduction of the endocyclic 1,2-double
CC       bond, and is stereoselective, producing only the 1R-configured
CC       product.
PR   PROSITE; PDOC00060;
DR   Q6WAU1, IPIPR_MENPI;
