ID   1.3.1.92
DE   Artemisinic aldehyde Delta(11(13)) reductase.
CA   (11R)-dihydroartemisinic aldehyde + NADP(+) = artemisinic aldehyde +
CA   NADPH.
CC   -!- Cloned from Artemisia annua.
CC   -!- In addition to the reduction of artemisinic aldehyde it is also able
CC       to a lesser extent to reduce artemisinic alcohol and artemisinic
CC       acid.
CC   -!- Part of the biosyntheis of artemisinin.
DR   C5H429, DBR2_ARTAN ;
//
ID   1.3.1.93
DE   Very-long-chain enoyl-CoA reductase.
CA   A very-long-chain acyl-CoA + NADP(+) = a very-long-chain trans-2,3-
CA   dehydroacyl-CoA + NADPH.
CC   -!- This is the fourth component of the elongase, a microsomal protein
CC       complex responsible for extending palmitoyl-CoA and stearoyl-CoA (and
CC       modified forms thereof) to very-long-chain acyl CoAs.
CC   -!- Cf. EC 2.3.1.199, EC 1.1.1.330 and EC 4.2.1.134.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 2.3.1.119.
DR   Q9M2U2, TECR_ARATH ;  Q3ZCD7, TECR_BOVIN ;  Q9N5Y2, TECR_CAEEL ;
DR   Q55C17, TECR_DICDI ;  Q9NZ01, TECR_HUMAN ;  Q9CY27, TECR_MOUSE ;
DR   Q64232, TECR_RAT   ;  Q99190, TECR_YEAST ;
//
ID   1.3.1.94
DE   Polyprenol reductase.
CA   Ditrans,polycis-dolichol + NADP(+) = ditrans,polycis-polyprenol + NADPH.
CC   -!- The reaction occurs in the reverse direction with reduction of the
CC       terminal double bond next to the alcohol group.
CC   -!- Isolated from human fetal brain tissue but present in all eukaryotes.
CC   -!- In mammalian cells dolichols are predominantly 18-21 isoprene units
CC       in length.
DR   P40526, DFG10_YEAST;  Q9CAH5, POED1_ARATH;  A2XWN6, POED1_ORYSI;
DR   Q7XUH5, POED1_ORYSJ;  Q9SI62, POED2_ARATH;  B8B6G5, POED2_ORYSI;
DR   Q7F0Q2, POED2_ORYSJ;  D2HBV9, PORED_AILME;  A8X8R3, PORED_CAEBR;
DR   Q17428, PORED_CAEEL;  Q5RIU9, PORED_DANRE;  Q9VLP9, PORED_DROME;
DR   Q9H8P0, PORED_HUMAN;  C7T2J9, PORED_MESAU;  Q9WUP4, PORED_MOUSE;
DR   Q5RJM1, PORED_RAT  ;  Q8AVI9, PORED_XENLA;  Q0P4J9, PORED_XENTR;
//
ID   1.3.1.95
DE   Acryloyl-CoA reductase (NADH).
CA   Propanoyl-CoA + NAD(+) = acryloyl-CoA + NADH.
CF   FAD.
CC   -!- The reaction is catalyzed in the opposite direction to that shown.
CC   -!- The enzyme from the bacterium Clostridium propionicum is a complex
CC       that includes an electron-transfer flavoprotein (ETF).
CC   -!- The ETF is reduced by NADH and transfers the electrons to the active
CC       site.
CC   -!- Catalyzes a step in a pathway for L-alanine fermentation to
CC       propanoate.
CC   -!- Cf. EC 1.3.1.84.
DR   G3KIM8, ACRC_CLOPR ;
//
ID   1.3.1.96
DE   Botryococcus squalene synthase.
CA   Squalene + diphosphate + NADP(+) = presqualene diphosphate + NADPH.
CC   -!- Isolated from the green alga Botryococcus braunii BOT22.
CC   -!- Acts in the reverse direction.
CC   -!- cf. EC 2.5.1.21, where squalene is formed directly from farnesyl
CC       diphosphate.
DR   G0Y287, BOSS_BOTBR ;
//
ID   1.3.1.97
DE   Botryococcene synthase.
CA   C(30) botryococcene + NADP(+) + diphosphate = presqualene diphosphate +
CA   NADPH.
CC   -!- Isolated from the green alga Botryococcus braunii BOT22.
CC   -!- Acts in the reverse direction.
CC   -!- Involved in the production of botryococcenes, which are triterpenoid
CC       hydrocarbons of isoprenoid origin produced in large amount by this
CC       alga.
DR   G0Y288, BOCS_BOTBR ;
//
ID   1.3.1.98
DE   UDP-N-acetylmuramate dehydrogenase.
AN   UDP-GlcNAc-enoylpyruvate reductase.
AN   UDP-N-acetylenolpyruvoylglucosamine reductase.
AN   UDP-N-acetylglucosamine-enoylpyruvate reductase.
AN   Uridine diphospho-N-acetylglucosamine-enolpyruvate reductase.
AN   Uridine diphosphoacetylpyruvoylglucosamine reductase.
CA   UDP-N-acetyl-alpha-D-muramate + NADP(+) = UDP-N-acetyl-3-
CA   O-(1-carboxyvinyl)-alpha-D-glucosamine + NADPH.
CF   FAD.
CC   -!- NADH can to a lesser extent replace NADPH.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.1.1.158.
