ID   1.3.1.99
DE   Iridoid synthase.
CA   (6E)-8-oxogeranial + NAD(P)H = cis-trans-nepetalactol + NAD(P)(+).
CC   -!- Isolated from the plant Catharanthus roseus.
CC   -!- The reaction may involve cyclization via a Diels-Alder or Michael
CC       reaction.
CC   -!- Iridoids are involved in the biosynthesis of many indole alkaloids.
CC   -!- The cyclic hemiacetal is readily hydrolyzed to the corresponding
CC       dial.
DR   A0A1C9CX56, CYC1_CAMAC ;  A0A1C9CX66, CYC2_CAMAC ;  K7WDL7, IRIS_CATRO ;
//
ID   1.3.1.100
DE   Chanoclavine-I aldehyde reductase.
CA   Dihydrochanoclavine-I aldehyde + NADP(+) = chanoclavine-I aldehyde +
CA   NADPH.
CF   FMN.
CC   -!- The enzyme participates in the biosynthesis of fumigaclavine C,
CC       an ergot alkaloid produced by some fungi of the Trichocomaceae
CC       family.
CC   -!- The enzyme catalyzes the reduction of chanoclavine-I aldehyde to
CC       dihydrochanoclavine-I aldehyde.
CC   -!- This hydrolyzes spontaneously to form 6,8-dimethyl-6,7-
CC       didehydroergoline, which is converted to festuclavine by EC 1.5.1.44.
DR   Q4WZ70, EASA_ASPFU ;  W6Q9S9, FGOX3_PENRF;  W6Q2D7, IFGG_PENRF ;
//
ID   1.3.1.101
DE   2,3-bis-O-geranylgeranyl-sn-glycerol 1-phosphate reductase (NAD(P)H).
AN   2,3-digeranylgeranylglycerophospholipid reductase.
AN   DGGGPL reductase.
AN   Digeranylgeranylglycerophospholipid reductase.
CA   2,3-bis-(O-phytanyl)-sn-glycerol 1-phosphate + 8 NAD(P)(+) = 2,3-bis-
CA   (O-geranylgeranyl)-sn-glycerol 1-phosphate + 8 NAD(P)H.
CF   FAD.
CC   -!- The enzyme from the archaeon Thermoplasma acidophilum is involved in
CC       the biosynthesis of membrane lipids.
CC   -!- In vivo the reaction occurs in the reverse direction with the
CC       formation of 2,3-bis-O-phytanyl-sn-glycerol 1-phosphate.
CC   -!- cf. EC 1.3.7.11.
DR   Q6L0M1, GGR_PICTO  ;  Q9HKS9, GGR_THEAC  ;  Q979Y7, GGR_THEVO  ;
//
ID   1.3.1.102
DE   2-alkenal reductase (NADP(+)).
AN   NADPH-dependent alkenal/one oxidoreductase.
CA   An n-alkanal + NADP(+) = an alk-2-enal + NADPH.
CC   -!- Shows highest activity with 1-nitrocyclohexene but also has
CC       significant activity with 2-methylpentenal and trans-cinnamaldehyde.
CC   -!- Involved in the detoxification of alpha,beta-unsaturated aldehydes
CC       and ketones.
CC   -!- Has very low activity with NAD as reductant (cf. EC 1.3.1.74).
DR   Q9SLN8, DBR_TOBAC  ;
//
ID   1.3.1.103
DE   2-haloacrylate reductase.
CA   (S)-2-chloropropanoate + NADP(+) = 2-chloroacrylate + NADPH.
CC   -!- The enzyme acts in the degradation pathway of unsaturated
CC       organohalogen compounds by the bacterium Burkholderia sp. WS.
DR   Q59I44, CAA43_BURSP;
//
ID   1.3.1.104
DE   Enoyl-[acyl-carrier-protein] reductase.
AN   Acyl-ACP dehydrogenase.
AN   Enoyl-ACP reductase.
CA   An acyl-[acyl-carrier protein] + NADP(+) = a trans-2,3-dehydroacyl-[acyl-
CA   carrier protein] + NADPH.
CC   -!- The enzyme completes each cycle of fatty acid elongation by
CC       catalyzing the stereospecific reduction of the double bond at
CC       position 2 of a growing fatty acid chain, while linked to the acyl-
CC       carrier protein, in an NADPH-dependent manner.
CC   -!- This entry stands for enzymes whose stereo-specificity with respect
CC       to NADP(+) is not known (cf. EC 1.3.1.39, EC 1.3.1.10 and
CC       EC 1.3.1.9).
DR   Q757U3, ETR1_ASHGO ;  Q6FXN7, ETR1_CANGA ;  Q8WZM3, ETR1_CANTR ;
DR   Q6BLV6, ETR1_DEBHA ;  Q6CIR6, ETR1_KLULA ;  Q10488, ETR1_SCHPO ;
DR   Q6CBE4, ETR1_YARLI ;  P38071, ETR1_YEAST ;  Q8WZM4, ETR2_CANTR ;
DR   Q6BV30, ETR2_DEBHA ;  P71079, FABL_BACSU ;  O45903, MECR1_CAEEL;
DR   Q9XXC8, MECR2_CAEEL;  Q8LCU7, MECR_ARATH ;  Q7YS70, MECR_BOVIN ;
DR   Q6GQN8, MECR_DANRE ;  Q54YT4, MECR_DICDI ;  Q9V6U9, MECR_DROME ;
DR   Q9BV79, MECR_HUMAN ;  Q9DCS3, MECR_MOUSE ;  Q9Z311, MECR_RAT   ;
DR   Q28GQ2, MECR_XENTR ;
//
ID   1.3.1.105
DE   2-methylene-furan-3-one reductase.
AN   Enone oxidoreductase.
CA   4-hydroxy-2,5-dimethylfuran-3(2H)-one + NADP(+) = 4-hydroxy-5-methyl-2-
CA   methylenefuran-3(2H)-one + NADPH.
CC   -!- The enzyme was dicovered in strawberry (Fragaria x ananassa), where
CC       it produces furaneol, one of the major aroma compounds in the fruits.
CC   -!- It has also been detected in tomato (Solanum lycopersicum) and
CC       pineapple (Ananas comosus).
CC   -!- The enzyme can also act on derivatives substituted at the methylene
CC       functional group.
CC   -!- The enzyme from the yeast Saccharomyces cerevisiae acts on (2E)-2-
CC       ethylidene-4-hydroxy-5-methylfuran-3(2H)-one and produces
CC       homofuraneol, an important aroma compound in soy sauce and miso.
CC   -!- NADPH is the preferred cofactor.
DR   Q941I0, ENOXC_FRAAN;  Q84V25, ENOXE_FRAAN;  O23939, ENOX_FRAVE ;
DR   K4BW79, ENOX_SOLLC ;
//
ID   1.3.1.106
DE   Cobalt-precorrin-6A reductase.
CA   Cobalt-precorrin-6B + NAD(+) = cobalt-precorrin-6A + NADH.
CC   -!- The enzyme catalyzes a step in the anaerobic (early cobalt insertion)
CC       pathway of adenosylcobalamin biosynthesis.
CC   -!- The enzyme from the bacterium Bacillus megaterium has no activity
CC       with NADPH.
CC   -!- The equivalent enzyme in the aerobic pathway is EC 1.3.1.54.
DR   O87691, CBIJ_BACME ;  Q57972, CBIJ_METJA ;  Q977V1, CBIJ_METMI ;
DR   O27083, CBIJ_METTH ;  Q05591, CBIJ_SALTY ;  P72711, CBIJ_SYNY3 ;
//
ID   1.3.1.107
DE   Sanguinarine reductase.
CA   (1) Dihydrosanguinarine + NAD(P)(+) = sanguinarine + NAD(P)H.
CA   (2) Dihydrochelirubine + NAD(P)(+) = chelirubine + NAD(P)H.
CC   -!- The enzyme, purified from the California poppy (Eschscholzia
CC       californica), is involved in detoxifying the phytoalexin sanguinarine
CC       produced by poppy itself (cf. EC 1.5.3.12), when it binds to the cell
CC       wall of the poppy cell.
CC   -!- The reaction with NADPH is up to three times faster than that with
CC       NADH at low concentrations (<10 uM) of the dinucleotide.
CC   -!- At higher concentrations the reaction with NADPH is inhibited but not
CC       that with NADH.
DR   D5JWB3, SARED_ESCCA;
//
ID   1.3.1.108
DE   Caffeoyl-CoA reductase.
AN   Caffeoyl-CoA reductase-Etf complex.
AN   Electron-bifurcating caffeoyl-CoA reductase.
CA   3-(3,4-dihydroxyphenyl)propanoyl-CoA + 2 NAD(+) + 2 reduced ferredoxin
CA   [iron-sulfur] cluster = (2E)-3-(3,4-dihydroxyphenyl)prop-2-enoyl-CoA +
CA   2 NADH + 2 oxidized ferredoxin [iron-sulfur] cluster.
CF   FAD; Iron-sulfur.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Acetobacterium woodii,
CC       couples the endergonic ferredoxin reduction with NADH as reductant to
CC       the exergonic reduction of caffeoyl-CoA with the same reductant.
CC   -!- It uses the mechanism of electron bifurcation to overcome the steep
CC       energy barrier in ferredoxin reduction.
CC   -!- It also reduces 4-coumaroyl-CoA and feruloyl-CoA.
DR   H6LGM6, CARC_ACEWD ;  H6LGM7, CARD_ACEWD ;  H6LGM8, CARE_ACEWD ;
//
ID   1.3.1.109
DE   Butanoyl-CoA dehydrogenase (NAD(+),ferredoxin).
AN   Bifurcating butanoyl-CoA dehydrogenase.
AN   Butanoyl-CoA dehydrogenase/Etf complex.
CA   Butanoyl-CoA + 2 NAD(+) + 2 reduced ferredoxin [iron-sulfur] cluster =
CA   (E)-but-2-enoyl-CoA + 2 NADH + 2 oxidized ferredoxin [iron-sulfur]
CA   cluster.
CF   Flavoprotein.
CC   -!- This enzyme, isolated from the bacteria Acidaminococcus fermentans
CC       and butanoate-producing Clostridia species, couples the exergonic
CC       reduction of (E)-but-2-enoyl-CoA to butanoyl-CoA with NADH to the
CC       endergonic reduction of ferredoxin by NADH, using electron
CC       bifurcation to overcome the steep energy barrier in ferredoxin
CC       reduction.
//
ID   1.3.1.110
DE   Lactate dehydrogenase (NAD(+),ferredoxin).
AN   Electron bifurcating LDH/Etf complex.
CA   Lactate + 2 NAD(+) + 2 reduced ferredoxin [iron-sulfur] cluster =
CA   pyruvate + 2 NADH + 2 oxidized ferredoxin [iron-sulfur] cluster.
CC   -!- The enzyme, isolated from the bacterium Acetobacterium woodii, uses
CC       flavin-based electron confurcation to drive endergonic lactate
CC       oxidation with NAD(+) as oxidant at the expense of simultaneous
CC       exergonic electron flow from reduced ferredoxin to NAD(+).
//
ID   1.3.1.111
DE   Geranylgeranyl-bacteriochlorophyllide a reductase.
CA   Bacteriochlorophyll a + 3 NADP(+) =
CA   geranylgeranyl bacteriochlorophyllide a + 3 NADPH.
CC   -!- The enzyme catalyzes the successive reduction of the geranylgeraniol
CC       esterifying group to phytol, reducing three out of four double bonds,
CC       and transforming geranylgeranyl bacteriochlorophyllide a via
CC       dihydrogeranylgeranyl bacteriochlorophyllide a and
CC       tetrahydrogeranylgeranyl bacteriochlorophyllide a to
CC       bacteriochlorophyll a.
CC   -!- The enzyme can also accept the pheophytin derivative geranylgeranyl
CC       bacteriopheophytin, converting it to bacteriopheophytin a.
//
ID   1.3.1.112
DE   Anthocyanidin reductase ((2S)-flavan-3-ol-forming).
CA   (1) A (2S,3R)-flavan-3-ol + 2 NADP(+) = an anthocyanidin with a 3-hydroxy
CA   group + 2 NADPH.
CA   (2) A (2S,3S)-flavan-3-ol + 2 NADP(+) = an anthocyanidin with a 3-hydroxy
CA   group + 2 NADPH.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from Vitis vinifera (grape), participates
CC       in the flavonoid biosynthesis pathway.
CC   -!- It catalyzes the double reduction of anthocyanidins, producing a
CC       mixture of (2S,3S)- and (2S,3R)-flavan-3-ols.
CC   -!- The enzyme catalyzes sequential hydride transfers to C-2 and C-4,
CC       respectively.
CC   -!- Epimerization at C-3 is achieved by tautomerization that occurs
CC       between the two hydride transfers.
CC   -!- Cf. EC 1.3.1.77.
DR   Q7PCC4, ANRCH_VITVI;  Q5FB34, ANRCS_VITVI;  D7U6G6, ANRPN_VITVI;
//
ID   1.3.1.113
DE   (4-alkanoyl-5-oxo-2,5-dihydrofuran-3-yl)methyl phosphate reductase.
CA   A ((3S)-4-alkanoyl-5-oxooxolan-3-yl)methyl phosphate + NADP(+) =
CA   a (4-alkanoyl-5-oxo-2,5-dihydrofuran-3-yl)methyl phosphate + NADPH.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacteria Streptomyces griseus and
CC       Streptomyces coelicolor, is involved in the biosynthesis of gamma-
CC       butyrolactone autoregulators that control secondary metabolism and
CC       morphological development in Streptomyces bacteria.
//
ID   1.3.1.114
DE   3-dehydro-bile acid Delta(4,6)-reductase.
CA   (1) 3-oxocholan-24-oyl-CoA + NAD(+) = 3-oxochol-4-en-24-oyl-CoA + NADH.
CA   (2) 3-oxochol-4-en-24-oyl-CoA + NAD(+) = 3-oxochol-4,6-dien-24-oyl-CoA +
CA   NADH.
CA   (3) 12-alpha-hydroxy-3-oxocholan-24-oyl-CoA + NAD(+) = 12-alpha-hydroxy-
CA   3-oxochol-4-en-24-oyl-CoA + NADH.
CA   (4) 12-alpha-hydroxy-3-oxochol-4-en-24-oyl-CoA + NAD(+) = 12-alpha-
CA   hydroxy-3-oxochol-4,6-dien-24-oyl-CoA + NADH.
CF   Flavoprotein.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Clostridium scindens,
CC       participates in the bile acid 7-alpha-dehydroxylation pathway.
CC   -!- The enzyme catalyzes two subsequent reductions of the double bonds
CC       within the bile acid A/B rings, following 7-alpha-dehydration.
DR   B0NAQ4, BAIN_CLOS5 ;
//
ID   1.3.1.115
DE   3-oxocholoyl-CoA 4-desaturase.
AN   3-oxo-choloyl-CoA dehydrogenase.
CA   (1) 7-alpha,12-alpha-dihydroxy-3-oxochol-24-oyl-CoA + NAD(+) =
CA   7-alpha,12-alpha-dihydroxy-3-oxochol-4-en-24-oyl-CoA + NADH.
CA   (2) 7-alpha-hydroxy-3-oxochol-24-oyl-CoA + NAD(+) = 7-alpha-hydroxy-3-
CA   oxochol-4-en-24-oyl-CoA + NADH.
CF   Flavoprotein.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Clostridium scindens,
CC       participates in the bile acid 7-alpha-dehydroxylation pathway.
CC   -!- The enzyme catalyzes the stereo-specific oxidation of its substrates
CC       and has no activity with the 7-beta anomers.
CC   -!- Cf. EC 1.3.1.116.
//
ID   1.3.1.116
DE   7-beta-hydroxy-3-oxochol-24-oyl-CoA 4-desaturase.
CA   7-beta-hydroxy-3-oxochol-24-oyl-CoA + NAD(+) = 7-beta-hydroxy-3-oxochol-
CA   4-en-24-oyl-CoA + NADH.
CF   FAD; FMN.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Clostridium scindens,
CC       participates in the bile acid 7-alpha-dehydroxylation pathway.
CC   -!- The enzyme catalyzes the stereo-specific oxidation of its substrate
CC       and has no activity with the 7-alpha anomer.
CC   -!- Cf. EC 1.3.1.115.
//
ID   1.3.1.117
DE   Hydroxycinnamoyl-CoA reductase.
AN   Hydroxycinnamoyl-CoA double bond reductase.
CA   (1) Dihydro-4-coumaroyl-CoA + NADP(+) = trans-4-coumaroyl-CoA + NADPH.
CA   (2) Dihydroferuloyl-CoA + NADP(+) = trans-feruloyl-CoA + NADPH.
CC   -!- Isolated from Malus X domestica (apple).
CC   -!- Involved in dihydrochalcone biosynthesis.
//
