ID   1.3.3.8
DE   Tetrahydroberberine oxidase.
AN   THB oxidase.
CA   (S)-tetrahydroberberine + 2 O(2) = berberine + 2 H(2)O(2).
CF   Flavoprotein.
CC   -!- (R)-tetrahydroberberines are not oxidized.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.5.3.8.
//
ID   1.3.3.9
DE   Transferred entry: 1.14.19.62.
//
ID   1.3.3.10
DE   Tryptophan alpha,beta-oxidase.
AN   L-tryptophan 2',3'-oxidase.
AN   L-tryptophan alpha,beta-dehydrogenase.
CA   L-tryptophan + O(2) = alpha,beta-didehydrotryptophan + H(2)O(2).
CF   Heme.
CC   -!- The enzyme from Chromobacterium violaceum is specific for tryptophan
CC       derivatives possessing its carboxyl group free or as an amide or
CC       ester, and an unsubstituted indole ring.
CC   -!- Also catalyzes the alpha,beta dehydrogenation of L-tryptophan side
CC       chains in peptides.
CC   -!- The product of the reaction can hydrolyze spontaneously to form
CC       indolepyruvate.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.4.3.17.
//
ID   1.3.3.11
DE   Pyrroloquinoline-quinone synthase.
CA   6-(2-amino-2-carboxyethyl)-7,8-dioxo-1,2,3,4,7,8-hexahydroquinoline-2,4-
CA   dicarboxylate + 3 O(2) = 4,5-dioxo-4,5-dihydro-1H-pyrrolo[2,3-
CA   f]quinoline-2,7,9-tricarboxylate + 2 H(2)O(2) + 2 H(2)O.
CC   -!- So far only a single turnover of the enzyme has been observed,
CC       and the pyrroloquinoline quinone remains bound to it; it is not yet
CC       known what releases the product in the bacterium.
