//
ID   1.3.5.2
DE   Dihydroorotate dehydrogenase (quinone).
AN   DHOD.
AN   DHOdehase.
AN   DHODH.
CA   (S)-dihydroorotate + a quinone = orotate + a quinol.
CF   FMN.
CC   -!- This Class 2 dihydroorotate dehydrogenase enzyme contains FMN.
CC   -!- The enzyme is found in eukaryotes in the mitochondrial membrane,
CC       in cyanobacteria, and in some Gram-negative and Gram-positive
CC       bacteria associated with the cytoplasmic membrane.
CC   -!- The reaction is the only redox reaction in the de-novo biosynthesis
CC       of pyrimidine nucleotides.
CC   -!- The best quinone electron acceptors for the enzyme from bovine liver
CC       are ubiquinone-6 and ubiquinone-7, although simple quinones, such as
CC       benzoquinone, can also act as acceptor at lower rates.
CC   -!- Methyl-, ethyl-, tert-butyl and benzyl-(S)-dihydroorotates are also
CC       substrates, but methyl esters of (S)-1-methyl and (S)-3-methyl and
CC       (S)-1,3-dimethyldihydroorotates are not.
CC   -!- Class 1 dihydroorotate dehydrogenases use either fumarate
CC       (EC 1.3.98.1), NAD(+) (EC 1.3.1.14) or NADP(+) (EC 1.3.1.15) as
CC       electron acceptor.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.3.99.11.
