ID   1.3.7.4
DE   Phytochromobilin:ferredoxin oxidoreductase.
AN   P-Phi-B synthase.
AN   PFB synthase.
AN   Phytochromobilin synthase.
CA   (3Z)-phytochromobilin + 2 oxidized [2Fe-2S] ferredoxin = biliverdin
CA   IX-alpha + 2 reduced [2Fe-2S] ferredoxin.
CC   -!- Catalyzes the two-electron reduction of biliverdin IX-alpha.
CC   -!- Can use [2Fe-2S] ferredoxins from a number of sources as acceptor but
CC       not the [4Fe-4S] ferredoxin from Clostridium pasteurianum.
CC   -!- The isomerization of (3Z)-phytochromobilin to (3E)-phytochromobilin
CC       is thought to occur prior to covalent attachment to apophytochrome in
CC       the plant cell cytoplasm.
CC   -!- Flavodoxins can be used instead of ferredoxin.
DR   Q9SR43, PFBS_ARATH ;
//
ID   1.3.7.5
DE   Phycocyanobilin:ferredoxin oxidoreductase.
CA   (3Z)-phycocyanobilin + 4 oxidized ferredoxin = biliverdin IX-alpha +
CA   4 reduced ferredoxin.
CC   -!- Catalyzes the four-electron reduction of biliverdin IX-alpha
CC       (2-electron reduction at both the A and D rings).
CC   -!- Reaction proceeds via an isolatable 2-electron intermediate,
CC       18(1),18(2)-dihydrobiliverdin.
CC   -!- Flavodoxins can be used instead of ferredoxin.
CC   -!- The direct conversion of biliverdin IX-alpha (BV) to (3Z)-
CC       phycocyanobilin (PCB) in the cyanobacteria Synechocystis sp.
CC       PCC 6803, Anabaena sp. PCC7120 and Nostoc punctiforme is in contrast
CC       to the proposed pathways of PCB biosynthesis in the red alga
CC       Cyanidium caldarium, which involves (3Z)-phycoerythrobilin (PEB) as
CC       an intermediate and in the green alga Mesotaenium caldariorum,
CC       in which PCB is an isolable intermediate.
