ID   1.3.7.6
DE   Phycoerythrobilin synthase.
CA   (3Z)-phycoerythrobilin + 2 oxidized ferredoxin = biliverdin IX-alpha +
CA   2 reduced ferredoxin.
CC   -!- This enzyme, from a cyanophage infecting oceanic cyanobacteria of the
CC       Prochlorococcus genus, uses a four-electron reduction to carry out
CC       the reactions catalyzed by EC 1.3.7.2 and EC 1.3.7.3.
CC   -!- 15,16-dihydrobiliverdin is formed as a bound intermediate.
CC   -!- Free 15,16-dihydrobiliverdin can also act as a substrate to form
CC       phycoerythrobilin.
DR   Q58MU6, PEBS_BPPRM ;
//
ID   1.3.7.7
DE   Ferredoxin:protochlorophyllide reductase (ATP-dependent).
AN   Light-independent protochlorophyllide reductase.
CA   Protochlorophyllide a + reduced ferredoxin + 2 ATP + 2 H(2)O =
CA   chlorophyllide a + oxidized ferredoxin + 2 ADP + 2 phosphate.
CF   Iron-sulfur.
CC   -!- Occurs in photosynthetic bacteria, cyanobacteria, green algae and
CC       gymnosperms.
CC   -!- The enzyme catalyzes trans-reduction of the D-ring of
CC       protochlorophyllide; the product has the (7S,8S)-configuration.
CC   -!- Unlike EC 1.3.1.33 light is not required.
CC   -!- The enzyme contains a [4Fe-4S] cluster, and structurally resembles
CC       the Fe protein/MoFe protein complex of EC 1.18.6.1, which catalyzes
CC       an ATP-driven reduction.
