ID   1.3.7.8
DE   Benzoyl-CoA reductase.
CA   Cyclohexa-1,5-diene-1-carbonyl-CoA + oxidized ferredoxin + 2 ADP +
CA   2 phosphate = benzoyl-CoA + reduced ferredoxin + 2 ATP + 2 H(2)O.
CF   Iron-sulfur; Mg(2+) or Mn(2+).
CC   -!- Inactive toward aromatic acids that are not CoA esters but will also
CC       catalyze the reaction: NH(3) + acceptor + 2 ADP + 2 phosphate =
CC       hydroxylamine + reduced acceptor + 2 ATP + H(2)O.
CC   -!- In the presence of reduced acceptor, but in the absence of oxidizable
CC       substrate, the enzyme catalyzes the hydrolysis of ATP to ADP plus
CC       phosphate.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.3.99.15.
DR   O87876, BCRA_THAAR ;  O87875, BCRB_THAAR ;  O87874, BCRC_THAAR ;
DR   O87877, BCRD_THAAR ;
//
ID   1.3.7.9
DE   4-hydroxybenzoyl-CoA reductase.
CA   Benzoyl-CoA + oxidized ferredoxin = 4-hydroxybenzoyl-CoA +
CA   reduced ferredoxin.
CF   Flavin; Iron-sulfur; Mo cation.
CC   -!- Involved in the anaerobic pathway of phenol metabolism in bacteria.
CC   -!- A ferredoxin with two [4Fe-4S] clusters functions as the natural
CC       electron donor.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.3.99.20.
DR   O33819, HCRA_THAAR ;  O33820, HCRB_THAAR ;  O33818, HCRC_THAAR ;
//
ID   1.3.7.10
DE   Transferred entry: 1.14.19.8.
//
ID   1.3.7.11
DE   2,3-bis-O-geranylgeranyl-sn-glycero-phospholipid reductase.
AN   2,3-bis-O-geranylgeranyl-sn-glycerol 1-phosphate reductase (donor).
CA   A 2,3-bis-(O-phytanyl)-sn-glycero-phospholipid + 16 oxidized ferredoxin
CA   [iron-sulfur] cluster = a 2,3-bis-(O-geranylgeranyl)-sn-glycero-
CA   phospholipid + 16 reduced ferredoxin [iron-sulfur] cluster + 16 H(+).
CF   FAD.
CC   -!- The enzyme is involved in the biosynthesis of archaeal membrane
CC       lipids.
CC   -!- It catalyzes the reduction of all 8 double bonds in 2,3-bis-O-
CC       geranylgeranyl-sn-glycero-phospholipids and all 4 double bonds in
CC       3-O-geranylgeranyl-sn-glycerol phospholipids with comparable
CC       activity.
CC   -!- Unlike EC 1.3.1.101, this enzyme shows no activity with NADPH,
CC       and requires a dedicated ferredoxin.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.3.99.34.
