ID   1.3.7.12
DE   Red chlorophyll catabolite reductase.
AN   RCC reductase.
AN   RCCR.
AN   Red Chl catabolite reductase.
CA   Primary fluorescent chlorophyll catabolite + 2 oxidized ferredoxin [iron-
CA   sulfur] cluster = red chlorophyll catabolite + 2 reduced ferredoxin
CA   [iron-sulfur] cluster + 2 H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme participates in chlorophyll degradation, which occurs
CC       during leaf senescence and fruit ripening in higher plants.
CC   -!- The reaction requires reduced ferredoxin, which is generated from
CC       NADPH produced either through the pentose-phosphate pathway or by the
CC       action of photosystem I.
CC   -!- This reaction takes place while red chlorophyll catabolite is still
CC       bound to EC 1.14.15.17.
CC   -!- Depending on the plant species used as the source of enzyme, one of
CC       two possible C-1 epimers of primary fluorescent chlorophyll
CC       catabolite (pFCC), pFCC-1 or pFCC-2, is normally formed, with all
CC       genera or species within a family producing the same isomer.
CC   -!- After modification and export, pFCCs are eventually imported into the
CC       vacuole, where the acidic environment causes their non-enzymic
CC       conversion into colorless breakdown products called non-fluorescent
CC       chlorophyll catabolites (NCCs).
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.3.1.80.
DR   Q8LDU4, RCCR_ARATH ;  Q9MTQ6, RCCR_HORVU ;
//
ID   1.3.7.13
DE   3,8-divinyl protochlorophyllide a 8-vinyl-reductase (ferredoxin).
AN   Cyano-type divinyl chlorophyllide a 8-vinyl-reductase.
CA   Protochlorophyllide a + 2 oxidized ferredoxin [iron-sulfur] cluster =
CA   3,8-divinyl protochlorophyllide a + 2 reduced ferredoxin [iron-sulfur]
CA   cluster + 2 H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme, found in many phototrophic bacteria, land plants,
CC       and some green and red algae, is involved in the production of
CC       monovinyl versions of (bacterio)chlorophyll pigments from their
CC       divinyl precursors.
CC   -!- It can also act on 3,8-divinyl chlorophyllide a, 3,8-divinyl
CC       chlorophyll a, and chlorophyll c2.
CC   -!- Cf. EC 1.3.1.75.
//
ID   1.3.7.14
DE   3,8-divinyl chlorophyllide a reductase.
CA   Bacteriochlorophyllide g + 2 oxidized ferredoxin [iron-sulfur] cluster +
CA   ADP + phosphate = 3,8-divinyl chlorophyllide a + 2 reduced ferredoxin
CA   [iron-sulfur] cluster + ATP + H(2)O + 2 H(+).
CF   Iron-sulfur.
CC   -!- The enzyme, found only in bacteriochlorophyll b-producing bacteria,
CC       catalyzes the introduction of a C-8 ethylidene group.
CC   -!- The enzyme contains a [4Fe-4S] cluster, and structurally resembles
CC       the Fe protein/MoFe protein complex of nitrogenase.
CC   -!- It is very similar to EC 1.3.7.15 and is composed of three subunits.
CC   -!- Two of them form the catalytic component, while the third one
CC       functions as an ATP-dependent reductase component that catalyzes the
CC       electron transfer from ferredoxin to the catalytic component.
//
ID   1.3.7.15
DE   Chlorophyllide a reductase.
CA   (1) 3-deacetyl-3-vinylbacteriochlorophyllide a + 2 oxidized ferredoxin
CA   [iron-sulfur] cluster + ADP + phosphate = chlorophyllide a + 2 reduced
CA   ferredoxin [iron-sulfur] cluster + ATP + H(2)O + 2 H(+).
CA   (2) Bacteriochlorophyllide a + 2 oxidized ferredoxin [iron-sulfur]
CA   cluster + ADP + phosphate = 3-acetyl-3-devinylchlorophyllide a +
CA   2 reduced ferredoxin [iron-sulfur] cluster + ATP + H(2)O + 2 H(+).
CA   (3) 3-deacetyl-3-(1-hydroxyethyl)bacteriochlorophyllide a + 2 oxidized
CA   ferredoxin [iron-sulfur] cluster + ADP + phosphate = 3-devinyl-3-
CA   (1-hydroxyethyl)chlorophyllide a + 2 reduced ferredoxin [iron-sulfur]
CA   cluster + ATP + H(2)O + 2 H(+).
CF   Iron-sulfur.
CC   -!- The enzyme, together with EC 1.1.1.396 and EC 4.2.1.165, is involved
CC       in the conversion of chlorophyllide a to bacteriochlorophyllide a.
CC   -!- These enzymes can act in multiple orders, resulting in the formation
CC       of different intermediates, but the final product of the cumulative
CC       action of the three enzymes is always bacteriochlorophyllide a.
CC   -!- This enzyme catalyzes a trans-reduction of the B-ring; the product
CC       has the (7R,8R)-configuration.
CC   -!- In addition, the enzyme has a latent activity of EC 1.3.7.13.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.3.99.35.
