DE   Coproporphyrinogen dehydrogenase.
AN   Coproporphyrinogen III oxidase.
AN   Oxygen-independent coproporphyrinogen-III oxidase.
CA   Coproporphyrinogen III + 2 S-adenosyl-L-methionine = protoporphyrinogen
CA   IX + 2 CO(2) + 2 L-methionine + 2 5'-deoxyadenosine.
CF   Iron-sulfur.
CC   -!- Differs from EC 1.3.3.3 by using S-adenosyl-L-methionine (AdoMet)
CC       instead of oxygen as oxidant.
CC   -!- Occurs mainly in bacteria, whereas eukaryotes use the oxygen-
CC       dependent oxidase.
