CC       combining the produced NH(3) with 2-oxoglutarate to produce a second
CC       molecule of L-glutamate (cf. EC 1.4.1.4).
CC   -!- The beta subunit transfers electrons to the cosubstrate.
CC   -!- The NH(3) is channeled through a 31 A channel in the active protein.
CC   -!- In the absence of the beta subunit, coupling between the two domains
CC       of the alpha subunit is compromised and some ammonium can be
CC       produced.
CC   -!- In the intact alpha-beta complex, ammonia production only takes place
CC       as part of the overall reaction.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 2.6.1.53.
