ID   1.4.99.5
DE   Glycine dehydrogenase (cyanide-forming).
AN   HCN synthase.
AN   Hydrogen cyanide synthase.
CA   Glycine + 2 A = hydrogen cyanide + CO(2) + 2 AH(2).
CF   FAD.
CC   -!- The enzyme is membrane-bound, and the 2-electron acceptor is a
CC       component of the respiratory chain.
CC   -!- The enzyme can act with various artificial electron acceptors,
CC       including phenazine methosulfate.
DR   G3XD67, HCNA_PSEAE ;  O85226, HCNA_PSEPH ;  Q9I1S2, HCNB_PSEAE ;
DR   O85227, HCNB_PSEPH ;  G3XD12, HCNC_PSEAE ;  O85228, HCNC_PSEPH ;
//
ID   1.4.99.6
DE   D-arginine dehydrogenase.
AN   D-amino-acid dehydrogenase.
CA   D-arginine + acceptor + H(2)O = 5-guanidino-2-oxopentanoate + NH(3) +
CA   reduced acceptor.
CF   FAD.
CC   -!- The enzyme, which has been isolated from the bacterium Pseudomonas
CC       aeruginosa PAO1, forms with EC 1.4.1.25 a two-enzyme complex involved
CC       in the racemization of D- and L-arginine.
CC   -!- The enzyme has a broad substrate range and can act on most D-amino
CC       acids with the exception of D-glutamate and D-aspartate.
CC   -!- However, activity is maximal with D-arginine and D-lysine.
CC   -!- Not active on glycine.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.4.99.1.
DR   Q9HXE3, DAUA_PSEAE ;
//
ID   1.5.1.1
DE   1-piperideine-2-carboxylate/1-pyrroline-2-carboxylate reductase
DE   (NAD(P)H).
AN   Pyrroline-2-carboxylate reductase.
CA   (1) L-pipecolate + NAD(P)(+) = 1-piperideine-2-carboxylate + NAD(P)H.
CA   (2) L-proline + NAD(P)(+) = 1-pyrroline-2-carboxylate + NAD(P)H.
CC   -!- The enzymes, characterized from the bacterium Azospirillum
CC       brasilense, is involved in trans-3-hydroxy-L-proline metabolism.
CC   -!- In contrast to EC 1.5.1.21, which is specific for NADPH, this enzyme
CC       shows similar activity with NADPH and NADH.
DR   V5YW53, PY2CR_AZOBR;
//
