DR   P38230, QOR_YEAST  ;  Q9AYU1, QR1_TRIVS  ;
//
ID   1.6.5.6
DE   p-benzoquinone reductase (NADPH).
CA   NADPH + p-benzoquinone = NADP(+) + hydroquinone.
CC   -!- Involved in the 4-nitrophenol degradation pathway in bacteria.
DR   C1I202, PNPB_PSEWB ;
//
ID   1.6.5.7
DE   2-hydroxy-1,4-benzoquinone reductase.
AN   Hydroxybenzoquinone reductase.
CA   2-hydroxy-1,4-benzoquinone + NADH = hydroxyquinol + NAD(+).
CF   FMN.
CC   -!- The enzyme differs in substrate speificity from other quinone
CC       reductases.
CC   -!- The enzyme in Burkholderia cepacia is inducible by 2,4,5-
CC       trichlorophenoxyacetate.
DR   D3KVM6, HBQR_BURSP ;
//
ID   1.6.5.8
DE   Transferred entry: 7.2.1.1.
//
ID   1.6.5.9
DE   NADH:ubiquinone reductase (non-electrogenic).
AN   Coenzyme Q reductase.
AN   Electron transfer complex I.
AN   NADH(2) dehydrogenase (ubiquinone).
AN   NADH-coenzyme Q oxidoreductase.
AN   NADH-coenzyme Q reductase.
AN   NADH-CoQ oxidoreductase.
AN   NADH-CoQ reductase.
AN   NADH-Q6 oxidoreductase.
AN   NADH-ubiquinone oxidoreductase.
AN   NADH-ubiquinone reductase.
AN   Ubiquinone reductase.
CA   NADH + ubiquinone = NAD(+) + ubiquinol.
CF   FAD.
CC   -!- Occurs in mitochondria of yeast and plants, and in aerobic bacteria.
CC   -!- Has low activity with NADPH.
DR   M1BYJ7, ENDB1_SOLTU;  M0ZYF3, INDA1_SOLTU;  Q8GWA1, NDA1_ARATH ;
