//
ID   1.6.5.10
DE   NADPH dehydrogenase (quinone).
CA   NADPH + a quinone = NADP(+) + a quinol.
CF   Flavoprotein.
CC   -!- The enzyme from Escherichia coli is specific for NADPH and is most
CC       active with quinone derivatives and ferricyanide as electron
CC       acceptors.
CC   -!- Menaquinone can act as acceptor.
CC   -!- The enzyme from hog liver is inhibited by dicoumarol and folic acid
CC       derivatives but not by 2,4-dinitrophenol.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.6.99.6.
//
ID   1.6.5.11
DE   NADH dehydrogenase (quinone).
CA   NADH + a quinone = NAD(+) + a quinol.
CC   -!- Menaquinone or other quinones can act as acceptor.
CC   -!- Inhibited by AMP and 2,4-dinitrophenol but not by dicoumarol or folic
CC       acid derivatives.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.6.99.5.
