ID   1.7.1.14
DE   Nitric oxide reductase (NAD(P)(+), nitrous oxide-forming).
AN   Cytochrome P450nor.
AN   Fungal nitric oxide reductase.
AN   NOR.
CA   Nitrous oxide + NAD(P)(+) + H(2)O = 2 nitric oxide + NAD(P)H.
CF   Heme-thiolate.
CC   -!- The enzyme from Fusarium oxysporum utilizes only NADH, but the
CC       isozyme from Trichosporon cutaneum utilizes both NADH and NADPH.
CC   -!- The electron transfer from NAD(P)H to heme occurs directly,
CC       not requiring flavin or other redox cofactors.
DR   P23295, NOR_FUSOX  ;
//
ID   1.7.1.15
DE   Nitrite reductase (NADH).
AN   Assimilatory nitrite reductase.
AN   NADH-nitrite oxidoreductase.
AN   Nitrite reductase (reduced nicotinamide adenine dinucleotide).
CA   Ammonia + 3 NAD(+) + 2 H(2)O = nitrite + 3 NADH.
CF   FAD; Iron-sulfur; Siroheme.
CC   -!- This prokaryotic enzyme is specific for NADH.
CC   -!- In addition to catalyzing the 6-electron reduction of nitrite to
CC       ammonia, the enzyme from Escherichia coli can also catalyze the
CC       2-electron reduction of hydroxylamine to ammonia.
CC   -!- cf. EC 1.7.1.4.
DR   P08201, NIRB_ECOLI ;  P0A9I9, NIRD_ECO57 ;  P0A9I8, NIRD_ECOLI ;
DR   P0A230, NIRD_SALTI ;  P0A229, NIRD_SALTY ;
//
ID   1.7.1.16
DE   Nitrobenzene nitroreductase.
CA   N-phenylhydroxylamine + 2 NADP(+) + H(2)O = nitrobenzene + 2 NADPH.
CF   FMN.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from Pseudomonas species, catalyzes two
CC       successive reductions of nitrobenzene, via a nitrosobenzene
CC       intermediate.
CC   -!- It is also active on 1-chloro-4-nitrobenzene.
DR   Q5XW77, CNBA_COMTE ;  Q6DLR9, NBZA_PSEPS ;
//
ID   1.7.1.17
DE   FMN-dependent NADH-azoreductase.
CA   Anthranilate + N,N-dimethyl-1,4-phenylenediamine + 2 NAD(+) =
CA   2-(4-dimethylaminophenyl)diazenylbenzoate + 2 NADH.
CF   FMN.
CC   -!- The enzyme catalyzes the reductive cleavage of an azo bond in
CC       aromatic azo compounds to form the corresponding amines.
CC   -!- Does not accept NADPH.
CC   -!- Cf. EC 1.7.1.6.
//
ID   1.7.2.1
DE   Nitrite reductase (NO-forming).
AN   cd-cytochrome nitrite reductase.
AN   Cytochrome c-551:O(2), NO(2)(+) oxidoreductase.
AN   Cytochrome cd.
AN   Cytochrome cd1.
AN   Hydroxylamine (acceptor) reductase.
AN   Methyl viologen-nitrite reductase.
AN   Nitrite reductase.
AN   Nitrite reductase (cytochrome).
AN   Nitrite reductase (cytochrome; NO-forming).
AN   Pseudomonas cytochrome oxidase.
CA   Nitric oxide + H(2)O + ferricytochrome c = nitrite + ferrocytochrome c +
CA   2 H(+).
CF   Cu cation or Fe cation; FAD.
CC   -!- The reaction is catalyzed by two types of enzymes, found in the
CC       perimplasm of denitrifying bacteria.
CC   -!- One type comprises proteins containing multiple copper centers,
CC       the other a heme protein, cytochrome cd1.
CC   -!- Acceptors include c-type cytochromes such as cytochrome c-550 or
CC       cytochrome c-551 from Paracoccus denitrificans or Pseudomonas
CC       aeruginosa, and small blue copper proteins such as azurin and
CC       pseudoazurin.
CC   -!- Cytochrome cd1 also has oxidase and hydroxylamine reductase
CC       activities.
CC   -!- May also catalyze the reaction of EC 1.7.99.1 since this is a well-
CC       known activity of cytochrome cd1.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.6.6.5, EC 1.7.99.3 and EC 1.9.3.2.
DR   Q02219, ANIA_NEIGO ;  Q9JTB8, ANIA_NEIMA ;  Q9JYE1, ANIA_NEIMB ;
DR   Q92Z29, NIRK_RHIME ;  Q51700, NIRS_PARDP ;  P72181, NIRS_PARPN ;
