ID   1.7.3.2
DE   Acetylindoxyl oxidase.
CA   N-acetylindoxyl + O(2) = N-acetylisatin + H(2)O.
//
ID   1.7.3.3
DE   Factor independent urate hydroxylase.
AN   Urate oxidase.
AN   Uric acid oxidase.
AN   Uricase.
AN   Uricase II.
CA   Urate + O(2) + H(2)O = 5-hydroxyisourate + H(2)O(2).
CC   -!- Was previously thought to be a copper protein, but it is now known
CC       that the enzymes from soybean (Glycine max), the mold Aspergillus
CC       flavus and Bacillus subtilis contains no copper nor any other
CC       transition-metal ion.
CC   -!- The 5-hydroxyisourate formed decomposes spontaneously to form
CC       allantoin and CO(2), although there is an enzyme-catalyzed pathway in
CC       which EC 3.5.2.17 catalyzes the first step.
CC   -!- The enzyme is different from EC 1.14.13.113.
