ID   1.7.3.6
DE   Hydroxylamine oxidase (cytochrome).
AN   HAO.
AN   Hydroxylamine oxidase.
AN   Hydroxylamine oxidoreductase.
CA   Hydroxylamine + O(2) = nitrite + H(2)O + H(+).
CF   Fe cation.
CC   -!- The enzyme from the heterotrophic nitrifying bacterium Paracoccus
CC       denitrificans contains three to five non-heme, non-iron-sulfur iron
CC       atoms and interacts with cytochrome c(556) and pseudoazurin.
CC   -!- Under anaerobic conditions in vitro only nitrous oxide is formed.
CC   -!- Presumably nitroxyl is released and combines with a second nitroxyl
CC       to give nitrous oxide and water.
CC   -!- When oxygen is present, nitrite is formed.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.7.3.4.
