ID   1.8.5.7
DE   Glutathionyl-hydroquinone reductase.
CA   Glutathione + 2-(glutathione-S-yl)-hydroquinone = glutathione disulfide +
CA   hydroquinone.
CC   -!- This type of enzymes, which are found in bacteria, halobacteria,
CC       fungi, and plants, catalyze the glutathione-dependent reduction of
CC       glutathionyl-hydroquinones.
CC   -!- The enzyme from the bacterium Sphingobium chlorophenolicum can act on
CC       halogenated substrates such as 2,6-dichloro-3-(glutathione-S-yl)-
CC       hydroquinone and 2,3,5-trichloro-6-(glutathione-S-yl)-hydroquinone.
CC   -!- Substrates for these enzymes are often formed spontaneously by
CC       interaction of benzoquinones with glutathione.
DR   Q8KN33, PCPF_SPHCR ;  P42620, YQJG_ECOLI ;
