ID   1.11.1.8
DE   Iodide peroxidase.
AN   Iodinase.
AN   Iodotyrosine deiodase.
AN   Iodotyrosine deiodinase.
AN   Thyroid peroxidase.
AN   Thyroperoxidase.
AN   TPO.
CA   (1) 2 iodide + H(2)O(2) + 2 H(+) = diiodine + 2 H(2)O.
CA   (2) [Thyroglobulin]-L-tyrosine + iodide + H(2)O(2) = [thyroglobulin]-3-
CA   iodo-L-tyrosine + 2 H(2)O.
CA   (3) [Thyroglobulin]-3-iodo-L-tyrosine + iodide + H(2)O(2) =
CA   [thyroglobulin]-3,5-diiodo-L-tyrosine + 2 H(2)O.
CA   (4) 2 [thyroglobulin]-3,5-diiodo-L-tyrosine + H(2)O(2) = [thyroglobulin]-
CA   L-thyroxine + [thyroglobulin]-aminoacrylate + 2 H(2)O.
CA   (5) [Thyroglobulin]-3-iodo-L-tyrosine + [thyroglobulin]-3,5-diiodo-L-
CA   tyrosine + H(2)O(2) = [thyroglobulin]-3,5,3'-triiodo-L-thyronine +
CA   [thyroglobulin]-aminoacrylate + 2 H(2)O.
CF   Heme.
CC   -!- Thyroid peroxidase catalyzes the biosynthesis of the thyroid hormones
CC       L-thyroxine and triiodo-L-thyronine.
CC   -!- It catalyzes both the iodination of tyrosine residues in
CC       thyroglobulin (forming mono- and di-iodinated forms) and their
CC       coupling to form either L-thyroxine or triiodo-L-thyronine.
PR   PROSITE; PDOC00394;
