ID   1.13.12.13
DE   Oplophorus-luciferin 2-monooxygenase.
AN   Oplophorus luciferase.
CA   Oplophorus luciferin + O(2) = oxidized Oplophorus luciferin + CO(2) +
CA   light.
CC   -!- The luciferase from the deep sea shrimp Oplophorus gracilirostris is
CC       a complex composed of more than one protein.
CC   -!- The enzyme's specificity is quite broad, with both coelenterazine and
CC       bisdeoxycoelenterazine being good substrates.
DR   Q9GV45, LUCI_OPLGR ;
//
ID   1.13.12.14
DE   Transferred entry: 1.14.13.122.
//
ID   1.13.12.15
DE   3,4-dihydroxyphenylalanine oxidative deaminase.
AN   DOPA oxidative deaminase.
AN   DOPAODA.
AN   Oxidative deaminase.
CA   2 L-dopa + O(2) = 2 3,4-dihydroxyphenylpyruvate + 2 NH(3).
CC   -!- One of the three enzymes involved in L-dopa (3,4-
CC       dihydroxyphenylalanine) catabolism in the non-oxygenic phototrophic
CC       bacterium Rubrivivax benzoatilyticus OU5 (and not Rhodobacter
CC       sphaeroides OU5 as had been thought), the other two being EC 4.3.1.22
CC       and EC 2.6.1.49.
CC   -!- In addition to DOPA, the enzyme can also use L-tyrosine,
CC       L-phenylalanine, L-tryptophan and glutamate as substrate, but more
CC       slowly.
CC   -!- Inhibited by NADH and 2-oxoglutarate.
//
ID   1.13.12.16
DE   Nitronate monooxygenase.
AN   2-nitropropane dioxygenase.
AN   2-NPD.
AN   Nitroalkane oxidase.
AN   NMO.
CA   Ethylnitronate + O(2) = acetaldehyde + nitrite + other products.
CF   FMN.
CC   -!- Previously classified as EC 1.13.11.32, but it is now recognized that
CC       this was the result of the slow ionization of nitroalkanes to their
CC       nitronate (anionic) forms.
CC   -!- The enzymes from the fungus Neurospora crassa and the yeast
CC       Williopsis saturnus var. mrakii (formerly classified as Hansenula
CC       mrakii) contain non-covalently bound FMN as the cofactor.
CC   -!- Neither hydrogen peroxide nor superoxide were detected during enzyme
CC       turnover.
CC   -!- Active toward linear alkyl nitronates of lengths between 2 and 6
CC       carbon atoms and, with lower activity, toward propyl-2-nitronate.
CC   -!- The enzyme from N.crassa can also utilize neutral nitroalkanes,
CC       but with lower activity.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.13.11.32.
DR   P47177, 2NDP_YEAST ;  Q12723, 2NPD_CYBMR ;  Q01284, 2NPD_NEUCR ;
//
ID   1.13.12.17
DE   Dichloroarcyriaflavin A synthase.
CA   Dichlorochromopyrrolate + 4 O(2) + 4 NADH = dichloroarcyriaflavin A +
CA   2 CO(2) + 6 H(2)O + 4 NAD(+).
CC   -!- The conversion of dichlorochromopyrrolate to dichloroarcyriaflavin A
CC       is a complex process that involves two enzyme components.
CC   -!- RebP is an NAD-dependent cytochrome P(450) oxygenase that performs an
CC       aryl-aryl bond formation yielding the six-ring indolocarbazole
CC       scaffold.
CC   -!- Along with RebC, a flavin-dependent hydroxylase, it also catalyzes
CC       the oxidative decarboxylation of both carboxyl groups.
CC   -!- The presence of RebC ensures that the only product is the
CC       rebeccamycin aglycone dichloroarcyriaflavin A.
CC   -!- The enzymes are similar, but not identical, to StaP and StaC, which
CC       are involved in the synthesis of staurosporine.
PR   PROSITE; PDOC00081;
//
ID   1.13.12.18
DE   Dinoflagellate luciferase.
CA   Dinoflagellate luciferin + O(2) = oxidized dinoflagellate luciferin +
CA   H(2)O + light.
CC   -!- A luciferase from dinoflagelates such as Gonyaulax polyhedra,
CC       Lingulodinium polyedrum, Noctiluca scintillans, and Pyrocystis
CC       lunula.
CC   -!- It is a single protein with three luciferase domains.
CC   -!- The luciferin is strongly bound by a luciferin binding protein above
CC       a pH of 7.
DR   O77206, LUCIF_LINPO;
//
ID   1.13.12.19
DE   2-oxuglutarate dioxygenase (ethene-forming).
AN   Ethylene-forming enzyme.
CA   2-oxoglutarate + O(2) = ethylene + 3 CO(2) + H(2)O.
CC   -!- This is one of two simultaneous reactions catalyzed by the enzyme,
CC       which is responsible for ethene production in bacteria of the
CC       Pseudomonas syringae group.
CC   -!- In the other reaction (EC 1.14.11.34) the enzyme catalyzes the mono-
CC       oxygenation of both 2-oxoglutarate and L-arginine, forming succinate,
CC       carbon dioxide and L-hydroxyarginine, which is subsequently cleaved
CC       into guanidine and (S)-1-pyrroline-5-carboxylate.
CC   -!- The enzymes catalyze two cycles of the ethene-forming reaction for
CC       each cycle of the succinate-forming reaction, so that the
CC       stoichiometry of the products ethene and succinate is 2:1.
DR   Q9Z377, EFE_PSEAQ  ;  Q7BS31, EFE_PSECA  ;  Q7BS32, EFE_PSESG  ;
DR   P32021, EFE_PSESH  ;  Q9Z3T0, EFE_PSESJ  ;  Q8XPV7, EFE_RALSO  ;
//
ID   1.13.12.20
DE   Noranthrone monooxygenase.
AN   Norsolorinate anthrone oxidase.
CA   Norsolorinic acid anthrone + O(2) = norsolorinic acid + H(2)O.
CC   -!- Involved in the synthesis of aflatoxins in the fungus Aspergillus
CC       parasiticus.
DR   B8NI03, HYPC_ASPFN ;
//
ID   1.13.12.21
DE   Tetracenomycin-F1 monooxygenase.
CA   Tetracenomycin F1 + O(2) = tetracenomycin D3 + H(2)O.
CC   -!- The enzyme is involved in biosynthesis of the anthracycline
CC       antibiotic tetracenomycin C by the bacterium Streptomyces
CC       glaucescens.
DR   P39889, TCMH_STRGA ;
//
ID   1.13.12.22
DE   Deoxynogalonate monooxygenase.
AN   12-deoxynogalonic acid monooxygenase.
AN   12-deoxynogalonic acid oxidoreductase.
AN   Deoxynogalonate oxidase.
CA   Deoxynogalonate + O(2) = nogalonate + H(2)O.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Streptomyces nogalater,
CC       is involved in the biosynthesis of the aromatic polyketide
CC       nogalamycin.
DR   O54259, SNOAB_STRNO;
//
ID   1.13.12.23
DE   4-hydroxy-3-prenylbenzoate synthase.
CA   3-dimethylallyl-4-hydroxymandelate + O(2) = 3-dimethylallyl-4-
CA   hydroxybenzoate + CO(2) + H(2)O.
CC   -!- Isolated from the bacterium Streptomyces roseochromogenes DS 12976.
CC   -!- A bifunctional enzyme involved in clorobiocin biosynthesis that also
CC       catalyzes the activity of EC 1.13.11.83.
DR   Q8GHB1, CLOR_STRRC ;
