ID   1.14.11.29
DE   Hypoxia-inducible factor-proline dioxygenase.
AN   HIF hydroxylase.
CA   Hypoxia-inducible factor-L-proline + 2-oxoglutarate + O(2) = hypoxia-
CA   inducible factor-trans-4-hydroxy-L-proline + succinate + CO(2).
CF   Fe(2+); L-ascorbate.
CC   -!- Contains iron, and requires ascorbate.
CC   -!- Specifically hydroxylates a proline residue in HIF-alpha, the alpha
CC       subunit of the transcriptional regulator HIF (hypoxia-inducible
CC       factor), which targets HIF for proteasomal destruction.
CC   -!- The requirement of oxygen for the hydroxylation reaction enables
CC       animals to respond to hypoxia.
