ID   1.14.11.n2
DE   Methylcytosine dioxygenase.
CA   DNA 5-methylcytosine + 2-oxoglutarate + O(2) =
CA   DNA 5-hydroxymethylcytosine + succinate + CO(2).
CF   Fe(2+).
CC   -!- Dioxygenase that catalyzes the conversion of the modified genomic
CC       base 5-methylcytosine (5mC) into 5-hydroxymethylcytosine (5hmC).
CC   -!- Might initiate a process leading to cytosine demethylation through
CC       deamination into 5-hydroxymethyluracil (5hmU) and subsequent
CC       replacement by unmethylated cytosine by the base excision repair
CC       system.
CC   -!- Methylation at the C5 position of cytosine bases is an epigenetic
CC       modification of the mammalian genome which plays an important role in
CC       transcriptional regulation.
DR   Q8NFU7, TET1_HUMAN ;  Q3URK3, TET1_MOUSE ;  D2W6T1, TET1_NAEGR ;
DR   Q6N021, TET2_HUMAN ;  Q4JK59, TET2_MOUSE ;  A0A1L8GSA2, TET3A_XENLA;
DR   K9JHZ4, TET3B_XENLA;  O43151, TET3_HUMAN ;  Q8BG87, TET3_MOUSE ;
DR   A0JP82, TET3_XENTR ;
