ID   1.14.12.22
DE   Carbazole 1,9a-dioxygenase.
AN   CARDO.
CA   9H-carbazole + NAD(P)H + O(2) = 2'-aminobiphenyl-2,3-diol + NAD(P)(+).
CF   Fe cation; Iron-sulfur.
CC   -!- This enzyme catalyzes the first reaction in the pathway of carbazole
CC       degradation.
CC   -!- The enzyme attacks at the 1 and 9a positions of carbazole, resulting
CC       in the formation of a highly unstable hemiaminal intermediate that
CC       undergoes a spontaneous cleavage and rearomatization, resulting in
CC       2'-aminobiphenyl-2,3-diol.
CC   -!- In most bacteria the enzyme is a complex composed of a terminal
CC       oxygenase, a ferredoxin, and a ferredoxin reductase.
CC   -!- The terminal oxygenase component contains a nonheme iron center and a
CC       Rieske [2Fe-2S] iron-sulfur cluster.
DR   Q8G8B6, CARAA_PSERE;  D5IGG0, CARAA_SPHSX;
//
ID   1.14.12.23
DE   Nitroarene dioxygenase.
CA   Nitrobenzene + NADH + O(2) = catechol + nitrite + NAD(+).
CF   Fe(2+).
CC   -!- This enzyme is a member of the naphthalene family of bacterial Rieske
CC       non-heme iron dioxygenases.
CC   -!- It comprises a multicomponent system, containing a Rieske [2Fe-2S]
CC       ferredoxin, an NADH-dependent flavoprotein reductase (EC 1.18.1.3),
CC       and an alpha-3-beta-3 oxygenase.
CC   -!- The enzyme forms of a cis-dihydroxylated product that spontaneously
CC       rearranges to form a catechol with accompanying release of nitrite.
CC   -!- It can typically act on many different nitroaromatic compounds,
CC       including chlorinated species.
CC   -!- Enzymes found in different strains may have different substrate
CC       preferences.
//
ID   1.14.12.24
DE   2,4-dinitrotoluene dioxygenase.
CA   2,4-dinitrotoluene + NADH + O(2) = 4-methyl-5-nitrocatechol + nitrite +
CA   NAD(+).
CC   -!- This enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Burkholderia sp. strain
CC       DNT, is a member of the naphthalene family of bacterial Rieske non-
CC       heme iron dioxygenases.
CC   -!- It comprises a multicomponent system, containing a Rieske [2Fe-2S]
CC       ferredoxin, an NADH-dependent flavoprotein reductase (EC 1.18.1.3),
CC       and an alpha-3-beta-3 oxygenase.
CC   -!- The enzyme forms a cis-dihydroxylated product that spontaneously
CC       rearranges to form a catechol with accompanying release of nitrite.
CC   -!- It does not act on nitrobenzene.
CC   -!- Cf. EC 1.14.12.23.
DR   Q45695, DNTAC_BURSR;
//
ID   1.14.12.25
DE   p-cumate 2,3-dioxygenase.
CA   p-cumate + NADH + O(2) = (2R,3S)-2,3-dihydroxy-2,3-dihydro-p-cumate +
CA   NAD(+).
