DE   4-nitrocatechol 4-monooxygenase.
CA   4-nitrocatechol + NAD(P)H + O(2) = 2-hydroxy-1,4-benzoquinone + nitrite +
CA   NAD(P)(+) + H(2)O.
CF   FAD.
CC   -!- The enzyme catalyzes the oxidation of 4-nitrocatechol with the
CC       concomitant removal of the nitro group as nitrite.
CC   -!- Forms a two-component system with a flavoprotein reductase.
CC   -!- The enzymes from the bacteria Lysinibacillus sphaericus JS905 and
CC       Rhodococcus sp. strain PN1 were shown to also catalyze EC 1.14.13.29,
CC       while the enzyme from Pseudomonas sp. WBC-3 was shown to also
CC       catalyze EC 1.14.13.167.
