ID   1.14.13.200
DE   Tetracenomycin A2 monooxygenase-diooxygenase.
CA   Tetracenomycin A2 + 2 O(2) + 2 NAD(P)H = tetracenomycin C + 2 NAD(P)(+) +
CA   H(2)O.
CC   -!- Isolated from the bacterium Streptomyces glaucescens.
CC   -!- The enzyme was also isolated from the bacterium Streptomyces
CC       olivaceus, where it acts on 8-demethyltetracenomycin A2
CC       (tetracenomycin B2) as part of elloramycin biosynthesis.
CC   -!- The reaction involves a monooxygenase reaction which is followed by a
CC       dioxygenase reaction giving a gem-diol and an epoxide.
CC   -!- Water opens the epoxide giving two hydroxy groups.
CC   -!- The gem-diol eliminates water to give a ketone which is then reduced
CC       to a hydroxy group.
//
ID   1.14.13.201
