DE   F-actin monooxygenase.
CA   [F-actin]-L-methionine + NADPH + O(2) + H(+) = [F-actin]-L-methionine-
CA   (R)-S-oxide + NADP(+) + H(2)O.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the fruit fly Drosophila melanogaster,
CC       is a multi-domain oxidoreductase that acts as an F-actin disassembly
CC       factor.
CC   -!- The enzyme selectively reduces two L-Met residues of F-actin, causing
CC       fragmentation of the filaments and preventing repolymerization.
CC   -!- Free methionine is not a substrate.
CC   -!- The reaction is stereospecific and generates the (R)-sulfoxide.
