ID   1.14.13.234
DE   12-dehydrotetracycline 5-monooxygenase.
CA   12-dehydrotetracycline + NADPH + O(2) = 5a,11a-dehydrooxytetracycline +
CA   NADP(+) + H(2)O.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Streptomyces rimosus,
CC       is bifunctional, catalyzing two successive monooxygenation reactions.
CC   -!- It starts by catalyzing the stereospecific hydroxylation of
CC       anhydrotetracycline at C(6) (EC 1.14.13.38).
CC   -!- If the released product is captured by EC 1.3.98.4 it is reduced to
CC       tetracycline.
CC   -!- However, if the released product is recaptured by OxyS, it performs
CC       an additional hydroxylation at C(5), producing 5a,11a-
CC       dehydrooxytetracycline, which, following the action of EC 1.3.98.4,
CC       becomes oxytetracycline.
DR   L8EUQ6, OXYS_STRR1 ;
