ID   1.14.14.3
DE   Bacterial luciferase.
AN   Aldehyde monooxygenase.
AN   Alkanal monooxygenase (FMN-linked).
CA   A long-chain aldehyde + FMNH(2) + O(2) = a long-chain fatty acid + FMN +
CA   H(2)O + light.
CC   -!- The reaction sequence starts with the incorporation of a molecule of
CC       oxygen into reduced FMN bound to the enzyme, forming luciferase
CC       peroxyflavin.
CC   -!- The peroxyflavin interacts with an aliphatic long-chain aldehyde,
CC       producing a highly fluorescent species believed to be luciferase
CC       hydroxyflavin.
CC   -!- The enzyme is highly specific for reduced FMN and for long-chain
CC       aliphatic aldehydes with eight carbons or more.
CC   -!- The highest efficiency is achieved with tetradecanal.
CC   -!- Cf. EC 1.13.12.18.
PR   PROSITE; PDOC00397;
DR   P09140, LUXA1_PHOLE;  P19839, LUXA1_PHOLU;  P29238, LUXA2_PHOLE;
DR   P23146, LUXA2_PHOLU;  P19907, LUXA_ALIFS ;  P18299, LUXA_KRYAS ;
