ID   1.14.14.8
DE   Anthranilate 3-monooxygenase (FAD).
AN   Anthranilate 3-hydroxylase.
AN   Anthranilate hydroxylase.
CA   Anthranilate + FADH(2) + O(2) = 3-hydroxyanthranilate + FAD + H(2)O.
CC   -!- This enzyme, isolated from the bacterium Geobacillus
CC       thermodenitrificans, participates in the pathway of tryptophan
CC       degradation.
CC   -!- The enzyme is part of a system that also includes a bifunctional
CC       riboflavin kinase/FMN adenylyltransferase and an FAD reductase, which
CC       ensures ample supply of FAD to the monooxygenase.
DR   A4IT51, HPAH_GEOTN ;
//
ID   1.14.14.9
DE   4-hydroxyphenylacetate 3-monooxygenase.
AN   4 HPA 3-hydroxylase.
AN   4-hydroxyphenylacetic acid-3-hydroxylase.
AN   p-hydroxyphenylacetate 3-hydroxylase.
CA   4-hydroxyphenylacetate + FADH(2) + O(2) = 3,4-dihydroxyphenylacetate +
CA   FAD + H(2)O.
CF   FAD.
CC   -!- The enzyme from Escherichia coli attacks a broad spectrum of phenolic
CC       compounds.
CC   -!- The enzyme uses FADH(2) as a substrate rather than a cofactor.
CC   -!- FADH(2) is provided by EC 1.5.1.36.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.14.13.3.
DR   Q57160, HPAB_ECOLX ;  Q48440, HPAB_KLEOX ;  Q9HWT7, HPAB_PSEAE ;
DR   Q5SJP8, HPAB_THET8 ;  Q6Q272, HPAH_ACIBA ;  Q4L1M7, HPAH_GEOP9 ;
DR   A4IT51, HPAH_GEOTN ;  C0SPC0, YOAI_BACSU ;
//
ID   1.14.14.10
DE   Nitrilotriacetate monooxygenase.
CA   Nitrilotriacetate + FMNH(2) + H(+) + O(2) = iminodiacetate + glyoxylate +
CA   FMN + H(2)O.
CF   Mg(2+).
CC   -!- The enzyme from Aminobacter aminovorans (previously Chelatobacter
CC       heintzii) is part of a two component system that also includes
CC       EC 1.5.1.42 (FMN reductase), which provides reduced flavin
CC       mononucleotide for this enzyme.
DR   P54989, NTAA_AMIAI ;
//
ID   1.14.14.11
DE   Styrene monooxygenase.
CA   Styrene + FADH(2) + O(2) = (S)-2-phenyloxirane + FAD + H(2)O.
CC   -!- The enzyme catalyzes the first step in the aerobic styrene
CC       degradation pathway.
CC   -!- It forms a two-component system with a reductase (StyB) that utilizes
CC       NADH to reduce FAD, which is then transferred to the oxygenase.
DR   O06834, STYA_PSEFL ;  O50214, STYA_PSESP ;
//
ID   1.14.14.12
DE   3-hydroxy-9,10-secoandrosta-1,3,5(10)-triene-9,17-dione monooxygenase.
CA   3-hydroxy-9,10-secoandrosta-1,3,5(10)-triene-9,17-dione + FMNH(2) + O(2)
CA   = 3,4-dihydroxy-9,10-secoandrosta-1,3,5(10)-triene-9,17-dione + FMN +
CA   H(2)O.
CC   -!- This bacterial enzyme participates in the degradation of several
CC       steroids, including cholesterol and testosterone.
CC   -!- It can use either FADH or FMNH(2) as flavin cofactor.
CC   -!- The enzyme forms a two-component system with a reductase (HsaB) that
CC       utilizes NADH to reduce the flavin, which is then transferred to the
CC       oxygenase subunit.
DR   P9WJA0, HSAA_MYCTO ;  P9WJA1, HSAA_MYCTU ;  Q0S811, HSAA_RHOJR ;
//
ID   1.14.14.13
DE   4-(gamma-L-glutamylamino)butanoyl-[BtrI acyl-carrier protein]
DE   monooxygenase.
CA   4-(gamma-L-glutamylamino)butanoyl-[BtrI acyl-carrier protein] + FMNH(2) +
CA   O(2) = 4-(gamma-L-glutamylamino)-(2S)-2-hydroxybutanoyl-[BtrI acyl-
CA   carrier protein] + FMN + H(2)O.
CF   FMNH(2).
CC   -!- Catalyzes a step in the biosynthesis of the side chain of the
CC       aminoglycoside antibiotics of the butirosin family.
CC   -!- Forms a complex with a dedicated NAD(P)H:FMN oxidoreductase.
CC   -!- The enzyme is not able to hydroxylate free substrates, activation by
CC       the acyl-carrier protein is mandatory.
CC   -!- Octanoyl-S-[BtrI acyl-carrier protein] is also accepted.
DR   Q4H4E5, BTRO_BACCI ;  Q4H4E3, BTRV_BACCI ;
//
ID   1.14.14.14
DE   Aromatase.
AN   CYP19A1.
AN   Estrogen synthetase.
CA   (1) Testosterone + 3 [reduced NADPH--hemoprotein reductase] + 3 O(2) =
CA   17-beta-estradiol + formate + 4 H(2)O + 3 [oxidized NADPH--hemoprotein
CA   reductase].
CA   (2) Androst-4-ene-3,17-dione + 3 [reduced NADPH--hemoprotein reductase] +
CA   3 O(2) = estrone + formate + 4 H(2)O + 3 [oxidized NADPH--hemoprotein
CA   reductase].
CC   -!- The enzyme catalyzes three sequential hydroxylations of the androgens
CC       androst-4-ene-3,17-dione and testosterone, resulting in their
CC       aromatization and forming the estrogens estrone and 17-beta-
CC       estradiol, respectively.
DR   O42145, C19AA_DANRE;  P79690, CP191_CARAU;  Q29624, CP191_PIG  ;
DR   O73686, CP192_CARAU;  P79430, CP192_PIG  ;  P79304, CP193_PIG  ;
DR   Q6QHT9, CP19A_ANGJA;  P46194, CP19A_BOVIN;  Q95M61, CP19A_CALJA;
DR   Q5QQX7, CP19A_CANLF;  Q6YI21, CP19A_CAPHI;  P19098, CP19A_CHICK;
DR   P79699, CP19A_COTJA;  O46512, CP19A_HORSE;  P11511, CP19A_HUMAN;
DR   Q92111, CP19A_ICTPU;  Q69FB6, CP19A_LAGAC;  P28649, CP19A_MOUSE;
DR   P70091, CP19A_ORENI;  Q92087, CP19A_ORYLA;  Q29605, CP19A_RABIT;
DR   P22443, CP19A_RAT  ;  Q9XS28, CP19A_SHEEP;  Q92112, CP19A_TAEGU;
//
ID   1.14.14.15
DE   (3S)-3-amino-3-(3-chloro-4-hydroxyphenyl)propanoyl-[peptidyl-carrier
DE   protein SgcC2] monooxygenase.
CA   (3S)-3-amino-3-(3-chloro-4-hydroxyphenyl)propanoyl-[peptidyl-carrier
CA   protein SgcC2] + FADH2 + O(2) = (3S)-3-amino-3-(3-chloro-4,5-
CA   dihydroxyphenyl)propanoyl-[peptidyl-carrier protein SgcC2] + FAD + H(2)O.
CC   -!- The enzyme from the bacterium Streptomyces globisporus is involved in
CC       the biosynthesis of the (S)-3-chloro-5-hydroxy-beta-tyrosine moiety
CC       prior to incorporation into the chromoprotein antitumor antibiotic
CC       C-1027.
//
ID   1.14.14.16
DE   Steroid 21-monooxygenase.
AN   CYP21A2.
AN   Cytochrome p450 XXIA1.
AN   Steroid 21-hydroxylase.
CA   A C(21) steroid + [reduced NADPH--hemoprotein reductase] + O(2) =
CA   a 21-hydroxy-C(21)-steroid + [oxidized NADPH--hemoprotein reductase] +
CA   H(2)O.
CF   Heme-thiolate.
CC   -!- For the conversion of progesterone and 17-alpha-hydroxyprogesterone
CC       to their respective 21-hydroxylated derivatives,
CC       11-deoxycorticosterone and 11-deoxycortisol.
CC   -!- Involved in the biosynthesis of the hormones aldosterone and
CC       cortisol.
CC   -!- The electron donor is EC 1.6.2.4.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.14.1.8, EC 1.14.99.10 and EC 1.99.1.11.
PR   PROSITE; PDOC00081;
DR   P00191, CP21A_BOVIN;  Q8WNW0, CP21A_CANLF;  Q2LCM1, CP21A_CANLU;
DR   Q2LA60, CP21A_FELCA;  P08686, CP21A_HUMAN;  Q2LA59, CP21A_LYNLY;
DR   P03940, CP21A_MOUSE;  P15540, CP21A_PIG  ;  Q64562, CP21A_RAT  ;
