ID   1.14.14.19
DE   Steroid 17-alpha-monooxygenase.
AN   CYP17.
AN   CYP17A1.
AN   Cytochrome p450 XVIIA1.
AN   Steroid 17-alpha-hydroxylase.
AN   Steroid 17-alpha-hydroxylase/17,20 lyase.
CA   A C(21)-steroid + [reduced NADPH--hemoprotein reductase] + O(2) =
CA   a 17-alpha-hydroxy-C(21)-steroid + [oxidized NADPH--hemoprotein
CA   reductase] + H(2)O.
CF   Heme-thiolate.
CC   -!- Requires NADPH and EC 1.6.2.4.
CC   -!- Catalyzes two independent reactions at the same active site - the
CC       17-alpha-hydroxylation of pregnenolone and progesterone, which is
CC       part of glucocorticoid hormones biosynthesis, and the conversion of
CC       the 17-alpha-hydroxylated products via a 17,20-lyase reaction to form
CC       androstenedione and dehydroepiandrosterone, leading to sex hormone
CC       biosynthesis (EC 1.14.14.32).
CC   -!- The ratio of the 17-alpha-hydroxylase and 17,20-lyase activities is
CC       an important factor in determining the directions of steroid hormone
CC       biosynthesis toward biosynthesis of glucocorticoid or sex hormones.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.14.1.7, EC 1.14.99.9 and EC 1.99.1.9.
PR   PROSITE; PDOC00081;
DR   Q9GMC7, CP17A_BISBI;  P05185, CP17A_BOVIN;  Q9N0U7, CP17A_CAPHI;
DR   Q64410, CP17A_CAVPO;  P12394, CP17A_CHICK;  Q9GMC8, CP17A_FELCA;
DR   Q95328, CP17A_HORSE;  P05093, CP17A_HUMAN;  O73853, CP17A_ICTPU;
DR   Q2XVA1, CP17A_MACFA;  Q8HYM9, CP17A_MACMU;  P70687, CP17A_MESAU;
DR   P27786, CP17A_MOUSE;  P30437, CP17A_ONCMY;  P70085, CP17A_ORYLA;
