ID   1.14.14.20
DE   Phenol 2-monooxygenase (FADH(2)).
CA   Phenol + FADH(2) + O(2) = catechol + FAD + H(2)O.
CC   -!- The enzyme catalyzes the ortho-hydroxylation of simple phenols into
CC       the corresponding catechols.
CC   -!- It accepts 4-methylphenol, 4-chlorophenol, and 4-fluorophenol as well
CC       as 4-nitrophenol, 3-nitrophenol, and resorcinol.
CC   -!- The enzyme is part of a two-component system that also includes an
CC       NADH-dependent flavin reductase.
CC   -!- It is strictly dependent on FADH(2) and does not accept FMNH(2).
CC   -!- Cf. EC 1.14.13.7.
//
ID   1.14.14.21
DE   Dibenzothiophene monooxygenase.
CA   Dibenzothiophene + 2 FMNH(2) + 2 O(2) = dibenzothiophene-5,5-dioxide +
CA   2 FMN + 2 H(2)O.
CC   -!- This bacterial enzyme catalyzes the first two steps in the
CC       desulfurization pathway of dibenzothiophenes, the oxidation of
CC       dibenzothiophene into dibenzothiophene sulfone via dibenzothiophene-
CC       5-oxide.
CC   -!- The enzyme forms a two-component system with EC 1.5.1.42, which also
CC       interacts with EC 1.14.14.22.
//
ID   1.14.14.22
DE   Dibenzothiophene sulfone monooxygenase.
CA   Dibenzothiophene-5,5-dioxide + 2 FMNH(2) + O(2) = 2'-hydroxybiphenyl-2-
CA   sulfinate + 2 FMN + H(2)O.
CC   -!- This bacterial enzyme catalyzes a step in the desulfurization pathway
CC       of dibenzothiophenes.
CC   -!- The enzyme forms a two-component system with EC 1.5.1.42, which also
CC       interacts with EC 1.14.14.21.
//
ID   1.14.14.23
