ID   1.14.14.25
DE   Cholesterol 24-hydroxylase.
AN   Cholesterol 24-monooxygenase.
AN   Cholesterol 24S-hydroxylase.
AN   CYP46A1.
AN   Cytochrome P450 46A1.
CA   Cholesterol + [reduced NADPH--hemoprotein reductase] + O(2) = (24S)-
CA   cholest-5-ene-3-beta,24-diol + [oxidized NADPH--hemoprotein reductase] +
CA   H(2)O.
CF   Heme-thiolate.
CC   -!- The enzyme can also produce 25-hydroxycholesterol.
CC   -!- In addition, it can further hydroxylate the product to 24,25-
CC       dihydroxycholesterol and 24,27-dihydroxycholesterol.
CC   -!- This reaction is the first step in the enzymic degradation of
CC       cholesterol in the brain as hydroxycholesterol can pass the blood-
CC       brain barrier whereas cholesterol cannot.
CC   -!- The direct electron donor to the enzyme is EC 1.6.2.4.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.14.13.98.
PR   PROSITE; PDOC00081;
DR   Q9Y6A2, CP46A_HUMAN;  Q9WVK8, CP46A_MOUSE;
