ID   1.14.14.27
DE   Resorcinol 4-hydroxylase (FADH(2)).
CA   Resorcinol + FADH(2) + O(2) = hydroxyquinol + FAD + H(2)O.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Rhizobium sp. strain
CC       MTP-10005, uses FADH(2) as a substrate rather than a cofactor.
CC   -!- FADH(2) is provided by a dedicated EC 1.5.1.36.
CC   -!- The enzyme participates in the degradation of alpha-resorcylate and
CC       resorcinol.
CC   -!- Cf. EC 1.14.13.220 and EC 1.14.13.219.
//
ID   1.14.14.28
DE   Long-chain alkane monooxygenase.
CA   A long-chain alkane + FMNH(2) + O(2) = a long-chain primary alcohol +
CA   FMN + H(2)O.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Geobacillus
CC       thermodenitrificans NG80-2, is capable of converting alkanes ranging
CC       from C(15) to C(36) into their corresponding primary alcohols.
CC   -!- The FMNH(2) cofactor is provided by an FMN reductase.
//
ID   1.14.14.29
DE   25/26-hydroxycholesterol 7-alpha-hydroxylase.
AN   25-hydroxycholesterol 7-alpha-hydroxylase.
AN   25-hydroxycholesterol 7-alpha-monooxygenase.
AN   27-hydroxycholesterol 7-alpha-hydroxylase.
AN   27-hydroxycholesterol 7-monooxygenase.
CA   (1) Cholest-5-ene-3-beta,25-diol + [reduced NADPH--hemoprotein reductase]
CA   + O(2) = cholest-5-ene-3-beta,7-alpha,25-triol + [oxidized NADPH-
CA   -hemoprotein reductase] + H(2)O.
CA   (2) (25R)-cholest-5-ene-3-beta,26-diol + [reduced NADPH--hemoprotein
CA   reductase] + O(2) = (25R)-cholest-5-ene-3-beta,7-alpha,26-triol +
CA   [oxidized NADPH--hemoprotein reductase] + H(2)O.
CF   Heme-thiolate.
CC   -!- Unlike EC 1.14.14.26, which is specific for its oxysterol substrate,
CC       this enzyme can also metabolize the oxysterols 24,25-
CC       epoxycholesterol, 22-hydroxycholesterol and 24-hydroxycholesterol,
CC       but to a lesser extent.
CC   -!- The direct electron donor to the enzyme is EC 1.6.2.4.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.14.13.60 and EC 1.14.13.100.
