ID   1.14.14.30
DE   Isobutylamine N-monooxygenase.
CA   (1) 2-methylpropan-1-amine + FADH(2) + O(2) =
CA   N-(2-methylpropyl)hydroxylamine + FAD + H(2)O.
CA   (2) 2-methylpropan-1-amine + FMNH(2) + O(2) =
CA   N-(2-methylpropyl)hydroxylamine + FMN + H(2)O.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Streptomyces
CC       viridifaciens, is part of a two component system that also includes a
CC       flavin reductase, which provides reduced flavin mononucleotide for
CC       this enzyme.
CC   -!- The enzyme, which is involved in the biosynthesis of the azoxy
CC       antibiotic valanimycin, has a similar activity with either FMNH(2) or
CC       FADH(2).
CC   -!- It exhibits broad specificity, and also accepts propan-1-amine,
CC       butan-1-amine, butan-2-amine and benzylamine.
DR   P96072, VLMH_STRVF ;
