ID   1.14.14.43
DE   (Methylsulfanyl)alkanaldoxime N-monooxygenase.
AN   (Methylthio)alkanaldoxime N-monooxygenase.
AN   CYP83A1.
CA   An (E)-omega-(methylthio)alkanal oxime + O(2) + glutathione + [reduced
CA   NADPH--hemoprotein reductase] = an (E)-1-(glutathione-S-yl)-omega-
CA   (methylthio)-alkylhydroximate + 2 H(2)O + [oxidized NADPH--hemoprotein
CA   reductase].
CF   Heme-thiolate.
CC   -!- Involved in the biosynthesis of glucosinolates in plants.
CC   -!- Catalyzes an N-hydroxylation of the E isomer of
CC       n-(methylsulfanyl)aldoximes, forming an aci-nitro intermediate that
CC       reacts non-enzymically with glutathione to produce an N-alkyl-
CC       thiohydroximate adduct, the committed precursor of glucosinolates.
CC   -!- In the absence of a thiol compound, the enzyme is suicidal, probably
CC       due to interaction of the reactive aci-nitro intermediate with active
CC       site residues.
DR   P48421, C83A1_ARATH;
//
ID   1.14.14.44
DE   Phenylacetaldehyde oxime monooxygenase.
AN   CYP71AN24.
CA   (E)-phenylacetaldehyde oxime + [reduced NADPH--hemoprotein reductase] +
CA   O(2) = (R)-mandelonitrile + [oxidized NADPH--hemoprotein reductase] +
CA   2 H(2)O.
CF   Heme-thiolate.
CC   -!- Involved in the biosynthesis of the cyanogenic glucosides (R)-
CC       prunasin and (R)-amygdalin.
CC   -!- It catalyzes three different activities - isomerization of the (E)
CC       isomer to the (Z) isomer, dehydration, and C-hydroxylation.
