ID   1.14.14.45
DE   Aromatic aldoxime N-monooxygenase.
AN   CYP83B1.
CA   (1) (E)-indol-3-ylacetaldehyde oxime + [reduced NADPH--hemoprotein
CA   reductase] + glutathione + O(2) = S-((E)-N-hydroxy(indol-3-
CA   yl)acetimidoyl)-L-glutathione + [oxidized NADPH--hemoprotein reductase] +
CA   2 H(2)O.
CA   (2) (E)-phenylacetaldehyde oxime + [reduced NADPH--hemoprotein reductase]
CA   + glutathione + O(2) = S-((Z)-N-hydroxy(phenyl)acetimidoyl)-L-glutathione
CA   + [oxidized NADPH--hemoprotein reductase] + 2 H(2)O (overall reaction).
CF   Heme-thiolate.
CC   -!- Involved in the biosynthesis of glucosinolates in plants.
CC   -!- The enzyme catalyzes the N-hydroxylation of aromatic aldoximes
CC       derived from L-tryptophan and L-phenylalanine, forming an aci-nitro
CC       intermediate that reacts non-enzymically with glutathione to produce
CC       an N-alkyl-thiohydroximate adduct, the committed precursor of
