ID   1.14.14.73
DE   Albendazole monooxygenase (sufoxide-forming).
AN   Albendazole hydroxylase.
AN   Albendazole sulfoxidase.
AN   CYP1A2.
AN   CYP2J2.
AN   CYP3A4.
CA   (1) Albendazole + [reduced NADPH--hemoprotein reductase] + O(2) =
CA   albendazole S-oxide + [oxidized NADPH--hemoprotein reductase] + H(2)O.
CA   (2) Fenbendazole + [reduced NADPH--hemoprotein reductase] + O(2) =
CA   fenbendazole S-oxide + [oxidized NADPH--hemoprotein reductase] + H(2)O.
CC   -!- This is one of the activities carried out by some microsomal
CC       cytochrome P450 monooxygenases.
CC   -!- A similar conversion is also carried out by a different microsomal
CC       enzyme (EC 1.14.13.32), but it is estimated that cytochrome P450s are
CC       responsible for 70% of the activity.
//
ID   1.14.14.74
DE   Albendazole monooxygenase (hydroxylating).
AN   CYP2J2.
CA   Albendazole + [reduced NADPH--hemoprotein reductase] + O(2) =
CA   hydroxyalbendazole + [oxidized NADPH--hemoprotein reductase] + H(2)O.
CC   -!- CYP2J2 is a microsomal cytochrome P450 monooxygenase that catalyzes
CC       the hydroxylation of the terminal carbon of the propylsulfanyl chain
CC       in albendazole, a broad-spectrum anthelmintic used against
CC       gastrointestinal nematodes and the larval stages of cestodes.
CC   -!- Cf. EC 1.14.14.73.
//
ID   1.14.14.75
DE   Fenbendazole monooxygenase (4'-hydroxylating).
AN   CYP2C19.
CA   Fenbendazole + [reduced NADPH--hemoprotein reductase] + O(2) =
CA   4'-hydroxyfenbendazole + [oxidized NADPH--hemoprotein reductase] + H(2)O.
CC   -!- CYP2C19 is microsomal cytochrome P450 monooxygenase that catalyzes
CC       the hydroxylation of the benzene ring of fenbendazole, a broad-
CC       spectrum anthelmintic used against gastrointestinal nematodes and the
CC       larval stages of cestodes.
CC   -!- This activity is also carried out by CYP2J2.
CC   -!- Cf. EC 1.14.14.74.
CC   -!- CYP2C19 does not act on albendazole.
//
ID   1.14.14.76
