CC       ciliate Tetrahymena thermophila, is a Rieske oxygenase.
CC   -!- In insects it participates in the the biosythesis of ecdysteroid
CC       hormones.
CC   -!- The electrons are transferred from NAD(P)H via an electron transfer
CC       chain likely to include ferredoxin reductase and ferredoxin.
CC   -!- The enzyme differs from regular desaturases, such as EC 1.14.19.20,
CC       which are cytochrome b5-dependent and contain the three His-boxes
CC       that are typical to most desaturases.
DR   Q17938, DAF36_CAEEL;
//
ID   1.14.19.22
DE   Acyl-lipid omega-6 desaturase (cytochrome b5).
AN   Linoleate synthase.
AN   Oleate desaturase.
AN   Oleoyl-CoA desaturase.
AN   Phosphatidylcholine desaturase.
CA   An oleoyl-[glycerolipid] + 2 ferrocytochrome b5 + O(2) + 2 H(+) =
CA   a linoleoyl-[glycerolipid] + 2 ferricytochrome b5 + 2 H(2)O.
CC   -!- This microsomal enzyme introduces a cis double bond in fatty acids
CC       attached to lipid molecules at a location 6 carbons away from the
CC       methyl end of the fatty acid.
CC   -!- The distance from the carboxylic acid end of the molecule does not
CC       affect the location of the new double bond.
CC   -!- The most common substrates are oleoyl groups attached to either sn-1
CC       or sn-2 position of the glycerol backbone in phosphatidylcholine.
CC   -!- Cf. EC 1.14.19.23.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.3.1.35.
DR   P46313, FAD6E_ARATH;
//
ID   1.14.19.23
DE   Acyl-lipid (n+3)-(Z)-desaturase (ferredoxin).
AN   Acyl-lipid omega(6)-desaturase (ferredoxin).
AN   Linoleate synthase.
AN   Oleate desaturase.
AN   Oleoyl-CoA desaturase.
AN   Phosphatidylcholine desaturase.
CA   An oleoyl-[glycerolipid] + 2 reduced ferredoxin [iron-sulfur] cluster +
CA   O(2) + 2 H(+) = a linoleoyl-[glycerolipid] + 2 oxidized ferredoxin [iron-
CA   sulfur] cluster + 2 H(2)O.
CC   -!- This plastidial enzyme is able to insert a cis double bond in
CC       monounsaturated fatty acids incorporated into glycerolipids.
CC   -!- The enzyme introduces the new bond at a position 3 carbons away from
CC       the existing double bond, toward the methyl end of the fatty acid.
CC   -!- The native substrates are oleoyl (18:1 Delta(9)) and (Z)-hexadec-7-
CC       enoyl (16:1 Delta(7)) groups attached to either position of the
CC       glycerol backbone in glycerolipids, resulting in the introduction of
CC       the second double bond at positions 12 and 10, respectively This
CC       prompted the suggestion that this is an omega(6) desaturase.
CC   -!- However, when acting on palmitoleoyl groups(16:1 Delta(9)),
CC       the enzyme introduces the second double bond at position 12
CC       (omega(4)), indicating it is an (n+3) desaturase.
CC   -!- Cf. EC 1.14.19.34.
DR   P46312, FAD6C_ARATH;  P48627, FAD6C_BRANA;  P48628, FAD6C_SOYBN;
DR   P48629, FAD6C_SPIOL;
//
ID   1.14.19.24
DE   Acyl-CoA 11-(E)-desaturase.
CA   An acyl-CoA + 2 ferrocytochrome b5 + O(2) + 2 H(+) = an (11E)-enoyl-CoA +
CA   2 ferricytochrome b5 + 2 H(2)O.
CC   -!- Involved in sex pheromone synthesis in the Lepidoptera (moths).
CC   -!- The enzyme from the moth Spodoptera littoralis prefers 13:0 and 14:0
CC       substrates.
CC   -!- The product is formed by the stereospecific removal of the pro-R H at
CC       C-11 and the pro-S H at C-12.
CC   -!- Cf. EC 1.14.19.5.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.14.99.31.
//
ID   1.14.19.25
DE   Acyl-lipid omega-3 desaturase (cytochrome b5).
CA   A linoleoyl-[glycerolipid] + 2 ferrocytochrome b5 + O(2) + 2 H(+) =
CA   an alpha-linolenoyl-[glycerolipid] + ferricytochrome b5 + 2 H(2)O.
CC   -!- This microsomal enzyme introduces a cis double bond three carbons
CC       away from the methyl end of a fatty acid incorporated into a
CC       glycerolipid.
CC   -!- The distance from the carboxylic acid end of the molecule does not
CC       have an effect.
CC   -!- The plant enzyme acts on carbon 15 of linoleoyl groups incorporated
CC       into both the sn-1 and sn-2 positions of the glycerol backbone of
CC       phosphatidylcholine and other phospholipids, converting them into
CC       alpha-linolenoyl groups.
CC   -!- The enzyme from the fungus Mortierella alpina acts on gamma-
CC       linolenoyl and arachidonoyl groups, converting them into stearidonoyl
CC       and icosapentaenoyl groups, respectively.
CC   -!- Cf. EC 1.14.19.35.
DR   P48623, FAD3E_ARATH;  P48624, FAD3E_BRANA;  Q59J82, FAD3E_MORAP;
//
ID   1.14.19.26
DE   Acyl-[acyl-carrier-protein] 6-desaturase.
CA   Palmitoyl-[acyl-carrier protein] + 2 reduced ferredoxin [iron-sulfur]
CA   cluster + O(2) + 2 H(+) = (6Z)-hexadec-6-enoyl-[acyl-carrier protein] +
CA   2 oxidized ferredoxin [iron-sulfur] cluster + 2 H(2)O.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the endosperm of the plant Thunbergia
CC       alata (black-eyed Susan vine), introduces a cis double bond at carbon
CC       6 of several saturated acyl-[acyl-carrier protein]s.
CC   -!- It is most active with palmitoyl-[acyl-carrier protein] (16:0),
CC       but can also act on myristoyl-[acyl-carrier protein] (14:0) and
CC       stearoyl-[acyl-carrier protein] (18:0).
CC   -!- The position of the double bond is determined by its distance from
CC       the carboxyl end of the fatty acid.
DR   Q41510, PALAD_THUAT;
//
ID   1.14.19.27
DE   sn-2 palmitoyl-lipid 9-desaturase.
CA   A 1-acyl-2-palmitoyl-[glycerolipid] + 2 reduced ferredoxin [iron-sulfur]
CA   cluster + O(2) + 2 H(+) = a 1-acyl-2-palmitoleoyl-[glycerolipid] +
CA   2 oxidized ferredoxin [iron-sulfur] cluster + 2 H(2)O.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the cyanobacterium Nostoc sp. 36,
CC       introduces a cis double bond at carbon 9 of palmitoyl groups (16:0)
CC       attached to the sn-2 position of glycerolipids.
//
ID   1.14.19.28
DE   sn-1 stearoyl-lipid 9-desaturase.
CA   A 1-stearoyl-2-acyl-[glycerolipid] + 2 reduced ferredoxin [iron-sulfur]
CA   cluster + O(2) + 2 H(+) = a 1-oleoyl-2-acyl-[glycerolipid] + 2 oxidized
CA   ferredoxin [iron-sulfur] cluster + 2 H(2)O.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from cyanobacteria, introduces a cis double
CC       bond at carbon 9 of stearoyl groups (18:0) attached to the sn-1
CC       position of glycerolipids.
CC   -!- The enzyme is nonspecific with respect to the polar head group of the
CC       glycerolipid.
//
ID   1.14.19.29
DE   Sphingolipid 8-(E/Z)-desaturase.
AN   8 fatty acid desaturase.
AN   8-sphingolipid desaturase.
CA   (1) A (4R)-4-hydroxysphinganine ceramide + 2 ferrocytochrome b5 + O(2) +
CA   2 H(+) = a (4R,8E)-4-hydroxysphing-8-enine ceramide + 2 ferricytochrome
CA   b5 + 2 H(2)O.
CA   (2) A (4R)-4-hydroxysphinganine ceramide + 2 ferrocytochrome b5 + O(2) +
CA   2 H(+) = a (4R,8Z)-4-hydroxysphing-8-enine ceramide + 2 ferricytochrome
CA   b5 + 2 H(2)O.
CC   -!- The enzymes from higher plants convert sphinganine, 4E-sphing-4-enine
CC       and phytosphinganine into E/Z-mixtures of Delta(8)-desaturated
CC       products displaying different proportions of geometrical isomers
CC       depending on plant species.
CC   -!- The nature of the actual desaturase substrate has not yet been
CC       studied experimentally.
CC   -!- The enzymes contain an N-terminal cytochrome b5 domain that acts as
CC       the direct electron donor to the active site of the desaturase.
CC   -!- The homologous enzymes from some yeasts and diatoms, EC 1.14.19.18,
CC       act on sphing-4-enine ceramides and produce only the trans isomer.
DR   Q9ZRP7, SLD1_ARATH ;  Q9FR82, SLD1_BOROF ;  Q43469, SLD1_HELAN ;
DR   Q3EBF7, SLD2_ARATH ;
//
ID   1.14.19.30
DE   Acyl-lipid (8-3)-desaturase.
AN   Acyl-lipid 5-desaturase.
AN   Delta(5)-fatty-acid desaturase.
CA   (1) An (8Z,11Z,14Z)-icosa-8,11,14-trienoyl-[glycerolipid] +
CA   2 ferrocytochrome b5 + O(2) + 2 H(+) = a (5Z,8Z,11Z,14Z)-icosatetra-
CA   5,8,11,14-tetraenoyl-[glycerolipid] + 2 ferricytochrome b5 + 2 H(2)O.
CA   (2) An (8Z,11Z,14Z,17Z)-icosa-8,11,14,17-tetraenoyl-[glycerolipid] +
CA   2 ferrocytochrome b5 + O(2) + 2 H(+) = a (5Z,8Z,11Z,14Z,17Z)-icosa-
CA   5,8,11,14,17-pentaenoyl-[glycerolipid] + 2 ferricytochrome b5 + 2 H(2)O.
CC   -!- The enzyme, which has been characterized from multiple organisms
CC       including the moss Physcomitrella patens, the marine microalga
CC       Rebecca salina, and the filamentous fungus Mortierella alpina,
CC       introduces a cis double bond at the 5-position in 20-carbon
CC       polyunsaturated fatty acids incorporated in a glycerolipid that
CC       contain a Delta(8) double bond.
CC   -!- The enzyme contains a cytochrome b5 domain that acts as the direct
CC       electron donor to the active site of the desaturase, and does not
CC       require an external cytochrome.
DR   O74212, D5FAD_MORAP;  A9SIZ6, D5FAD_PHYPA;  A4KDP0, D5FAD_REBSA;
DR   Q8S3C1, D5FAD_THRSP;  O96099, FAD5B_DICDI;
//
ID   1.14.19.31
DE   Acyl-lipid (7-3)-desaturase.
AN   Acyl-lipid 4-desaturase.
CA   (1) A (7Z,10Z,13Z,16Z,19Z)-docosa-7,10,13,16,19-pentaenoyl-[glycerolipid]
CA   + 2 ferrocytochrome b5 + O(2) + 2 H(+) = a (4Z,7Z,10Z,13Z,16Z,19Z)-
CA   docosa-4,7,10,13,16,19-hexaenoyl-[glycerolipid] + 2 ferricytochrome b5 +
CA   2 H(2)O.
CA   (2) A (7Z,10Z,13Z,16Z)-docosa-7,10,13,16-tetraenoyl-[glycerolipid] +
CA   2 ferrocytochrome b5 + O(2) + 2 H(+) = a (4Z,7Z,10Z,13Z,16Z)-docosa-
CA   4,7,10,13,16-pentaenoyl-[glycerolipid] + 2 ferricytochrome b5 + 2 H(2)O.
CC   -!- The enzymes from several algae introduce a cis double bond at the
CC       4-position in 22-carbon polyunsaturated fatty acids that contain a
CC       Delta(7) double bond.
CC   -!- The enzyme from the fresh water alga Chlamydomonas reinhardtii acts
CC       on the 16 carbon fatty acid (7Z,10Z,13Z)-hexadeca-7,10,13-trienoate.
CC   -!- The enzyme contains an N-terminal cytochrome b5 domain that acts as
CC       the direct electron donor to the active site of the desaturase,
CC       and does not require an external cytochrome.
DR   I2CYZ4, D4FAD_CHLRE;  Q6VPV2, D4FAD_DIALT;  Q6WNG7, D4FAD_EUGGR;
DR   A0PJ29, D4FAD_REBSA;  Q8S3C0, D4FAD_THRSP;
//
ID   1.14.19.32
DE   Palmitoyl-CoA 14-(E/Z)-desaturase.
CA   (1) Palmitoyl-CoA + 2 ferrocytochrome b5 + O(2) + 2 H(+) = (14E)-hexadec-
CA   14-enoyl-CoA + 2 ferricytochrome b5 + 2 H(2)O.
CA   (2) Palmitoyl-CoA + 2 ferrocytochrome b5 + O(2) + 2 H(+) = (14Z)-hexadec-
CA   14-enoyl-CoA + 2 ferricytochrome b5 + 2 H(2)O.
CC   -!- The enzyme, found in the moth Ostrinia furnacalis (Asian corn borer),
CC       produces a mixture of (E)- and (Z)- isomers.
CC   -!- The products are subsequently truncated by partial beta-oxidation to
CC       a blend of 12(E/Z)-tetradec-12-enoyl-CoA, which are converted to the
CC       species-specific sex pheromones (E)- and (Z)-tetradec-12-enoyl
CC       acetates.
//
ID   1.14.19.33
DE   Delta(12) acyl-lipid conjugase (11E,13E-forming).
AN   Fatty acid Delta(12)-conjugase.
CA   (1) A linoleoyl-[glycerolipid] + 2 ferrocytochrome b5 + O(2) + 2 H(+) =
CA   an alpha-eleostearoyl-[glycerolipid] + 2 ferricytochrome b5 + 2 H(2)O.
CA   (2) A gamma-linolenoyl-[glycerolipid] + 2 ferrocytochrome b5 + O(2) +
CA   2 H(+) = an alpha-parinaroyl-[glycerolipid] + 2 ferricytochrome b5 +
CA   2 H(2)O.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the plants Impatiens balsamina,
CC       Momordica charantia (bitter gourd) and Vernicia fordii (tung tree),
CC       converts a single cis double bond at carbon 12 to two conjugated
CC       trans bonds at positions 11 and 13.
CC   -!- The enzyme from Vernicia fordii can also act as a 12(E) desaturase
CC       when acting on the monounsaturated fatty acids oleate and
CC       palmitoleate.
CC   -!- Cf. EC 1.14.19.16.
DR   Q9SP62, FADX_IMPBA ;  Q9SP61, FADX_MOMCH ;  Q8GZC2, FADX_VERFO ;
//
ID   1.14.19.34
DE   Acyl-lipid (9+3)-(E)-desaturase.
AN   Acyl-lipid 12-(E)-desaturase.
CA   (1) An oleoyl-[glycerolipid] + 2 ferrocytochrome b5 + O(2) + 2 H(+) =
CA   a (9Z,12E)-octadeca-9,12-dienoyl-[glycerolipid] + 2 ferricytochrome b5 +
CA   2 H(2)O.
CA   (2) A palmitoleoyl-[glycerolipid] + 2 ferrocytochrome b5 + O(2) + 2 H(+)
CA   = a (9Z,12E)-hexadeca-9,12-dienoyl-[glycerolipid] + 2 ferricytochrome b5
CA   + 2 H(2)O.
CC   -!- The enzymes from the plants Dimorphotheca sinuata (African daisy) and
CC       Vernicia fordii (tung oil tree) insert a trans double bond in
CC       position C-12 of oleate and palmitoleate incorporated into
CC       glycerolipids.
CC   -!- The enzyme introduces the new double bond at a position three carbons
CC       away from an existing double bond at position 9, toward the methyl
CC       end of the fatty acid.
CC   -!- The enzyme from tung oil tree also possesses the activity of
CC       EC 1.14.19.33.
DR   Q6RS95, FAD21_DIMSI;  Q8GZC2, FADX_VERFO ;
//
ID   1.14.19.35
DE   sn-2 acyl-lipid omega-3 desaturase (ferredoxin).
CA   (1) A (7Z,10Z)-hexadeca-7,10-dienoyl-[glycerolipid] + 2 reduced
CA   ferredoxin [iron-sulfur] cluster + O(2) + 2 H(+) = a (7Z,10Z,13Z)-
CA   hexadeca-7,10,13-trienoyl-[glycerolipid] + 2 oxidized ferredoxin [iron-
CA   sulfur] cluster + 2 H(2)O.
CA   (2) A linoleoyl-[glycerolipid] + 2 reduced ferredoxin [iron-sulfur]
CA   cluster + O(2) + 2 H(+) = an alpha-linolenoyl-[glycerolipid] + 2 oxidized
CA   ferredoxin [iron-sulfur] cluster + 2 H(2)O.
CC   -!- This plastidial enzyme desaturates 16:2 fatty acids attached to the
CC       sn-2 position of glycerolipids to 16:3 fatty acids, and converts18:2
CC       to 18:3 in both the sn-1 and sn-2 positions.
CC   -!- It acts on all 16:2- or 18:2-containing chloroplast membrane lipids,
CC       including phosphatidylglycerol, monogalactosyldiacylglycerol,
CC       digalactosyldiaclyglycerol, and sulfoquinovosyldiacylglycerol.
CC   -!- The enzyme introduces a cis double bond at a location 3 carbons away
CC       from the methyl end of the fatty acid.
CC   -!- The distance from the carboxylic acid end of the molecule does not
CC       affect the location of the new double bond.
CC   -!- Cf. EC 1.14.19.25 and EC 1.14.19.36.
DR   P46310, FAD3C_ARATH;  Q56VS4, FAD3C_HELAN;  P48622, FAD3D_ARATH;
//
ID   1.14.19.36
DE   sn-1 acyl-lipid omega-3 desaturase (ferredoxin).
CA   (1) A 1-gamma-linolenoyl-2-acyl-[glycerolipid] + 2 reduced ferredoxin
CA   [iron-sulfur] cluster + O(2) + 2 H(+) = a 1-stearidonoyl-2-acyl-
CA   [glycerolipid] + 2 oxidized ferredoxin [iron-sulfur] cluster + 2 H(2)O.
CA   (2) A 1-linoleoyl-2-acyl-[glycerolipid] + 2 reduced ferredoxin [iron-
CA   sulfur] cluster + O(2) + 2 H(+) = a 1-alpha-linolenoyl-2-acyl-
CA   [glycerolipid] + 2 oxidized ferredoxin [iron-sulfur] cluster + 2 H(2)O.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from cyanobacteria, introduces a cis double
CC       bond at carbon 15 of linoleoyl and gamma-linolenoyl groups attached
CC       to the sn-1 position of glycerolipids.
CC   -!- The enzyme is an omega desaturase, and determines the location of the
CC       double bond by counting three carbons from the methyl end of the
CC       fatty acid.
CC   -!- It is nonspecific with respect to the polar head group of the
CC       glycerolipid.
CC   -!- Cf. EC 1.14.19.35.
//
ID   1.14.19.37
DE   Acyl-CoA 5-desaturase.
AN   Acyl-CoA 5-desaturase (non-methylene-interrupted).
CA   (1) (11Z,14Z)-icosa-11,14-dienoyl-CoA + reduced acceptor + O(2) =
CA   (5Z,11Z,14Z)-icosa-5,11,14-trienoyl-CoA + acceptor + 2 H(2)O.
CA   (2) (11Z,14Z,17Z)-icosa-11,14,17-trienoyl-CoA + reduced acceptor + O(2) =
CA   (5Z,11Z,14Z,17Z)-icosa-5,11,14,17-tetraenoyl-CoA + acceptor + 2 H(2)O.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the plant Anemone leveillei,
CC       introduces a cis double bond at carbon 5 of acyl-CoAs that do not
CC       contain a double bond at position 8.
CC   -!- In vivo it forms non-methylene-interrupted polyunsaturated fatty
CC       acids such as sciadonate and juniperonate.
CC   -!- When expressed in Arabidopsis thaliana the enzyme could also act on
CC       unsaturated substrates such as palmitoyl-CoA.
CC   -!- Cf. EC 1.14.19.44.
DR   P0DOW2, AL10_ANELE ;  P0DOW3, AL21_ANELE ;
//
ID   1.14.19.38
DE   Acyl-lipid Delta(6)-acetylenase.
CA   (1) A gamma-linolenoyl-[glycerolipid] + 2 ferrocytochrome b5 + O(2) +
CA   2 H(+) = a (9Z,12Z)-octadeca-9,12-dien-6-ynoyl-[glycerolipid] +
CA   2 ferricytochrome b5 + 2 H(2)O.
CA   (2) A stearidonoyl-[glycerolipid] + 2 ferrocytochrome b5 + O(2) + 2 H(+)
CA   = a (9Z,12Z,15Z)-octadeca-9,12,15-trien-6-ynoyl-[glycerolipid] +
CA   2 ferricytochrome b5 + 2 H(2)O.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the moss Ceratodon purpureus, converts
CC       the double bond at position 6 of gamma-linolenate and stearidonate
CC       into a triple bond.
CC   -!- The product of the latter, dicranin, is the main fatty acid found in
CC       C.purpureus.
CC   -!- The enzyme contains a cytochrome b5 domain that acts as the direct
CC       electron donor to the desaturase active site.
CC   -!- The enzyme also has the activity of EC 1.14.19.47.
DR   Q9LEN0, ACET6_CERPU;
//
ID   1.14.19.39
DE   Acyl-lipid Delta(12)-acetylenase.
AN   Delta-12 fatty acid acetylenase.
CA   Linoleoyl-[glycerolipid] + 2 ferrocytochrome b5 + O(2) + 2 H(+) =
CA   crepenynyl-[glycerolipid] + 2 ferricytochrome b5 + 2 H(2)O.
