CC   -!- It is specific for hexanoate or hex-5-enoate loaded onto a dedicated
CC       acyl-carrier protein (JamC), which is encoded by a gene in the same
CC       operon.
//
ID   1.14.19.41
DE   Sterol 22-desaturase.
CA   Ergosta-5,7,24(28)-trien-3-beta-ol + NADPH + O(2) = ergosta-
CA   5,7,22,24(28)-tetraen-3-beta-ol + NADP(+) + 2 H(2)O.
CF   Heme-thiolate.
CC   -!- The enzyme, found in yeast and plants, catalyzes the introduction of
CC       a double bond between the C-22 and C-23 carbons of certain sterols.
CC   -!- In yeast the enzyme acts on ergosta-5,7,24(28)-trien-3-beta-ol,
CC       a step in the biosynthesis of ergosterol.
CC   -!- The enzyme from the plant Arabidopsis thaliana acts on sitosterol and
