DR   Q9SZ42, FAD4_ARATH ;
//
ID   1.14.19.44
DE   Acyl-CoA (8-3)-desaturase.
AN   Acyl-CoA 5-desaturase (methylene-interrupted).
CA   (1) (8Z,11Z,14Z)-icosa-8,11,14-trienoyl-CoA + 2 ferrocytochrome b5 + O(2)
CA   + 2 H(+) = arachidonoyl-CoA + 2 ferricytochrome b5 + 2 H(2)O.
CA   (2) (8Z,11Z,14Z,17Z)-icosa-8,11,14,17-tetraenoyl-CoA + 2 ferrocytochrome
CA   b5 + O(2) + 2 H(+) = (5Z,8Z,11Z,14Z,17Z)-icosa-5,8,11,14,17-pentaenoyl-
CA   CoA + 2 ferricytochrome b5 + 2 H(2)O.
CC   -!- The enzyme introduces a cis double bond at carbon 5 of acyl-CoAs that
CC       contain a double bond at position 8.
CC   -!- The enzymes from algae, mosses, mammals and the protozoan Leishmania
CC       major catalyze the desaturation of dihomo-gamma-linoleate
CC       ((8Z,11Z,14Z)-icosa-8,11,14-trienoate) and (8Z,11Z,14Z,17Z)-icosa-
CC       8,11,14,17-tetraenoate to generate arachidonate and
