ID   1.14.20.8
DE   (-)-deoxypodophyllotoxin synthase.
CA   (-)-yatein + 2-oxoglutarate + O(2) = (-)-deoxypodophyllotoxin + succinate
CA   + CO(2) + H(2)O.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the plant Sinopodophyllum hexandrum,
CC       is involved in the biosynthetic pathway of podophyllotoxin, a non-
CC       alkaloid toxin lignan whose derivatives are important anticancer
CC       drugs.
CC   -!- It catalyzes the closure of the central six-membered ring in the
CC       aryltetralin scaffold.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.14.11.50.
//
ID   1.14.20.9
DE   Tyrosine isonitrile desaturase.
CA   (2S)-3-(4-hydroxyphenyl)-2-isocyanopropanoate + 2-oxoglutarate + O(2) =
CA   (2E)-3-(4-hydroxyphenyl)-2-isocyanoprop-2-enoate + succinate + CO(2) +
CA   H(2)O.
CC   -!- The enzyme is a member of the Fe(2+), 2-oxoglutarate-dependent
CC       oxygenases and requires Fe(2+).
CC   -!- It has been characterized from bacteria that form the isonitrile-
CC       functionalized compound paerucumarin.
CC   -!- Cf. EC 1.14.20.10.
//
ID   1.14.20.10
DE   Tyrosine isonitrile desaturase/decarboxylase.
CA   (2S)-3-(4-hydroxyphenyl)-2-isocyanopropanoate + 2-oxoglutarate + O(2) =
CA   4-((E)-2-isocyanoethenyl)phenol + succinate + 2 CO(2) + H(2)O.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Xenorhabdus nematophila,
CC       is involved in rhabduscin biosynthesis.
CC   -!- The enzyme is a member of the Fe(2+), 2-oxoglutarate-dependent
CC       oxygenases.
CC   -!- It is similar to EC 1.14.20.9; however, the latter does not catalyze
CC       a decarboxylation of the substrate.
//
ID   1.14.20.11
DE   3-((Z)-2-isocyanoethenyl)-1H-indole synthase.
CA   (2S)-3-(1H-indol-3-yl)-2-isocyanopropanoate + 2-oxoglutarate + O(2) =
CA   3-((Z)-2-isocyanoethenyl)-1H-indole + succinate + 2 CO(2) + H(2)O.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the cyanobacterium Fischerella ambigua
CC       UTEX 1903, participates in the biosynthesis of hapalindole-type
CC       alkaloids.
CC   -!- The enzyme catalyzes an Fe(2+), 2-oxoglutarate-dependent
CC       monooxygenation at C-3, which is followed by decarboxylation and
CC       dehydration, resulting in the generation of a cis C-C double bond.
CC   -!- Cf. EC 1.14.20.12.
//
ID   1.14.20.12
DE   3-((E)-2-isocyanoethenyl)-1H-indole synthase.
CA   (2S)-3-(1H-indol-3-yl)-2-isocyanopropanoate + 2-oxoglutarate + O(2) =
CA   3-((E)-2-isocyanoethenyl)-1H-indole + succinate + 2 CO(2) + H(2)O.
CC   -!- The enzyme has been characterized from an unidentified soil
CC       bacterium.
CC   -!- It catalyzes an Fe(2+), 2-oxoglutarate-dependent monooxygenation at
CC       C-3, which is followed by decarboxylation and dehydration, resulting
CC       in the generation of a trans C-C double bond.
CC   -!- Cf. EC 1.14.20.11.
//
