ID   1.16.1.6
DE   Cyanocobalamin reductase (cyanide-eliminating).
AN   Cyanocobalamin reductase.
AN   Cyanocobalamin reductase (NADPH, cyanide-eliminating).
AN   Cyanocobalamin reductase (NADPH; CN-eliminating).
AN   NADPH:cyanocob(III)alamin oxidoreductase (cyanide-eliminating).
CA   Cob(I)alamin + cyanide + NADP(+) = cyanocob(III)alamin + NADPH.
CF   Flavoprotein.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.6.99.12.
//
ID   1.16.1.7
DE   Ferric-chelate reductase (NADH).
AN   Ferric chelate reductase.
AN   Iron chelate reductase.
AN   NADH:Fe(3+) oxidoreductase.
AN   NADH:Fe(3+)-EDTA reductase.
CA   2 Fe(II)-siderophore + NAD(+) + H(+) = 2 Fe(III)-siderophore + NADH.
CF   FAD.
CC   -!- The enzyme catalyzes the reduction of bound ferric iron in a variety
CC       of iron chelators (siderophores), resulting in the release of ferrous
CC       iron.
CC   -!- The plant enzyme is involved in the transport of iron across plant
CC       plasma membranes.
CC   -!- The enzyme from the bacterium Paracoccus denitrificans can also
CC       reduce chromate.
CC   -!- Cf. EC 1.16.1.9 and EC 1.16.1.10.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.6.99.13.
DR   P84468, FERA_PARDE ;  P84469, FERB_PARDE ;  Q75CQ8, FRE8_ASHGO ;
DR   Q12209, FRE8_YEAST ;  P78588, FREL_CANAX ;  Q9LMM2, FRO1_ARATH ;
