ID   1.16.1.9
DE   Ferric-chelate reductase (NADPH).
AN   Ferric chelate reductase.
AN   Iron chelate reductase.
AN   NADPH:Fe(3+)-EDTA reductase.
CA   2 Fe(II)-siderophore + NADP(+) + H(+) = 2 Fe(III)-siderophore + NADPH.
CF   FAD.
CC   -!- The enzyme, which is widespread among bacteria, catalyzes the
CC       reduction of ferric iron bound to a variety of iron chelators
CC       (siderophores), including ferric triscatecholates and ferric
CC       dicitrate, resulting in the release of ferrous iron.
CC   -!- The enzyme from the bacterium Escherichia coli has the highest
CC       efficiency with the hydrolyzed ferric enterobactin complex ferric
CC       N-(2,3-dihydroxybenzoyl)-L-serine.
CC   -!- Cf. EC 1.16.1.7 and EC 1.16.1.10.
