ID   1.17.1.9
DE   Formate dehydrogenase.
AN   Formate dehydrogenase (NAD(+)).
AN   Formic hydrogen-lyase.
AN   NAD(+)-formate dehydrogenase.
CA   Formate + NAD(+) = CO(2) + NADH.
CF   Flavin; Iron-sulfur; Mo cation.
CC   -!- The enzyme from most aerobic organisms is devoid of redox-active
CC       centers but that from the proteobacterium Methylosinus trichosporium
CC       contains iron-sulfur centers, flavin and a molybdenum center.
CC   -!- Together with EC 1.12.1.2, forms a system previously known as formate
CC       hydrogenlyase.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.2.1.2.
