ID   1.17.4.2
DE   Ribonucleoside-triphosphate reductase (thioredoxin).
AN   Ribonucleotide reductase.
CA   2'-deoxyribonucleoside triphosphate + thioredoxin disulfide + H(2)O =
CA   ribonucleoside triphosphate + thioredoxin.
CF   Adenosylcob(III)alamin.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Lactobacillus
CC       leichmannii, is similar to class II ribonucleoside-diphosphate
CC       reductase (cf. EC 1.17.4.1); however, it is specific for the
CC       triphosphate versions of its substrates.
CC   -!- The enzyme contains an adenosylcobalamin cofactor that is involved in
CC       generation of a transient thiyl (sulfanyl) radical on a cysteine
CC       residue.
CC   -!- This radical attacks the substrate, forming a ribonucleotide
CC       3'-radical, followed by water loss to form a ketyl (alpha-oxoacyl)
CC       radical.
CC   -!- The ketyl radical is reduced to 3'-keto-deoxynucleotide concomitant
CC       with formation of a disulfide anion radical between two cysteine
CC       residues.
CC   -!- A proton-coupled electron-transfer from the disulfide radical to the
CC       substrate generates a 3'-deoxynucleotide radical, and the the final
CC       product is formed when the hydrogen atom that was initially removed
CC       from the 3'-position of the nucleotide by the thiyl radical is
CC       returned to the same position.
CC   -!- The disulfide bridge is reduced by the action of thioredoxin.
CC   -!- Cf. EC 1.1.98.6.
PR   PROSITE; PDOC00665;
DR   Q54CW7, RTPR_DICDI ;  Q2PDF6, RTPR_EUGGR ;  Q5FMX8, RTPR_LACAC ;
DR   Q03PB4, RTPR_LACBA ;  Q1G7W2, RTPR_LACDA ;  Q04CQ7, RTPR_LACDB ;
DR   Q041L3, RTPR_LACGA ;  A8YW74, RTPR_LACH4 ;  Q59490, RTPR_LACLE ;
DR   Q035U1, RTPR_LACP3 ;  A6Q367, RTPR_NITSB ;  Q857H2, VG50_BPMB2 ;
DR   O64240, VG50_BPMD2 ;  Q05262, VG50_BPML5 ;
//
ID   1.17.4.3
DE   Transferred entry: 1.17.7.1.
//
ID   1.17.4.4
DE   Vitamin-K-epoxide reductase (warfarin-sensitive).
AN   Phylloquinone epoxide reductase.
AN   Vitamin K1 epoxide reductase.
CA   (1) Phylloquinone + a protein with a disulfide bond + H(2)O = 2,3-
CA   epoxyphylloquinone + a protein with reduced L-cysteine residues.
CA   (2) Phylloquinol + a protein with a disulfide bond = phylloquinone +
CA   a protein with reduced L-cysteine residues.
CC   -!- The enzyme catalyzes the reduction of vitamin K 2,3-epoxide, which is
CC       formed by the activity of EC 4.1.1.90, back to its phylloquinol
CC       active form.
CC   -!- The enzyme forms a tight complex with EC 5.3.4.1, which transfers the
CC       required electrons from newly-synthesized proteins by catalyzing the
CC       formation of disulfide bridges.
CC   -!- The enzyme acts on the epoxide forms of both phylloquinone (vitamin
CC       K1) and menaquinone (vitamin K2).
CC   -!- Inhibited strongly by (S)-warfarin and ferulenol.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.1.4.1.
DR   Q6B4J2, VKOR1_BOVIN;  Q9BQB6, VKOR1_HUMAN;  Q9CRC0, VKOR1_MOUSE;
DR   Q6TEK4, VKOR1_RAT  ;  Q8N0U8, VKORL_HUMAN;  Q6TEK5, VKORL_MOUSE;
DR   Q6TEK3, VKORL_RAT  ;
//
ID   1.17.4.5
DE   Vitamin-K-epoxide reductase (warfarin-insensitive).
AN   Vitamin K 2,3-epoxide reductase.
CA   3-hydroxy-2-methyl-3-phytyl-2,3-dihydronaphthoquinone + oxidized
CA   dithiothreitol = 2,3-epoxy-2,3-dihydro-2-methyl-3-phytyl-1,4-
CA   naphthoquinone + 1,4-dithiothreitol.
CC   -!- Vitamin K 2,3-epoxide is reduced to 3-hydroxy- (and 2-hydroxy-)
CC       vitamin K by 1,4-dithiothreitol, which is oxidized to a disulfide.
CC   -!- Not inhibited by warfarin (cf. EC 1.17.4.4).
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.1.4.2.
//
ID   1.17.5.1
DE   Phenylacetyl-CoA dehydrogenase.
AN   Phenylacetyl-CoA:acceptor oxidoreductase.
CA   Phenylacetyl-CoA + H(2)O + 2 quinone = phenylglyoxylyl-CoA + 2 quinol.
CF   Iron-sulfur; Mo-molybdopterin.
CC   -!- The enzyme is specific for phenylacetyl-CoA as substrate.
CC   -!- Phenylacetate, acetyl-CoA, benzoyl-CoA, propanoyl-CoA, crotonyl-CoA,
CC       succinyl-CoA and 3-hydroxybenzoyl-CoA cannot act as substrates.
CC   -!- The oxygen atom introduced into the product, phenylglyoxylyl-CoA,
CC       is derived from water and not molecular oxygen.
CC   -!- Duroquinone, menaquinone and 2,6-dichlorophenolindophenol (DCPIP) can
CC       act as acceptor, but the likely physiological acceptor is ubiquinone.
CC   -!- A second enzyme, EC 3.1.2.25 converts the phenylglyoxylyl-CoA formed
CC       into phenylglyoxylate.
//
ID   1.17.5.2
DE   Caffeine dehydrogenase.
CA   Caffeine + ubiquinone + H(2)O = 1,3,7-trimethylurate + ubiquinol.
CC   -!- This enzyme, characterized from the soil bacterium Pseudomonas sp.
CC       CBB1, catalyzes the incorporation of an oxygen atom originating from
CC       a water molecule into position C-8 of caffeine.
CC   -!- The enzyme utilizes short-tail ubiquinones as the preferred electron
CC       acceptor.
DR   D7REY3, CDHA_PSEU3 ;  D7REY4, CDHB_PSEU3 ;  D7REY5, CDHC_PSEU3 ;
//
ID   1.17.5.3
DE   Formate dehydrogenase-N.
AN   Formate dehydrogenase N.
AN   Nitrate inducible formate dehydrogenase.
CA   Formate + a quinone = CO(2) + a quinol.
CF   Heme; Iron-sulfur; Molybdopterin guanine dinucleotide.
CC   -!- Formate dehydrogenase-N oxidizes formate in the periplasm,
CC       transferring electrons via the menaquinone pool in the cytoplasmic
CC       membrane to a dissimilatory nitrate reductase (EC 1.7.5.1), which
CC       transfers electrons to nitrate in the cytoplasm.
CC   -!- The system generates proton motive force under anaerobic conditions.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.1.5.6.
PR   PROSITE; PDOC00392;
DR   P24183, FDNG_ECOLI ;
//
ID   1.17.7.1
DE   (E)-4-hydroxy-3-methylbut-2-enyl-diphosphate synthase (ferredoxin).
AN   (E)-4-hydroxy-3-methylbut-2-enyl diphosphate synthase.
AN   4-hydroxy-3-methylbut-2-en-1-yl diphosphate synthase.
CA   (E)-4-hydroxy-3-methylbut-2-en-1-yl diphosphate + H(2)O + 2 oxidized
CA   ferredoxin = 2-C-methyl-D-erythritol 2,4-cyclodiphosphate + 2 reduced
CA   ferredoxin.
CF   Iron-sulfur.
CC   -!- Forms part of an alternative non-mevalonate pathway for isoprenoid
CC       biosynthesis.
CC   -!- Bacteria have a similar enzyme that uses flavodoxin rather than
CC       ferredoxin (cf. EC 1.17.7.3).
CC   -!- The enzyme from the plant Arabidopsis thaliana is active with
CC       photoreduced 5-deazaflavin but not with flavodoxin.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.17.4.3.
DR   B0C6E1, ISPG_ACAM1 ;  Q3MG27, ISPG_ANAVT ;  F4K0E8, ISPG_ARATH ;
