//
ID   1.17.7.4
DE   4-hydroxy-3-methylbut-2-enyl diphosphate reductase.
AN   (E)-4-hydroxy-3-methylbut-2-en-1-yl diphosphate reductase.
AN   HMBPP reductase.
CA   (1) Isopentenyl diphosphate + 2 oxidized ferredoxin [iron-sulfur] cluster
CA   + H(2)O = (E)-4-hydroxy-3-methylbut-2-en-1-yl diphosphate + 2 reduced
CA   ferredoxin [iron-sulfur] cluster + 2 H(+).
CA   (2) Dimethylallyl diphosphate + 2 oxidized ferredoxin [iron-sulfur]
CA   cluster + H(2)O = (E)-4-hydroxy-3-methylbut-2-en-1-yl diphosphate +
CA   2 reduced ferredoxin [iron-sulfur] cluster + 2 H(+).
CF   Iron-sulfur.
CC   -!- Forms a system with a ferredoxin or a flavodoxin and an
CC       NAD(P)H-dependent reductase.
CC   -!- This is the last enzyme in the non-mevalonate pathway for isoprenoid
CC       biosynthesis.
CC   -!- This pathway, also known as the 1-deoxy-D-xylulose 5-phosphate (DOXP)
CC       or as the 2-C-methyl-D-erythritol-4-phosphate (MEP) pathway, is found
CC       in most bacteria and in plant chloroplasts.
CC   -!- The enzyme acts in the reverse direction, producing a 5:1 mixture of
CC       isopentenyl diphosphate and dimethylallyl diphosphate.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.17.1.2.
