DE   Thyroxine 5'-deiodinase.
AN   Diiodothyronine 5'-deiodinase.
AN   Iodothyronine 5'-deiodinase.
AN   Iodothyronine outer ring monodeiodinase.
AN   L-thyroxine iodohydrolase (reducing).
AN   Thyroxine 5-deiodinase.
AN   Type I iodothyronine deiodinase.
AN   Type II iodothyronine deiodinase.
CA   3,5,3'-triiodo-L-thyronine + iodide + A + H(+) = L-thyroxine + AH(2).
CC   -!- The enzyme activity has only been demonstrated in the direction of
CC       5'-deiodination, which renders the thyroid hormone more active.
CC   -!- The enzyme consists of type I and type II enzymes, both containing
CC       selenocysteine, but with different kinetics.
CC   -!- For the type I enzyme the first reaction is a reductive deiodination
CC       converting the -Se-H group of the enzyme into an -Se-I group; the
CC       reductant then reconverts this into -Se-H, releasing iodide.
