DE   [Formate-C-acetyltransferase]-activating enzyme.
AN   [Pyruvate formate-lyase]-activating enzyme.
AN   Formate acetyltransferase activating enzyme.
AN   Formate acetyltransferase-glycine dihydroflavodoxin:S-adenosyl-L-
AN   methionine oxidoreductase (S-adenosyl-L-methionine cleaving).
AN   PFL activase.
AN   PFL-glycine:S-adenosyl-L-methionine H transferase (flavodoxin-oxidizing,
AN   S-adenosyl-L-methionine-cleaving).
AN   Pyruvate formate-lyase 1 activating enzyme.
CA   S-adenosyl-L-methionine + dihydroflavodoxin + [formate
CA   C-acetyltransferase]-glycine = 5'-deoxyadenosine + L-methionine +
CA   flavodoxin semiquinone + [formate C-acetyltransferase]-glycin-2-yl
CA   radical.
CF   Iron-sulfur.
CC   -!- A single glycine residue in EC 2.3.1.54 is oxidized to the
CC       corresponding radical by transfer of H from its CH(2) to AdoMet with
CC       concomitant cleavage of the latter.
CC   -!- The first stage is reduction of the AdoMet to give methionine and the
CC       5'-deoxyadenosin-5'-yl radical, which then abstracts a hydrogen
CC       radical from the glycine residue.
