ID   2.1.1.18
DE   Polysaccharide O-methyltransferase.
CA   S-adenosyl-L-methionine + a (1->4)-alpha-D-glucooligosaccharide =
CA   S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine + an oligosaccharide containing 6-methyl-D-
CA   glucose units.
//
ID   2.1.1.19
DE   Trimethylsulfonium--tetrahydrofolate N-methyltransferase.
CA   Trimethylsulfonium + tetrahydrofolate = dimethylsulfide +
CA   5-methyltetrahydrofolate.
//
ID   2.1.1.20
DE   Glycine N-methyltransferase.
AN   Glycine methyltransferase.
CA   S-adenosyl-L-methionine + glycine = S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine +
CA   sarcosine.
CC   -!- Thought to play an important role in the regulation of methyl group
CC       metabolism in the liver and pancreas by regulating the ratio between
CC       S-adenosyl-L-methionine and S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine.
CC   -!- Inhibited by 5-methyltetrahydrofolate pentaglutamate.
CC   -!- Sarcosine, which has no physiological role, is converted back into
CC       glycine by the action of EC 1.5.8.3.
DR   Q14749, GNMT_HUMAN ;  Q9QXF8, GNMT_MOUSE ;  Q29555, GNMT_PIG   ;
DR   Q29513, GNMT_RABIT ;  P13255, GNMT_RAT   ;
//
ID   2.1.1.21
DE   Methylamine--glutamate N-methyltransferase.
AN   N-methylglutamate synthase.
CA   Methylamine + L-glutamate = NH(3) + N-methyl-L-glutamate.
//
ID   2.1.1.22
DE   Carnosine N-methyltransferase.
CA   S-adenosyl-L-methionine + carnosine = S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine +
CA   anserine.
