//
ID   2.1.1.57
DE   Methyltransferase cap1.
AN   Cap1-MTase.
AN   mRNA (nucleoside-2'-O)-methyltransferase.
CA   S-adenosyl-L-methionine + a 5'-(N(7)-methyl 5'-triphosphoguanosine)-
CA   (purine-ribonucleotide)-[mRNA] = S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine + a 5'-(N(7)-
CA   methyl 5'-triphosphoguanosine)-(2'-O-methyl-purine-ribonucleotide)-
CA   [mRNA].
CC   -!- This enzyme catalyzes the methylation of the ribose on the first
CC       transcribed nucleotide of mRNA or snRNA molecules, which may be
CC       either guanosine or adenosine.
CC   -!- This methylation event is known as cap1, and occurs in all mRNAs and
CC       snRNAs of higher eukaryotes, including insects, vertebrates and their
CC       viruses.
CC   -!- The human enzyme can also methylate mRNA molecules that lack
CC       methylation on the capping 5'-triphosphoguanosine.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 2.1.1.58.
