ID   2.1.1.63
DE   Methylated-DNA--[protein]-cysteine S-methyltransferase.
AN   6-O-methylguanine-DNA methyltransferase.
AN   O-6-methylguanine-DNA-alkyltransferase.
CA   (1) DNA (containing 6-O-methylguanine) + protein L-cysteine =
CA   DNA (without 6-O-methylguanine) + protein S-methyl-L-cysteine.
CA   (2) DNA (containing 4-O-methylthymine) + protein L-cysteine =
CA   DNA (without 4-O-methylthymine) + protein S-methyl-L-cysteine.
CC   -!- This protein is involved in the repair of methylated DNA.
CC   -!- Unlike EC 3.2.2.20 and EC 3.2.2.21, which remove the methylated base
CC       leaving an apurinic/apyrimidinic site, this enzyme transfers the
CC       methyl group from the methylated DNA to an internal cysteine residue,
CC       leaving an intact nucleotide.
CC   -!- Since the methyl transfer is irreversible, the enzyme can only
CC       catalyze a single turnover.
PR   PROSITE; PDOC00320;
