ID   2.1.1.74
DE   Methylenetetrahydrofolate--tRNA-(uracil(54)-C(5))-methyltransferase
DE   (FADH(2)-oxidizing).
AN   Folate-dependent ribothymidyl synthase.
AN   Folate/FAD-dependent tRNA T54 methyltransferase.
CA   5,10-methylenetetrahydrofolate + uracil(54) in tRNA + FADH(2) =
CA   tetrahydrofolate + 5-methyluracil(54) in tRNA + FAD.
CC   -!- Up to 25% of the bases in mature tRNA are post-translationally
CC       modified or hypermodified.
CC   -!- One almost universal post-translational modification is the
CC       conversion of U54 into ribothymidine in the T-Psi-C loop, and this
CC       modification is found in most species studied to date.
CC   -!- Unlike this enzyme, which uses 5,10-methylenetetrahydrofolate and
CC       FADH(2) to supply the atoms for methylation of U54, EC 2.1.1.35 uses
CC       S-adenosyl-L-methionine.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 2.1.2.12.
