ID   2.1.1.106
DE   Tryptophan 2-C-methyltransferase.
CA   S-adenosyl-L-methionine + L-tryptophan = S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine + L-2-
CA   methyltryptophan.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Streptomyces laurentii,
CC       is involved in thiostrepton biosynthesis.
CC   -!- It is a radical SAM enzyme that contains a [4Fe-4S] center and a
CC       cobalamin cofactor.
CC   -!- The enzyme first transfers the methyl group from SAM to the bound
CC       cobalamin, followed by transfer from methylcobalamin to L-tryptophan,
CC       resulting in retention of the original methyl group configuration.
CC   -!- The second transfer is likely to involve a CH(3) radical species
CC       formed from methylcobalamin by the concerted action of a partially
CC       ligated radical SAM [4Fe-4S](2+/1+) center.
DR   C0JRZ9, TSRM_STRLU ;
