ID   2.1.1.145
DE   Trans-aconitate 3-methyltransferase.
CA   S-adenosyl-L-methionine + trans-aconitate = S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine +
CA   (E)-2-(methoxycarbonylmethyl)butenedioate.
CC   -!- Also catalyzes the formation of the methyl monoester of cis-
CC       aconitate, isocitrate and citrate, but more slowly.
CC   -!- While the enzyme from Saccharomyces cerevisiae forms (E)-2-
CC       (methoxycarbonylmethyl)butenedioate as the product, that from
CC       Escherichia coli forms (E)-3-(methoxycarbonyl)-pent-2-enedioate and
CC       is therefore classified as a separate enzyme (cf. EC 2.1.1.144).
DR   A6ZRD1, TMT1_YEAS7 ;  P32643, TMT1_YEAST ;
//
ID   2.1.1.146
DE   (Iso)eugenol O-methyltransferase.
CA   S-adenosyl-L-methionine + isoeugenol = S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine +
CA   isomethyleugenol.
CC   -!- Acts on eugenol and chavicol as well as isoeugenol.
DR   Q93WU3, CVMT1_OCIBA;  Q93WU2, EOMT1_OCIBA;  O04385, IEMT_CLABR ;
DR   A8QW52, OMT1_SORBI ;
//
ID   2.1.1.147
DE   Corydaline synthase.
CA   S-adenosyl-L-methionine + palmatine + 2 NADPH = S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine
CA   + corydaline + 2 NADP(+).
CC   -!- Also acts on 7,8-dihydropalmatine.
//
ID   2.1.1.148
DE   Thymidylate synthase (FAD).
AN   FDTS.
AN   Flavin dependent thymidylate synthase.
CA   5,10-methylenetetrahydrofolate + dUMP + NADPH = dTMP + tetrahydrofolate +
CA   NADP(+).
CC   -!- Contains FAD.
CC   -!- All thymidylate synthases catalyze a reductive methylation involving
CC       the transfer of the methylene group of 5,10-methylenetetrahydrofolate
CC       to the C5-position of dUMP and a two electron reduction of the
CC       methylene group to a methyl group.
CC   -!- Unlike the classical thymidylate synthase, ThyA (EC 2.1.1.45), which
CC       uses folate as both a 1-carbon donor and a source of reducing
CC       equivalents, this enzyme uses a flavin coenzyme as a source of
CC       reducing equivalents, which are derived from NADPH.
