//
ID   2.1.1.164
DE   Demethylrebeccamycin-D-glucose O-methyltransferase.
CA   4'-demethylrebeccamycin + S-adenosyl-L-methionine = rebeccamycin +
CA   S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine.
CC   -!- Catalyzes the last step in the biosynthesis of rebeccamycin,
CC       an indolocarbazole alkaloid produced by the bacterium Lechevalieria
CC       aerocolonigenes.
CC   -!- The enzyme is able to use a wide variety substrates, tolerating
CC       variation on the imide heterocycle, deoxygenation of the sugar
CC       moiety, and even indolocarbazole glycoside anomers.
DR   Q8KZ94, REBMT_NOCAE;
//
ID   2.1.1.165
DE   Methyl halide transferase.
AN   Methyl chloride transferase.
CA   S-adenosyl-L-methionine + iodide = S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine + methyl
CA   iodide.
CC   -!- This enzyme contributes to the methyl halide emissions from
CC       Arabidopsis.
//
ID   2.1.1.166
DE   23S rRNA (uridine(2552)-2'-O)-methyltransferase.
AN   FTSJ.
AN   Um(2552) 23S ribosomal RNA methyltransferase.
AN   Um2552 methyltransferase.
CA   S-adenosyl-L-methionine + uridine(2552) in 23S rRNA = S-adenosyl-L-
CA   homocysteine + 2'-O-methyluridine(2552) in 23S rRNA.
CC   -!- The enzyme catalyzes the 2'-O-methylation of the universally
CC       conserved U2552 in the A loop of 23S rRNA.
