DE   16S rRNA (guanine(1405)-N(7))-methyltransferase.
AN   Sisomicin-gentamicin methyltransferase.
CA   S-adenosyl-L-methionine + guanine(1405) in 16S rRNA = S-adenosyl-L-
CA   homocysteine + N(7)-methylguanine(1405) in 16S rRNA.
CC   -!- The enzyme from the antibiotic-producing bacterium Micromonospora
CC       zionensis specifically methylates guanine(1405) at N(7) in 16S rRNA,
CC       thereby rendering the ribosome resistant to 4,6-disubstituted
CC       deoxystreptamine aminoglycosides, which include gentamicins and
CC       kanamycins.
