//
ID   2.1.1.192
DE   23S rRNA (adenine(2503)-C(2))-methyltransferase.
CA   (1) 2 S-adenosyl-L-methionine + adenine(2503) in 23S rRNA + 2 reduced
CA   [2Fe-2S] ferredoxin = S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine + L-methionine +
CA   5'-deoxyadenosine + 2-methyladenine(2503) in 23S rRNA + 2 oxidized [2Fe-
CA   2S] ferredoxin.
CA   (2) 2 S-adenosyl-L-methionine + adenine(37) in tRNA + 2 reduced [2Fe-2S]
CA   ferredoxin = S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine + L-methionine + 5'-deoxyadenosine
CA   + 2-methyladenine(37) in tRNA + 2 oxidized [2Fe-2S] ferredoxin.
CF   Iron-sulfur.
CC   -!- This enzyme is a member of the 'AdoMet radical' (radical SAM) family.
CC   -!- S-adenosyl-L-methionine acts as both a radical generator and as the
CC       source of the appended methyl group.
CC   -!- RlmN first transfers an CH(2) group to a conserved cysteine (Cys(355)
CC       in Escherichia coli), the generated radical from a second S-adenosyl-
CC       L-methionine then attacks the methyl group, exctracting a hydrogen.
CC   -!- The formed radical forms a covalent intermediate with the adenine
CC       group of the tRNA.
CC   -!- RlmN is an endogenous enzyme used by the cell to refine functions of
CC       the ribosome in protein synthesis.
CC   -!- The enzyme methylates adenosine by a radical mechanism with CH(2)
CC       from the S-adenosyl-L-methionine and retention of the hydrogen at C-2
CC       of adenosine(2503) of 23S rRNA.
CC   -!- It will also methylate 8-methyladenosine(2503) of 23S rRNA (cf.
CC       EC 2.1.1.224).
