ID   2.1.1.207
DE   tRNA (cytidine(34)-2'-O)-methyltransferase.
AN   tRNA (cytidine(34)/5-carboxymethylaminomethyluridine(34)-2'-O)-
AN   methyltransferase.
AN   tRNA methyltransferase L.
CA   (1) S-adenosyl-L-methionine + cytidine(34) in tRNA = S-adenosyl-L-
CA   homocysteine + 2'-O-methylcytidine(34) in tRNA.
CA   (2) S-adenosyl-L-methionine + 5-carboxymethylaminomethyluridine(34) in
CA   tRNA(Leu) = S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine + 5-carboxymethylaminomethyl-2'-O-
CA   methyluridine(34) in tRNA(Leu).
CC   -!- The enzyme from Escherichia coli catalyzes the 2'-O-methylation of
CC       cytidine or 5-carboxymethylaminomethyluridine at the wobble position
CC       at nucleotide 34 in tRNA(Leu)CmAA and tRNA(Leu)cmnm(5)UmAA.
CC   -!- The enzyme is selective for the two tRNA(Leu) isoacceptors and only
CC       methylates these when they present the correct anticodon loop
CC       sequence and modification pattern.
CC   -!- Specifically, YibK requires a pyrimidine nucleoside at position 34,
CC       it has a clear preference for an adenosine at position 35, and it
CC       fails to methylate without prior addition of the N(6)-(isopentenyl)-
CC       2-methylthioadenosine modification at position 37.
