ID   2.1.1.228
DE   tRNA (guanine(37)-N(1))-methyltransferase.
AN   Transfer RNA (m(1)G(37)) methyltransferase.
AN   tRNA (m(1)G(37)) methyltransferase.
AN   tRNA-(N(1)G37) methyltransferase.
CA   S-adenosyl-L-methionine + guanine(37) in tRNA = S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine
CA   + N(1)-methylguanine(37) in tRNA.
CC   -!- This enzyme is important for the maintenance of the correct reading
CC       frame during translation.
CC   -!- Unlike TrmD from Escherichia coli, which recognizes the G(36)pG(37)
CC       motif preferentially, the human enzyme (encoded by TRMT5) also
CC       methylates inosine at position 37.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 2.1.1.31.
