ID   2.1.1.229
DE   tRNA (carboxymethyluridine(34)-5-O)-methyltransferase.
AN   tRNA methyltransferase 9.
CA   S-adenosyl-L-methionine + carboxymethyluridine(34) in tRNA = S-adenosyl-
CA   L-homocysteine + 5-(2-methoxy-2-oxoethyl)uridine(34) in tRNA.
CC   -!- The enzyme catalyzes the posttranslational modification of uridine
CC       residues at the wobble position 34 of the anticodon loop of tRNA.
DR   A1A4L5, ALKB8_BOVIN;  Q96BT7, ALKB8_HUMAN;  Q95K79, ALKB8_MACFA;
DR   Q80Y20, ALKB8_MOUSE;  Q07G10, ALKB8_XENTR;  Q94A09, TRM9_ARATH ;
DR   Q10224, TRM9_SCHPO ;  P49957, TRM9_YEAST ;
//
ID   2.1.1.230
DE   23S rRNA (adenosine(1067)-2'-O)-methyltransferase.
AN   23S rRNA A(1067) 2'-methyltransferase.
AN   Nosiheptide-resistance methyltransferase.
AN   Thiostrepton-resistance methylase.
CA   S-adenosyl-L-methionine + adenosine(1067) in 23S rRNA = S-adenosyl-L-
CA   homocysteine + 2'-O-methyladenosine(1067) in 23S rRNA.
CC   -!- The methylase that is responsible for autoimmunity in the
CC       thiostrepton producer Streptomyces azureus, renders ribosomes
CC       completely resistant to thiostrepton.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 2.1.1.66.
DR   P52391, NSHR_STRAS ;  P18644, TSNR_STRAJ ;  P52393, TSNR_STRLU ;
//
ID   2.1.1.231
DE   Flavonoid 4'-O-methyltransferase.
AN   4'-hydroxyisoflavone methyltransferase.
AN   Isoflavone O-methyltransferase.
CA   S-adenosyl-L-methionine + a 4'-hydroxyflavanone = S-adenosyl-L-
CA   homocysteine + a 4'-methoxyflavanone.
