ID   2.1.1.246
DE   [Methyl-Co(III) methanol-specific corrinoid protein]:coenzyme M
DE   methyltransferase.
CA   A [methyl-Co(III) methanol-specific corrinoid protein] + coenzyme M =
CA   methyl-CoM + a [Co(I) methanol-specific corrinoid protein].
CC   -!- The enzyme, which is involved in methanogenesis from methanol,
CC       catalyzes the transfer of a methyl group from a corrinoid protein
CC       (see EC 2.1.1.90), where it is bound to the cobalt cofactor,
CC       to coenzyme M, forming the substrate for EC 2.8.4.1, the enzyme that
CC       catalyzes the final step in methanogenesis.
CC   -!- Free methylcob(I)alamin can substitute for the corrinoid protein in
CC       vitro.
DR   Q48927, MTAA_METBA ;  Q48949, MTAA_METBF ;
//
ID   2.1.1.247
DE   [Methyl-Co(III) methylamine-specific corrinoid protein]:coenzyme M
DE   methyltransferase.
AN   MT2-A.
CA   A [methyl-Co(III) methylamine-specific corrinoid protein] + coenzyme M =
CA   methyl-CoM + a [Co(I) methylamine-specific corrinoid protein].
CF   Zn(2+).
CC   -!- The enzyme, which is involved in methanogenesis from mono-, di-,
CC       and trimethylamine, catalyzes the transfer of a methyl group bound to
CC       the cobalt cofactor of several corrinoid proteins (mono-, di-,
CC       and trimethylamine-specific corrinoid proteins, cf. EC 2.1.1.248,
CC       EC 2.1.1.249 and EC 2.1.1.250) to coenzyme M, forming the substrate
CC       for EC 2.8.4.1, the enzyme that catalyzes the final step in
CC       methanogenesis.
DR   P58869, MTBA_METAC ;  O30640, MTBA_METBA ;  P58984, MTBA_METMA ;
//
ID   2.1.1.248
DE   [Methylamine--corrinoid protein] Co-methyltransferase.
AN   Monomethylamine methyltransferase.
CA   Methylamine + a [Co(I) methylamine-specific corrinoid protein] =
CA   a [methyl-Co(III) methylamine-specific corrinoid protein] + ammonia.
CC   -!- The enzyme, which catalyzes the transfer of a methyl group from
CC       methylamine to a methylamine-specific corrinoid protein (MtmC),
CC       is involved in methanogenesis from methylamine.
CC   -!- The enzyme contains the unusual amino acid pyrrolysine.
CC   -!- Methylation of the corrinoid protein requires the central cobalt to
CC       be in the Co(I) state.
CC   -!- During methylation the cobalt is oxidized to the Co(III) state.
CC   -!- The methylated corrinoid protein is substrate for EC 2.1.1.247.
DR   P58865, MTMB1_METAC;  O30642, MTMB1_METBA;  Q46E72, MTMB1_METBF;
