AN   Dimethylamine methyltransferase.
CA   Dimethylamine + a [Co(I) dimethylamine-specific corrinoid protein] =
CA   a [methyl-Co(III) dimethylamine-specific corrinoid protein] +
CA   methylamine.
CC   -!- The enzyme, which catalyzes the transfer of a methyl group from
CC       dimethylamine to a dimethylamine-specific corrinoid protein (MtbC),
CC       is involved in methanogenesis from dimethylamine.
CC   -!- The enzyme contains the unusual amino acid pyrrolysine.
CC   -!- Methylation of the corrinoid protein requires the central cobalt to
CC       be in the Co(I) state.
CC   -!- During methylation the cobalt is oxidized to the Co(III) state.
CC   -!- The methylated corrinoid protein is substrate for EC 2.1.1.247.
