CA   dimethylamine.
CC   -!- The enzyme, which catalyzes the transfer of a methyl group from
CC       trimethylamine to a trimethylamine-specific corrinoid protein (MttC),
CC       is involved in methanogenesis from trimethylamine.
CC   -!- The enzyme contains the unusual amino acid pyrrolysine.
CC   -!- Methylation of the corrinoid protein requires the central cobalt to
CC       be in the Co(I) state.
CC   -!- During methylation the cobalt is oxidized to the Co(III) state.
CC   -!- The methylated corrinoid protein is substrate for EC 2.1.1.247.
DR   Q8TTA9, MTTB1_METAC;  P58973, MTTB1_METMA;  Q8TS73, MTTB2_METAC;
DR   P58974, MTTB2_METMA;  Q18TV3, MTTB_DESHD ;  Q24MI3, MTTB_DESHY ;
DR   O93658, MTTB_METBA ;  P0C0W7, MTTB_METBF ;  Q12TR2, MTTB_METBU ;
DR   Q9P995, MTTB_METTE ;
//
ID   2.1.1.251
DE   Methylated-thiol--coenzyme M methyltransferase.
CA   Methanethiol + coenzyme M = methyl-CoM + hydrogen sulfide.
CC   -!- The enzyme, which is involved in methanogenesis from methylated
CC       thiols, such as methane thiol, dimethyl sulfide, and 3-S-
CC       methylmercaptopropionate, catalyzes two successive steps - the
CC       transfer of a methyl group from the substrate to the cobalt cofactor
CC       of a methylated-thiol-specific corrinoid protein (MtsB), and the
CC       subsequent transfer of the methyl group from the corrinoid protein to
CC       coenzyme M.
CC   -!- With most other methanogenesis substrates this process is carried out
CC       by two different enzymes (for example, EC 2.1.1.90 and EC 2.1.1.246).
CC   -!- The cobalt is oxidized during methylation from the Co(I) state to the
CC       Co(III) state, and is reduced back to the Co(I) form during
CC       demethylation.
DR   Q48924, MTSA_METBA ;  Q8PUA8, MTSA_METMA ;
//
ID   2.1.1.252
DE   Tetramethylammonium--corrinoid protein Co-methyltransferase.
AN   Tetramethylammonium methyltransferase.
CA   Tetramethylammonium + a [Co(I) tetramethylammonium-specific corrinoid
CA   protein] = a [methyl-Co(III) tetramethylammonium-specific corrinoid
CA   protein] + trimethylamine.
CC   -!- The enzyme, which catalyzes the transfer of a methyl group from
CC       tetramethylammonium to a tetramethylammonium-specific corrinoid
CC       protein (MtqC), is involved in methanogenesis from
CC       tetramethylammonium.
CC   -!- Methylation of the corrinoid protein requires the central cobalt to
CC       be in the Co(I) state.
CC   -!- During methylation the cobalt is oxidized to the Co(III) state.
CC   -!- The methylated corrinoid protein is substrate for EC 2.1.1.253.
//
ID   2.1.1.253
DE   [Methyl-Co(III) tetramethylammonium-specific corrinoid protein]:coenzyme
DE   M methyltransferase.
CA   A [methyl-Co(III) tetramethylammonium-specific corrinoid protein] +
CA   coenzyme M = methyl-CoM + a [Co(I) tetramethylammonium-specific corrinoid
CA   protein].
CC   -!- The enzyme, which is involved in methanogenesis from
CC       tetramethylammonium, catalyzes the transfer of a methyl group from a
CC       corrinoid protein (see EC 2.1.1.252), where it is bound to the cobalt
CC       cofactor, to coenzyme M, forming the substrate for EC 2.8.4.1,
CC       the enzyme that catalyzes the final step in methanogenesis.
//
ID   2.1.1.254
