ID   2.2.1.9
DE   2-succinyl-5-enolpyruvyl-6-hydroxy-3-cyclohexene-1-carboxylic-acid
DE   synthase.
AN   SEPHCHC synthase.
CA   Isochorismate + 2-oxoglutarate = 5-enolpyruvoyl-6-hydroxy-2-succinyl-
CA   cyclohex-3-ene-1-carboxylate + CO(2).
CF   Mg(2+).
CC   -!- Involved in the biosynthesis of vitamin K(2) (menaquinone).
CC   -!- In most anaerobes and all Gram-positive aerobes, menaquinone is the
CC       sole electron transporter in the respiratory chain and is essential
CC       for their survival.
CC   -!- It had previously been thought that the products of the reaction were
CC       (1R,6R)-6-hydroxy-2-succinylcyclohexa-2,4-diene-1-carboxylate
CC       (SHCHC), pyruvate and CO(2) but it is now known that two separate
CC       enzymes are involved: this enzyme and EC 4.2.99.20.
CC   -!- Under basic conditions, the product can spontaneously lose pyruvate
CC       to form SHCHC.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 2.5.1.64 and EC 2.5.1.n1.
