ID   2.2.1.10
DE   2-amino-3,7-dideoxy-D-threo-hept-6-ulosonate synthase.
AN   ADH synthase.
CA   L-aspartate 4-semialdehyde + 1-deoxy-D-threo-hexo-2,5-diulose 6-phosphate
CA   = 2-amino-2,3,7-trideoxy-D-lyxo-hept-6-ulosonate + 2,3-
CA   dioxopropylaldehyde phosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme plays a key role in an alternative pathway of the
CC       biosynthesis of 3-dehydroquinate (DHQ), which is involved in the
CC       canonical pathway for the biosynthesis of aromatic amino acids.
CC   -!- The enzyme can also catalyze the cleavage of fructose-1,6-
CC       bisphosphate to glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate and dihydroxyacetone
CC       phosphate.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 4.1.2.n5.
DR   O30009, ADHS1_ARCFU;  O30128, ADHS2_ARCFU;  O67506, ADHS_AQUAE ;
DR   Q9HSB8, ADHS_HALSA ;  A6UTT2, ADHS_META3 ;  Q57843, ADHS_METJA ;
