ID   2.2.1.11
DE   6-deoxy-5-ketofructose 1-phosphate synthase.
AN   DKFP synthase.
CA   (1) 2-oxopropanal + D-fructose 1,6-bisphosphate = D-glyceraldehyde
CA   3-phosphate + 1-deoxy-D-threo-hexo-2,5-diulose 6-phosphate.
CA   (2) 2-oxopropanal + D-fructose 1-phosphate = D-glyceraldehyde + 1-deoxy-
CA   D-threo-hexo-2,5-diulose 6-phosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme plays a key role in an alternative pathway of the
CC       biosynthesis of 3-dehydroquinate (DHQ), which is involved in the
CC       canonical pathway for the biosynthesis of aromatic amino acids.
CC   -!- The enzyme can also catalyze the reaction of EC 4.1.2.13.
DR   Q58980, DKFP_METJA ;
//
ID   2.2.1.12
DE   3-acetyloctanal synthase.
CA   Pyruvate + (E)-oct-2-enal = (S)-3-acetyloctanal + CO(2).
CF   Thiamine diphosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Serratia marcescens,
CC       participates in the biosynthesis of the antibiotic prodigiosin.
CC   -!- The enzyme decarboxylates pyruvate, followed by attack of the
CC       resulting two-carbon fragment on (E)-oct-2-enal, resulting in a
CC       Stetter reaction.
CC   -!- In vitro the enzyme can act on a number of alpha,beta-unsaturated
CC       carbonyl compounds, including aldehydes and ketones, and can catalyze
CC       both 1-2 and 1-4 carboligations depending on the substrate.
DR   Q5W251, PIGD_SERMA ;  Q5W268, PIGD_SERS3 ;
//
ID   2.3.1.1
