CA   (2) A long-chain acyl-[mycocerosate synthase] + 4 methylmalonyl-CoA +
CA   8 NADPH = a tetramethylated-mycocerosoyl-[mycocerosate synthase] + 4 CoA
CA   + 4 CO(2) + 8 NADP(+) + 4 H(2)O.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from mycobacteria, is loaded with a long-
CC       chain acyl moiety by EC 6.2.1.49 and elongates it by incorporation of
CC       three or four methylmalonyl (but not malonyl) residues, to form tri-
CC       or tetramethyl-branched fatty-acids, respectively, such as 2,4,6,8-
CC       tetramethyloctacosanoate (C(32)-mycocerosate).
CC   -!- Since the enzyme lacks a thioesterase domain, the product remains
CC       bound and requires additional enzyme(s) for removal.
CC   -!- Even though the enzyme can accept C(6) to C(20) substrates in vitro,
CC       it prefers to act on C(14)-C(20) substrates in vivo.
PR   PROSITE; PDOC00529;
DR   Q02251, MCAS_MYCBO ;
//
ID   2.3.1.112
DE   D-tryptophan N-malonyltransferase.
CA   Malonyl-CoA + D-tryptophan = CoA + N(2)-malonyl-D-tryptophan.
CC   -!- 1-aminocyclopropane-1-carboxylate can act instead of malonyl-CoA.
//
ID   2.3.1.113
DE   Anthranilate N-malonyltransferase.
CA   Malonyl-CoA + anthranilate = CoA + N-malonylanthranilate.
//
ID   2.3.1.114
DE   3,4-dichloroaniline N-malonyltransferase.
CA   Malonyl-CoA + 3,4-dichloroaniline = CoA + N-(3,4-dichlorophenyl)-
CA   malonamate.
//
ID   2.3.1.115
DE   Isoflavone-7-O-beta-glucoside 6''-O-malonyltransferase.
AN   Flavone/flavonol 7-O-beta-D-glucoside malonyltransferase.
CA   Malonyl-CoA + biochanin A 7-O-beta-D-glucoside = CoA + biochanin A 7-O-
CA   (6-O-malonyl-beta-D-glucoside).
CC   -!- The 6-position of the glucose residue of formononetin can also act as
CC       acceptor; some other 7-O-glucosides of isoflavones, flavones and
CC       flavonols can also act, but more slowly.
//
ID   2.3.1.116
DE   Flavonol-3-O-beta-glucoside O-malonyltransferase.
CA   Malonyl-CoA + flavonol 3-O-beta-D-glucoside = CoA + flavonol 3-O-(6-O-
CA   malonyl-beta-D-glucoside).
//
ID   2.3.1.117
DE   2,3,4,5-tetrahydropyridine-2,6-dicarboxylate N-succinyltransferase.
AN   Succinyl-CoA:tetrahydrodipicolinate N-succinyltransferase.
AN   Tetrahydrodipicolinate N-succinyltransferase.
AN   Tetrahydrodipicolinate succinylase.
AN   Tetrahydrodipicolinate succinyltransferase.
CA   Succinyl-CoA + (S)-2,3,4,5-tetrahydropyridine-2,6-dicarboxylate + H(2)O =
CA   CoA + N-succinyl-L-2-amino-6-oxoheptanedioate.
CC   -!- Involved in the biosynthesis of lysine in bacteria, cyanobacteria and
CC       higher plants.
CC   -!- Earlier erroneously called 2,3,4,5-tetrahydropyridine-2-carboxylate
CC       N-succinyltransferase.
