AN   KASIII.
CA   Acetyl-CoA + malonyl-[acyl-carrier-protein] = acetoacetyl-[acyl-carrier-
CA   protein] + CoA + CO(2).
CC   -!- Involved in the dissociated (or type II) fatty-acid biosynthesis
CC       system that occurs in plants and bacteria.
CC   -!- In contrast to EC 2.3.1.41 and EC 2.3.1.179, this enzyme specifically
CC       uses CoA thioesters rather than acyl-ACP as the primer.
CC   -!- In addition to the above reaction, the enzyme can also catalyze the
CC       reaction of EC 2.3.1.38, but to a much lesser extent.
CC   -!- Responsible for initiating both straight- and branched-chain fatty-
CC       acid biosynthesis, with the substrate specificity in an organism
CC       reflecting the fatty-acid composition found in that organism.
CC   -!- For example, Streptococcus pneumoniae, a Gram-positive bacterium,
CC       is able to use both straight- and branched-chain (C4--C6) acyl-CoA
CC       primers whereas Escherichia coli, a Gram-negative organism, uses
CC       primarily short straight-chain acyl CoAs, with a preference for
CC       acetyl-CoA.
