ID   2.3.1.182
DE   (R)-citramalate synthase.
CA   Acetyl-CoA + pyruvate + H(2)O = CoA + (2R)-2-hydroxy-2-
CA   methylbutanedioate.
CC   -!- Involved in a novel pyruvate pathway for isoleucine biosynthesis that
CC       is found mainly in archaea.
CC   -!- Can be inhibited by isoleucine, the end-product of the pathway,
CC       but not by leucine.
CC   -!- Highly specific for pyruvate as substrate, as the 2-oxo acids
CC       3-methyl-2-oxobutanoate, 2-oxobutanoate, 4-methyl-2-oxopentanoate,
CC       2-oxohexanoate and 2-oxoglutarate cannot act as substrate.
DR   O66682, CIMA_AQUAE ;  O29305, CIMA_ARCFU ;  Q74C76, CIMA_GEOSL ;
