ID   2.3.1.226
DE   Carboxymethylproline synthase.
CA   Malonyl-CoA + (S)-1-pyrroline-5-carboxylate + H(2)O = CoA + (2S,5S)-5-
CA   carboxymethylproline + CO(2).
CC   -!- The enzyme is involved in the biosynthesis of the carbapenem beta-
CC       lactam antibiotic (5R)-carbapen-2-em-3-carboxylate in the bacterium
CC       Pectobacterium carotovorum.
DR   Q9XB60, CARB_PECCC ;
//
ID   2.3.1.227
DE   GDP-perosamine N-acetyltransferase.
AN   GDP-alpha-D-perosamine N-acetyltransferase.
CA   Acetyl-CoA + GDP-4-amino-4,6-dideoxy-alpha-D-mannose = CoA + GDP-4-
CA   acetamido-4,6-dideoxy-alpha-D-mannose.
CC   -!- D-perosamine is one of several dideoxy sugars found in the O-antigen
CC       component of the outer membrane lipopolysaccharides of Gram-negative
CC       bacteria.
DR   Q7DBF7, PERB_ECO57 ;
//
ID   2.3.1.228
DE   Isovaleryl-homoserine lactone synthase.
AN   IV-HSL synthase.
CA   Isovaleryl-CoA + S-adenosyl-L-methionine = CoA + S-methyl-
CA   5'-thioadenosine + N-isovaleryl-L-homoserine lactone.
CC   -!- The enzyme, found in the bacterium Bradyrhizobium japonicum, does not
CC       accept isovaleryl-[acyl-carrier protein] as acyl donor (cf.
CC       EC 2.3.1.184).
DR   Q89VI2, BJAI_BRADU ;
//
ID   2.3.1.229
DE   4-coumaroyl-homoserine lactone synthase.
AN   p-coumaryl-homoserine lactone synthase.
CA   4-coumaroyl-CoA + S-adenosyl-L-methionine = CoA + S-methyl-5-
CA   thioadenosine + N-(4-coumaroyl)-L-homoserine lactone.
CC   -!- The enzyme is found in the bacterium Rhodopseudomonas palustris,
CC       which produces N-(4-coumaroyl)-L-homoserine lactone as a quorum-
CC       sensing signal.
DR   Q6NCZ6, RPAI_RHOPA ;
//
ID   2.3.1.230
DE   2-heptyl-4(1H)-quinolone synthase.
CA   Octanoyl-CoA + 2-aminobenzoylacetate = 2-heptyl-4(1H)-quinolone + CoA +
CA   CO(2) + H(2)O.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Pseudomonas aeruginosa,
CC       is a heterodimeric complex.
CC   -!- The PqsC subunit acquires an octanoyl group from octanoyl-CoA and
CC       attaches it to an internal cysteine residue.
CC   -!- Together with the PqsB subunit, the proteins catalyze the coupling of
CC       the octanoyl group with (2-aminobenzoyl)acetate, leading to
CC       decarboxylation and dehydration events that result in closure of the
CC       quinoline ring.
DR   Q9I4X1, PQSC_PSEAE ;
//
ID   2.3.1.231
DE   tRNA(Phe) (7-(3-amino-3-(methoxycarbonyl)propyl)wyosine(37)-N)-
DE   methoxycarbonyltransferase.
AN   tRNA-yW synthesizing enzyme-4.
CA   S-adenosyl-L-methionine + 7-((3S)-3-amino-3-
CA   (methoxycarbonyl)propyl)wyosine(37) in tRNA(Phe) + CO(2) = S-adenosyl-L-
CA   homocysteine + wybutosine(37) in tRNA(Phe).
CC   -!- The enzyme is found only in eukaryotes, where it is involved in the
CC       biosynthesis of wybutosine, a hypermodified tricyclic base found at
CC       position 37 of certain tRNAs.
CC   -!- The modification is important for translational reading-frame
CC       maintenance.
CC   -!- In some species that produce hydroxywybutosine the enzyme uses
CC       7-(2-hydroxy-3-amino-3-(methoxycarbonyl)propyl)wyosine(37) in
CC       tRNA(Phe) as substrate.
CC   -!- The enzyme also has the activity of EC 2.1.1.290.
DR   Q75AW4, TYW4_ASHGO ;  Q4WVD1, TYW4_ASPFU ;  Q2U6D4, TYW4_ASPOR ;
DR   Q5A931, TYW4_CANAL ;  Q6FXA5, TYW4_CANGA ;  Q5BH52, TYW4_EMENI ;
DR   Q4IER0, TYW4_GIBZE ;  O60294, TYW4_HUMAN ;  Q8BYR1, TYW4_MOUSE ;
DR   Q9P3K9, TYW4_NEUCR ;  Q5XIA3, TYW4_RAT   ;  O60157, TYW4_SCHPO ;
DR   Q6C3P4, TYW4_YARLI ;  Q08282, TYW4_YEAST ;
