DE   Lysine/arginine leucyltransferase.
AN   L/F transferase.
AN   Leucyl-tRNA--protein transferase.
AN   Leucyl/phenylalanyl-tRNA--protein transferase.
AN   Leucyltransferase.
CA   (1) L-leucyl-tRNA(Leu) + N-terminal L-lysyl-[protein] = tRNA(Leu) +
CA   N-terminal L-leucyl-L-lysyl-[protein].
CA   (2) L-leucyl-tRNA(Leu) + N-terminal L-arginyl-[protein] = tRNA(Leu) +
CA   N-terminal L-leucyl-L-arginyl-[protein].
CF   Monovalent cation.
CC   -!- Participates in the N-end rule protein degradation pathway in certain
CC       bacteria, by attaching the primary destabilizing residue L-leucine to
CC       the N-termini of proteins that have an N-terminal L-arginine or
CC       L-lysine residue.
CC   -!- Once modified, the proteins are recognized by EC 3.4.21.92.
CC   -!- The enzyme also transfers L-phenylalanine in vitro, but this has not
CC       been observed in vivo.
CC   -!- Cf. EC 2.3.2.8 and EC 2.3.2.29.
