DE   Lipid II:glycine glycyltransferase.
CA   MurNAc-L-Ala-D-isoglutaminyl-L-Lys-D-Ala-D-Ala-diphospho-ditrans,octacis-
CA   undecaprenyl-GlcNAc + glycyl-tRNA(Gly) = MurNAc-L-Ala-D-isoglutaminyl-L-
CA   Lys-(N(6)-Gly)-D-Ala-D-Ala-diphospho-ditrans,octacis-undecaprenyl-GlcNAc
CA   + tRNA(Gly).
CC   -!- This enzyme from Staphylococcus aureus catalyzes the transfer of
CC       glycine from a charged tRNA to MurNAc-L-Ala-D-isoglutaminyl-L-Lys-D-
CC       Ala-D-Ala-diphosphoundecaprenyl-GlcNAc (lipid II), attaching it to
CC       the N(6) of the L-lysine at position 3 of the pentapeptide.
CC   -!- This is the first step in the synthesis of the pentaglycine
CC       interpeptide bridge that is used in S.aureus for the crosslinking of
CC       different glycan strands to each other.
CC   -!- Four additional glycine residues are subsequently attached by
CC       EC 2.3.2.17 (FemA) and EC 2.3.2.18 (FemB).
