CA   ditrans,octacis-undecaprenyl-GlcNAc + 2 glycyl-tRNA = MurNAc-L-Ala-D-
CA   isoglutaminyl-L-Lys-(N(6)-tri-Gly)-D-Ala-D-Ala-diphospho-ditrans,octacis-
CA   undecaprenyl-GlcNAc + 2 tRNA.
CC   -!- This enzyme catalyzes the successive transfer of two glycine moieties
CC       from charged tRNAs to MurNAc-L-Ala-D-isoglutaminyl-L-Lys-(N(6)-Gly)-
CC       D-Ala-D-Ala-diphospho-ditrans,octacis-undecaprenyl-GlcNAc, attaching
CC       them to a glycine residue previously attached by EC 2.3.2.16 (FemX)
CC       to the N(6) of the L-lysine at position 3 of the pentapeptide.
CC   -!- This is the second step in the synthesis of the pentaglycine
CC       interpeptide bridge that is used by Staphylococcus aureus for the
CC       crosslinking of different glycan strands to each other.
CC   -!- The next step is catalyzed by EC 2.3.2.18 (FemB).
CC   -!- This enzyme is essential for methicillin resistance.
