CA   ditrans,octacis-undecaprenyl-GlcNAc + 2 tRNA.
CC   -!- This Staphylococcus aureus enzyme catalyzes the successive transfer
CC       of two glycine moieties from charged tRNAs to MurNAc-L-Ala-D-
CC       isoglutaminyl-L-Lys-(N(6)-tri-Gly)-D-Ala-D-Ala-diphospho-
CC       ditrans,octacis-undecaprenyl-GlcNAc, attaching them to the three
CC       glycine molecules that were previously attached to the N(6) of the
CC       L-lysine at position 3 of the pentapeptide by EC 2.3.2.16 (FemX) and
CC       EC 2.3.2.17 (FemA).
CC   -!- This is the last step in the synthesis of the pentaglycine
CC       interpeptide bridge that is used in this organism for the
CC       crosslinking of different glycan strands to each other.
