CA   N-terminal L-leucyl-L-glutamyl-[protein].
CA   (2) L-leucyl-tRNA(Leu) + N-terminal L-aspartyl-[protein] = tRNA(Leu) +
CA   N-terminal L-leucyl-L-aspartyl-[protein].
CC   -!- The enzyme participates in the N-end rule protein degradation pathway
CC       in certain bacteria, by attaching the primary destabilizing residue
CC       L-leucine to the N-termini of proteins that have an N-terminal
CC       L-aspartate or L-glutamate residue.
CC   -!- Once modified, the proteins are recognized by EC 3.4.21.92.
CC   -!- Cf. EC 2.3.2.6 and EC 2.3.2.8.
