CA   glucosyl-((1->6)-alpha-D-glucosyl)(n).
CC   -!- The enzyme was characterized from the dental caries bacterium
CC       Streptococcus mutans.
CC   -!- It transfers glucosyl residues from sucrose to either the 6- or the
CC       3-positions of glucose residues in glucans, producing a highly-
CC       branched extracellular D-glucan polymers that promote attachment of
CC       the bacteria to teeth.
CC   -!- Three types of the enzyme have been described; the insoluble polymers
CC       produced by GTF-I and GTF-SI contain 85% alpha(1->3) bonds and 15%
CC       alpha(1->6) bonds, while the soluble polymers produced by GTF-S
CC       contain only 30% of alpha(1->3) bonds and 70% alpha(1->6) bonds.
CC   -!- Cf. EC 2.4.1.5.
