ID   2.4.1.132
DE   GDP-Man:Man(1)GlcNAc(2)-PP-dolichol alpha-1,3-mannosyltransferase.
AN   GDP-Man:Man(1)GlcNAc(2)-PP-Dol alpha-1,3-mannosyltransferase.
AN   Mannosyltransferase II.
CA   GDP-D-mannose + D-Man-beta-(1->4)-D-GlcNAc-beta-(1->4)-D-GlcNAc-
CA   diphosphodolichol = GDP + D-Man-alpha-(1->3)-D-Man-beta-(1->4)-D-GlcNAc-
CA   beta-(1->4)-GlcNAc-diphosphodolichol.
CC   -!- The biosynthesis of asparagine-linked glycoproteins utilizes a
CC       dolichyl diphosphate-linked glycosyl donor, which is assembled by the
CC       series of membrane-bound glycosyltransferases that comprise the
CC       dolichol pathway.
CC   -!- Alg2 mannosyltransferase from Saccharomyces cerevisiae carries out an
CC       alpha-1,3-mannosylation of D-Man-beta-(1->4)-D-GlcNAc-beta-(1->4)-D-
CC       GlcNAc-diphosphodolichol, followed by an alpha-1,6-mannosylation (cf.
CC       EC 2.4.1.257), to form the first branched pentasaccharide
CC       intermediate of the dolichol pathway.
DR   Q755C1, ALG2_ASHGO ;  Q59LF2, ALG2_CANAL ;  Q6FJJ9, ALG2_CANGA ;
DR   Q6BVA4, ALG2_DEBHA ;  Q7KWM5, ALG2_DICDI ;  Q9H553, ALG2_HUMAN ;
