ID   2.4.1.138
DE   Mannotetraose 2-alpha-N-acetylglucosaminyltransferase.
AN   Alpha-N-acetylglucosaminyltransferase.
CA   UDP-N-acetyl-alpha-D-glucosamine + alpha-D-Man-(1->3)-alpha-D-Man-(1->2)-
CA   alpha-D-Man-(1->2)-D-Man = UDP + alpha-D-Man-(1->3)-(alpha-D-GlcNAc-
CA   (1->2))-alpha-D-Man-(1->2)-alpha-D-Man-(1->2)-D-Man.
//
ID   2.4.1.139
DE   Maltose synthase.
CA   2 alpha-D-glucose 1-phosphate + H(2)O = maltose + 2 phosphate.
CC   -!- Neither free phosphate nor maltose 1-phosphate is an intermediate in
CC       the reaction.
//
ID   2.4.1.140
DE   Alternansucrase.
AN   Sucrose-1,6(3)-alpha-glucan 6(3)-alpha-glucosyltransferase.
AN   Sucrose:1,6-, 1,3-alpha-D-glucan 3-alpha- and 6-alpha-D-
AN   glucosyltransferase.
CA   Transfers alternately an alpha-D-glucosyl residue from sucrose to the
CA   6-position and the 3-position of the non-reducing terminal residue of an
CA   alpha-D-glucan, thus producing a glucan having alternating alpha-(1->6)-
CA   and alpha-(1->3)-linkages.
CC   -!- The product, which has quite different properties from other
CC       dextrans, has been called alternan.
//
ID   2.4.1.141
DE   N-acetylglucosaminyldiphosphodolichol N-acetylglucosaminyltransferase.
