ID   2.4.1.245
DE   Alpha,alpha-trehalose synthase.
AN   Trehalose synthase.
AN   Trehalose synthetase.
CA   NDP-alpha-D-glucose + D-glucose = alpha,alpha-trehalose + NDP.
CF   Mg(2+).
CC   -!- The enzyme-catalyzed reaction is reversible.
CC   -!- In the reverse direction to that shown above, the enzyme is specific
CC       for alpha,alpha-trehalose as substrate, as it cannot use alpha- or
CC       beta-paranitrophenyl glucosides, maltose, sucrose, lactose or
CC       cellobiose.
CC   -!- While the enzymes from the thermophilic bacterium Rubrobacter
CC       xylanophilus and the hyperthermophilic archaeon Pyrococcus horikoshii
CC       can use ADP-, UDP- and GDP-alpha-D-glucose to the same extent, that
CC       from the hyperthermophilic archaeon Thermococcus litoralis has a
CC       marked preference for ADP-alpha-D-glucose and that from the
CC       hyperthermophilic archaeon Thermoproteus tenax has a marked
CC       preference for UDP-alpha-D-glucose.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 2.4.1.n1.
