DE   Glucosyl-3-phosphoglycerate synthase.
AN   Glucosylphosphoglycerate synthase.
AN   GPG synthase.
CA   NDP-glucose + 3-phospho-D-glycerate = NDP + 2-O-(alpha-D-glucopyranosyl)-
CA   3-phospho-D-glycerate.
CC   -!- The enzyme is involved in biosynthesis of 2-O-(alpha-D-
CC       glucopyranosyl)-D-glycerate via the two-step pathway in which
CC       glucosyl-3-phosphoglycerate synthase catalyzes the conversion of GDP-
CC       glucose and 3-phospho-D-glycerate into 2-O-(alpha-D-glucopyranosyl)-
CC       3-phospho-D-glycerate, which is then converted to 2-O-(alpha-D-
CC       glucopyranosyl)-D-glycerate by EC 3.1.3.85.
CC   -!- The activity is dependent on divalent cations (Mn(2+), Co(2+),
CC       or Mg(2+)).
CC   -!- The enzyme from Persephonella marina shows moderate flexibility on
CC       the sugar donor concerning the nucleotide moiety (UDP-glucose, ADP-
CC       glucose, GDP-glucose) but is strictly specific for glucose.
CC   -!- The enzyme is also strictly specific for 3-phospho-D-glycerate as
CC       acceptor.
CC   -!- The enzyme from Methanococcoides burtonii is strictly specific for
CC       GDP-glucose and 3-phospho-D-glycerate.
CC   -!- This enzyme catalyzes the first glucosylation step in methylglucose
