CA   dolichyl N-acetyl-alpha-D-glucosaminyl phosphate = UDP + an archaeal
CA   dolichyl 3-O-(2,3-diacetamido-2,3-dideoxy-beta-D-glucuronsyl)-N-acetyl-
CA   alpha-D-glucosaminyl phosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the methanogenic archaeon
CC       Methanococcus voltae, participates in the N-glycosylation of
CC       proteins.
CC   -!- Dolichol used by archaea is different from that used by eukaryotes;
CC       it is much shorter (C(55)-C(60)), it is alpha,omega-saturated and it
CC       may have additional unsaturated positions in the chain.
