ID   2.4.2.19
DE   Nicotinate-nucleotide diphosphorylase (carboxylating).
AN   Nicotinate-nucleotide pyrophosphorylase (carboxylating).
AN   Quinolinate phosphoribosyltransferase (decarboxylating).
CA   Beta-nicotinate D-ribonucleotide + diphosphate + CO(2) = pyridine-2,3-
CA   dicarboxylate + 5-phospho-alpha-D-ribose 1-diphosphate.
CC   -!- The reaction is catalyzed in the opposite direction.
CC   -!- Since quinolinate is synthesized from L-tryptophan in eukaryotes,
CC       but from L-aspartate in some prokaryotes, this is the first NAD(+)
CC       biosynthesis enzyme shared by both eukaryotes and prokaryotes.
DR   Q9ZU32, NADC_ARATH ;  O28439, NADC_ARCFU ;  P39666, NADC_BACSU ;
DR   Q3T063, NADC_BOVIN ;  Q75JX0, NADC_DICDI ;  P30011, NADC_ECOLI ;
DR   Q9ZJN2, NADC_HELPJ ;  O25909, NADC_HELPY ;  Q15274, NADC_HUMAN ;
