ID   2.4.2.29
DE   tRNA-guanine(34) transglycosylase.
AN   Guanine insertion enzyme.
AN   Q-insertase.
AN   Queuine tRNA-ribosyltransferase.
AN   Queuine(34) transfer ribonucleate ribosyltransferase.
AN   TGT.
AN   tRNA guanine(34) transglycosidase.
AN   tRNA transglycosylase.
CA   (1) Guanine(34) in tRNA + queuine = queuosine(34) in tRNA + guanine.
CA   (2) Guanine(34) in tRNA + 7-aminomethyl-7-carbaguanine = 7-aminomethyl-7-
CA   carbaguanine(34) in tRNA + guanine.
CC   -!- Certain prokaryotic and eukaryotic tRNAs contain the modified base
CC       queuine at position 34.
CC   -!- In eukaryotes queuine is salvaged from food and incorporated into
CC       tRNA directly via a base-exchange reaction, replacing guanine.
CC   -!- In eubacteria, which produce queuine de novo, the enzyme catalyzes
CC       the exchange of guanine with the queuine precursor preQ(1), which is
CC       ultimately modified to queuine.
CC   -!- The eubacterial enzyme can also use an earlier intermediate, preQ(0),
CC       to replace guanine in unmodified tRNA(Tyr) and tRNA(Asn).
CC   -!- This enzyme acts after EC 1.7.1.13 in the queuine-biosynthesis
CC       pathway.
