AN   KDO transferase.
AN   Lipid IV(A) KDO transferase.
CA   Lipid IV(A) + CMP-beta-Kdo = alpha-Kdo-(2->6)-lipid IV(A) + CMP.
CC   -!- The bifunctional enzyme from Escherichia coli transfers two 3-deoxy-
CC       D-manno-octulosonate residues to lipid IV(A) (cf. EC 2.4.99.13).
CC   -!- The monofunctional enzymes from Aquifex aeolicus and Haemophilus
CC       influenzae catalyze the transfer of a single 3-deoxy-D-manno-
CC       octulosonate residue from CMP-3-deoxy-D-manno-octulosonate to lipid
CC       IV(A).
CC   -!- The enzymes from Chlamydia transfer three or more 3-deoxy-D-manno-
CC       octulosonate residues and generate genus-specific epitopes.
