CC   -!- 4-hydroxybenzoate, 1,4-dihydroxy 2-naphthoate, homogentisate and
CC       alpha-glycerophosphate cannot act as prenyl-acceptor substrates.
CC   -!- The other enzymes involved in the biosynthesis of polar lipids in
CC       archaea are EC 1.1.1.261, EC 2.5.1.41, which, together with this
CC       enzyme, alkylates the hydroxy groups of glycerol 1-phosphate to yield
CC       unsaturated archaetidic acid, which is acted upon by EC 2.7.7.67 to
CC       form CDP-unsaturated archaeol.
CC   -!- The final step in the pathway involves the addition of L-serine, with
CC       concomitant removal of CMP, leading to the production of unsaturated
CC       archaetidylserine.
