ID   2.5.1.44
DE   Homospermidine synthase.
CA   (1) 2 putrescine = sym-homospermidine + NH(3) + H(+).
CA   (2) Putrescine + spermidine = sym-homospermidine + propane-1,3-diamine.
CF   NAD(+).
CC   -!- The reaction of this enzyme occurs in three steps, with some of the
CC       intermediates presumably remaining enzyme-bound: NAD(+)-dependent
CC       dehydrogenation of putrescine, transfer of the 4-aminobutylidene
CC       group from dehydroputrescine to a second molecule of putrescine and
CC       reduction of the imine intermediate to form homospermidine.
CC   -!- Hence the overall reaction is transfer of a 4-aminobutyl group.
CC   -!- Differs from EC 2.5.1.45, which cannot use putrescine as donor of the
CC       aminobutyl group.
DR   O32323, HSS_BLAVI  ;  Q98H64, HSS_RHILO  ;
