ID   2.5.1.59
DE   Protein geranylgeranyltransferase type I.
AN   GGTase-I.
AN   GGTaseI.
AN   Type I protein geranyl-geranyltransferase.
CA   Geranylgeranyl diphosphate + protein-cysteine = S-geranylgeranyl-
CA   protein + diphosphate.
CF   Zn(2+).
CC   -!- This enzyme, along with EC 2.5.1.58 and EC 2.5.1.60, constitutes the
CC       protein prenyltransferase family of enzymes.
CC   -!- Catalyzes the formation of a thioether linkage between the C-1 atom
CC       of the geranylgeranyl group and a cysteine residue fourth from the
CC       C-terminus of the protein.
CC   -!- These protein acceptors have the C-terminal sequence CA(1)A(2)X,
CC       where the terminal residue, X, is preferably leucine; serine,
CC       methionine, alanine or glutamine makes the protein a substrate for
CC       EC 2.5.1.58.
CC   -!- The enzymes are relaxed in specificity for A(1), but cannot act if
CC       A(2) is aromatic.
CC   -!- Known targets of this enzyme include most gamma-subunits of
CC       heterotrimeric G proteins and Ras-related GTPases such as members of
CC       the Ras and Rac/Rho families.
CC   -!- The Zn(2+) is required for peptide, but not for isoprenoid, substrate
CC       binding.
PR   PROSITE; PDOC00703;
