ID   2.5.1.79
DE   Thermospermine synthase.
CA   S-adenosyl 3-(methylthio)propylamine + spermidine = S-methyl-
CA   5'-thioadenosine + thermospermine + H(+).
CC   -!- This enzyme is required for correct xylem specification through
CC       regulation of the lifetime of the xylem elements.
PR   PROSITE; PDOC01033;
DR   Q9S7X6, ACL5_ARATH ;  A2BIX4, SPEE1_HYPBU;  P09158, SPEE_ECOLI ;
DR   Q8ZXM4, SPEE_PYRAE ;  Q9UXE4, SPEE_SULSO ;  Q5SK28, SPEE_THET8 ;
//
ID   2.5.1.80
DE   7-dimethylallyltryptophan synthase.
AN   7-DMATS.
CA   Dimethylallyl diphosphate + L-tryptophan = diphosphate + 7-(3-methylbut-
CA   2-enyl)-L-tryptophan.
CC   -!- This enzyme is more flexible toward the aromatic substrate than
CC       EC 2.5.1.34, but similar to that enzyme, accepts only dimethylallyl
CC       diphosphate as the prenyl donor.
DR   Q4WYG3, 7DMAW_ASPFU;
//
ID   2.5.1.81
DE   Geranylfarnesyl diphosphate synthase.
AN   FGPP synthase.
CA   Geranylgeranyl diphosphate + isopentenyl diphosphate = (2E,6E,10E,14E)-
CA   geranylfarnesyl diphosphate + diphosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme from Methanosarcina mazei is involved in biosynthesis of
CC       the polyprenyl side-chain of methanophenazine, an electron carrier
CC       utilized for methanogenesis.
CC   -!- It prefers geranylgeranyl diphosphate and farnesyl diphosphate as
CC       allylic substrate.
CC   -!- The enzyme from Aeropyrum pernix prefers farnesyl diphosphate as
CC       allylic substrate.
CC   -!- The enzyme is involved in the biosynthesis of C(25)-C(25) membrane
CC       lipids.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 2.5.1.n2.
DR   Q9UWR6, GFPS_AERPX ;  Q8PYS1, GFPS_METMA ;  Q3IPL1, GFPS_NATPD ;
//
ID   2.5.1.82
DE   Hexaprenyl diphosphate synthase (geranylgeranyl-diphosphate specific).
AN   (All-trans)-hexaprenyl-diphosphate synthase.
CA   Geranylgeranyl diphosphate + 2 isopentenyl diphosphate = 2 diphosphate +
CA   all-trans-hexaprenyl diphosphate.
CF   Mg(2+).
CC   -!- The enzyme prefers geranylgeranyl diphosphate to farnesyl diphosphate
CC       as an allylic substrate and does not show activity for geranyl
CC       diphosphate and dimethylallyl diphosphate.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 2.5.1.33.
DR   Q97W92, HEXPP_SULSO;
//
ID   2.5.1.83
DE   Hexaprenyl-diphosphate synthase ((2E,6E)-farnesyl-diphosphate specific).
AN   Hexaprenyl diphosphate synthase.
AN   Hexaprenyl pyrophosphate synthetase.
AN   HexPS.
CA   (2E,6E)-farnesyl diphosphate + 3 isopentenyl diphosphate = 3 diphosphate
CA   + all-trans-hexaprenyl diphosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme prefers farnesyl diphosphate to geranylgeranyl diphosphate
CC       as an allylic substrate and does not show activity for geranyl
CC       diphosphate and dimethylallyl diphosphate.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 2.5.1.33.
DR   O66127, HEXA_MICLU ;  O66129, HEXB_MICLU ;
//
ID   2.5.1.84
DE   All-trans-nonaprenyl-diphosphate synthase (geranyl-diphosphate specific).
AN   Nonaprenyl diphosphate synthase.
AN   Solanesyl-diphosphate synthase.
CA   Geranyl diphosphate + 7 isopentenyl diphosphate = 7 diphosphate + all-
CA   trans-nonaprenyl diphosphate.
CC   -!- (2E,6E)-Farnesyl diphosphate and geranylgeranyl diphosphate are less
CC       effective as substrates than geranyl diphosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme is involved in the synthesis of the side chain of
CC       menaquinone-9.
CC   -!- In Oryza sativa the enzyme SPS2 is involved in providing solanesyl
CC       diphosphate for plastoquinone-9 formation.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 2.5.1.11.
DR   O24743, SDSA_RHOCA ;  Q653T6, SPS1_ORYSJ ;  Q75HZ9, SPS2_ORYSJ ;
DR   Q0INZ4, SPS3_ORYSJ ;
//
ID   2.5.1.85
DE   All-trans-nonaprenyl-diphosphate synthase (geranylgeranyl-diphosphate
DE   specific).
AN   Nonaprenyl diphosphate synthase.
AN   Solanesyl diphosphate synthase.
CA   Geranylgeranyl diphosphate + 5 isopentenyl diphosphate = 5 diphosphate +
CA   all-trans-nonaprenyl diphosphate.
CC   -!- Geranylgeranyl diphosphate is preferred over farnesyl diphosphate as
CC       allylic substrate.
CC   -!- The plant Arabidopsis thaliana has two different enzymes that
CC       catalyze this reaction.
CC   -!- SPS1 contributes to the biosynthesis of the ubiquinone side-chain
CC       while SPS2 supplies the precursor of the plastoquinone side-chains.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 2.5.1.11.
DR   Q8S948, SPS1_ARATH ;  Q76FS5, SPS2_ARATH ;  Q5HZ00, SPS3_ARATH ;
//
ID   2.5.1.86
DE   Trans,polycis-decaprenyl diphosphate synthase.
AN   (2Z,6Z,10Z,14Z,18Z,22Z,26Z,30Z,34E)-decaprenyl diphosphate synthase.
CA   (2Z,6E)-farnesyl diphosphate + 7 isopentenyl diphosphate = 7 diphosphate
CA   + (2Z,6Z,10Z,14Z,18Z,22Z,26Z,30Z,34E)-decaprenyl diphosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme is involved in the biosynthesis of decaprenyl phosphate,
CC       which plays a central role in the biosynthesis of essential
CC       mycobacterial cell wall components, such as the mycolyl-
CC       arabinogalactan-peptidoglycan complex and lipoarabinomannan.
DR   P60478, DPDS_MYCBO ;  P38119, DPDS_MYCLE ;  A0R0S4, DPDS_MYCS2 ;
DR   P9WFF6, DPDS_MYCTO ;  P9WFF7, DPDS_MYCTU ;
//
ID   2.5.1.87
DE   Ditrans,polycis-polyprenyl diphosphate synthase ((2E,6E)-farnesyl
DE   diphosphate specific).
AN   Dehydrodolichyl diphosphate synthase 1.
AN   Rer2p Z-prenyltransferase.
CA   (2E,6E)-farnesyl diphosphate + n isopentenyl diphosphate = n diphosphate
CA   + ditrans,polycis-polyprenyl diphosphate (n = 10-55).
CC   -!- The enzyme is involved in biosynthesis of dolichol (a long-chain
CC       polyprenol) with a saturated alpha-isoprene unit, which serves as a
CC       glycosyl carrier in protein glycosylation.
CC   -!- The yeast Saccharomyces cerevisiae has two different enzymes that
CC       catalyze this reaction.
CC   -!- Rer2p synthesizes a well-defined family of polyprenols of 13-18
CC       isoprene residues with dominating C(80) (16 isoprene residues)
CC       extending to C(120), while Srt1p synthesizes mainly polyprenol with
CC       22 isoprene subunits.
CC   -!- Largest Srt1p products reach C(290).
CC   -!- The enzyme from Arabidopsis thaliana catalyzes the formation of
CC       polyprenyl diphosphates with predominant carbon number C(120).
DR   O80458, DDPS1_ARATH;  Q86SQ9, DHDDS_HUMAN;  Q99KU1, DHDDS_MOUSE;
DR   P60478, DPDS_MYCBO ;  P38119, DPDS_MYCLE ;  A0R0S4, DPDS_MYCS2 ;
DR   P9WFF6, DPDS_MYCTO ;  P9WFF7, DPDS_MYCTU ;  Q6DHR8, NGBR_DANRE ;
DR   Q96E22, NGBR_HUMAN ;  Q99LJ8, NGBR_MOUSE ;  P35196, RER2_YEAST ;
DR   Q03175, SRT1_YEAST ;  Q9Y7K8, UPPS_SCHPO ;  Q12063, UPPS_YEAST ;
DR   O14171, YE54_SCHPO ;
//
ID   2.5.1.88
DE   Trans,polycis-polyprenyl diphosphate synthase ((2Z,6E)-farnesyl
DE   diphosphate specific).
CA   (2Z,6E)-farnesyl diphosphate + n isopentenyl diphosphate = n diphosphate
CA   + trans,polycis-polyprenyl diphosphate (n = 9-11).
CC   -!- Highest activity with (2Z,6E)-farnesyl diphosphate as allylic
CC       substrate.
CC   -!- Broad product specificity with the major product being dodecaprenyl
CC       diphosphate.
CC   -!- Synthesizes even C(70) prenyl diphosphate as the maximum chain-length
CC       product.
DR   Q47RM6, DPDP_THEFY ;
//
ID   2.5.1.89
DE   Tritrans,polycis-undecaprenyl-diphosphate synthase (geranylgeranyl-
DE   diphosphate specific).
CA   Geranylgeranyl diphosphate + 7 isopentenyl diphosphate = 7 diphosphate +
CA   tritrans,heptacis-undecaprenyl diphosphate.
CC   -!- This enzyme is involved in the biosynthesis of the glycosyl carrier
CC       lipid in some archaebacteria.
CC   -!- Unlike EC 2.5.1.31, its counterpart in most bacteria, it prefers
CC       geranylgeranyl diphosphate to farnesyl diphosphate as the allylic
CC       substrate, resulting in production of a tritrans,polycis variant of
CC       undecaprenyl diphosphate.
DR   Q9YC66, UPPS_AERPE ;  O29049, UPPS_ARCFU ;  Q5V1I1, UPPS_HALMA ;
DR   Q9HP68, UPPS_HALSA ;  Q8TJQ7, UPPS_METAC ;  Q58767, UPPS_METJA ;
DR   Q8TXA7, UPPS_METKA ;  Q8PZ76, UPPS_METMA ;  O26334, UPPS_METTH ;
DR   Q6KZ89, UPPS_PICTO ;  Q9V157, UPPS_PYRAB ;  Q8ZU54, UPPS_PYRAE ;
DR   Q8U0I8, UPPS_PYRFU ;  O59258, UPPS_PYRHO ;  Q9HH76, UPPS_SULAC ;
DR   Q980W4, UPPS_SULSO ;  Q976K2, UPPS_SULTO ;  Q9HKQ0, UPPS_THEAC ;
DR   Q5JGE1, UPPS_THEKO ;  Q97B58, UPPS_THEVO ;
//
ID   2.5.1.90
DE   All-trans-octaprenyl-diphosphate synthase.
AN   Octaprenyl pyrophosphate synthetase.
AN   Terpenyl pyrophosphate synthetase.
AN   Trans-heptaprenyltranstransferase.
AN   Trans-prenyltransferase.
CA   (2E,6E)-farnesyl diphosphate + 5 isopentenyl diphosphate = 5 diphosphate
CA   + all-trans-octaprenyl diphosphate.
CC   -!- This enzyme catalyzes the condensation reactions resulting in the
CC       formation of all-trans-octaprenyl diphosphate, the isoprenoid side
CC       chain of ubiquinone-8 and menaquinone-8.
CC   -!- The enzyme adds five isopentenyl diphosphate molecules sequentially
CC       to farnesyl diphosphate with trans stereochemistry.
DR   P0AD57, ISPB_ECOLI ;  P44916, ISPB_HAEIN ;  P0AD58, ISPB_SHIFL ;
//
ID   2.5.1.91
DE   All-trans-decaprenyl-diphosphate synthase.
AN   Decaprenyl pyrophosphate synthetase.
AN   Decaprenyl-diphosphate synthase.
AN   Polyprenylpyrophosphate synthetase.
AN   Terpenoidallyltransferase.
AN   Terpenyl pyrophosphate synthetase.
AN   Trans-prenyltransferase.
CA   (2E,6E)-farnesyl diphosphate + 7 isopentenyl diphosphate = 7 diphosphate
CA   + all-trans-decaprenyl diphosphate.
CC   -!- This enzyme catalyzes the condensation reactions resulting in the
CC       formation of all-trans-decaprenyl diphosphate, the isoprenoid side
CC       chain of ubiquinone-10 and menaquinone-10.
CC   -!- The enzyme adds seven isopentenyl diphosphate molecules sequentially
CC       to farnesyl diphosphate with trans stereochemistry.
DR   Q86YH6, DLP1_HUMAN ;  Q33DR3, DLP1_MOUSE ;  Q5U2R1, DLP1_RAT   ;
DR   O13851, DLP1_SCHPO ;  Q54VJ9, DPS1_DICDI ;  Q5T2R2, DPS1_HUMAN ;
DR   Q33DR2, DPS1_MOUSE ;  O43091, DPS1_SCHPO ;
