ID   2.5.1.92
DE   (2Z,6Z)-farnesyl diphosphate synthase.
AN   Cis,cis-farnesyl diphosphate synthase.
AN   Z,Z-farnesyl pyrophosphate synthase.
AN   Z,Z-FPP synthase.
AN   ZFPS.
CA   Dimethylallyl diphosphate + 2 isopentenyl diphosphate = 2 diphosphate +
CA   (2Z,6Z)-farnesyl diphosphate.
CC   -!- This enzyme, originally characterized from wild tomato, specifically
CC       forms (2Z,6Z)-farnesyl diphosphate via neryl diphosphate and
CC       isopentenyl diphosphate.
CC   -!- In wild tomato it is involved in the biosynthesis of several
CC       sesquiterpenes.
CC   -!- Cf. EC 2.5.1.68 and EC 2.5.1.10.
DR   B8XA40, ZFPS_SOLHA ;
//
ID   2.5.1.93
DE   4-hydroxybenzoate geranyltransferase.
AN   4HB geranyltransferase.
AN   p-hydroxybenzoate geranyltransferase.
AN   PHB geranyltransferase.
CA   Geranyl diphosphate + 4-hydroxybenzoate = 3-geranyl-4-hydroxybenzoate +
CA   diphosphate.
CF   Mg(2+).
CC   -!- The enzyme is involved in shikonin biosynthesis.
CC   -!- It has a strict substrate specificity for geranyl diphosphate.
DR   Q8W405, PGT1_LITER ;  Q8W404, PGT2_LITER ;
//
ID   2.5.1.94
DE   Adenosyl-chloride synthase.
AN   5'-chloro-5'-deoxyadenosine synthase.
AN   Chlorinase.
CA   S-adenosyl-L-methionine + chloride = 5-deoxy-5-chloroadenosine +
CA   L-methionine.
CC   -!- This enzyme, isolated from the marine bacterium Salinispora tropica,
CC       catalyzes an early step in the pathway leading to biosynthesis of the
CC       proteosome inhibitor salinosporamide A.
CC   -!- The enzyme is very similar to EC 2.5.1.63 but does not accept
CC       fluoride.
DR   A4X3Q0, SALL_SALTO ;
//
ID   2.5.1.95
DE   Xanthan pyruvate transferase.
CA   Phosphoenolpyruvate + D-Man-beta-(1->4)-D-GlcA-beta-(1->2)-D-Man-alpha-
CA   (1->3)-D-Glc-beta-(1->4)-D-Glc-alpha-1-diphospho-ditrans,octacis-
CA   undecaprenol = 4,6-CH3(COO(-))C-D-Man-beta-(1->4)-D-GlcA-beta-(1->2)-D-
CA   Man-alpha-(1->3)-D-Glc-beta-(1->4)-D-Glc-alpha-1-diphospho-
CA   ditrans,octacis-undecaprenol + phosphate.
CC   -!- Involved in the biosynthesis of the polysaccharide xanthan.
