CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the thermophilic archaeon Pyrobaculum
CC       aerophilum, can also synthesize norspermidine from propane-1,3-
CC       diamine and thermospermine from spermidine (with lower activity).
CC   -!- The long-chain polyamines stabilize double-stranded DNA at high
CC       temperatures.
CC   -!- In contrast to EC 2.5.1.127, this enzyme does not accept norspermine
CC       as a substrate.
DR   A2BIX4, SPEE1_HYPBU;  Q8ZXM4, SPEE_PYRAE ;  Q9UXE4, SPEE_SULSO ;
DR   Q5SK28, SPEE_THET8 ;
//
ID   2.5.1.127
DE   Caldopentamine synthase.
AN   Long-chain polyamine synthase.
CA   S-adenosyl 3-(methylthio)propylamine + norspermine = S-methyl-
CA   5'-thioadenosine + caldopentamine.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the thermophilic archaeon Hyperthermus
CC       butylicus, can also synthesize norspermine from norspermidine and
CC       thermospermine from spermidine (with lower activity).
CC   -!- The long-chain polyamines stabilize double-stranded DNA at high
CC       temperatures.
CC   -!- In contrast to EC 2.5.1.23 and EC 2.5.1.126, this enzyme shows no
CC       activity with propane-1,3-diamine.
DR   A2BIX4, SPEE1_HYPBU;
//
ID   2.5.1.128
DE   N(4)-bis(aminopropyl)spermidine synthase.
CA   2 S-adenosyl 3-(methylthio)propylamine + spermidine = 2 S-methyl-
CA   5'-thioadenosine + N(4)-bis(aminopropyl)spermidine.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the thermophilic archaeon Thermococcus
CC       kodakarensis, synthesizes the branched-chain polyamine N(4)-
CC       bis(aminopropyl)spermidine, which is required for cell growth at
CC       high-temperature.
CC   -!- When spermine is used as substrate, the enzyme forms N(4)-
CC       aminopropylspermine.
DR   Q58669, BPSA_METJA ;  Q5JIZ3, BPSA_THEKO ;  P25125, BPSA_THETH ;
//
ID   2.5.1.129
DE   Flavin prenyltransferase.
CA   Dimethylallyl phosphate + FMNH(2) = prenylated FMNH(2) + phosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme produces the modified flavin cofactor prenylated FMNH(2),
CC       which is required by EC 4.1.1.98 and EC 4.1.1.102.
CC   -!- The enzyme acts as a flavin prenyltransferase, linking a
CC       dimethylallyl moiety to the flavin N-5 and C-6 atoms and thus adding
CC       a fourth non-aromatic ring to the flavin isoalloxazine group.
DR   F9UT67, LPDB_LACPL ;  P33751, PAD1_YEAST ;  P94404, PADL_BACSU ;
DR   P69773, PADL_ECO11 ;  P69772, PADL_ECO57 ;  P69774, PADL_ECOLX ;
