ID   2.5.1.142
DE   Nerylneryl diphosphate synthase.
AN   CPT2.
CA   Dimethylallyl diphosphate + 3 isopentenyl diphosphate = 3 diphosphate +
CA   nerylneryl diphosphate.
CC   -!- Isolated from the plant Solanum lycopersicum (tomato).
//
ID   2.5.1.143
DE   Pyridinium-3,5-biscarboxylic acid mononucleotide synthase.
AN   NaAD carboxylase/hydrolase.
AN   Nicotinic acid adenine dinucleotide carboxylase/hydrolase.
AN   P2CMN synthase.
CA   Deamido-NAD(+) + hydrogencarbonate = AMP + pyridinium-3,5-biscarboxylate
CA   mononucleotide.
CC   -!- This enzyme, found in the bacterium Lactobacillus plantarum,
CC       is involved in the biosynthesis of a nickel-pincer cofactor.
CC   -!- It carboxylates the pyridinium ring of deamido-NAD(+) and cleaves the
CC       phosphoanhydride bond to release AMP and generate pyridinium-3,5-
CC       biscarboxylic acid mononucleotide (P2CMN).
//
ID   2.5.1.144
DE   S-sulfo-L-cysteine synthase (O-acetyl-L-serine-dependent).
AN   Cysteine synthase B.
CA   O-acetyl-L-serine + thiosulfate = S-sulfo-L-cysteine + acetate.
CC   -!- In plants, the activity is catalyzed by a chloroplastic enzyme that
CC       plays an important role in chloroplast function and is essential for
CC       light-dependent redox regulation within the chloroplast.
CC   -!- The bacterial enzyme also catalyzes the activity of EC 2.5.1.47.
CC   -!- Cf. EC 2.8.5.1.
//
ID   2.5.1.145
DE   Phosphatidylglycerol--prolipoprotein diacylglyceryl transferase.
CA   L-1-phosphatidyl-sn-glycerol + a [prolipoprotein]-L-cysteine =
CA   sn-glycerol 1-phosphate + an [prolipoprotein]-S-1,2-diacyl-sn-glyceryl-L-
CA   cysteine.
CC   -!- This bacterial enzyme, which is associated with the membrane,
CC       catalyzes the transfer of an sn-1,2-diacylglyceryl group from
CC       phosphatidylglycerol to the sulfhydryl group of the prospective
CC       N-terminal cysteine of a prolipoprotein, the first step in the
CC       formation of mature triacylated lipoproteins.
//
ID   2.5.1.146
DE   3-geranyl-3-((Z)-2-isocyanoethenyl)indole synthase.
CA   Geranyl diphosphate + 3-((Z)-2-isocyanoethenyl)-1H-indole = 3-geranyl-3-
CA   ((Z)-2-isocyanoethenyl)-1H-indole + diphosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the cyanobacterium Fischerella ambigua
CC       UTEX 1903, participates in the biosynthesis of hapalindole-type
CC       alkaloids.
//
ID   2.5.1.147
DE   5-amino-6-(D-ribitylamino)uracil--L-tyrosine 4-hydroxyphenyl transferase.
CA   5-amino-6-(D-ribitylamino)uracil + L-tyrosine + S-adenosyl-L-methionine =
CA   5-amino-5-(4-hydroxybenzyl)-6-(D-ribitylimino)-5,6-dihydrouracil +
CA   2-iminoacetate + L-methionine + 5'-deoxyadenosine.
CF   Iron-sulfur.
CC   -!- The enzyme is involved in the production of 7,8-didemethyl-8-hydroxy-
CC       5-deazariboflavin (FO), the precursor of the redox cofactor coenzyme
CC       F420, which is found in methanogens and in various actinobacteria.
CC   -!- FO is also produced by some cyanobacteria and eukaryotes.
CC   -!- The enzyme, which forms a complex with EC 4.3.1.32 is a radical SAM
CC       enzyme that uses the 5'-deoxyadenosyl radical to initiate the
CC       reaction.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 2.5.1.77.
