//
ID   2.6.1.4
DE   Glycine transaminase.
AN   Glycine aminotransferase.
CA   Glycine + 2-oxoglutarate = glyoxylate + L-glutamate.
CF   Pyridoxal 5'-phosphate.
DR   Q9LR30, GGT1_ARATH ;  Q9S7E9, GGT2_ARATH ;
//
ID   2.6.1.5
DE   Tyrosine transaminase.
AN   TyrAT.
AN   Tyrosine aminotransferase.
CA   L-tyrosine + 2-oxoglutarate = 4-hydroxyphenylpyruvate + L-glutamate.
CF   Pyridoxal 5'-phosphate.
CC   -!- L-phenylalanine can act instead of L-tyrosine.
CC   -!- The mitochondrial enzyme may be identical with EC 2.6.1.1.
CC   -!- The three isoenzymic forms are interconverted by EC 3.4.22.32 and
CC       EC 3.4.22.33.
CC   -!- The enzyme can also catalyze the final step in the methionine-salvage
CC       pathway of Klebsiella pneumoniae.
PR   PROSITE; PDOC00098;
DR   F8P1W6, AMT1_SERL9 ;  B7STY2, ATRD_TAPPA ;  Q58CZ9, ATTY_BOVIN ;
DR   Q54K95, ATTY_DICDI ;  P17735, ATTY_HUMAN ;  Q8QZR1, ATTY_MOUSE ;
DR   P04694, ATTY_RAT   ;  Q02636, ATTY_RHIME ;  P33447, ATTY_TRYCR ;
DR   Q9C969, ISS1_ARATH ;  Q9LVY1, TAT_ARATH  ;  O85746, TYRB_KLEPN ;
//
ID   2.6.1.6
DE   Leucine transaminase.
AN   Leucine aminotransferase.
CA   L-leucine + 2-oxoglutarate = 4-methyl-2-oxopentanoate + L-glutamate.
CF   Pyridoxal 5'-phosphate.
CC   -!- Differs from EC 2.6.1.42 in that it does not act on L-valine or
CC       L-isoleucine, although it does act on L-methionine.
//
ID   2.6.1.7
DE   Kynurenine--oxoglutarate transaminase.
AN   Kynurenine aminotransferase.
AN   Kynurenine--oxoglutarate aminotransferase.
CA   L-kynurenine + 2-oxoglutarate = 4-(2-aminophenyl)-2,4-dioxobutanoate +
CA   L-glutamate.
CF   Pyridoxal 5'-phosphate.
CC   -!- Also acts on 3-hydroxykynurenine.
CC   -!- The product 4-(2-aminophenyl)-2,4-dioxobutanoate is converted into
CC       kynurenate by a spontaneous reaction.
DR   Q5E9N4, AADAT_BOVIN;  Q8N5Z0, AADAT_HUMAN;  Q9WVM8, AADAT_MOUSE;
