CC       pyridoxal 5'-phosphate in E.coli (using reaction 2 above).
CC   -!- In E.coli, pyridoxal 5'-phosphate is synthesized de novo by a pathway
CC       that involves EC 1.2.1.72, EC 1.1.1.290, EC 2.6.1.52, EC 1.1.1.262,
CC       EC 2.6.99.2 and EC 1.4.3.5 (with pyridoxine 5'-phosphate as
CC       substrate).
CC   -!- Pyridoxal phosphate is the cofactor for both activities and therefore
CC       seems to be involved in its own biosynthesis.
CC   -!- Non-phosphorylated forms of serine and threonine are not substrates.
