ID   2.6.1.77
DE   Taurine--pyruvate aminotransferase.
CA   Taurine + pyruvate = L-alanine + 2-sulfoacetaldehyde.
CF   Pyridoxal 5'-phosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme from Bilophila wadsworthia catalyzes a reversible reaction
CC       that starts an anaerobic taurine degradation pathway.
CC   -!- beta-alanine is also a significant amino group donor.
CC   -!- The enzyme from the bacterium Pseudomonas denitrificans PD1222 can
CC       also use hypotaurine, producing 2-sulfinoacetaldehyde, which
CC       spontaneously hydrolyzes to sulfite and acetaldehyde.
CC   -!- Unlike EC 2.6.1.55, 2-oxoglutarate cannot serve as an acceptor for
CC       the amino group.
PR   PROSITE; PDOC00519;
DR   Q9APM5, TPA_BILWA  ;  D5AKY0, TPA_RHOCB  ;
//
ID   2.6.1.78
DE   Aspartate--prephenate aminotransferase.
AN   L-aspartate:prephenate aminotransferase.
AN   PAT.
AN   Prephenate aspartate aminotransferase.
AN   Prephenate transaminase.
CA   L-arogenate + oxaloacetate = prephenate + L-aspartate.
CF   Pyridoxal 5'-phosphate.
CC   -!- Glutamate can also act as the amino donor, but more slowly (cf.
CC       EC 2.6.1.79).
DR   Q9SIE1, PAT_ARATH  ;  E9L7A5, PAT_PETHY  ;
//
ID   2.6.1.79
DE   Glutamate--prephenate aminotransferase.
AN   L-glutamate:prephenate aminotransferase.
AN   PAT.
AN   Prephenate transaminase.
CA   L-arogenate + 2-oxoglutarate = prephenate + L-glutamate.
CF   Pyridoxal 5'-phosphate.
CC   -!- Aspartate can also act as the amino donor, but more slowly (cf.
CC       EC 2.6.1.78).
CC   -!- The enzyme from higher plants shows a marked preference for
CC       prephenate as substrate compared to pyruvate, phenylpyruvate or
CC       4-hydroxyphenylpyruvate.
DR   Q9SIE1, PAT_ARATH  ;  E9L7A5, PAT_PETHY  ;
//
ID   2.6.1.80
DE   Nicotianamine aminotransferase.
AN   NAAT.
AN   NAAT-I.
AN   NAAT-II.
AN   NAAT-III.
AN   Nicotianamine transaminase.
CA   Nicotianamine + 2-oxoglutarate = 3''-deamino-3''-oxonicotianamine +
CA   L-glutamate.
CF   Pyridoxal 5'-phosphate.
CC   -!- This enzyme is produced by grasses.
CC   -!- They secrete both the nicotianamine and the transaminated product
CC       into the soil around them.
CC   -!- Both compounds chelate Fe(2+) and Fe(3+); these chelators, called
CC       mugineic acid family phytosiderophores, are taken up by the grass,
CC       which is thereby supplied with iron.
DR   Q9ST02, NAATA_HORVU;  Q9ST03, NAATB_HORVU;
//
ID   2.6.1.81
DE   Succinylornithine transaminase.
AN   N(2)-succinylornithine 5-aminotransferase.
AN   SOAT.
AN   Succinylornithine aminotransferase.
CA   N(2)-succinyl-L-ornithine + 2-oxoglutarate = N-succinyl-L-glutamate
CA   5-semialdehyde + L-glutamate.
CF   Pyridoxal 5'-phosphate.
CC   -!- Also acts on N(2)-acetyl-L-ornithine and L-ornithine, but more
CC       slowly.
CC   -!- In Pseudomonas aeruginosa, the arginine-inducible succinylornithine
CC       transaminase, EC 2.6.1.11 and EC 2.6.1.13 activities are catalyzed by
CC       the same enzyme, but this is not the case in all species.
CC   -!- This is the third enzyme in the arginine succinyltransferase (AST)
CC       pathway for the catabolism of arginine.
CC   -!- This pathway converts the carbon skeleton of arginine into glutamate,
CC       with the concomitant production of ammonia and conversion of
CC       succinyl-CoA into succinate and CoA.
CC   -!- The five enzymes involved in this pathway are EC 2.3.1.109,
CC       EC 3.5.3.23, EC 2.6.1.81, EC 1.2.1.71 and EC 3.5.1.96.
