ID   2.6.1.84
DE   Arginine--pyruvate transaminase.
AN   Arginine:pyruvate transaminase.
CA   L-arginine + pyruvate = 5-guanidino-2-oxopentanoate + L-alanine.
CF   Pyridoxal 5'-phosphate.
CC   -!- While L-arginine is the best substrate, the enzyme exhibits broad
CC       substrate specificity, with L-lysine, L-methionine, L-leucine,
CC       L-ornithine and L-glutamine also able to act as substrates, but more
CC       slowly.
CC   -!- Pyruvate cannot be replaced by 2-oxoglutarate as amino-group
CC       acceptor.
CC   -!- This is the first catalytic enzyme of the arginine transaminase
CC       pathway for L-arginine utilization in Pseudomonas aeruginosa.
CC   -!- This pathway is only used when the major route of arginine
CC       catabolism, i.e. the arginine succinyltransferase pathway,
CC       is blocked.
DR   Q9HUI9, ARUH_PSEAE ;
//
ID   2.6.1.85
DE   Aminodeoxychorismate synthase.
AN   4-amino-4-deoxychorismate synthase.
AN   ADC synthase.
CA   Chorismate + L-glutamine = 4-amino-4-deoxychorismate + L-glutamate.
CF   Mg(2+).
CC   -!- Composed of two subunits, PabA and PabB.
CC   -!- In the absence of PabA and glutamine, PabB converts ammonia and
CC       chorismate into 4-amino-4-deoxychorismate.
CC   -!- PabA converts glutamine into glutamate only in the presence of
CC       stoichiometric amounts of PabB.
CC   -!- Coupled with EC 4.1.3.38, to form 4-aminobenzoate.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 6.3.5.8.
