CC       or O-6.
//
ID   2.7.1.62
DE   Phosphoramidate--hexose phosphotransferase.
CA   Phosphoramidate + D-hexose = NH(3) + alpha-D-hexose 1-phosphate.
CC   -!- Activity is observed with several hexoses; of these glucose is the
CC       best substrate and the product from it is alpha-D-glucose
CC       1-phosphate.
CC   -!- The phosphoramidate donor can be replaced by N-phosphoglycine and by
CC       an N-phosphohistidine.
CC   -!- May be identical with EC 3.1.3.9.
//
ID   2.7.1.63
DE   Polyphosphate--glucose phosphotransferase.
AN   Polyphosphate glucokinase.
CA   (Phosphate)(n) + D-glucose = (phosphate)(n-1) + D-glucose 6-phosphate.
CC   -!- Requires a neutral salt, e.g. KCl, for maximum activity.
CC   -!- Also acts on glucosamine.
