ID   2.7.1.171
DE   Protein-fructosamine 3-kinase.
AN   Fructosamine 3-kinase.
CA   ATP + [protein]-N(6)-D-fructosyl-L-lysine = ADP + [protein]-N(6)-(3-O-
CA   phospho-D-fructosyl)-L-lysine.
CC   -!- Nonenzymatic glycation is an important factor in the pathogenesis of
CC       diabetic complications.
CC   -!- Key early intermediates in this process are fructosamines, such as
CC       [protein]-N(6)-D-fructosyl-L-lysine.
CC   -!- Fructosamine-3-kinase is part of an ATP-dependent system for removing
CC       carbohydrates from nonenzymatically glycated proteins.
CC   -!- The phosphorylation destablilizes the [protein]-N(6)-D-fructosyl-L-
CC       lysine adduct and leads to its spontaneous decomposition.
CC   -!- Cf. EC 2.7.1.172.
//
ID   2.7.1.172
DE   Protein-ribulosamine 3-kinase.
AN   FN3K-related protein.
AN   Ribulosamine 3-kinase.
AN   Ribulosamine/erythrulosamine 3-kinase.
CA   ATP + [protein]-N(6)-D-ribulosyl-L-lysine = ADP + [protein]-N(6)-(3-O-
CA   phospho-D-ribulosyl)-L-lysine.
CC   -!- This enzyme plays a role in freeing proteins from ribulosamines or
CC       psicosamines, which might arise from the reaction of amines with
CC       glucose and/or glycolytic intermediates.
CC   -!- This role is shared by EC 2.7.1.171, which has, in addition,
CC       the unique capacity to phosphorylate fructosamines.
CC   -!- The plant enzyme also phosphorylates [protein]-N(6)-D-erythrulosyl-L-
CC       lysine.
CC   -!- No activity with [protein]-N(6)-D-fructosyl-L-lysine.
DR   Q9LEW8, FN3KR_ARATH;  A2XBT1, FN3KR_ORYSI;  Q10SM2, FN3KR_ORYSJ;
//
ID   2.7.1.173
DE   Nicotinate riboside kinase.
AN   Ribosylnicotinic acid kinase.
CA   ATP + beta-D-ribosylnicotinate = ADP + nicotinate beta-D-ribonucleotide.
CC   -!- The enzyme from yeast and human also has the activity of EC 2.7.1.22.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 2.7.1.n4.
DR   P62511, NRK1_ASHGO ;  Q9NWW6, NRK1_HUMAN ;  Q91W63, NRK1_MOUSE ;
DR   Q6AY91, NRK1_RAT   ;  Q9C0W1, NRK1_SCHPO ;  P53915, NRK1_YEAST ;
DR   Q9NPI5, NRK2_HUMAN ;  Q9D7C9, NRK2_MOUSE ;
//
ID   2.7.1.174
DE   Diacylglycerol kinase (CTP).
AN   CTP-dependent diacylglycerol kinase.
AN   DAG kinase.
AN   Diacylglycerol kinase (CTP dependent).
AN   Diglyceride kinase.
CA   CTP + 1,2-diacyl-sn-glycerol = CDP + 1,2-diacyl-sn-glycerol 3-phosphate.
CF   Mg(2+) or Ca(2+).
CC   -!- Involved in synthesis of membrane phospholipids and the neutral lipid
CC       triacylglycerol.
CC   -!- Unlike the diacylglycerol kinases from bacteria, plants, and animals
CC       (cf. EC 2.7.1.107), the enzyme from Saccharomyces cerevisiae utilizes
CC       CTP.
CC   -!- The enzyme can also use dCTP, but not ATP, GTP or UTP.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 2.7.1.n5.
DR   Q753I3, DGK1_ASHGO ;  P87170, DGK1_SCHPO ;  Q12382, DGK1_YEAST ;
//
ID   2.7.1.175
DE   Maltokinase.
CA   ATP + maltose = ADP + alpha-maltose 1-phosphate.
CF   Mg(2+).
CC   -!- Formerly EC 2.7.1.n8.
