ID   2.7.1.176
DE   UDP-N-acetylglucosamine kinase.
AN   UNAG kinase.
CA   ATP + UDP-N-acetyl-alpha-D-glucosamine = ADP + UDP-N-acetyl-alpha-D-
CA   glucosamine 3'-phosphate.
CC   -!- Toxic component of a toxin-antitoxin (TA) module.
CC   -!- The phosphorylation of UDP-N-acetyl-alpha-D-glucosamine results in
CC       the inhibition of EC 2.5.1.7, which is then blocked.
CC   -!- Phosphorylation is inhibited by cognate epsilon antitoxin.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 2.7.1.n7.
DR   Q97QZ1, PEZT_STRPN ;  P0A4M1, ZTOX_ENTFL ;  Q93CM1, ZTOX_ENTHR ;
DR   P0A4M2, ZTOX_STRAG ;  Q54944, ZTOX_STRPY ;
//
ID   2.7.1.177
DE   L-threonine kinase.
CA   ATP + L-threonine = ADP + O-phospho-L-threonine.
CC   -!- The enzyme is involved in the de novo synthesis of adenosylcobalamin.
CC   -!- It is specific for ATP and free L-threonine.
CC   -!- In the bacterium Salmonella enterica the activity with CTP, GTP,
CC       or UTP is 6, 11, and 3% of the activity with ATP.
DR   Q9XDM4, PDUX_SALTY ;
//
ID   2.7.1.178
DE   2-dehydro-3-deoxyglucono/galactono-kinase.
AN   2-keto-3-deoxy-D-gluconate kinase.
AN   KDG kinase.
CA   (1) ATP + 2-dehydro-3-deoxy-D-gluconate = ADP + 2-dehydro-3-deoxy-6-
CA   phospho-D-gluconate.
CA   (2) ATP + 2-dehydro-3-deoxy-D-galactonate = ADP + 2-dehydro-3-deoxy-6-
CA   phospho-D-galactonate.
CC   -!- The enzyme from the archaeon Sulfolobus solfataricus is involved in
CC       glucose and galactose catabolism via the branched variant of the
CC       Entner-Doudoroff pathway.
CC   -!- It phosphorylates 2-dehydro-3-deoxy-D-gluconate and 2-dehydro-3-
CC       deoxy-D-galactonate with similar catalytic efficiency.
CC   -!- Cf. EC 2.7.1.45 and EC 2.7.1.58.
DR   Q97U29, KDGK_SULSO ;
//
ID   2.7.1.179
DE   Kanosamine kinase.
CA   ATP + kanosamine = ADP + kanosamine 6-phosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme from the bacterium Amycolatopsis mediterranei is specific
CC       for kanosamine.
DR   G0FS68, RIFN_AMYMS ;
//
ID   2.7.1.180
DE   FAD:protein FMN transferase.
AN   Flavin transferase.
CA   FAD + [protein]-L-threonine = [protein]-FMN-L-threonine + AMP.
CF   Mg(2+).
CC   -!- The enzyme catalyzes the transfer of the FMN portion of FAD and its
CC       covalent binding to the hydroxyl group of an L-threonine residue in a
CC       target flavin-binding protein such as the B and C subunits of
CC       EC 1.6.5.8.
DR   B5XP00, APBE1_KLEP3;  B5XRA9, APBE2_KLEP3;  Q52718, APBEF_RHOCA;
DR   O85292, APBE_BUCAP ;  Q89AP6, APBE_BUCBP ;  Q9PKW2, APBE_CHLMU ;
DR   Q9Z8K2, APBE_CHLPN ;  O84080, APBE_CHLTR ;  P0AB86, APBE_ECO57 ;
DR   P0AB85, APBE_ECOLI ;  P44550, APBE_HAEIN ;  P41780, APBE_SALTY ;
DR   O83774, APBE_TREPA ;  A5F5Y3, APBE_VIBC3 ;
