ID   2.7.1.181
DE   Polymannosyl GlcNAc-diphospho-ditrans,octacis-undecaprenol kinase.
CA   ATP + alpha-D-Man-(1->2)-alpha-D-Man-(1->2)-(alpha-D-Man-(1->3)-alpha-D-
CA   Man-(1->3)-alpha-D-Man-(1->2)-alpha-D-Man-(1->2))(n)-alpha-D-Man-(1->3)-
CA   alpha-D-Man-(1->3)-alpha-D-Man-(1->3)-alpha-D-GlcNAc-diphospho-
CA   ditrans,octacis-undecaprenol = ADP + 3-O-phospho-alpha-D-Man-(1->2)-
CA   alpha-D-Man-(1->2)-(alpha-D-Man-(1->3)-alpha-D-Man-(1->3)-alpha-D-Man-
CA   (1->2)-alpha-D-Man-(1->2))(n)-alpha-D-Man-(1->3)-alpha-D-Man-(1->3)-
CA   alpha-D-Man-(1->3)-alpha-D-GlcNAc-diphospho-ditrans,octacis-undecaprenol.
CC   -!- The enzyme is involved in the biosynthesis of the polymannose
CC       O-polysaccharide in the outer leaflet of the membrane of Escherichia
CC       coli serotype O9a.
CC   -!- O-polysaccharide structures vary extensively because of differences
CC       in the number and type of sugars in the repeat unit.
CC   -!- The dual kinase/methylase WbdD also catalyzes the methylation of
CC       3-phospho-alpha-D-Man-(1->2)-alpha-D-Man-(1->2)-(alpha-D-Man-(1->3)-
CC       alpha-D-Man-(1->3)-alpha-D-Man-(1->2)-alpha-D-Man-(1->2))(n)-alpha-D-
CC       Man-(1->3)-alpha-D-Man-(1->3)-alpha-D-Man-(1->3)-alpha-D-GlcNAc-
CC       diphospho-ditrans,octacis-undecaprenol (Cf. EC 2.1.1.294).
DR   Q47592, WBDD2_ECOLX;  J7I4B7, WBDD_ECOLX ;
//
ID   2.7.1.182
DE   Phytol kinase.
CA   CTP + phytol = CDP + phytyl phosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme is found in plants and photosynthetic algae and is
CC       involved in phytol salvage.
CC   -!- It can use UTP as an alternative phosphate donor with lower activity.
DR   Q9LZ76, PHYK1_ARATH;  Q7XR51, PHYK1_ORYSJ;  Q2N2K1, PHYK1_SOYBN;
DR   Q5N9J9, PHYK2_ORYSJ;  Q2N2K2, PHYK2_SOYBN;  Q2N2K0, PHYK3_SOYBN;
DR   Q2N2K4, PHYK_MAIZE ;  P74653, PHYK_SYNY3 ;  Q2N2K3, PHYK_WHEAT ;
//
ID   2.7.1.183
DE   Glycoprotein-mannosyl O(6)-kinase.
AN   Protein O-mannose kinase.
CA   ATP + O(3)-(N-acetyl-beta-D-galactosaminyl-(1->3)-N-acetyl-beta-D-
CA   glucosaminyl-(1->4)-alpha-D-mannosyl)-L-threonyl/L-seryl-[protein] =
CA   ADP + O(3)-(N-acetyl-beta-D-galactosaminyl-(1->3)-N-acetyl-beta-D-
CA   glucosaminyl-(1->4)-alpha-D-(6-phospho)mannosyl)-L-threonyl/L-seryl-
CA   [protein].
CC   -!- In humans this phosphorylated trisaccharide is attached to an
CC       L-threonine residue of alpha-dystroglycan, an extracellular
CC       peripheral glycoprotein that acts as a receptor for extracellular
CC       matrix proteins containing laminin-G domains, and is important for
CC       its activity.
DR   Q5F349, SG196_CHICK;  Q5U3W1, SG196_DANRE;  Q9H5K3, SG196_HUMAN;
DR   Q95JJ0, SG196_MACFA;  Q3TUA9, SG196_MOUSE;  Q4V8A9, SG196_RAT  ;
DR   Q5HZP7, SG196_XENLA;
//
ID   2.7.1.184
DE   Sulfofructose kinase.
CA   ATP + 6-deoxy-6-sulfo-D-fructose = ADP + 6-deoxy-6-sulfo-D-fructose
CA   1-phosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Escherichia coli,
CC       is involved in the degradation pathway of sulfoquinovose, the polar
CC       headgroup of sulfolipids found in the photosynthetic membranes of all
CC       higher plants, mosses, ferns, algae, and most photosynthetic
CC       bacteria, as well as the surface layer of some archaea.
DR   P32143, SQUV_ECOLI ;
//
ID   2.7.1.185
DE   Mevalonate 3-kinase.
CA   ATP + (R)-mevalonate = ADP + (R)-3-phosphomevalonate.
CC   -!- Mevalonate 3-kinase and EC 2.7.1.186 act sequentially in an alternate
CC       mevalonate pathway in the archaeon Thermoplasma acidophilum.
CC   -!- Mevalonate 3-kinase is different from EC 2.7.1.36, which transfers
CC       phosphate to position 5 of (R)-mevalonate and is part of the
CC       classical mevalonate pathway in eukaryotes and archaea.
DR   Q6KZB1, MV3K_PICTO ;  Q9HIN1, MV3K_THEAC ;
//
ID   2.7.1.186
DE   Mevalonate-3-phosphate 5-kinase.
CA   ATP + (R)-3-phosphomevalonate = ADP + 3,5-diphosphomevalonate.
DR   Q9HK44, MVP5K_THEAC;
//
ID   2.7.1.187
