ID   2.7.1.212
DE   Alpha-D-ribose-1-phosphate 5-kinase (ADP).
CA   ADP + alpha-D-ribose-1-phosphate = AMP + alpha-D-ribose 1,5-bisphosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the archaeon Thermococcus
CC       kodakarensis, participates in an archaeal pathway for nucleoside
CC       degradation.
DR   Q5JDG9, R1PK_THEKO ;
//
ID   2.7.1.213
DE   Cytidine kinase.
CA   ATP + cytidine = ADP + CMP.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the archaeon Thermococcus
CC       kodakarensis, participates in a pathway for nucleoside degradation.
CC   -!- The enzyme can also act on deoxycytidine and uridine, but unlike
CC       EC 2.7.1.48 it is most active with cytidine.
DR   Q5JEK6, CYDK_THEKO ;  Q57849, NK_METJA   ;  Q9HJT3, NK_THEAC   ;
//
ID   2.7.1.214
DE   C(7)-cyclitol 7-kinase.
CA   (1) ATP + valienone = ADP + valienone 7-phosphate.
CA   (2) ATP + validone = ADP + validone 7-phosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Streptomyces
CC       hygroscopicus var. jinggangensis, is involved in the biosynthesis of
CC       the antifungal agent validamycin A.
DR   Q3T6E2, VALC_STRHJ ;  Q15JG5, VLDC_STRHL ;
//
ID   2.7.1.215
DE   Erythritol kinase (D-erythritol 1-phosphate-forming).
CA   ATP + erythritol = ADP + D-erythritol 1-phosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the pathogenic bacterium Brucella
CC       abortus, which causes brucellosis in livestock, participates in
CC       erythritol catabolism.
CC   -!- Cf. EC 2.7.1.27.
DR   Q2YIQ1, ERYA_BRUA2 ;
//
ID   2.7.1.216
DE   Farnesol kinase.
CA   CTP + (2E,6E)-farnesol = CDP + (2E,6E)-farnesyl phosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme, found in plants and animals, can also use other
CC       nucleotide triphosphates as phosphate donor, albeit less efficiently.
CC   -!- The plant enzyme can also use geraniol and geranylgeraniol as
CC       substrates with lower activity, but not farnesyl phosphate (cf.
CC       EC 2.7.4.32).
DR   Q67ZM7, FOLK_ARATH ;
//
