ID   2.7.2.1
DE   Acetate kinase.
AN   Acetate kinase (phosphorylating).
AN   Acetic kinase.
AN   Acetokinase.
AN   AK.
CA   ATP + acetate = ADP + acetyl phosphate.
CF   Mg(2+).
CC   -!- While purified enzyme from Escherichia coli is specific for acetate,
CC       others have found that the enzyme can also use propanoate as a
CC       substrate, but more slowly.
CC   -!- Acetate can be converted into the key metabolic intermediate acetyl-
CC       CoA by coupling acetate kinase with EC 2.3.1.8.
CC   -!- Both this enzyme and EC 2.7.2.15 play important roles in the
CC       production of propanoate.
PR   PROSITE; PDOC00826;
