ID   2.7.3.7
DE   Opheline kinase.
CA   ATP + guanidinoethyl methyl phosphate = ADP +
CA   N'-phosphoguanidinoethyl methylphosphate.
CC   -!- Has a little activity on taurocyamine, lombricine and
CC       phosphotaurocyamine.
//
ID   2.7.3.8
DE   Ammonia kinase.
CA   ATP + NH(3) = ADP + phosphoramide.
CC   -!- Has a wide specificity.
CC   -!- In the reverse direction, N-phosphoglycine and N-phosphohistidine can
CC       also act as phosphate donors, and ADP, dADP, GDP, CDP, dTDP, dCDP,
CC       IDP and UDP can act as phosphate acceptors (in decreasing order of
CC       activity).
