ID   2.7.4.25
DE   (d)CMP kinase.
AN   dCMP kinase.
AN   Deoxycytidine monophosphokinase.
AN   Deoxycytidylate kinase.
CA   ATP + (d)CMP = ADP + (d)CDP.
CC   -!- The prokaryotic cytidine monophosphate kinase specifically
CC       phosphorylates CMP (or dCMP), using ATP as the preferred phosphoryl
CC       donor.
CC   -!- Unlike EC 2.7.4.14, a eukaryotic enzyme that phosphorylates UMP and
CC       CMP with similar efficiency, the prokaryotic enzyme phosphorylates
CC       UMP with very low rates, and this function is catalyzed in
CC       prokaryotes by EC 2.7.4.22.
CC   -!- The enzyme phosphorylates dCMP nearly as well as it does CMP.
