CC       triphosphate.
//
ID   2.7.7.46
DE   Gentamicin 2''-nucleotidyltransferase.
AN   2''-aminoglycoside nucleotidyltransferase.
CA   Nucleoside triphosphate + gentamicin = diphosphate +
CA   2''-nucleotidylgentamicin.
CC   -!- ATP, dATP, CTP, ITP and GTP can act as donors.
CC   -!- Kanamycin, tobramycin and sisomicin can also act as acceptors.
CC   -!- The nucleotidyl residue is transferred to the 2-hydroxy group of the
CC       3-amino-3-deoxy-D-glucose moiety in the antibiotic.
