ID   2.7.7.66
DE   Malonate decarboxylase holo-[acyl-carrier protein] synthase.
AN   Holo ACP synthase.
AN   Holo-malonate-decarboxylase synthase.
CA   2'-(5-triphosphoribosyl)-3'-dephospho-CoA + malonate decarboxylase apo-
CA   [acyl-carrier protein] = malonate decarboxylase holo-[acyl-carrier
CA   protein] + diphosphate.
CC   -!- The delta subunit of malonate decarboxylase serves as an an acyl-
CC       carrier protein (ACP) and contains the prosthetic group
CC       2'-(5-triphosphoribosyl)-3'-dephospho-CoA.
CC   -!- Two reactions are involved in the production of the holo-ACP form of
CC       this enzyme.
CC   -!- The first reaction is catalyzed by EC 2.4.2.52.
CC   -!- The resulting prosthetic group is then attached to the ACP subunit
CC       via a phosphodiester linkage to a serine residue, thus forming the
CC       holo form of the enzyme, in a manner analogous to that of
CC       EC 2.7.7.61.
