ID   2.7.7.73
DE   Sulfur carrier protein ThiS adenylyltransferase.
CA   ATP + [ThiS] = diphosphate + adenylyl-[ThiS].
CF   Zn(2+).
CC   -!- The enzyme catalyzes the adenylation of ThiS, a sulfur carrier
CC       protein involved in the biosynthesis of thiamine.
CC   -!- The enzyme shows significant structural similarity to ubiquitin-
CC       activating enzyme.
CC   -!- In Escherichia coli, but not in Bacillus subtilis, the enzyme forms a
CC       cross link from Cys-184 to the ThiS carboxy terminus (the position
CC       that is also thiolated) via an acyldisulfide.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 2.7.7.n3.
DR   O31619, THIF_BACSU ;  P30138, THIF_ECOLI ;  Q72J02, TTUC_THET2 ;
//
ID   2.7.7.74
DE   1L-myo-inositol 1-phosphate cytidylyltransferase.
AN   IPCT.
AN   L-myo-inositol-1-phosphate cytidylyltransferase.
CA   CTP + 1L-myo-inositol 1-phosphate = diphosphate + CDP-1L-myo-inositol.
CC   -!- In many organisms this activity is catalyzed by a bifunctional
CC       enzyme.
CC   -!- The cytidylyltransferase domain of the bifunctional
CC       EC 2.7.7.74/EC 2.7.8.34 (CTP:inositol-1-phosphate
CC       cytidylyltransferase/CDP-inositol:inositol-1-phosphate transferase)
CC       is absolutely specific for CTP and 1L-myo-inositol 1-phosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme is involved in biosynthesis of bis(1L-myo-inositol)
CC       1,3'-phosphate, a widespread organic solute in microorganisms adapted
CC       to hot environments.
CC   -!- In many organisms this activity is catalyzed by a bifunctional
CC       enzyme.
CC   -!- The cytidylyltransferase domain of the bifunctional
CC       EC 2.7.7.74/EC 2.7.8.34 is absolutely specific for CTP and 1L-myo-
CC       inositol 1-phosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme is involved in biosynthesis of bis(1L-myo-inositol)
CC       1,3'-phosphate, a widespread organic solute in microorganisms adapted
CC       to hot environments.
DR   O67379, DIPPS_AQUAE;  O29976, DIPPS_ARCFU;  Q8U1Z6, DIPPS_PYRFU;
DR   Q1AWQ0, DIPPS_RUBXD;  Q5JDA9, DIPPS_THEKO;
