ID   2.7.7.80
DE   Molybdopterin-synthase adenylyltransferase.
CA   ATP + [molybdopterin-synthase sulfur-carrier protein]-Gly-Gly =
CA   diphosphate + [molybdopterin-synthase sulfur-carrier protein]-Gly-
CA   Gly-AMP.
CC   -!- Adenylates the C-terminus of the small subunit of the molybdopterin
CC       synthase.
CC   -!- This activation is required to form the thiocarboxylated C-terminus
CC       of the active molybdopterin synthase small subunit.
CC   -!- The reaction occurs in prokaryotes and eukaryotes.
CC   -!- In the human, the reaction is catalyzed by the N-terminal domain of
CC       the protein MOCS3, which also includes a molybdopterin-synthase
CC       sulfurtransferase (EC 2.8.1.11) C-terminal domain.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 2.7.7.n4.
