//
ID   2.7.8.12
DE   Teichoic acid poly(glycerol phosphate) polymerase.
AN   Poly(glycerol phosphate) polymerase.
AN   Tag polymerase.
AN   Teichoic acid glycerol transferase.
AN   Teichoic-acid synthase.
CA   n CDP-glycerol + 4-O-((2R)-glycerophospho)-N-acetyl-beta-D-mannosaminyl-
CA   (1->4)-N-acetyl-alpha-D-glucosaminyl-diphospho-ditrans,octacis-
CA   undecaprenol = n CMP + 4-O-(((2R)-glycerophospho)n-(2R)-glycerophospho)-
CA   N-acetyl-beta-D-mannosaminyl-(1->4)-N-acetyl-alpha-D-glucosaminyl-
CA   diphospho-ditrans,octacis-undecaprenol.
CC   -!- Involved in the biosynthesis of poly glycerol phosphate teichoic
CC       acids in bacterial cell walls.
CC   -!- This enzyme adds 30-50 glycerol units to the linker molecule,
CC       but only after it has been primed with the first glycerol unit by
CC       EC 2.7.8.44.
CC   -!- Cf. EC 2.7.8.45.
DR   P13485, TAGF_BACSU ;  Q5HLM5, TAGF_STAEQ ;  Q8RKI5, TARF_BACPZ ;
//
ID   2.7.8.13
DE   Phospho-N-acetylmuramoyl-pentapeptide-transferase.
AN   MraY transferase.
AN   Phospho-MurNAc-pentapeptide transferase.
AN   Phospho-N-acetylmuramoyl pentapeptide translocase.
AN   Phospho-NAc-muramoyl-pentapeptide translocase (UMP).
AN   Phosphoacetylmuramoylpentapeptide translocase.
AN   Phosphoacetylmuramoylpentapeptidetransferase.
AN   UDP-MurNAc-Ala-gamma-DGlu-Lys-DAla-DAla:undecaprenylphosphate
AN   transferase.
AN   UDP-MurNAc-L-Ala-D-gamma-Glu-L-Lys-D-Ala-D-Ala:C(55)-isoprenoid alcohol
AN   transferase.
AN   UDP-MurNAc-pentapeptide phosphotransferase.
CA   UDP-Mur2Ac(oyl-L-Ala-gamma-D-Glu-L-Lys-D-Ala-D-Ala) + undecaprenyl
CA   phosphate = UMP + Mur2Ac(oyl-L-Ala-gamma-D-Glu-L-Lys-D-Ala-D-Ala)-
CA   diphosphoundecaprenol.
CC   -!- In Gram-negative and some Gram-positive organisms the L-lysine is
CC       replaced by meso-2,6-diaminoheptanedioate (meso-2,6-diaminopimelate,
CC       A2pm), which is combined with adjacent residues through its L-center.
CC   -!- The undecaprenol involved is ditrans,octacis-undecaprenol.
