DE   Fas-activated serine/threonine kinase.
AN   FAST.
AN   FASTK.
CA   ATP + [Fas-activated serine/threonine protein] = ADP + [Fas-activated
CA   serine/threonine phosphoprotein].
CC   -!- This enzyme is activated during Fas-mediated apoptosis.
CC   -!- Following Fas ligation, the enzyme, which is constitutively
CC       phosphorylated, is dephosphorylated, and it is the dephosphorylated
CC       form that causes phosphorylation of TIA-1, a nuclear RNA-binding
CC       protein.
CC   -!- Phosphorylation of TIA-1 precedes the onset of DNA fragmentation.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 2.7.1.37.
