ID   2.7.11.10
DE   I-kappa-B kinase.
AN   CHUK.
AN   IKBKA.
AN   IKBKB.
AN   IKK.
AN   IKK-1.
AN   IKK-2.
AN   Inhibitor of NF-kappa-B kinase.
AN   TANK-binding kinase 1.
AN   TBK1.
CA   ATP + [I-kappa-B protein] = ADP + [I-kappa-B phosphoprotein].
CC   -!- Phosphorylates I-kappa-B proteins at specific serine residues, which
CC       marks them for destruction via the ubiquitination pathway.
CC   -!- Subsequent degradation of the I-kappa-B complex (IKK) activates
CC       NF-kappa-B, a translation factor that plays an important role in
CC       inflammation, immunity, cell proliferation and apoptosis.
CC   -!- If the serine residues are replaced by threonine residues,
CC       the activity of the enzyme is decreased considerably.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 2.7.1.37.
