//
ID   2.8.1.9
DE   Molybdenum cofactor sulfurtransferase.
AN   MoCo sulfurase.
AN   MoCo sulfurtransferase.
AN   Molybdenum cofactor sulfurase.
CA   Molybdenum cofactor + L-cysteine + reduced acceptor + 2 H(+) = thio-
CA   molybdenum cofactor + L-alanine + H(2)O + oxidized acceptor.
CF   Pyridoxal 5'-phosphate.
CC   -!- Replaces the equatorial oxo ligand of the molybdenum by sulfur via an
CC       enzyme-bound persulfide.
CC   -!- The reaction occurs in prokaryotes and eukaryotes but MoCo
CC       sulfurtransferases are only found in eukaryotes.
CC   -!- In prokaryotes the reaction is catalyzed by two enzymes: EC 2.8.1.7,
CC       which is homologous to the N-terminus of eukaryotic MoCo
CC       sulfurtransferases, and a molybdo-enzyme specific chaperone which
CC       binds the MoCo and acts as an adapter protein.
