ID   2.8.1.12
DE   Molybdopterin synthase.
AN   MPT synthase.
CA   Cyclic pyranopterin phosphate + 2 [molybdopterin-synthase sulfur-carrier
CA   protein]-Gly-NH-CH(2)-C(O)SH + H(2)O = molybdopterin + 2 [molybdopterin-
CA   synthase sulfur-carrier protein].
CC   -!- Catalyzes the synthesis of molybdopterin from cyclic pyranopterin
CC       phosphate.
CC   -!- Two sulfur atoms are transferred to cyclic pyranopterin phosphate in
CC       order to form the characteristic ene-dithiol group found in the
CC       molybdenum cofactor.
CC   -!- Molybdopterin synthase consists of two large subunits forming a
CC       central dimer and two small subunits (molybdopterin-synthase sulfur-
CC       carrier proteins) that are thiocarboxylated at the C-terminus by
CC       EC 2.8.1.11, molybdopterin synthase sulfurtransferase.
CC   -!- The reaction occurs in prokaryotes and eukaryotes.
