ID   2.8.2.14
DE   Bile-salt sulfotransferase.
AN   BAST I.
AN   Bile acid sulfotransferase I.
AN   Bile acid:3'-phosphoadenosine-5'-phosphosulfate sulfotransferase.
AN   Bile salt:3'phosphoadenosine-5'-phosphosulfate:sulfotransferase.
AN   Glycolithocholate sulfotransferase.
CA   (1) 3'-phosphoadenylyl sulfate + glycolithocholate = adenosine
CA   3',5'-bisphosphate + glycolithocholate 3-sulfate.
CA   (2) 3'-phosphoadenylyl sulfate + taurolithocholate = adenosine
CA   3',5'-bisphosphate + taurolithocholate sulfate.
CC   -!- The formation of sulfate esters of bile acids is an essential step in
CC       the prevention of toxicity by monohydroxy bile acids in many species.
CC   -!- This enzyme is both a bile salt and a 3-hydroxysteroid
CC       sulfotransferase.
CC   -!- In addition to the 5-beta-bile acid glycolithocholate, deoxycholate,
CC       3-beta-hydroxy-5-cholenoate and dehydroepiandrosterone (3-beta-
CC       hydroxyandrost-5-en-17-one) also act as substrates (see also
CC       EC 2.8.2.2 and EC 2.8.2.34).
CC   -!- May be identical to EC 2.8.2.2.
