ID   2.8.5.1
DE   S-sulfo-L-cysteine synthase (3-phospho-L-serine-dependent).
CA   3-phospho-L-serine + thiosulfate = S-sulfo-L-cysteine + phosphate.
CF   Pyridoxal 5'-phosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme, which has been characterized from the bacterium
CC       Mycobacterium tuberculosis, has no activity with O-acetyl-L-serine.
CC   -!- Cf. EC 2.5.1.144.
//
ID   2.8.5.2
DE   L-cysteine S-thiosulfotransferase.
CA   (1) [SoxY protein]-L-cysteine + thiosulfate + 2 ferricytochrome c = [SoxY
CA   protein]-S-sulfosulfanyl-L-cysteine + 2 ferrocytochrome c + 2 H(+).
CA   (2) [SoxY protein]-S-sulfanyl-L-cysteine + thiosulfate +
CA   2 ferricytochrome c = [SoxY protein]-S-(2-sulfodisulfanyl)-L-cysteine +
CA   2 ferrocytochrome c + 2 H(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme is part of the Sox enzyme system, which participates in a
CC       bacterial thiosulfate oxidation pathway that produces sulfate.
CC   -!- It catalyzes two reactions in the pathway - early in the pathway it
CC       attaches a thiosulfate molecule to the sulfur atom of an L-cysteine
CC       of a SoxY protein; later it transfers a second thiosulfate molecule
CC       to a sulfane group that is already attached to the same cysteine
CC       residue.
