DE   L-seryl-tRNA(Sec) selenium transferase.
AN   Cysteinyl-tRNA(Sec)-selenium transferase.
AN   Cysteinyl-tRNA(Sel)-selenium transferase.
AN   L-selenocysteinyl-tRNA(Sec) synthase.
AN   L-selenocysteinyl-tRNA(Sel) synthase.
AN   Selenocysteine synthase.
CA   L-seryl-tRNA(Sec) + selenophosphate = L-selenocysteinyl-tRNA(Sec) +
CA   phosphate.
CF   Pyridoxal 5'-phosphate.
CC   -!- Recognizes specifically tRNA(Sec)-species.
CC   -!- Binding of tRNA(Sec) also occurs in the absence of the seryl group.
CC   -!- 2-aminoacryloyl-tRNA, bound to the enzyme as an imine with the
CC       pyridoxal phosphate, is an intermediate in the reaction.
CC   -!- Since the selenium atom replaces oxygen in serine, the product may
CC       also be referred to as L-selenoseryl-tRNA(Sel).
CC   -!- The abbreviation Sel has also been used for selenocysteine but Sec is
CC       preferred.
