//
ID   3.1.1.97
DE   Methylated diphthine methylhydrolase.
AN   Diphthine methylesterase.
CA   Diphthine methyl ester-[translation elongation factor 2] + H(2)O =
CA   diphthine-[translation elongation factor 2] + methanol.
CC   -!- The protein is only present in eukaryotes.
DR   Q55C80, DPH7_DICDI ;  Q9BTV6, DPH7_HUMAN ;  Q9CYU6, DPH7_MOUSE ;
DR   O74865, DPH7_SCHPO ;  P38332, DPH7_YEAST ;
//
ID   3.1.1.98
DE   [Wnt protein] O-palmitoleoyl-L-serine hydrolase.
AN   Notum.
CA   [Wnt]-O-(9Z)-hexadec-9-enoyl-L-serine + H(2)O = [Wnt]-L-serine + (9Z)-
CA   hexadec-9-enoate.
CC   -!- The enzyme removes the palmitoleate modification that is introduced
CC       to specific L-serine residues in Wnt proteins by EC 2.3.1.250.
DR   C5H5C4, NOT1A_DANRE;  A0A0D3QS98, NOT1P_XENLA;  A0A0D3QS99, NOT1_XENLA ;
DR   A0A0D3QS97, NOTU2_XENLA;  Q9VUX3, NOTUM_DROME;  Q6P988, NOTUM_HUMAN;
DR   Q8R116, NOTUM_MOUSE;  F8U830, NOTUM_SCHMD;
//
ID   3.1.1.99
DE   6-deoxy-6-sulfogluconolactonase.
AN   SGL lactonase.
CA   6-deoxy-6-sulfo-D-glucono-1,5-lactone + H(2)O = 6-deoxy-6-sulfo-D-
CA   gluconate.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Pseudomonas putida SQ1,
CC       participates in a sulfoquinovose degradation pathway.
DR   P0DOV6, SGL_PSEPU  ;
//
ID   3.1.1.100
DE   Chlorophyllide a hydrolase.
AN   BciC (gene name).
CA   Chlorophyllide a + H(2)O = 8-ethyl-12-methyl-3-vinyl-
CA   bacteriochlorophyllide d + methanol + CO(2).
CC   -!- This enzyme, found in green sulfur bacteria (Chlorobiaceae) and green
CC       filamentous bacteria (Chloroflexaceae), catalyzes the first committed
CC       step in the biosynthesis of bacteriochlorophylls c, d and e,
CC       the removal of the C-13(2)-methylcarboxyl group from chlorophyllide
CC       a.
CC   -!- The reaction is very similar to the conversion of pheophorbide a to
CC       pyropheophorbide a during chlorophyll a degradation, which is
CC       catalyzed by EC 3.1.1.82.
//
ID   3.1.1.101
DE   Poly(ethylene terephthalate) hydrolase.
AN   PET hydrolase.
AN   PETase.
CA   (Ethylene terephthalate)(n) + H(2)O = (ethylene terephthalate)(n-1) +
CA   ethylene terephthalate.
CC   -!- The enzyme, isolated from the bacterium Ideonella sakaiensis, also
CC       produces small amounts of terephthalate (cf. EC 3.1.1.102).
CC   -!- The reaction takes place on PET-film placed in solution.
DR   A0A0K8P6T7, PETH_IDESA ;
//
ID   3.1.1.102
DE   Mono(ethylene terephthalate) hydrolase.
AN   MHET hydrolase.
AN   MHETase.
CA   Ethylene terephthalate + H(2)O = terephthalate + ethylene glycol.
CC   -!- The enzyme, isolated from the bacterium Ideonella sakaiensis, has no
CC       activity with poly(ethylene terephthalate) PET (cf. EC 3.1.1.101).
DR   A0A0K8P8E7, MHETH_IDESA;
//
ID   3.1.1.103
DE   Teichoic acid D-alanine hydrolase.
CA   ((4-D-Ala)-(2-GlcNAc)-Rib-ol-P)(n)-(Gro-P)(m)-ManNAc-GlcNAc-
CA   PP-peptidoglycan + n H(2)O = ((2-GlcNAc)-Rib-ol-P)(n)-(Gro-P)(m)-ManNAc-
CA   GlcNAc-PP-peptidoglycan + n D-alanine.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Staphylococcus aureus,
CC       removes D-alanine groups from the teichoic acid produced by this
CC       organism, thus modulating the electrical charge of the bacterial
CC       surface.
CC   -!- The activity greatly increases methicillin resistance in MRSA
CC       strains.
//
ID   3.1.1.n1
DE   Transferred entry: 3.5.1.103.
//
ID   3.1.1.n2
DE   Protein-S-isoprenylcysteine alpha-carbonyl methylesterase.
AN   Isoprenylcysteine methylesterase.
AN   Prenylcysteine methylesterase.
CA   Protein C-terminal S-farnesyl-L-cysteine methyl ester + H(2)O = protein
CA   C-terminal S-farnesyl-L-cysteine + methanol.
DR   Q94AS5, ICME_ARATH ;  Q8VYP9, ICML1_ARATH;  Q1PET6, ICML2_ARATH;
DR   Q6L5F5, IMCE_ORYSJ ;  Q5Z9I2, IMCL1_ORYSJ;  Q5VNW5, IMCL2_ORYSJ;
//
ID   3.1.2.1
DE   Acetyl-CoA hydrolase.
AN   Acetyl-CoA acylase.
AN   Acetyl-CoA deacylase.
CA   Acetyl-CoA + H(2)O = CoA + acetate.
DR   Q754Q2, ACH1_ASHGO ;  P83773, ACH1_CANAL ;  Q6FPF3, ACH1_CANGA ;
DR   Q6BKW1, ACH1_DEBHA ;  Q54K91, ACH1_DICDI ;  Q6CNR2, ACH1_KLULA ;
DR   P15937, ACH1_NEUCR ;  Q9UUJ9, ACH1_SCHPO ;  Q6C3Z9, ACH1_YARLI ;
DR   P32316, ACH1_YEAST ;  Q8WYK0, ACO12_HUMAN;  Q9DBK0, ACO12_MOUSE;
DR   Q99NB7, ACO12_RAT  ;
//
ID   3.1.2.2
DE   Palmitoyl-CoA hydrolase.
AN   Long-chain fatty-acyl-CoA hydrolase.
CA   Palmitoyl-CoA + H(2)O = CoA + palmitate.
CC   -!- Also hydrolyzes CoA thioesters of other long-chain fatty acids.
PR   PROSITE; PDOC00112;
