ID   3.1.2.29
DE   Fluoroacetyl-CoA thioesterase.
CA   Fluoroacetyl-CoA + H(2)O = fluoroacetate + CoA.
CC   -!- Fluoroacetate is extremely toxic.
CC   -!- It reacts with CoA to form fluoroacetyl-CoA, which substitutes for
CC       acetyl CoA and reacts with EC 2.3.3.1 to produce fluorocitrate,
CC       a metabolite of which binds very tightly to EC 4.2.1.3 and halts the
CC       TCA cycle.
CC   -!- This enzyme hydrolyzes fluoroacetyl-CoA before it can react with
CC       citrate synthase, and thus confers fluoroacetate resistance on the
CC       organisms that produce it.
CC   -!- It has been described in the poisonous plant Dichapetalum cymosum and
CC       the bacterium Streptomyces cattleya, both of which are fluoroacetate
CC       producers.
DR   Q1EMV2, FLK_STRCT  ;
//
ID   3.1.2.30
DE   (3S)-malyl-CoA thioesterase.
CA   (S)-malyl-CoA + H(2)O = (S)-malate + CoA.
CC   -!- The enzyme has no activity with (2R,3S)-2-methylmalyl-CoA (cf.
CC       EC 4.1.3.24) or other CoA esters.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 3.1.2.n2.
DR   Q5V0X0, AMASY_HALMA;  A3PN16, MCTE_RHOS1 ;  D3JV05, MCTE_RHOS4 ;
