ID   3.1.3.79
DE   Mannosylfructose-phosphate phosphatase.
AN   Mannosylfructose-6-phosphate phosphatase.
AN   MFPP.
CA   Beta-D-fructofuranosyl-alpha-D-mannopyranoside 6(F)-phosphate + H(2)O =
CA   alpha-D-fructofuranosyl-alpha-D-mannopyranoside + phosphate.
CF   Mg(2+).
CC   -!- Mannosylfructose is the major endogenous osmolyte produced by several
CC       alpha-proteobacteria in response to osmotic stress and is synthesized
CC       by the sequential action of EC 2.4.1.246 followed by this enzyme.
CC   -!- While mannosylfructose 6-phosphate is the physiological substrate,
CC       the enzyme can use sucrose 6-phosphate very efficiently.
CC   -!- The F in mannosylfructose 6(F)-phosphate is used to indicate that the
CC       fructose residue of sucrose carries the substituent.
DR   A9CK30, MFPP_AGRFC ;
