ID   3.1.3.81
DE   Diacylglycerol diphosphate phosphatase.
AN   DGPP phosphatase.
AN   DGPP phosphohydrolase.
AN   Pyrophosphate phosphatase.
CA   1,2-diacyl-sn-glycerol 3-diphosphate + H(2)O = 1,2-diacyl-sn-glycerol
CA   3-phosphate + phosphate.
CC   -!- The bifunctional enzyme catalyzes the dephosphorylation of
CC       diacylglycerol diphosphate to phosphatidate and the subsequent
CC       dephosphorylation of phosphatidate to diacylglycerol (cf.
CC       EC 3.1.3.4).
CC   -!- It regulates intracellular levels of diacylglycerol diphosphate and
CC       phosphatidate, phospholipid molecules believed to play a signaling
CC       role in stress response.
CC   -!- The phosphatase activity of the bifunctional enzyme is Mg(2+)-
CC       independent and N-ethylmaleimide-insensitive and is distinct from the
CC       Mg(2+)-dependent and N-ethylmaleimide-sensitive enzyme EC 3.1.3.4.
CC   -!- The diacylglycerol pyrophosphate phosphatase activity in
CC       Saccharomyces cerevisiae is induced by zinc depletion, by inositol
CC       supplementation, and when cells enter the stationary phase.
DR   Q9UUA6, DPP1_SCHPO ;  Q05521, DPP1_YEAST ;  Q04396, LPP1_YEAST ;
DR   P0A925, PGPB_ECO57 ;  P0A924, PGPB_ECOLI ;  P44570, PGPB_HAEIN ;
