ID   3.1.3.100
DE   Thiamine phosphate phosphatase.
CA   Thiamine phosphate + H(2)O = thiamine + phosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme participates in the thiamine biosynthesis pathway in
CC       eukaryotes and a few prokaryotes.
CC   -!- These organisms lack EC 2.7.4.16 and need to convert thiamine
CC       phosphate to thiamine diphosphate, the active form of the vitamin,
CC       by first removing the phosphate group, followed by diphosphorylation
CC       by EC 2.7.6.2.
DR   Q9SU92, PPSP3_ARATH;  F4KFT7, TENAC_ARATH;
//
ID   3.1.3.101
DE   Validoxylamine A 7'-phosphate phosphatase.
CA   Validoxylamine A 7'-phosphate + H(2)O = validoxylamine A + phosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Streptomyces
CC       hygroscopicus subsp. limoneus, is involved in the biosynthesis of the
CC       antifungal agent validamycin A.
DR   Q15JF8, VLDH_STRHL ;
//
ID   3.1.3.102
DE   FMN hydrolase.
AN   FMN phosphatase.
CA   FMN + H(2)O = riboflavin + phosphate.
CF   Mg(2+).
CC   -!- The enzyme, found in many isoforms purified from both bacteria and
CC       plants, is a member of the haloacid dehalogenase superfamily.
CC   -!- Most of the isoforms have a wide substrate specificity, but isoforms
CC       specific for FMN also exist.
DR   Q84VZ1, FHY1C_ARATH;  Q84MD8, FHYRK_ARATH;
//
ID   3.1.3.103
DE   3-deoxy-D-glycero-D-galacto-nonulopyranosonate 9-phosphatase.
AN   2-keto-3-deoxy-D-glycero-D-galacto-non-2-ulopyranosonate-9-phosphate
AN   phosphatase.
CA   3-deoxy-D-glycero-beta-D-galacto-non-2-ulopyranosonate 9-phosphate +
CA   H(2)O = 3-deoxy-D-glycero-beta-D-galacto-non-2-ulopyranosonate +
CA   phosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Bacteroides
CC       thetaiotaomicron, is part of the biosynthesis pathway of the sialic
CC       acid 3-deoxy-D-glycero-beta-D-galacto-non-2-ulopyranosonate (Kdn).
CC   -!- Kdn is abundant in extracellular glycoconjugates of lower vertebrates
CC       such as fish and amphibians, but is also found in the capsular
CC       polysaccharides of bacteria that belong to the Bacteroides genus.
DR   Q8A712, KDGGP_BACTN;
