//
ID   3.1.11.7
DE   Adenosine-5'-diphospho-5'-(DNA) diphosphatase.
AN   5'-app5'-DNA adenylate hydrolase.
AN   Aprataxin.
CA   (1) Adenosine-5'-diphospho-5'-(DNA) + H(2)O = AMP + phospho-5'-(DNA).
CA   (2) Adenosine-5'-diphospho-5'-(ribonucleotide)-(DNA) + H(2)O = AMP +
CA   5'-phospho-(ribonucleotide)-(DNA).
CC   -!- Aprataxin is a DNA-binding protein involved in different types of DNA
CC       break repair.
CC   -!- The enzyme acts (among other activities) on abortive DNA ligation
CC       intermediates that contain an adenylate covalently linked to the
CC       5'-phosphate DNA terminus.
CC   -!- It also acts when the adenylate is covalently linked to the
CC       5'-phosphate of a ribonucleotide linked to a DNA strand, which is the
CC       result of abortive ligase activty on products of EC 3.1.26.4,
CC       an enzyme that cleaves RNA-DNA hybrids on the 5' side of the
CC       ribonucleotide found in the 5'-RNA-DNA-3' junction.
CC   -!- Aprataxin binds the adenylate group to a histidine residue within the
CC       active site, followed by its hydrolysis from the nucleic acid and
CC       eventual release, leaving a 5'-phosphate terminus that can be
CC       efficiently rejoined.
CC   -!- The enzyme also possesses the activities of EC 3.1.11.8 and
CC       EC 3.1.12.2.
DR   Q7YRZ2, APTX_BOVIN ;  P61797, APTX_CANLF ;  P61798, APTX_CHICK ;
DR   P61802, APTX_CIOIN ;  P61799, APTX_DANRE ;  Q7Z2E3, APTX_HUMAN ;
DR   Q9BGQ0, APTX_MACFA ;  Q7TQC5, APTX_MOUSE ;  Q7YRZ1, APTX_PIG   ;
DR   Q8K4H4, APTX_RAT   ;  O74859, APTX_SCHPO ;  P61800, APTX_TAKRU ;
DR   Q7T287, APTX_XENLA ;  P61801, APTX_XENTR ;  Q08702, APTX_YEAST ;
//
ID   3.1.11.8
DE   Guaosine-5'-diphospho-5'-(DNA) diphosphatase.
AN   Aprataxin.
AN   Pp5'G5'-DNA guanylate hydrolase.
AN   Pp5'G5'DNA diphosphatase.
CA   Guanosine-5'-diphospho-5'-(DNA) + H(2)O = phospho-5'-(DNA) + GMP.
CC   -!- Aprataxin is a DNA-binding protein that catalyzes (among other
CC       activities) the 5' decapping of Gpp-DNA (formed by homologs of RtcB3
CC       from the bacterium Myxococcus xanthus).
CC   -!- The enzyme binds the guanylate group to a histidine residue at its
CC       active site, forming a covalent enzyme-nucleotide phosphate
CC       intermediate, followed by the hydrolysis of the guanylate from the
CC       nucleic acid and eventual release.
CC   -!- The enzyme forms a 5'-phospho terminus that can be efficiently joined
CC       by 'classical' ligases.
CC   -!- The enzyme also possesses the activitiy of EC 3.1.11.7 and
CC       EC 3.1.12.2.
//
ID   3.1.12.1
DE   5' to 3' exodeoxyribonuclease (nucleoside 3'-phosphate-forming).
AN   5' to 3' single stranded DNA exonuclease.
CA   Exonucleolytic cleavage in the 5'- to 3'-direction to yield nucleoside
CA   3'-phosphates.
CF   Divalent metal cation; Iron-sulfur.
CC   -!- Preference for single-stranded DNA.
DR   Q9YCL9, CAS4_AERPE ;  A0Q5Y6, CAS4_FRATN ;  D4GQN9, CAS4_HALVD ;
DR   Q57822, CAS4_METJA ;  A3MTK6, CAS4_PYRCJ ;  Q2RRV2, CAS4_RHORT ;
DR   Q97TX9, CAS4_SULSO ;  G4RJY5, CAS4_THETK ;  Q74H36, CS4F1_GEOSL;
DR   Q8F1F5, CS4F1_LEPIN;  Q1CW50, CS4F1_MYXXD;  Q2RY11, CS4F1_RHORT;
//
ID   3.1.12.2
DE   DNA-3'-diphospho-5'-guanosine diphosphatase.
AN   Aprataxin.
AN   DNA-3'pp5'G guanylate hydrolase.
CA   (DNA)-3'-diphospho-5'-guanosine + H(2)O = (DNA)-3'-phosphate + GMP.
CC   -!- Aprataxin is a DNA-binding protein that catalyzes (among other
CC       activities) the 3' decapping of DNA-ppG (formed by EC 6.5.1.8).
CC   -!- The enzyme binds the guanylate group to a histidine residue at its
CC       active site, forming a covalent enzyme-nucleotide phosphate
CC       intermediate, followed by the hydrolysis of the guanylate from the
CC       nucleic acid and its eventual release.
CC   -!- The enzyme also possesses the activity of EC 3.1.11.7 and
CC       EC 3.1.11.8.
DR   Q7YRZ2, APTX_BOVIN ;  P61797, APTX_CANLF ;  P61798, APTX_CHICK ;
DR   P61802, APTX_CIOIN ;  P61799, APTX_DANRE ;  Q7Z2E3, APTX_HUMAN ;
DR   Q9BGQ0, APTX_MACFA ;  Q7TQC5, APTX_MOUSE ;  Q7YRZ1, APTX_PIG   ;
DR   Q8K4H4, APTX_RAT   ;  O74859, APTX_SCHPO ;  P61800, APTX_TAKRU ;
DR   Q7T287, APTX_XENLA ;  P61801, APTX_XENTR ;  Q08702, APTX_YEAST ;
