//
ID   3.1.21.8
DE   T(4) deoxyribonuclease II.
AN   T(4) endonuclease II.
CA   Endonucleolytic nicking and cleavage of cytosine-containing double-
CA   stranded DNA.
CF   Mg(2+).
CC   -!- This phage T(4) enzyme is involved in degradation of host DNA.
CC   -!- The enzyme primarily catalyzes nicking of the bottom strand of double
CC       stranded DNA between the first and second base pair to the right of a
CC       top-strand CCGC motif.
CC   -!- Double-stranded breaks are produced 5- to 10-fold less frequently.
CC   -!- It does not cleave the T4 native DNA, which contains
CC       5-hydroxymethylcytosine instead of cytosine.
DR   P07059, END2_BPT4  ;
//
ID   3.1.21.9
DE   T(4) deoxyribonuclease IV.
AN   T(4) endonuclease IV.
CA   Endonucleolytic cleavage of the 5' phosphodiester bond of deoxycytidine
CA   in single-stranded DNA.
CC   -!- This phage T(4) enzyme is involved in degradation of host DNA.
CC   -!- The enzyme does not cleave double-stranded DNA or native T4 DNA,
CC       which contains 5-hydroxymethylcytosine instead of cytosine.
DR   P39250, END4_BPT4  ;
//
ID   3.1.22.1
DE   Deoxyribonuclease II.
AN   DNase II.
AN   Lysosomal DNase II.
CA   Endonucleolytic cleavage to nucleoside 3'-phosphates and
CA   3'-phosphooligonucleotide end-products.
CC   -!- Preference for double-stranded DNA.
CC   -!- Similar enzymes: crab testis DNase, snail DNase, salmon testis DNase,
CC       liver acid DNase, human acid DNases of gastric mucosa and cervix.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 3.1.4.6.
