ID   3.1.25.1
DE   Deoxyribonuclease (pyrimidine dimer).
AN   Endodeoxyribonuclease (pyrimidine dimer).
CA   Endonucleolytic cleavage near pyrimidine dimers to products with
CA   5'-phosphate.
CC   -!- Acts on a damaged strand, 5' from the damaged site.
CC   -!- Similar enzymes: T4 endonuclease V, Escherichia coli endonuclease III
CC       and V, correndonuclease II.
//
ID   3.1.25.2
DE   Transferred entry: 4.2.99.18.
//
ID   3.1.26.1
DE   Physarum polycephalum ribonuclease.
CA   Endonucleolytic cleavage to 5'-phosphomonoester.
DR   P81477, PHYB_PHYPO ;
//
ID   3.1.26.2
DE   Ribonuclease alpha.
CA   Endonucleolytic cleavage to 5'-phosphomonoester.
CC   -!- Specific for O-methylated RNA.
//
ID   3.1.26.3
DE   Ribonuclease III.
AN   Ribonuclease 3.
AN   RNase III.
CA   Endonucleolytic cleavage to 5'-phosphomonoester.
CC   -!- An endoribonuclease that cleaves double-stranded RNA molecules.
CC   -!- The cleavage can be either a single-stranded nick or double-stranded
CC       break in the RNA, depending in part upon the degree of base-pairing
CC       in the region of the cleavage site.
CC   -!- Specificity is conferred by negative determinants, i.e., the presence
CC       of certain Watson-Crick base-pairs at specific positions that
CC       strongly inhibit cleavage.
CC   -!- RNase III is involved in both rRNA processing and mRNA processing and
CC       decay.
