ID   3.2.1.14
DE   Chitinase.
AN   1,4-beta-poly-N-acetylglucosaminidase.
AN   Chitodextrinase.
AN   Poly-beta-glucosaminidase.
CA   Random endo-hydrolysis of N-acetyl-beta-D-glucosaminide (1->4)-beta-
CA   linkages in chitin and chitodextrins.
CC   -!- The enzyme binds to chitin and randomly cleaves glycosidic linkages
CC       in chitin and chitodextrins in a non-processive mode, generating
CC       chitooligosaccharides and free ends on which exo-chitinases and exo-
CC       chitodextrinases can act.
CC   -!- Activity is greatly stimulated in the presence of EC 1.14.99.53,
CC       which attacks the crystalline structure of chitin and makes the
CC       polymer more accesible to the chitinase.
CC   -!- Cf. EC 3.2.1.202.
PR   PROSITE; PDOC00620;
