ID   3.2.1.155
DE   Xyloglucan-specific exo-beta-1,4-glucanase.
CA   Hydrolysis of (1->4)-D-glucosidic linkages in xyloglucans so as to
CA   successively remove oligosaccharides from the chain end.
CC   -!- The enzyme removes XXXG heptasaccharides, XXLG/XLXG octasaccharides
CC       and XLLG nonasaccharides from the end of tamarind seed xyloglucan
CC       polymers in a processive manner.
CC   -!- Hydrolysis occurs at the unsubstituted D-glucopyranose residue in the
CC       main backbone.
CC   -!- It is not known whether the cleavage takes place at the reducing or
CC       non-reducing end of the polymer.
CC   -!- Very low activity with beta-D-glucans.
CC   -!- The enzyme from Chrysosporium lucknowense shifts to an endoglucanase
CC       mode when acting on linear substrates without bulky substituents on
CC       the polymeric backbone such as barley beta-glucan.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 3.2.1.160.
DR   Q7Z9M8, XG74_HYPJQ ;
