ID   3.3.2.6
DE   Leukotriene-A(4) hydrolase.
AN   Leukotriene A(4) hydrolase.
AN   Leukotriene-A4 hydrolase.
AN   LTA-4 hydrolase.
CA   (7E,9E,11Z,14Z)-(5S,6S)-5,6-epoxyicosa-7,9,11,14-tetraenoate + H(2)O =
CA   (6Z,8E,10E,14Z)-(5S,12R)-5,12-dihydroxyicosa-6,8,10,14-tetraenoate.
CF   Zn(2+).
CC   -!- A bifunctional zinc metalloprotease that displays both epoxide
CC       hydrolase and aminopeptidase activities.
CC   -!- It preferentially cleaves tripeptides at an arginyl bond, with
CC       dipeptides and tetrapeptides being poorer substrates.
CC   -!- It also converts leukotriene A(4) into leukotriene B(4), unlike
CC       EC 3.2.2.10 which converts leukotriene A(4) into 5,6-dihydroxy-
CC       7,9,11,14-eicosatetraenoic acid.
