AN   Hepoxilin A(3) hydrolase.
AN   Hepoxilin epoxide hydrolase.
AN   Hepoxylin hydrolase.
CA   (5Z,9E,14Z)-(8-xi,11R,12S)-11,12-epoxy-8-hydroxyicosa-5,9,14-trienoate +
CA   H(2)O = (5Z,9E,14Z)-(8-xi,11-xi,12S)-8,11,12-trihydroxyicosa-5,9,14-
CA   trienoate.
CC   -!- Converts hepoxilin A(3) into trioxilin A(3).
CC   -!- Highly specific for the substrate, having only slight activity with
CC       other epoxides such as leukotriene A(4) and styrene oxide.
CC   -!- Probably plays a modulatory role in inflammation, vascular
CC       physiology, systemic glucose metabolism and neurological function.
//
ID   3.3.2.8
DE   Limonene-1,2-epoxide hydrolase.
AN   Limonene oxide hydrolase.
CA   1,2-epoxymenth-8-ene + H(2)O = menth-8-ene-1,2-diol.
CC   -!- Involved in the monoterpene degradation pathway of the actinomycete
CC       Rhodococcus erythropolis.
CC   -!- The enzyme hydrolyzes several alicyclic and 1-methyl-substituted
CC       epoxides, such as 1-methylcyclohexene oxide, indene oxide and
CC       cyclohexene oxide.
CC   -!- It differs from the previously described epoxide hydrolases
CC       (EC 3.3.2.4, EC 3.3.2.6, EC 3.3.2.7, EC 3.3.2.9 and EC 3.3.2.10) as
CC       it is not inhibited by 2-bromo-4'-nitroacetophenone, diethyl
CC       pyrocarbonate, 4-fluorochalcone oxide or 1,10-phenanthroline.
DR   Q9ZAG3, LIMA_RHOER ;
