ID   3.3.2.11
DE   Cholesterol-5,6-oxide hydrolase.
AN   ChEH.
AN   Cholesterol-epoxide hydrolase.
CA   (1) 5,6-alpha-epoxy-5-alpha-cholestan-3-beta-ol + H(2)O = cholestane-3-
CA   beta,5-alpha,6-beta-triol.
CA   (2) 5,6-beta-epoxy-5-beta-cholestan-3-beta-ol + H(2)O = cholestane-3-
CA   beta,5-alpha,6-beta-triol.
CC   -!- The enzyme appears to work equally well with both diastereoisomers of
CC       cholesterol 5,6-epoxide.
CC   -!- The product is a competitive inhibitor of the reaction.
DR   O33283, EPHG_MYCTU ;
//
ID   3.3.2.12
DE   Oxepin-CoA hydrolase.
CA   2-oxepin-2(3H)-ylideneacetyl-CoA + H(2)O = 3-oxo-5,6-dehydrosuberyl-CoA
CA   semialdehyde.
CC   -!- The enzyme from Escherichia coli is a bifunctional fusion protein
CC       that also catalyzes EC 1.17.1.7.
CC   -!- Combined the two activities result in a two-step conversion of
CC       oxepin-CoA to 3-oxo-5,6-dehydrosuberyl-CoA, part of an aerobic
CC       phenylacetate degradation pathway.
CC   -!- The enzyme from Escherichia coli also exhibits enoyl-CoA hydratase
CC       activity utilizing crotonyl-CoA as a substrate.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 3.7.1.16.
DR   P77455, PAAZ_ECOLI ;
//
ID   3.3.2.13
DE   Chorismatase.
AN   Chorismate/3,4-dihydroxycyclohexa-1,5-dienoate synthase.
CA   Chorismate + H(2)O = (3R,4R)-3,4-dihydroxy-3,4-dihydrobenzoate +
CA   pyruvate.
CC   -!- The enzyme found in several bacterial species is involved in the
CC       biosynthesis of macrocyclic polyketides.
DR   Q9KID9, FKBO_STRHY ;  Q54305, RAPK_STRRN ;
//
ID   3.3.2.14
DE   2,4-dinitroanisole O-demethylase.
AN   2,4-dinitroanisole ether hydrolase.
AN   DNAN demethylase.
CA   2,4-dinitroanisole + H(2)O = methanol + 2,4-dinitrophenol.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Nocardioides sp. JS1661,
CC       is involved in the degradation of 2,4-dinitroanisole.
CC   -!- Unlike other known O-demethylases, such as EC 1.14.99.15 or
CC       EC 1.14.11.32, it does not require oxygen or electron donors,
CC       and produces methanol rather than formaldehyde.
DR   A0A096ZEC9, DNHA_NOCS1 ;  A0A096ZED0, DNHB_NOCS1 ;
//
ID   3.3.2.15
DE   Trans-2,3-dihydro-3-hydroxyanthranilic acid synthase.
AN   Isochorismatase.
CA   (2S)-2-amino-4-deoxychorismate + H(2)O = (5S,6S)-6-amino-5-
CA   hydroxycyclohexa-1,3-diene-1-carboxylate + pyruvate.
CC   -!- Isolated from the bacterium Pseudomonas aeruginosa.
CC   -!- Involved in phenazine biosynthesis.
DR   P0DPB9, PHZD1_PSEAE;  P0DPC1, PHZD2_PSEAE;  Q51790, PHZD_PSEFL ;
