ID   3.4.11.19
DE   D-stereospecific aminopeptidase.
CA   Release of an N-terminal D-amino acid from a peptide, Xaa-|-Yaa-,
CA   in which Xaa is preferably D-Ala, D-Ser or D-Thr. D-amino acid amides and
CA   methyl esters also are hydrolyzed, as is glycine amide.
CC   -!- A thiol-dependent peptidase known from the bacterium Ochrobactrum
CC       anthropi.
CC   -!- A homolog of EC 3.4.16.4.
CC   -!- Not metal dependent; probably has serine at the active center.
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family S12.
