ID   3.4.11.24
DE   Aminopeptidase S.
AN   Double-zinc aminopeptidase.
AN   SGAP.
CA   Release of an N-terminal amino acid with a preference for large
CA   hydrophobic amino-terminus residues.
CF   Zn(2+).
CC   -!- Activated by Ca(2+).
CC   -!- In the presence of Ca(2+), the best substrates are Leu-Phe, Leu-Ser,
CC       Leu-pNA (aminoacyl-p-nitroanilide), Phe-Phe-Phe and Phe-Phe.
CC   -!- Peptides with proline in the P1' position are not substrates.
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family M28.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 3.4.11.n1.
DR   P80561, APX_STRGG  ;
//
ID   3.4.11.25
DE   Beta-peptidyl aminopeptidase.
CA   Cleaves N-terminal beta-homoamino acids from peptides composed of 2 to 6
CA   amino acids.
CC   -!- Sphingosinicella xenopeptidilytica strain 3-2W4 is able to utilize
CC       the beta-peptides beta-homoVal-beta-homoAla-beta-homoLeu and beta-
CC       homoAla-beta-homoLeu as sole carbon and energy sources.
DR   A0MTQ2, BAPA_SPHMI ;  Q52VH2, BAPA_SPHXN ;
//
ID   3.4.11.26
DE   Intermediate cleaving peptidase 55.
CA   The enzyme cleaves the 36-Pro-Pro-37 bond of cysteine desulfurase
CA   (EC 2.8.1.7) removing three amino acid residues (Tyr-Ser-Pro) from the
CA   N-terminus after cleavage by mitochondrial processing peptidase.
CC   -!- Icp55 removes the destabilizing N-terminal amino acid residues that
CC       are left after cleavage by the mitochondrial processing peptidase,
CC       leading to the stabilization of the substrate.
CC   -!- The enzyme can remove single amino acids or a short peptide, as in
CC       the case of cysteine desulfurase (EC 2.8.1.7), where three amino
CC       acids are removed.
DR   Q10439, ICP55_SCHPO;  P40051, ICP55_YEAST;
