CA   not Pro, and Yaa is neither Asp nor Glu. Thus, conversion of angiotensin
CA   I to angiotensin II, with increase in vasoconstrictor activity, but no
CA   action on angiotensin II.
CF   Zn(2+).
CC   -!- Cl(-)-dependent.
CC   -!- A glycoprotein that is generally membrane-bound.
CC   -!- Active at neutral pH.
CC   -!- Only single dipeptides are released from angiotensin I and bradykinin
CC       because of the lack of activity on bonds involving proline.
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family M2.
