ID   3.4.15.4
DE   Peptidyl-dipeptidase B.
AN   Atrial di-(tri-)peptidyl carboxylase.
AN   Atriopeptin convertase.
AN   Dipeptidyl carboxyhydrolase.
CA   Release of a C-terminal dipeptide or exceptionally a tripeptide.
CF   Zn(2+).
CC   -!- A membrane-bound, zinc metallopeptidase located in mammalian atrial,
CC       but not ventricular, myocytes.
CC   -!- Although it is capable of converting the 126-residue atriopeptin III
CC       directly to atriopeptin I by releasing a C-terminal tripeptide Phe-
CC       Arg-Tyr, it is generally restricted to the release of dipeptides.
CC   -!- In contrast to EC 3.4.15.1 it displays no chlorine dependence and
CC       shows no action on angiotensin I.
CC   -!- Conversely, peptidyl-dipeptidase a is unable to release Phe-Arg from
CC       the C-terminus of atriopeptin II.
