ID   3.4.21.6
DE   Coagulation factor Xa.
AN   Prothrombase.
AN   Prothrombinase.
AN   Stuart factor.
AN   Thrombokinase.
CA   Selective cleavage of Arg-|-Thr and then Arg-|-Ile bonds in prothrombin
CA   to form thrombin.
CC   -!- A blood coagulation factor formed from the proenzyme factor X by
CC       limited proteolysis.
CC   -!- Factor X is a glycoprotein composed of a heavy chain and a light
CC       chain, which are generated from a precursor protein by the excision
CC       of the tripeptide RKR and held together by one or more disulfide
CC       bonds.
CC   -!- The activated factor Xa converts prothrombin to thrombin in the
CC       presence of factor Va, Ca(2+) and phospholipids.
CC   -!- Scutelarin (EC 3.4.21.60) has similar specificity, but does not
CC       require factor Va.
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family S1.
PR   PROSITE; PDOC00124;
