ID   3.4.21.32
DE   Brachyurin.
AN   Collagenolytic protease.
CA   Hydrolysis of proteins, with broad specificity for peptide bonds. Native
CA   collagen is cleaved about 75% of the length of the molecule from the
CA   N-terminus. Low activity on small molecule substrates of both trypsin and
CA   chymotrypsin.
CC   -!- From hepatopancreas of the fiddler crab (Uca pugilator).
CC   -!- Other serine endopeptidases that degrade collagen, but are not listed
CC       separately here, include a second endopeptidase from U.pugilator,
CC       digestive enzymes from other decapod crustacea, and an enzyme from
CC       the fungus Entomophthora coronata.
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family S1.
PR   PROSITE; PDOC00124;
