ID   3.4.21.88
DE   Repressor LexA.
CA   Hydrolysis of Ala-|-Gly bond in repressor LexA.
CC   -!- In the presence of single-stranded DNA, the RecA protein interacts
CC       with LexA causing an autocatalytic cleavage which disrupts the DNA-
CC       binding part of LexA, leading to derepression of the SOS regulon and
CC       eventually DNA repair.
CC   -!- The activity was previously attributed to the RecA protein (formerly
CC       EC 3.4.99.37).
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family S24.
