ID   3.4.21.89
DE   Signal peptidase I.
AN   Bacterial leader peptidase I.
AN   Phage-procoat-leader peptidase.
AN   SPase I.
CA   Cleavage of hydrophobic, N-terminal signal or leader sequences from
CA   secreted and periplasmic proteins.
CC   -!- Unaffected by inhibitors of most serine peptidases, but site-directed
CC       mutagenesis implicates a Ser/Lys catalytic dyad in activity.
CC   -!- Cleaves a single bond -Ala-|-Ala- in M13 phage procoat protein,
CC       producing free signal peptide and coat protein.
CC   -!- Eukaryote signal peptidases that may have somewhat different
CC       specificity are known from the endoplasmic reticulum membrane and
CC       mitochondrial inner membrane.
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family S26.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 3.4.99.36.
