//
ID   3.4.21.93
DE   Proprotein convertase 1.
AN   NEC 1.
AN   Neuroendocrine convertase 1.
AN   PC1.
AN   Prohormone convertase I.
CA   Release of protein hormones, neuropeptides and renin from their
CA   precursors, generally by hydrolysis of -Lys-Arg-|- bonds.
CC   -!- A calcium dependent enzyme, maximally active at about pH 5.5.
CC   -!- Substrates include pro-opiomelanocortin, prorenin, proenkephalin,
CC       prodynorphin, prosomatostatin and proinsulin.
CC   -!- Unlike prohormone convertase 2, does not cleave proluteinizing-
CC       hormone-releasing hormone.
CC   -!- Usually processing of prodynorphin occurs at a bond in which P2 is
CC       Thr.
CC   -!- Present in the regulated secretory pathway of neuroendocrine cells,
CC       commonly actin co-operatively with prohormone convertase 2.
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family S8.
PR   PROSITE; PDOC00125;
DR   Q9GLR1, NEC1_BOVIN ;  P29120, NEC1_HUMAN ;  P63239, NEC1_MOUSE ;
DR   P63240, NEC1_MUSCO ;  P28840, NEC1_RAT   ;
//
ID   3.4.21.94
DE   Proprotein convertase 2.
AN   NEC 2.
AN   Neuroendocrine convertase 2.
AN   PC(2).
AN   Prohormone convertase II.
CA   Release of protein hormones and neuropeptides from their precursors,
CA   generally by hydrolysis of -Lys-Arg-|- bonds.
CC   -!- A calcium dependent enzyme, maximally active at about pH 5.5.
CC   -!- Specificity is broader than that of prohormone convertase 1.
CC   -!- Substrates include pro-opiomelanocortin, proenkephalin, prodynorphin,
CC       proinsulin and proluteinizing-hormone-releasing hormone.
CC   -!- Unlike prohormone convertase 1, does not cleave prorenin or
CC       prosomatostatin.
CC   -!- Usually processing of prodynorphin occurs at a bond in which P2 is
CC       Thr.
CC   -!- Present in the regulated secretory pathway of neuroendocrine cells,
CC       commonly actin co-operatively with prohormone convertase 1.
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family S8.
PR   PROSITE; PDOC00125;
DR   Q9GLR0, NEC2_BOVIN ;  G5ECN9, NEC2_CAEEL ;  P16519, NEC2_HUMAN ;
DR   P21661, NEC2_MOUSE ;  Q03333, NEC2_PIG   ;  Q5REC2, NEC2_PONAB ;
DR   P28841, NEC2_RAT   ;
//
ID   3.4.21.95
DE   Snake venom factor V activator.
AN   Factor V-activating proteinase.
AN   RVV-V component.
CA   Fully activates human clotting factor V by a single cleavage at the 1545-
CA   Trp-Tyr-Leu-Arg-|-Ser-Asn-Asn-Gly-1552 bond. Cattle, but not rabbit,
CA   factor V is cleaved, and no other proteins of the clotting system are
CA   attacked. Esterase activity is observed on Bz-Arg-OEt and Tos-Arg-OMe,
CA   and amidase activity on Phe-pipecolyl-Arg-NHPhNO(2).
CC   -!- Inhibited by diisopropyl fluorophosphate.
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family S1.
PR   PROSITE; PDOC00124;
