ID   3.4.21.114
DE   Equine arterivirus serine peptidase.
AN   3C-like Ser protease.
AN   3C-like serine protease.
AN   3CLSP.
AN   Arterivirus NSP4.
AN   Chymotrypsin-like serine proteinase nsp4.
AN   Equine arteritis virus serine peptidase.
AN   Nonstructural protein 4 serine protease.
CA   Cleavage of (Glu/Gln)-|-(Gly/Ser/Ala) in arterivirus replicase
CA   translation products ORF1a and ORF1ab.
CC   -!- In the equine arterivirus (EAV), the replicase gene is translated
CC       into open reading frame 1a (ORF1a) and ORF1ab polyproteins.
CC   -!- This enzyme is the main viral proteinase and processes five cleavage
CC       sites in the ORF1a protein and three in the ORF1b-encoded part of the
CC       ORF1ab protein to yield nonstructural proteins (nsp5-nsp12).
CC   -!- It combines the catalytic system of a chymotrypsin-like serine
CC       peptidase (His-Asp-Ser catalytic triad) with the substrate
CC       specificity of a 3C-like serine peptidase (Glu or Gln) at the P1
CC       position and a small amino-acid residue (Gly, Ser or Ala) at the P1'
CC       position.
CC   -!- Cleavage of ORF1ab by this enzyme is essential for viral replication.
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family S32.
//
ID   3.4.21.115
DE   Infectious pancreatic necrosis birnavirus Vp4 peptidase.
AN   Infectious pancreatic necrosis virus protease.
AN   IPNV Vp4 peptidase.
AN   IPNV Vp4 protease.
AN   NS protease.
AN   NS-associated protease.
AN   Vp4 protease.
CA   Cleaves the (Ser/Thr)-Xaa-Ala-|-(Ser/Ala)-Gly motif in the polyprotein
CA   NH(2)-pVP2-VP4-VP3-COOH of infectious pancreatic necrosis virus at the
CA   pVP2-VP4 and VP4-VP3 junctions.
CC   -!- Infectious pancreatic necrosis virus (IPNV) is a birnavirus that
CC       causes an acute, contagious disease in young salmonid fish.
CC   -!- As with most viruses that infect eukaryotic cells, the proteolytic
CC       processing of viral precursor proteins is a crucial step in the life
CC       cycle of this virus.
CC   -!- pVP2 is converted into VP2 by cleavage near the carboxy end of pVP2;
CC       this cleavage is most likely due to host-cell proteases rather than
CC       VP4.
CC   -!- Differs from most serine peptidases in not having the catalytic triad
CC       Ser-His-Asp.
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family S50.
//
ID   3.4.21.116
DE   SpoIVB peptidase.
AN   Sporulation factor IV B protease.
AN   Stage IV sporulation protein B.
CA   Self-cleaves 52-Val-|-Asn-53, 62-Ala-|-Phe-63 and 74-Val-|-Thr-75 at the
CA   N-terminus of SpoIVB.
CC   -!- This enzyme plays a central role in a regulatory checkpoint (the
CC       sigma(K) checkpoint), which coordinates gene expression during the
CC       later stages of spore formation in Bacillus subtilis.
CC   -!- The enzyme activates proteolytic processing of a sporulation-specific
CC       sigma factor, pro-sigma(K), to its mature and active form, sigma(K),
CC       by self-cleavage.
CC   -!- The enzyme is also subject to secondary proteolysis, which presumably
CC       inactivates SpoIVB.
CC   -!- The enzyme is also essential for the formation of heat-resistant
CC       spores.
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family S55.
PR   PROSITE; PDOC51494;
DR   P17896, SP4B_BACSU ;
