ID   3.4.21.117
DE   Stratum corneum chymotryptic enzyme.
AN   Kallikrein 7.
AN   SCCE.
AN   Serine protease 6.
CA   Cleavage of proteins with aromatic side chains in the P1 position.
CC   -!- This enzyme has wide substrate specificity, being able to degrade
CC       heat-denatured bovine casein and the alpha-chain of native human
CC       fibrinogen.
CC   -!- It cleaves the B chain of bovine insulin at 6-Leu-|-Cya-7 (cysteic
CC       acid), 16-Tyr-|-Leu-17, 25-Phe-|-Tyr-26 and 26-Tyr-|-Thr-27.
CC   -!- It is thought to play a role in the desquamation (skin-shedding) of
CC       the outer layer of skin, the stratum corneum, by degrading
CC       intercellular cohesive structures.
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family S1A.
