AN   PRECE-1.
AN   Prorenin converting enzyme 1.
AN   Prorenin-converting enzyme.
AN   Proteinase P.
CA   Hydrolyzes mouse Ren2 protein (a species of prorenin present in the
CA   submandibular gland) on the carboxy side of the arginine residue at the
CA   Lys-Arg-|- pair in the N-terminus, to yield mature renin.
CC   -!- Specific for prorenin from the mouse submandibular gland, as prorenin
CC       from the mouse kidney (Ren1) and human prorenin are not substrates.
CC   -!- Site-directed mutagenesis studies have shown that the enzyme will
CC       also cleave prorenin when Lys-Arg is replaced by Arg-Arg or Gln-Arg
CC       but the rate of reaction is much slower when Lys-Lys is used.
CC   -!- Also able to process pro-interleukin-1-beta (pro-IL-1-beta) in mouse
CC       submandibular gland to form IL-1-beta.
