CC       aliphatic (Leu) amino acids at the P1' position results in only minor
CC       differences in cleavage efficiency, suggesting that steric or
CC       conformational constraints may play a role in determining
CC       specificity.
CC   -!- Changes to the amino acid at the P2 position do not alter cleavage
CC       efficiency.
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family C37.
