ID   3.4.22.70
DE   Sortase A.
CA   The enzyme catalyzes a cell wall sorting reaction in which a surface
CA   protein with a sorting signal containing a LPXTG motif is cleaved between
CA   the Thr and Gly residue. The resulting threonine carboxyl end of the
CA   protein is covalently attached to a pentaglycine cross-bridge of
CA   peptidoglycan.
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family C60.
DR   Q2FV99, SRTA_STAA8 ;  Q9XA14, SRTE1_STRCO;  Q9XA15, SRTE2_STRCO;
//
ID   3.4.22.71
DE   Sortase B.
AN   SrtB.
CA   The enzyme catalyzes a cell wall sorting reaction in which a surface
CA   protein with a sorting signal containing a NPXTN motif is cleaved between
CA   the Thr and Asn residue. The resulting threonine carboxyl end of the
CA   protein is covalently attached to a pentaglycine cross-bridge of
CA   peptidoglycan.
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family C60.
DR   Q2FZE3, SRTB_STAA8 ;
//
ID   3.4.23.1
DE   Pepsin A.
AN   Pepsin.
CA   Preferential cleavage: hydrophobic, preferably aromatic, residues in P1
CA   and P1' positions. Cleaves 1-Phe-|-Val-2, 4-Gln-|-His-5, 13-Glu-|-Ala-14,
CA   14-Ala-|-Leu-15, 15-Leu-|-Tyr-16, 16-Tyr-|-Leu-17, 23-Gly-|-Phe-24,
CA   24-Phe-|-Phe-25 and 25-Phe-|-Tyr-26 bonds in the B chain of insulin.
CC   -!- The predominant endopeptidase in the gastric juice of vertebrates,
CC       formed from pepsinogen A by limited proteolysis.
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family A1.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 3.4.4.1.
