ID   3.4.23.3
DE   Gastricsin.
AN   Pepsin C.
CA   More restricted specificity than pepsin A, but shows preferential
CA   cleavage at Tyr-|-Xaa bonds. High activity on hemoglobin.
CC   -!- Formed from progastricsin, apparently in the gastric juice of most
CC       vertebrates.
CC   -!- In addition to the fundus, progastricsin is also secreted in antrum
CC       and proximal duodenum.
CC   -!- Seminal plasma contains a zymogen that is immunologically identical
CC       with progastricsin.
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family A1.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 3.4.4.22.
