ID   3.4.23.22
DE   Endothiapepsin.
AN   Endothia aspartic proteinase.
CA   Hydrolysis of proteins with specificity similar to that of pepsin A,
CA   prefers hydrophobic residues at P1 and P1', but does not cleave
CA   14-Ala-|-Leu-15 in the B chain of insulin or Z-Glu-Tyr. Clots milk.
CC   -!- From the ascomycete Endothia parasitica.
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family A1.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 3.4.4.17, EC 3.4.23.6 and EC 3.4.23.10.
