DR   P00799, CARP_RHIMI ;  P09177, CARP_RHIPU ;
//
ID   3.4.23.24
DE   Candidapepsin.
AN   Candida albicans aspartic proteinase.
CA   Preferential cleavage at the carboxyl of hydrophobic amino acids,
CA   but fails to cleave 15-Leu-|-Tyr-16, 16-Tyr-|-Leu-17 and 24-Phe-|-Phe-25
CA   of insulin B chain. Activates trypsinogen, and degrades keratin.
CC   -!- This endopeptidase from the imperfect yeast Candida albicans is
CC       inhibited by pepstatin, but not by methyl 2-diazoacetamido-hexanoate
CC       or 1,2-epoxy-3-(p-nitrophenoxy)propane.
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family A1.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 3.4.4.17 and EC 3.4.23.6.
