ID   3.4.23.26
DE   Rhodotorulapepsin.
AN   Rhodotorula aspartic proteinase.
CA   Specificity similar to that of pepsin A. Cleaves Z-Lys-|-Ala-Ala-Ala and
CA   activates trypsinogen.
CC   -!- From the imperfect yeast Rhodotorula glutinis.
CC   -!- Somewhat similar enzymes have been isolated from the imperfect yeast-
CC       like organism Cladosporium sp. and the imperfect fungus Paecilomyces
CC       varioti.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 3.4.4.17 and EC 3.4.23.6.
//
ID   3.4.23.27
DE   Transferred entry: 3.4.21.103.
//
ID   3.4.23.28
DE   Acrocylindropepsin.
AN   Acrocylindrium proteinase.
CA   Preference for hydrophobic residue at P1 and P1'. Action on the B chain
CA   of insulin is generally similar to that of pepsin A, but it also cleaves
CA   6-Leu-|-Cys(SO(3)H)-7, 21-Glu-|-Arg-22 and 3-Asn-|-Gln-4, although not
CA   4-Gln-|-His-5.
CC   -!- From the imperfect fungus Acrocylindrium sp.
CC   -!- Has a very low pH optimum on casein of 2.0.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 3.4.4.17, EC 3.4.23.6 and EC 3.4.99.1.
//
ID   3.4.23.29
DE   Polyporopepsin.
AN   Polyporus aspartic proteinase.
CA   Milk clotting activity, broad specificity, but fails to cleave
CA   15-Leu-|-Tyr-16 or 16-Tyr-|-Leu-17 of insulin B chain.
CC   -!- From the basidiomycete Irpex lacteus (also known as Polyporus
CC       tulipiferae).
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family A1.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 3.4.4.17.
PR   PROSITE; PDOC00128;
DR   P17576, CARP_IRPLA ;
//
ID   3.4.23.30
DE   Pycnoporopepsin.
AN   Proteinase Ia.
CA   Specificity similar to pepsin A, but narrower, cleaving only three bonds
CA   in the B chain of insulin: 14-Ala-|-Leu-15, 16-Tyr-|-Leu-17,
CA   and 24-Phe-|-Phe-25.
CC   -!- From the basidiomycete Pycnoporus sanguineus, formerly known as
CC       P.coccineus and Trametes sanguinea.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 3.4.4.17 and EC 3.4.23.6.
//
ID   3.4.23.31
DE   Scytalidopepsin A.
AN   Scytalidium aspartic proteinase A.
CA   Hydrolysis of proteins with specificity similar to that of pepsin A,
CA   but also cleaves 7-Cys(SO(3)H)-|-Gly-8 and 17-Leu-|-Val-18 in the B chain
CA   of insulin.
CC   -!- Isolated from the imperfect fungus Scytalidium lignicolum.
CC   -!- Not inhibited by pepstatin-Ac, methyl 2-diazoacetamidohexanoate or
CC       1,2-epoxy-3-(p-nitrophenyl)propane.
CC   -!- A related enzyme from the same organism, proteinase C, is also
CC       insensitive to these inhibitors and has molecular weight 406 kDa.
//
ID   3.4.23.32
DE   Scytalidopepsin B.
AN   Scytalidium aspartic proteinase B.
CA   Hydrolysis of proteins with broad specificity, cleaving 24-Phe-|-Phe-25,
CA   but not 15-Leu-|-Tyr-16 and 25-Phe-|-Tyr-26 in the B chain of insulin.
CC   -!- Isolated from the imperfect fungus Scytalidium lignicolum.
CC   -!- A second endopeptidase from S.lignicolum (see scytalidopepsin A) that
CC       is insensitive to pepstatin and methyl 2-diazoacetamidohexanoate.
CC   -!- 1,2-epoxy-3-(p-nitrophenoxy)propane reacts with Glu-53, which
CC       replaces one of the aspartic residues at the active center.
CC   -!- One of the smallest aspartic endopeptidases active as the monomer,
CC       with molecular weight 22 kDa.
CC   -!- Similarly inhibitor-resistant endopeptidases are found in the
CC       basidiomycetes Lentinus edodes and Ganoderma lucidum, and in
CC       Polyporus tulipiferae (a second endopeptidase distinct from
CC       polyporopepsin), but these are of typical aspartic endopeptidase
CC       size.
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family G1.
PR   PROSITE; PDOC00128;
DR   P15369, PRTB_SCYLI ;
