//
ID   3.4.24.87
DE   ADAMTS13 endopeptidase.
AN   ADAMTS VWF cleaving metalloprotease.
AN   ADAMTS13 peptidase.
AN   Upshaw factor.
AN   Von Willebrand factor cleaving protease.
AN   VWF-cleaving protease.
AN   VWF-degrading protease.
CA   The enzyme cleaves the von Willebrand factor at bond 842-Tyr-|-Met-843
CA   within the A2 domain.
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family M12.
PR   PROSITE; PDOC00129;
DR   Q76LX8, ATS13_HUMAN;  Q769J6, ATS13_MOUSE;
//
ID   3.4.24.88
DE   Transferred entry: 3.4.19.15.
//
ID   3.4.24.89
DE   Pro-Pro endopeptidase.
CA   The enzyme catalyzes the hydrolytic cleavage of peptide bonds between two
CA   proline residues.
CF   Zn(2+).
CC   -!- This metalloprotease is secreted by the bacterium Peptoclostridium
CC       difficile.
DR   Q183R7, ZMP1_PEPD6 ;
//
ID   3.4.25.1
DE   Proteasome endopeptidase complex.
AN   Ingensin.
AN   Lens neutral proteinase.
AN   Macropain.
AN   Multicatalytic endopeptidase complex.
AN   Multicatalytic proteinase (complex).
AN   Prosome.
AN   Proteasome.
CA   Cleavage of peptide bonds with very broad specificity.
CC   -!- A 20-S protein composed of 28 subunits arranged in four rings of
CC       seven.
CC   -!- The outer rings are composed of alpha subunits, but the beta subunits
CC       forming the inner rings are responsible for peptidase activity.
CC   -!- In eukaryotic organisms there are up to seven different types of beta
CC       subunits, three of which may carry the N-terminal threonine residues
CC       that are the nucleophiles in catalysis, and show different
CC       specificities.
CC   -!- The molecule is barrel-shaped, and the active sites are on the inner
CC       surfaces.
CC   -!- Terminal apertures restrict access of substrates to the active sites.
CC   -!- Inhibited by mercurial reagents and some inhibitors of serine
CC       endopeptidases.
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family T1.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 3.4.22.21, EC 3.4.24.5 and EC 3.4.99.46.
