//
ID   3.4.25.2
DE   HslU--HslV peptidase.
CA   ATP-dependent cleavage of peptide bonds with broad specificity.
CC   -!- The HslU subunit of the HslU--HslV complex functions as an ATP
CC       dependent 'unfoldase'.
CC   -!- The binding of ATP and its subsequent hydrolysis by HslU are
CC       essential for unfolding of protein substrates subsequently hydrolyzed
CC       by HslV.
CC   -!- HslU recognizes the N-terminal part of its protein substrates and
CC       unfolds these before they are guided to HslV for hydrolysis.
CC   -!- Belongs to peptidase family T1.
