ID   3.5.1.51
DE   4-acetamidobutyryl-CoA deacetylase.
AN   Aminobutyryl-CoA thiolesterase.
CA   4-acetamidobutanoyl-CoA + H(2)O = acetate + 4-aminobutanoyl-CoA.
CC   -!- The enzyme also hydrolyzes 4-aminobutanoyl-CoA to aminobutanoate and
CC       coenzyme A.
//
ID   3.5.1.52
DE   Peptide-N(4)-(N-acetyl-beta-glucosaminyl)asparagine amidase.
AN   Glycopeptidase.
AN   Glycopeptide N-glycosidase.
AN   N-glycanase.
AN   N-oligosaccharide glycopeptidase.
CA   Hydrolysis of an N(4)-(acetyl-beta-D-glucosaminyl)asparagine residue in
CA   which the glucosamine residue may be further glycosylated, to yield a
CA   (substituted) N-acetyl-beta-D-glucosaminylamine and a peptide containing
CA   an aspartate residue.
CC   -!- Does not act on (GlcNAc)-Asn, because it requires the presence of
CC       more than two amino-acid residues in the substrate (cf. EC 3.5.1.26).
CC   -!- Formerly EC 3.2.2.18.
