AN   HDAC.
CA   Hydrolysis of an N(6)-acetyl-lysine residue of a histone to yield a
CA   deacetylated histone.
CC   -!- A class of enzymes that remove acetyl groups from N(6)-acetyl-lysine
CC       residues on a histone.
CC   -!- The reaction of this enzyme is opposite to that of EC 2.3.1.48.
CC   -!- Histone deacetylases (HDACs) can be organized into three classes
CC       depending on sequence similarity and domain organization.
CC   -!- Histone acetylation plays an important role in regulation of gene
CC       expression.
CC   -!- In eukaryotes, HDACs play a key role in the regulation of
CC       transcription and cell proliferation.
CC   -!- May be identical to EC 3.5.1.17.
