ID   3.5.1.114
DE   N-acyl-aromatic-L-amino acid amidohydrolase.
AN   Aminoacylase 3.
AN   Aminoacylase III.
CA   (1) An N-acyl-aromatic-L-amino acid + H(2)O = an aromatic-L-amino acid +
CA   a carboxylate.
CA   (2) An N-acetyl-L-cysteine-S-conjugate + H(2)O = an L-cysteine-S-
CA   conjugate + acetate.
CF   Zn(2+).
CC   -!- This enzyme is found in animals and is involved in the hydrolysis of
CC       N-acylated or N-acetylated amino acids (except L-aspartate).
CC   -!- It preferentially deacetylates N(alpha)-acetylated aromatic amino
CC       acids and mercapturic acids (S-conjugates of N-acetyl-L-cysteine)
CC       that are usually not deacetylated by EC 3.5.1.14.
CC   -!- Some bacterial aminoacylases demonstrate substrate specificity for
CC       both EC 3.5.1.14 and EC 3.5.1.114.
CC   -!- Cf. EC 3.5.1.14 and EC 3.5.1.15.
DR   Q6DHI0, ACY3A_DANRE;  Q6DHQ3, ACY3B_DANRE;  Q96HD9, ACY3_HUMAN ;
DR   Q91XE4, ACY3_MOUSE ;  Q5M876, ACY3_RAT   ;  A0JMS7, ACY3_XENLA ;
DR   Q5BJ91, ACY3_XENTR ;
