ID   3.5.1.128
DE   Deaminated glutathione amidase.
AN   DGSH deaminase.
CA   N-(4-oxoglutaryl)-L-cysteinylglycine + H(2)O = 2-oxoglutarate +
CA   L-cysteinylglycine.
CC   -!- The enzyme, present in animals, fungi and bacteria, is involved in
CC       clearing cells of the toxic compound deaminated glutathione, which
CC       can be produced as an unwanted side product by several transaminases.
//
