ID   3.5.2.14
DE   N-methylhydantoinase (ATP-hydrolyzing).
AN   N-methylhydantoin amidohydrolase.
CA   ATP + N-methylimidazolidine-2,4-dione + 2 H(2)O = ADP + phosphate +
CA   N-carbamoylsarcosine.
//
ID   3.5.2.15
DE   Cyanuric acid amidohydrolase.
CA   Cyanuric acid + H(2)O = biuret + CO(2).
CC   -!- Along with EC 3.5.1.54 and EC 3.5.1.84, forms part of the cyanuric-
CC       acid metabolism pathway, which degrades s-triazide herbicides, such
CC       as atrazine (2-chloro-4-(ethylamino)-6-(isopropylamino)-1,3,5-
CC       triazine), in bacteria.
CC   -!- A key enzyme in the pathway, catalyzing the ring cleavage of cyanuric
CC       acid.
CC   -!- Specific for cyanuric acid as substrate as neither the structurally
CC       related compounds ammeline (2,4-diamino-6-hydroxy-s-triazine) and
CC       ammelide (2-amino-4,6-dihydroxy-s-triazine) nor a number of
CC       pyrimidine compounds, such as uracil and cytosine, can act as
CC       substrates.
DR   A8IKD2, CAH_AZOC5  ;  Q89E06, CAH_BRADU  ;  H0SH23, CAH_BRAS3  ;
DR   P0A3V4, CAH_ENTCL  ;  B0UET5, CAH_METS4  ;  Q2RGM7, CAH_MOOTA  ;
DR   W6RJ11, CAH_PSEP5  ;  P58329, CAH_PSESD  ;  P0A3V5, CAH_PSESP  ;
DR   F4CUJ4, CAH_PSEUX  ;  Q1M7F3, CAH_RHIL3  ;  C6BAU4, CAH_RHILS  ;
DR   H8ZKW0, CAH_RHOSO  ;  U3N9N6, CAH_SARSX  ;
//
ID   3.5.2.16
DE   Maleimide hydrolase.
AN   Cyclic imide hydrolase.
AN   Imidase.
CA   Maleimide + H(2)O = maleamic acid.
CC   -!- Succinimide and glutarimide, and sulfur-containing cyclic imides,
CC       such as rhodanine, can also act as substrates for the enzyme from
CC       Blastobacter sp. A17p-4.
CC   -!- The reverse, cyclization, reaction is also catalyzed, but much more
CC       slowly.
CC   -!- It has lower activity toward cyclic ureides, which are the substrates
CC       of EC 3.5.2.2.
//
ID   3.5.2.17
DE   Hydroxyisourate hydrolase.
AN   5-hydroxyisourate hydrolase.
AN   HIUHase.
CA   5-hydroxyisourate + H(2)O = 5-hydroxy-2-oxo-4-ureido-2,5-dihydro-
CA   1H-imidazole-5-carboxylate.
CC   -!- The reaction is the first stage in the conversion of
CC       5-hydroxyisourate into (S)-allantoin.
CC   -!- This reaction will also occur spontaneously, but more slowly.
