//
ID   3.5.99.10
DE   2-iminobutanoate/2-iminopropanoate deaminase.
AN   Enamine/imine deaminase.
CA   (1) 2-iminobutanoate + H(2)O = 2-oxobutanoate + NH(3).
CA   (2) 2-iminopropanoate + H(2)O = pyruvate + NH(3).
CC   -!- This enzyme, which has been found in all species and tissues
CC       examined, catalyzes the hydrolytic deamination of imine intermediates
CC       formed by several types of pyridoxal-5'-phosphate-dependent
CC       dehydratases, such as EC 4.3.1.19 and EC 4.3.1.17.
CC   -!- The reactions, which can occur spontaneously, are accelerated to
CC       minimize the cellular damage that could be caused by these reactive
CC       intermediates.
