ID   3.6.1.59
DE   5'-(N(7)-methyl 5'-triphosphoguanosine)-[mRNA] diphosphatase.
AN   M(7)GpppN m(7)GMP phosphohydrolase.
AN   M(7)GpppX diphosphatase.
AN   M(7)GpppX pyrophosphatase.
CA   A 5'-(N(7)-methyl 5'-triphosphoguanosine)-[mRNA] + H(2)O = N(7)-
CA   methylguanosine 5'-phosphate + a 5'-diphospho-[mRNA].
CC   -!- The enzyme removes (decaps) the N(7)-methylguanosine 5-phosphate cap
CC       from an mRNA degraded to a maximal length of 10 nucleotides.
CC   -!- Decapping is an important process in the control of eukaryotic mRNA
CC       degradation.
CC   -!- The enzyme functions to clear the cell of cap structure following
CC       decay of the RNA body.
CC   -!- The nematode enzyme can also decap triply methylated substrates,
CC       5'-(N(2),N(2),N(7)-trimethyl 5'-triphosphoguanosine)-[mRNA].
CC   -!- Formerly EC 3.6.1.30.
DR   D3K0N9, DCPS_ASCSU ;  Q8MJJ7, DCPS_BOVIN ;  G5EFS4, DCPS_CAEEL ;
DR   Q96C86, DCPS_HUMAN ;  Q9DAR7, DCPS_MOUSE ;  Q8MIZ3, DCPS_PIG   ;
