ID   3.6.1.60
DE   Diadenosine hexaphosphate hydrolase (AMP-forming).
CA   (1) P(1),P(6)-bis(5'-adenosyl)hexaphosphate + H(2)O = adenosine
CA   5'-pentaphosphate + AMP.
CA   (2) P(1),P(5)-bis(5'-adenosyl)pentaphosphate + H(2)O = adenosine
CA   5'-tetraphosphate + AMP.
CC   -!- A divalent cation is essential for activity.
CC   -!- Mn(2+) (2-6 mM) is most effective.
CC   -!- The enzyme controls intracellular levels of P(1),P(5)-
CC       bis(5'-adenosyl)pentaphosphate and P(1),P(6)-
CC       bis(5'-adenosyl)hexaphosphate.
CC   -!- Weak activity with P(1),P(4)-bis(5'-adenosyl)tetraphosphate.
CC   -!- Marked preference for adenine over guanine nucleotides.
DR   Q99321, DDP1_YEAST ;  Q8NFP7, NUD10_HUMAN;  P0C027, NUD10_MOUSE;
DR   Q58CW0, NUD11_BOVIN;  Q96G61, NUD11_HUMAN;  P0C028, NUD11_MOUSE;
//
ID   3.6.1.61
DE   Diadenosine hexaphosphate hydrolase (ATP-forming).
CA   (1) P(1),P(6)-bis(5'-adenosyl)hexaphosphate + H(2)O = 2 ATP.
CA   (2) P(1),P(5)-bis(5'-adenosyl)pentaphosphate + H(2)O = ATP + ADP.
CA   (3) P(1),P(4)-bis(5'-adenosyl)tetraphosphate + H(2)O = ATP + AMP.
CF   Divalent cation.
CC   -!- The enzyme hydrolyzes P(1),P(4)-bis(5-guanosyl) tetraphosphate very
CC       slowly (cf. EC 3.6.1.17).
DR   Q75UV1, NDX1_THETH ;
//
ID   3.6.1.62
DE   5'-(N(7)-methylguanosine 5'-triphospho)-[mRNA] hydrolase.
AN   M(7)GpppN-mRNA hydrolase.
CA   5'-(N(7)-methylguanosine 5'-triphospho)-[mRNA] + H(2)O = N(7)-
CA   methylguanosine 5'-diphosphate + 5'-phospho-[mRNA].
CC   -!- Decapping of mRNA is a critical step in eukaryotic mRNA turnover.
CC   -!- The enzyme is unable to cleave a free cap structure (m(7)GpppG).
CC   -!- The enzyme from Vaccinia virus is synergistically activated in the
CC       presence of Mg(2+) and Mn(2+).
