CC   -!- Involved in muscle contraction.
CC   -!- In the absence of actin, myosin shows only low ATPase activity, which
CC       requires Ca(2+).
CC   -!- Formerly EC 3.6.1.32.
//
ID   3.6.4.2
DE   Dynein ATPase.
CA   ATP + H(2)O = ADP + phosphate.
CC   -!- A multisubunit protein complex associated with microtubules.
CC   -!- Hydrolysis of ATP provides energy for the movement of organelles
CC       (endosomes, lysosomes, mitochondria) along microtubules to the
CC       centrosome toward the microtubule's minus end.
CC   -!- It also functions in the movement of eukaryotic flagella and cilia.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 3.6.1.33.
//
ID   3.6.4.3
DE   Transferred entry: 5.6.1.1.
//
ID   3.6.4.4
DE   Plus-end-directed kinesin ATPase.
AN   Kinesin.
CA   ATP + H(2)O = ADP + phosphate.
CC   -!- Microtubular motor protein, involved in organelle movement,
CC       in mitosis and meiosis.
CC   -!- In contrast to dynein, it moves along microtubules toward the plus
CC       end.
CC   -!- Also hydrolyzes GTP.
PR   PROSITE; PDOC00343;
//
ID   3.6.4.5
DE   Minus-end-directed kinesin ATPase.
CA   ATP + H(2)O = ADP + phosphate.
CC   -!- Structurally almost identical to EC 3.6.4.3 but the movement it
CC       catalyzes is toward the minus end of microtubules.
PR   PROSITE; PDOC00343;
//
ID   3.6.4.6
DE   Vesicle-fusing ATPase.
CA   ATP + H(2)O = ADP + phosphate.
CC   -!- A large family of ATP-hydrolyzing enzymes involved in the heterotypic
CC       fusion of membrane vesicles with target membranes and the homotypic
CC       fusion of various membrane compartments.
CC   -!- They belong to the AAA-type (ATPase associated with a variety of cell
CC       activities) ATPase superfamily.
CC   -!- They include peroxin, which apparently is involved in Zellweger's
CC       syndrome.
PR   PROSITE; PDOC00572;
