ID   3.6.4.7
DE   Peroxisome-assembly ATPase.
AN   Peroxisome assembly factor-2.
CA   ATP + H(2)O = ADP + phosphate.
CC   -!- An extremely diversified group of enzymes that use the energy of ATP
CC       hydrolysis to import and assemble peroxisome components into the
CC       organelle.
CC   -!- Their molecular masses range from 25 to 600 kDa.
//
ID   3.6.4.8
DE   Proteasome ATPase.
AN   RP triphosphatase.
AN   RP triple-A protein.
CA   ATP + H(2)O = ADP + phosphate.
CC   -!- Belongs to the AAA-type superfamily and, like EC 3.6.4.5, is involved
CC       in channel gating and polypeptide unfolding before proteolysis in the
CC       proteasome.
CC   -!- Six ATPase subunits are present in the regulatory particle (RP) of
CC       26S proteasome.
PR   PROSITE; PDOC00572;
//
ID   3.6.4.9
DE   Chaperonin ATPase.
AN   Chaperonin.
CA   ATP + H(2)O = ADP + phosphate.
CC   -!- Multisubunit proteins with 2x7 (Type I, in most cells) or 2x8 (Type
CC       II, in archaea) ATP-binding sites involved in maintaining an unfolded
CC       polypeptide structure before folding or to entry into mitochondria
CC       and chloroplasts.
CC   -!- Molecular masses of subunits ranges from 10-90 kDa.
