ID   3.6.4.12
DE   DNA helicase.
CA   ATP + H(2)O = ADP + phosphate.
CC   -!- DNA helicases utilize the energy from ATP hydrolysis to unwind
CC       double-stranded DNA.
CC   -!- Some of them unwind duplex DNA with a 3' to 5' polarity (1,3,5,8),
CC       other show 5' to 3' polarity (10,11,12,13) or unwind DNA in both
CC       directions (14,15).
CC   -!- Some helicases unwind DNA as well as RNA (4,9).
CC   -!- May be identical with EC 3.6.4.13 (RNA helicase).
