//
ID   4.1.2.5
DE   L-threonine aldolase.
AN   L-threonine acetaldehyde-lyase.
CA   L-threonine = glycine + acetaldehyde.
CF   Pyridoxal 5'-phosphate.
CC   -!- This enzyme is specific for L-threonine and can not utilize L-allo-
CC       threonine.
CC   -!- Different from EC 4.1.2.49 and EC 4.1.2.48.
//
ID   4.1.2.6
DE   Deleted entry.
//
ID   4.1.2.7
DE   Transferred entry: 4.1.2.13.
//
ID   4.1.2.8
DE   Indole-3-glycerol-phosphate lyase.
AN   (1S,2R)-1-C-(indol-3-yl)glycerol 3-phosphate D-glyceraldehyde-3-
AN   phosphate-lyase.
AN   Indole glycerol phosphate hydrolase.
AN   Indole synthase.
AN   Indole-3-glycerol phosphate lyase.
AN   Indole-3-glycerolphosphate D-glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate-lyase.
AN   Indoleglycerolphosphate aldolase.
AN   Tryptophan synthase alpha.
AN   TSA.
CA   (1S,2R)-1-C-(indol-3-yl)glycerol 3-phosphate = indole + D-glyceraldehyde
CA   3-phosphate.
CC   -!- Forms part of the defense mechanism against insects and microbial
CC       pathogens in the grass family, Gramineae, where it catalyzes one of
CC       the steps in the formation of the cyclic hydroxamic acids 2,4-
CC       dihydroxy-2H-1,4-benzoxazin-3(4H)-one (DIBOA) and 2,4-dihydroxy-7-
CC       methoxy-2H-1,4-benzoxazin-3(4H)-one (DIMBOA).
CC   -!- Resembles the alpha-subunit of EC 4.2.1.20 but, unlike tryptophan
CC       synthase, its activity is independent of the beta-subunit and free
CC       indole is released.
PR   PROSITE; PDOC00151;
DR   O22765, TRPA1_ARATH;  Q42529, TRPA2_ARATH;  P42390, TRPA_MAIZE ;
//
ID   4.1.2.9
DE   Phosphoketolase.
AN   D-xylulose-5-phosphate D-glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate-lyase (phosphate-
AN   acetylating).
AN   Xylulose-5-phosphate phosphoketolase.
CA   D-xylulose 5-phosphate + phosphate = acetyl phosphate + D-glyceraldehyde
CA   3-phosphate + H(2)O.
CF   Thiamine diphosphate.
DR   Q9AEM9, XFP_BIFAS  ;  Q937F6, XPKA_LACPE ;
//
ID   4.1.2.10
DE   (R)-mandelonitrile lyase.
AN   (R)-oxynitrilase.
AN   D-oxynitrilase.
AN   Hydroxynitrile lyase.
AN   Mandelonitrile benzaldehyde-lyase.
CA   (R)-mandelonitrile = cyanide + benzaldehyde.
CF   Flavoprotein.
CC   -!- A variety of enzymes from different sources and with different
CC       properties.
CC   -!- Some are flavoproteins, others are not.
CC   -!- Active toward a number of aromatic and aliphatic hydroxynitriles
CC       (cyanohydrins).
DR   Q9LFT6, HNL_ARATH  ;  O24243, MDL1_PRUDU ;  P52706, MDL1_PRUSE ;
DR   Q945K2, MDL2_PRUDU ;  O50048, MDL2_PRUSE ;  P52707, MDL3_PRUSE ;
DR   O82784, MDL4_PRUSE ;  Q9SSM2, MDLL_ARATH ;
//
ID   4.1.2.11
DE   Hydroxymandelonitrile lyase.
AN   (S)-4-hydroxymandelonitrile hydroxybenzaldehyde-lyase.
AN   Hydroxynitrile lyase.
CA   (S)-4-hydroxymandelonitrile = cyanide + 4-hydroxybenzaldehyde.
CC   -!- Does not accept aliphatic hydroxynitriles, unlike EC 4.1.2.10,
CC       EC 4.1.2.46 and EC 4.1.2.47.
DR   P52708, HNLS_SORBI ;
//
ID   4.1.2.12
DE   2-dehydropantoate aldolase.
AN   2-dehydropantoate formaldehyde-lyase.
AN   Ketopantoaldolase.
CA   2-dehydropantoate = 3-methyl-2-oxobutanoate + formaldehyde.
//
ID   4.1.2.13
DE   Fructose-bisphosphate aldolase.
AN   Aldolase.
AN   D-fructose-1,6-bisphosphate D-glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate-lyase.
AN   Fructose-1,6-bisphosphate triosephosphate-lyase.
CA   D-fructose 1,6-bisphosphate = glycerone phosphate + D-glyceraldehyde
CA   3-phosphate.
CF   Zn(2+).
CC   -!- Also acts on (3S,4R)-ketose 1-phosphates.
CC   -!- The enzymes increase electron-attraction by the carbonyl group, some
CC       (Class I) forming a protonated imine with it, others (Class II),
CC       mainly of microbial origin, polarizing it with a metal ion, e.g.
CC       zinc.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 4.1.2.7.
PR   PROSITE; PDOC00143;
