//
ID   4.1.99.18
DE   Transferred entry: 4.1.99.22 and 4.6.1.17.
//
ID   4.1.99.19
DE   2-iminoacetate synthase.
CA   L-tyrosine + S-adenosyl-L-methionine + NADPH = 2-iminoacetate +
CA   4-methylphenol + 5'-deoxyadenosine + L-methionine + NADP(+) + H(+).
CF   Iron-sulfur.
CC   -!- Binds a [4Fe-4S] cluster that is coordinated by 3 cysteines and an
CC       exchangeable S-adenosyl-L-methionine molecule.
CC   -!- The first stage of catalysis is reduction of the S-adenosyl-L-
CC       methionine to produce methionine and a 5-deoxyadenosin-5-yl radical
CC       that is crucial for the conversion of the substrate.
CC   -!- Part of the pathway for thiamine biosynthesis.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 1.3.99.n2.
DR   P30140, THIH_ECOLI ;  Q9S498, THIH_SALTY ;
//
ID   4.1.99.20
DE   3-amino-4-hydroxybenzoate synthase.
AN   3,4-AHBA synthase.
CA   2-amino-4,5-dihydroxy-6-oxo-7-(phosphooxy)heptanoate = 3-amino-4-
CA   hydroxybenzoate + phosphate + 2 H(2)O.
CF   Mn(2+).
CC   -!- The reaction is suggested to take place in several steps.
CC   -!- Schiff base formation, double bond migration and dephosphorylation
CC       followed by ring opening and closing to form a pyrrolidine ring,
CC       and finally dehydration to form the product 3-amino-4-
CC       hydroxybenzoate.
CC   -!- In the bacterium Streptomyces griseus the enzyme is involved in
CC       biosynthesis of grixazone, a yellow pigment that contains a
CC       phenoxazinone chromophore.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 4.3.3.n1.
DR   B1VTI7, GRIH_STRGG ;  A0JC76, GRIH_STRGR ;
//
ID   4.1.99.21
DE   Transferred entry: 4.2.3.153.
//
ID   4.1.99.22
DE   GTP 3',8-cyclase.
CA   GTP + S-adenosyl-L-methionine + reduced electron acceptor = (8S)-3',8-
CA   cyclo-7,8-dihydroguanosine 5'-triphosphate + 5'-deoxyadenosine +
CA   L-methionine + oxidized electron acceptor.
CF   Iron-sulfur; S-adenosyl-L-methionine.
CC   -!- The enzyme catalyzes an early step in the biosynthesis of the
CC       molybdenum cofactor (MoCo).
CC   -!- The enzyme belongs to the superfamily of radical S-adenosyl-L-
CC       methionine (radical SAM) enzymes.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 4.1.99.18.
