DE   ATP-dependent NAD(P)H-hydrate dehydratase.
AN   ATP-dependent H(4)NAD(P)OH dehydratase.
CA   (1) ATP + (6S)-6-beta-hydroxy-1,4,5,6-tetrahydronicotinamide-adenine
CA   dinucleotide = ADP + phosphate + NADH.
CA   (2) ATP + (6S)-6-beta-hydroxy-1,4,5,6-tetrahydronicotinamide-adenine
CA   dinucleotide phosphate = ADP + phosphate + NADPH.
CC   -!- Acts equally well on hydrated NADH and hydrated NADPH.
CC   -!- NAD(P)H spontaneously hydrates to both the (6S)- and (6R)- isomers,
CC       and these are interconverted by EC 5.1.99.6, to a 60:40 ratio.
CC   -!- Hence EC 4.2.1.93 together with EC 5.1.99.6 can restore the mixture
CC       of hydrates into NAD(P)H.
CC   -!- The enzyme from eukaryotes has no activity with ADP, contrary to the
CC       enzyme from bacteria (cf. EC 4.2.1.136).
