ID   4.2.1.115
DE   UDP-N-acetylglucosamine 4,6-dehydratase (inverting).
AN   UDP-N-acetylglucosamine 5-inverting 4,6-dehydratase.
CA   UDP-N-acetyl-alpha-D-glucosamine = UDP-2-acetamido-2,6-dideoxy-beta-L-
CA   arabino-hex-4-ulose + H(2)O.
CF   NADPH.
CC   -!- The first enzyme in the biosynthetic pathway of pseudaminic acid,
CC       a sialic-acid-like sugar that is unique to bacteria and is used by
CC       Helicobacter pylori to modify its flagellin.
CC   -!- Plays a critical role in H.pylori's pathogenesis, being involved in
CC       the synthesis of both functional flagella and lipopolysaccharides.
CC   -!- Completely inhibited by UDP-alpha-D-galactose.
CC   -!- The reaction results in the chirality of the C-5 atom being inverted.
CC   -!- It is thought that Lys-133 acts sequentially as a catalytic acid,
CC       protonating the C-6 hydroxy group and as a catalytic base,
CC       abstracting the C-5 proton, resulting in the elimination of water.
DR   Q0P8W4, PSEB_CAMJE ;  Q5QKR8, PSEB_CAMJJ ;  O25511, PSEB_HELPY ;
//
ID   4.2.1.116
DE   3-hydroxypropionyl-CoA dehydratase.
AN   3-hydroxypropanoate-CoA dehydratase.
AN   3-hydroxypropionyl-CoA hydro-lyase.
CA   3-hydroxypropanoyl-CoA = acryloyl-CoA + H(2)O.
CC   -!- Catalyzes a step in the 3-hydroxypropanoate/4-hydroxybutyrate cycle,
CC       an autotrophic CO(2) fixation pathway found in some thermoacidophilic
CC       archaea.
CC   -!- The enzyme from Metallosphaera sedula acts nearly equally as well on
CC       (S)-3-hydroxybutanoyl-CoA but not (R)-3-hydroxybutanoyl-CoA.
PR   PROSITE; PDOC00150;
DR   A4YI89, HPCD_METS5 ;
//
ID   4.2.1.117
DE   2-methylcitrate dehydratase (2-methyl-trans-aconitate forming).
CA   (2S,3S)-2-methylcitrate = 2-methyl-trans-aconitate + H(2)O.
CF   Iron-sulfur.
CC   -!- Catalyzes the dehydration of (2S,3S)-2-methylcitrate, forming the
CC       trans isomer of 2-methyl-aconitate (unlike EC 4.2.1.79, which forms
CC       only the cis isomer).
CC   -!- Part of a propanoate degradation pathway.
CC   -!- The enzyme from Shewanella oneidensis can also accept citrate and
CC       cis-aconitate, but activity with (2S,3S)-2-methylcitrate was
CC       approximately 2.5-fold higher.
CC   -!- 2-methylisocitrate and isocitrate were not substrates.
DR   Q8EJW3, ACND_SHEON ;
