ID   4.2.1.136
DE   ADP-dependent NAD(P)H-hydrate dehydratase.
AN   (6S)-6-beta-hydroxy-1,4,5,6-tetrahydronicotinamide-adenine-dinucleotide
AN   hydro-lyase (ADP-hydrolyzing; NADH-forming).
AN   (6S)-beta-6-hydroxy-1,4,5,6-tetrahydronicotinamide-adenine-dinucleotide
AN   hydro-lyase(ADP-hydrolyzing).
CA   (1) ADP + (6S)-6-beta-hydroxy-1,4,5,6-tetrahydronicotinamide adenine-
CA   dinucleotide = AMP + phosphate + NADH.
CA   (2) ADP + (6S)-6-beta-hydroxy-1,4,5,6-tetrahydronicotinamide adenine-
CA   dinucleotide phosphate = AMP + phosphate + NADPH.
CC   -!- Acts equally well on hydrated NADH and hydrated NADPH.
CC   -!- NAD(P)H spontaneously hydrates to both the (6S)- and (6R)- isomers.
CC   -!- The enzyme from bacteria consists of two domains, one of which acts
CC       as an NAD(P)H-hydrate epimerase that interconverts the two isomers to
CC       a 60:40 ratio (cf. EC 5.1.99.6), while the other catalyzes the
CC       dehydration.
CC   -!- Hence the enzyme can restore the complete mixture of isomers into
CC       NAD(P)H.
CC   -!- The enzyme has no activity with ATP, contrary to the enzyme from
CC       eukaryotes (cf. EC 4.2.1.93).
DR   P94368, NNRD_BACSU ;  Q7VU32, NNRD_BORPE ;  A0RU82, NNRD_CENSY ;
