DR   B0XPA2, RGLB_ASPFC ;  B8N5T6, RGLB_ASPFN ;  Q4WR79, RGLB_ASPFU ;
DR   A5ABH4, RGLB_ASPNC ;  Q2UDJ8, RGLB_ASPOR ;  Q0C7K7, RGLB_ASPTN ;
DR   Q5AZ85, RGLB_EMENI ;  A1D144, RGLB_NEOFI ;  Q2U5P7, RGLC_ASPOR ;
DR   Q5B5P1, RGLC_EMENI ;  Q8RJP2, RHIE_DICD3 ;  O31526, YESW_BACSU ;
//
ID   4.2.2.24
DE   Rhamnogalacturonan exolyase.
CA   Exotype eliminative cleavage of alpha-L-rhamnopyranosyl-(1->4)-alpha-D-
CA   galactopyranosyluronic acid bonds of rhamnogalacturonan I
CA   oligosaccharides containing alpha-L-rhamnopyranose at the reducing end
CA   and 4-deoxy-4,5-unsaturated D-galactopyranosyluronic acid at the non-
CA   reducing end. The products are the disaccharide 2-O-(4-deoxy-beta-L-
CA   threo-hex-4-enopyranuronosyl)-alpha-L-rhamnopyranose and the shortened
CA   rhamnogalacturonan oligosaccharide containing one 4-deoxy-4,5-unsaturated
CA   D-galactopyranosyluronic acid at the non-reducing end.
CC   -!- The enzyme is part of the degradation system for rhamnogalacturonan I
CC       in Bacillus subtilis strain 168.
DR   O31527, YESX_BACSU ;
//
ID   4.2.2.25
DE   Gellan lyase.
CA   Eliminative cleavage of beta-D-glucopyranosyl-(1->4)-beta-D-
CA   glucopyranosyluronate bonds of gellan backbone releasing tetrasaccharides
CA   containing a 4-deoxy-4,5-unsaturated D-glucopyranosyluronic acid at the
CA   non-reducing end. The tetrasaccharide produced from deacetylated gellan
CA   is beta-D-4-deoxy-Delta(4)-GlcAp-(1->4)-beta-D-Glcp-(1->4)-alpha-L-Rhap-
CA   (1->3)-beta-D-Glcp.
CC   -!- The enzyme is highly specific to gellan, especially deacetylated
CC       gellan.
DR   O82833, GELLY_BACSP;  P85513, GELL_GEOSE ;
//
ID   4.2.2.26
DE   Oligo-alginate lyase.
AN   Exo-oligoalginate lyase.
AN   Oligoalginate lyase.
CA   Cleavage of 4-deoxy-alpha-L-erythro-hex-4-enopyranuronoside
CA   oligosaccharides into 4-deoxy-alpha-L-erythro-hex-4-enopyranuronate
CA   monosaccharides.
CC   -!- The enzyme degrades unsaturated oligosaccharides produced by the
CC       action of alginate lyases (EC 4.2.2.3 and EC 4.2.2.11) on alginate,
CC       by repeatedly removing the unsaturated residue from the non-reducing
CC       end until only unsaturated monosaccharides are left.
CC   -!- The enzyme catalyzes a beta-elimination reaction, generating a new
CC       unsaturated non-reducing end after removal of the pre-existing one.
DR   Q21FJ0, EALGL_SACD2;  B2FSW8, EALGL_STRMK;
