//
ID   4.2.3.7
DE   Pentalenene synthase.
AN   Pentalenene synthetase.
CA   (2E,6E)-farnesyl diphosphate = pentalenene + diphosphate.
CC   -!- Isolated from Streptomyces avermitilis.
CC   -!- The enzyme is involved in the biosynthesis of pentalenolactone and
CC       related antibiotics.
CC   -!- The 9si hydrogen of farnesyl diphosphate undergoes a 1,2-hydride
CC       shift where it becomes the 1-alpha hydrogen of pentalenene.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 4.6.1.5.
DR   Q55012, PENA_STREX ;  E3VWJ0, PNTA_STRAE ;  Q82IY4, PTLA_STRAW ;
//
ID   4.2.3.8
DE   Casbene synthase.
AN   Casbene synthetase.
CA   Geranylgeranyl diphosphate = casbene + diphosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme from castor bean (Ricinus communis) produces the
CC       antifungal diterpene casbene.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 4.6.1.7.
DR   P59287, CASS_RICCO ;
//
ID   4.2.3.9
DE   Aristolochene synthase.
AN   Sesquiterpene cyclase.
AN   Trans,trans-farnesyl diphosphate aristolochene-lyase.
CA   (2E,6E)-farnesyl diphosphate = aristolochene + diphosphate.
CF   Mg(2+); Mn(2+).
CC   -!- The initial internal cyclization produces the monocyclic intermediate
CC       germacrene A; further cyclization and methyl transfer converts the
CC       intermediate into aristolochene.
CC   -!- While in some species germacrene A remains as an enzyme-bound
CC       intermediate, it has been shown to be a minor product of the reaction
CC       in Penicillium roqueforti (see also EC 4.2.3.23).
CC   -!- Aristolochene is the likely parent compound for a number of
CC       sesquiterpenes produced by filamentous fungi.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 2.5.1.40 and EC 4.1.99.7.
DR   Q9UR08, ARIS_ASPTE ;  Q03471, PRX2_PENRO ;  B6H063, PRX2_PENRW ;
//
ID   4.2.3.10
DE   (-)-endo-fenchol synthase.
CA   Geranyl diphosphate = (-)-endo-fenchol + diphosphate.
CC   -!- (3R)-linalyl diphosphate is an intermediate in the reaction.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 4.6.1.8.
DR   Q5SBP2, FES_OCIBA  ;
//
ID   4.2.3.11
DE   Sabinene-hydrate synthase.
AN   Sabinene hydrate cyclase.
CA   Geranyl diphosphate + H(2)O = sabinene hydrate + diphosphate.
CC   -!- Both cis- and trans- isomers of sabinene hydrate are formed.
CC   -!- (3R)-linalyl diphosphate is an intermediate in the reaction.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 4.6.1.9.
//
ID   4.2.3.12
DE   6-pyruvoyltetrahydropterin synthase.
AN   6-pyruvoyl tetrahydrobiopterin synthase.
AN   PTPS.
CA   7,8-dihydroneopterin 3'-triphosphate = 6-pyruvoyl-5,6,7,8-
CA   tetrahydropterin + triphosphate.
CF   Mg(2+).
CC   -!- Catalyzes triphosphate elimination and an intramolecular redox
CC       reaction.
CC   -!- The product is 6-pyruvoyltetrahydrobiopterin.
CC   -!- Involved in the de novo synthesis of tetrahydrobiopterin from GTP,
CC       with the other enzymes involved being EC 1.1.1.153 and EC 3.5.4.16.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 4.6.1.10.
PR   PROSITE; PDOC00759;
DR   O02058, PTPS_CAEEL ;  Q1ZXI0, PTPS_DICDI ;  P48611, PTPS_DROME ;
DR   Q03393, PTPS_HUMAN ;  Q9R1Z7, PTPS_MOUSE ;  Q90W95, PTPS_POERE ;
DR   Q5REZ5, PTPS_PONAB ;  P27213, PTPS_RAT   ;  P80081, PTPS_SALSA ;
//
ID   4.2.3.13
DE   (+)-delta-cadinene synthase.
AN   D-cadinene synthase.
CA   (2E,6E)-farnesyl diphosphate = (+)-delta-cadinene + diphosphate.
CF   Mg(2+).
CC   -!- The sesquiterpenoid (+)-delta-cadinene is an intermediate in
CC       phytoalexin biosynthesis.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 4.6.1.11.
DR   Q39761, DCS1_GOSAR ;  P93665, DCS1_GOSHI ;  Q39760, DCS2_GOSAR ;
DR   Q43714, DCS3_GOSAR ;  O49853, DCS4_GOSAR ;  B2KSJ5, GCSY1_CUCME;
DR   K4L9M2, STS1_THAGA ;  B9S9Z3, TPS1_RICCO ;
//
ID   4.2.3.14
DE   Transferred entry: 4.2.3.119 and 4.2.3.120.
//
ID   4.2.3.15
DE   Myrcene synthase.
CA   Geranyl diphosphate = myrcene + diphosphate.
CF   K(+); Mn(2+).
CC   -!- Mg(2+) is essentially ineffective as the divalent metal ion cofactor.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 4.1.99.9.
DR   B6SCF4, MTS2_HUMLU ;  Q9LRZ6, MYRS2_ARATH;  Q5SBP1, MYRS_OCIBA ;
DR   Q93X23, MYRS_QUEIL ;  Q84ND0, TPS2_ANTMA ;  Q84NC9, TPS3_ANTMA ;
DR   G1JUH1, TPS3_SOLLC ;  Q9ZUH4, TPSA_ARATH ;  O24474, TPSD2_ABIGR;
//
ID   4.2.3.16
DE   (4S)-limonene synthase.
AN   (-)-(4S)-limonene synthase.
AN   4S-(-)-limonene synthase.
CA   Geranyl diphosphate = (-)-(4S)-limonene + diphosphate.
CF   K(+); Mn(2+).
