//
ID   4.2.3.102
DE   Sesquithujene synthase.
AN   TPS5-del1.
CA   (2E,6E)-farnesyl diphosphate = sesquithujene + diphosphate.
CF   Mn(2+) or Mg(2+).
CC   -!- The enzyme from Zea mays, variety Delprim, gives mainly sesquithujene
CC       with (S)-beta-bisabolene and (E)-beta-farnesene plus traces of other
CC       sesquiterpenoids, cf. EC 4.2.3.55 and EC 4.2.3.47.
CC   -!- The exact product ratio is dependent on which metal ion is present.
DR   Q6JD70, TPS5A_MAIZE;
//
ID   4.2.3.103
DE   Ent-isokaurene synthase.
AN   Ent-isokaur-15-ene synthase.
CA   Ent-copalyl diphosphate = ent-isokaurene + diphosphate.
CC   -!- Two enzymes of the rice sub-species Oryza sativa subsp. indica,
CC       OsKSL5 and OsKSL6, produce ent-isokaurene.
CC   -!- A variant of OsKSL5 from the sub-species Oryza sativa subsp. japonica
CC       produces ent-pimara-8(14),15-diene instead (cf. EC 4.2.3.30).
CC   -!- Formerly EC 4.2.3.n8.
DR   A4KAG7, KSL5_ORYSI ;  A4KAG8, KSL6_ORYSJ ;
//
ID   4.2.3.104
DE   Alpha-humulene synthase.
AN   ZSS1.
CA   (2E,6E)-farnesyl diphosphate = alpha-humulene + diphosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme from Zingiber zerumbet, shampoo ginger, also gives traces
CC       of beta-caryophyllene.
DR   Q4U3F6, CS_HELAN   ;  B6SCF5, STS1_HUMLU ;  B1B1U3, ZSS1_ZINZE ;
//
ID   4.2.3.105
DE   Tricyclene synthase.
CA   Geranyl diphosphate = tricyclene + diphosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme from Solanum lycopersicum (tomato) gives a mixture of
CC       tricyclene, camphene, beta-myrcene, limonene, and traces of several
CC       other monoterpenoids.
CC   -!- See EC 4.2.3.117, EC 4.2.3.15 and EC 4.2.3.16.
DR   A4FVP2, TPS03_ARATH;  Q84NC8, TPS1_ANTMA ;  Q84ND0, TPS2_ANTMA ;
DR   Q672F7, TPS2_LOTJA ;  Q84NC9, TPS3_ANTMA ;  G1JUH1, TPS3_SOLLC ;
DR   Q5UB07, TPS4_MEDTR ;  Q9ZUH4, TPSA_ARATH ;
//
ID   4.2.3.106
DE   (E)-beta-ocimene synthase.
AN   Beta-ocimene synthase.
CA   Geranyl diphosphate = (E)-beta-ocimene + diphosphate.
CC   -!- Widely distributed in plants, which release beta-ocimene when
CC       attacked by herbivorous insects.
DR   A4FVP2, TPS03_ARATH;  Q84NC8, TPS1_ANTMA ;  Q672F7, TPS2_LOTJA ;
DR   I6RE61, TPS4_MATCR ;  Q5UB07, TPS4_MEDTR ;  Q9ZUH4, TPSA_ARATH ;
//
ID   4.2.3.107
DE   (+)-car-3-ene synthase.
AN   3-carene cyclase.
CA   Geranyl diphosphate = (+)-car-3-ene + diphosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme reacts with (3S)-linalyl diphosphate twice as rapidly as
CC       geranyl diphosphate, but 25 times as rapidly as (3R)-linalyl
CC       diphosphate.
CC   -!- It is assumed that (3S)-linalyl diphosphate is normally formed as an
CC       enzyme bound intermediate in the reaction.
CC   -!- In the reaction the 5-pro-R hydrogen of geranyl diphosphate is
CC       eliminated during cyclopropane ring formation.
CC   -!- In Picea abies (Norway spruce) and Picea sitchensis (Sitka spruce)
CC       terpinolene is also formed.
CC   -!- See EC 4.2.3.113.
CC   -!- (+)-car-3-ene is associated with resistance of Picea sitchensis
CC       (Sitka spruce) to white pine weevil.
DR   Q84SM8, 3CAR1_PICAB;  C7ASI9, 3CAR1_PICGL;  F1CKI6, 3CAR1_PICSI;
DR   F1CKI8, 3CAR2_PICSI;  F1CKI9, 3CAR3_PICSI;
//
ID   4.2.3.108
DE   1,8-cineole synthase.
AN   1,8-cineole cyclase.
CA   Geranyl diphosphate + H(2)O = 1,8-cineole + diphosphate.
CF   Zn(2+) or Mn(2+).
CC   -!- 1,8-cineole is the main product from the enzyme with just traces of
CC       other monoterpenoids.
CC   -!- The oxygen atom is derived from water.
CC   -!- The reaction proceeds via linalyl diphosphate and alpha-terpineol,
CC       the stereochemistry of both depends on the organism.
CC   -!- However neither intermediate can substitute for geranyl diphosphate.
CC   -!- The reaction in Salvia officinalis (sage) proceeds via (-)-(3R)-
CC       linalyl diphosphate while that in Arabidopsis (rock cress) proceeds
CC       via (+)-(3S)-linalyl diphosphate.
DR   P0DI76, CIN1_ARATH ;  P0DI77, CIN2_ARATH ;  B5GMG2, CNSA_STRC2 ;
DR   O81191, SCS_SALOF  ;
//
ID   4.2.3.109
DE   (-)-sabinene synthase.
CA   Geranyl diphosphate = (-)-sabinene + diphosphate.
CF   Mg(2+).
CC   -!- Isolated from Pinus contorta (lodgepole pine) as cyclase I and from
CC       Conocephalum conicum (liverwort).
//
ID   4.2.3.110
DE   (+)-sabinene synthase.
CA   Geranyl diphosphate = (+)-sabinene + diphosphate.
CC   -!- Isolated from Salvia officinalis (sage).
CC   -!- The recombinant enzyme gave 63% (+)-sabinene, 21% gamma-terpinene,
CC       and traces of other monoterpenoids.
CC   -!- See EC 4.2.3.114.
DR   F1CKJ1, SSS_PICSI  ;  O81193, SSS_SALOF  ;
//
ID   4.2.3.111
DE   (-)-alpha-terpineol synthase.
CA   Geranyl diphosphate + H(2)O = (-)-alpha-terpineol + diphosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme has been characterized from Vitis vinifera (grape).
CC   -!- Also forms some 1,8-cineole and traces of other monoterpenoids.
DR   B3TPQ7, ATESY_MAGGA;  Q6PWU2, ATESY_VITVI;  Q84KL4, PT10_PINTA ;
//
ID   4.2.3.112
DE   (+)-alpha-terpineol synthase.
CA   Geranyl diphosphate + H(2)O = (+)-alpha-terpineol + diphosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme has been characterized from Santalum album (sandalwood).
CC   -!- Also forms some (-)-limonene and traces of other monoterpenoids.
CC   -!- See EC 4.2.3.16.
DR   B3TPQ7, ATESY_MAGGA;  B5A434, MTPS1_SANAL;
//
ID   4.2.3.113
DE   Terpinolene synthase.
CA   Geranyl-diphosphate = terpinolene + diphosphate.
CF   Mn(2+) or Mg(2+).
CC   -!- Mn(2+) is less effective as cofactor than Mg(2+) and product ratio
CC       changes.
CC   -!- Forms traces of other monoterpenoids.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 4.2.3.n6.
DR   Q9M7D0, TPSD9_ABIGR;  Q5SBP0, TPSD_OCIBA ;
//
ID   4.2.3.114
DE   Gamma-terpinene synthase.
CA   Geranyl diphosphate = gamma-terpinene + diphosphate.
CF   Mg(2+).
CC   -!- Isolated from Thymus vulgaris (thyme), Citrus limon (lemon), Citrus
CC       unshiu (satsuma) and Origanum vulgare (oregano).
CC   -!- The reaction involves a 1,2-hydride shift.
CC   -!- The 5-pro-S hydrogen of geranyl diphosphate is lost.
CC   -!- Traces of several other monoterpenoids are formed in addition to
CC       gamma-terpinene.
DR   Q8L5K4, GTPS_CITLI ;  E2E2P0, GTPS_ORIVU ;
//
ID   4.2.3.115
DE   Alpha-terpinene synthase.
CA   Geranyl diphosphate = alpha-terpinene + diphosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme has been characterized from Dysphania ambrosioides
CC       (American wormseed).
CC   -!- The enzyme will also use (3R)-linalyl diphosphate.
CC   -!- The reaction involves a 1,2-hydride shift.
CC   -!- The 1-pro-S hydrogen of geranyl diphosphate is lost.
DR   E2E2P0, GTPS_ORIVU ;
//
ID   4.2.3.116
DE   (+)-camphene synthase.
CA   Geranyl diphosphate = (+)-camphene + diphosphate.
CC   -!- Cyclase I of Salvia officinalis (sage) gives about equal parts (+)-
CC       camphene and (+)-alpha-pinene.
CC   -!- (3R)-linalyl diphosphate can also be used by the enzyme in preference
CC       to (3S)-linalyl diphosphate.
CC   -!- See also EC 4.2.3.121.
DR   O81192, BPPS_SALOF ;
//
ID   4.2.3.117
DE   (-)-camphene synthase.
CA   Geranyl-diphosphate = (-)-camphene + diphosphate.
CC   -!- (-)-Camphene is the major product in Abies grandis (grand fir) with
CC       traces of other monoterpenoids.
CC   -!- In Pseudotsuga menziesii (Douglas-fir) there are about equal parts of
CC       (-)-camphene and (-)-alpha-pinene with traces of four other
CC       monoterpenoids.
CC   -!- In Solanum lycopersicum (tomato) tricyclene, beta-myrcene, limonene,
CC       and traces of several other monoterpenoids are also formed.
CC   -!- See also EC 4.2.3.15, EC 4.2.3.16, EC 4.2.3.119 and EC 4.2.3.105.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 4.2.3.n4.
DR   G1JUH1, TPS3_SOLLC ;  Q948Z0, TPSD6_ABIGR;
//
ID   4.2.3.118
DE   2-methylisoborneol synthase.
AN   2-MIB cyclase.
AN   MIB synthase.
CA   (E)-2-methylgeranyl diphosphate + H(2)O = 2-methylisoborneol +
CA   diphosphate.
CF   Mg(2+).
CC   -!- The product, 2-methylisoborneol, is a characteristc odiferous
CC       compound with a musty smell produced by soil microorganisms.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 4.2.3.n14.
DR   A4FG19, MIBS_SACEN ;  A3KI17, MIBS_STRAM ;  Q9F1Y6, MIBS_STRCO ;
DR   Q9F1V8, MIBS_STRGR ;  D3KYU2, MIBS_STRLS ;
//
ID   4.2.3.119
DE   (-)-alpha-pinene synthase.
AN   (-)-alpha-pinene cyclase.
AN   (-)-alpha-pinene/(-)-camphene synthase.
CA   Geranyl-diphosphate = (-)-alpha-pinene + diphosphate.
CC   -!- Cyclase II of Salvia officinalis (sage) gives about equal parts (-)-
CC       alpha-pinene, (-)-beta-pinene and (-)-camphene, plus traces of other
CC       monoterpenoids.
CC   -!- (3S)-linalyl diphosphate can also be used by the enzyme in preference
CC       to (3R)-linalyl diphosphate.
CC   -!- The 4-pro-S hydrogen of geranyl diphosphate is lost.
CC   -!- The enzyme from Abies grandis (grand fir) gives roughly equal parts
CC       (-)-alpha-pinene and (-)-beta-pinene.
CC   -!- However the clone ag11 gave 35% (-)-limonene, 24% (-)-alpha-pinene
CC       and 20% (-)-beta-phellandrene.
CC   -!- Synthase I from Pinus taeda (loblolly pine) produces (-)-alpha-pinene
CC       with traces of (-)-beta-pinene.
CC   -!- The enzyme from Picea sitchensis (Sika spruce) forms 70% (-)-alpha-
CC       pinene and 30% (-)-beta-pinene.
CC   -!- The recombinant PmeTPS1 enzyme from Pseudotsuga menziesii (Douglas
CC       fir) gave roughly equal proportions of (-)-alpha-pinene and (-)-
CC       camphene plus traces of other monoterpenoids.
CC   -!- See also EC 4.2.3.120, EC 4.2.3.117, EC 4.2.3.16 and EC 4.2.3.52.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 4.1.99.8, EC 4.2.3.14 and EC 4.2.3.n7.
DR   O23945, PINS_FRAVE ;  Q84KL6, PT1_PINTA  ;  Q6XDB5, TPSD2_PICSI;
DR   O24475, TPSD3_ABIGR;  Q9M7C9, TPSDB_ABIGR;
//
ID   4.2.3.120
DE   (-)-beta-pinene synthase.
AN   (-)-(1S,5S)-pinene synthase.
AN   Beta-geraniolene synthase.
CA   Geranyl diphosphate = (-)-beta-pinene + diphosphate.
CC   -!- Cyclase II of Salvia officinalis (sage) produces about equal parts
CC       (-)-alpha-pinene, (-)-beta-pinene and (-)-camphene, plus traces of
CC       other monoterpenoids.
CC   -!- The enzyme can also use (3S)-Linalyl diphosphate (preferred to (3R)-
CC       linalyl diphosphate).
CC   -!- The enzyme from Abies grandis (grand fir) produces roughly equal
CC       parts of (-)-alpha-pinene and (-)-beta-pinene.
CC   -!- Cyclase IV from Pinus contorta (lodgepole pine) produces 63% (-)-
CC       beta-pinene, 26% 3-carene, and traces of alpha-pinene.
CC   -!- Synthase III from Pinus taeda (loblolly pine) forms (-)-beta-pinene
CC       with traces of alpha-pinene.
CC   -!- A cloned enzyme from Artemisia annua (sweet wormwood) gave (-)-beta-
CC       pinene with traces of (-)-alpha-pinene.
CC   -!- The enzyme from Picea sitchensis (Sika spruce) forms 30% (-)-beta-
CC       pinene and 70% (-)-alpha-pinene.
CC   -!- See also EC 4.2.3.119, EC 4.2.3.117 and EC 4.2.3.107.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 4.1.99.8 and EC 4.2.3.14.
DR   Q94G53, QH6_ARTAN  ;  Q6XDB5, TPSD2_PICSI;  O24475, TPSD3_ABIGR;
//
ID   4.2.3.121
DE   (+)-alpha-pinene synthase.
AN   (+)-alpha-pinene cyclase.
CA   Geranyl diphosphate = (+)-alpha-pinene + diphosphate.
CC   -!- Cyclase I of Salvia officinalis (sage) gives about equal parts (+)-
CC       alpha-pinene and (+)-camphene, whereas cyclase III gives about equal
CC       parts of (+)-alpha-pinene and (+)-beta-pinene.
CC   -!- (3R)-linalyl diphosphate can also be used by the enzyme in preference
CC       to (3S)-linalyl diphosphate.
CC   -!- The 4-pro-R hydrogen of geranyl diphosphate is lost.
CC   -!- With synthase II of Pinus taeda (loblolly pine) (+)-beta-pinene was
CC       the only product.
CC   -!- See also EC 4.2.3.122 and EC 4.2.3.116.
DR   O81192, BPPS_SALOF ;  Q84KL3, PT30_PINTA ;  A7IZZ2, TPS2_CANSA ;
//
ID   4.2.3.122
DE   (+)-beta-pinene synthase.
AN   (+)-pinene cyclase.
CA   Geranyl diphosphate = (+)-beta-pinene + diphosphate.
CC   -!- Cyclase III from Salvia officinalis (sage) gives roughly equal parts
CC       of (+)-beta-pinene and (+)-alpha-pinene.
CC   -!- See EC 4.2.3.121.
//
ID   4.2.3.123
DE   Beta-sesquiphellandrene synthase.
AN   Tps1.
CA   (2E,6E)-farnesyl diphosphate = beta-sesquiphellandrene + diphosphate.
DR   C5YHI2, TPS2_SORBI ;
//
ID   4.2.3.124
DE   2-deoxy-scyllo-inosose synthase.
CA   D-glucose-6-phosphate = 2-deoxy-L-scyllo-inosose + phosphate.
CF   Cobalt cation.
CC   -!- Involved in the biosynthetic pathways of several clinically important
CC       aminocyclitol antibiotics, including kanamycin, butirosin, neomycin
CC       and ribostamycin.
CC   -!- Requires an NAD(+) cofactor, which is transiently reduced during the
CC       reaction.
CC   -!- The enzyme from the bacterium Bacillus circulans forms a complex with
CC       the glutamine amidotransferase subunit of pyridoxal 5'-phosphate
CC       synthase (EC 4.3.3.6), which appears to stabilize the complex.
DR   Q9S5E2, DOIS_BACCI ;  Q70KD0, DOIS_MICEC ;  Q53U19, DOIS_STRFR ;
DR   Q6L738, DOIS_STRKN ;  Q2MF70, DOIS_STRLV ;  Q4R0W3, DOIS_STRRI ;
DR   Q2MFP1, DOIS_STRRY ;  Q2MF16, DOIS_STRSD ;
//
ID   4.2.3.125
DE   Alpha-muurolene synthase.
CA   (2E,6E)-farnesyl diphosphate = alpha-muurolene + diphosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme has been characterized from the fungus Coprinus cinereus.
CC   -!- Also gives germacrene A and gamma-muurolene, see EC 4.2.3.23 and
CC       EC 4.2.3.126.
DR   A8NE23, COP3_COPC7 ;  Q4U3F6, CS_HELAN   ;
//
ID   4.2.3.126
DE   Gamma-muurolene synthase.
CA   (2E,6E)-farnesyl diphosphate = gamma-muurolene + diphosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme has been characterized from the fungus Coprinus cinereus.
CC   -!- Also gives germacrene A and alpha-muurolene, see EC 4.2.3.23 and
CC       EC 4.2.3.125.
DR   A8NE23, COP3_COPC7 ;
//
ID   4.2.3.127
DE   Beta-copaene synthase.
AN   Cop4.
CA   (2E,6E)-farnesyl diphosphate = beta-copaene + diphosphate.
CF   Mg(2+).
CC   -!- Isolated from the fungus Coprinus cinereus.
CC   -!- The enzyme also forms (+)-delta-cadinene, beta-cubebene, (+)-sativene
CC       and traces of several other sequiterpenoids.
CC   -!- beta-copaene is formed in the presence of Mg(2+) but not Mn(2+).
CC   -!- See EC 4.2.3.13 EC 4.2.3.128 and EC 4.2.3.129.
DR   A8NU13, COP4_COPC7 ;
//
ID   4.2.3.128
DE   Beta-cubebene synthase.
CA   (2E,6E)-farnesyl diphosphate = beta-cubebene + diphosphate.
CC   -!- Isolated from the fungus Coprinus cinereus.
CC   -!- The enzyme also forms (+)-delta-cadinene, beta-copaene, (+)-sativene
CC       and traces of several other sequiterpenoids.
CC   -!- It is found in many higher plants such as Magnolia grandiflora
CC       (Southern Magnolia) together with germacrene A.
CC   -!- See EC 4.2.3.13 EC 4.2.3.127 EC 4.2.3.129 and EC 4.2.3.23.
DR   B3TPQ6, BCUSY_MAGGA;  A8NU13, COP4_COPC7 ;
//
ID   4.2.3.129
DE   (+)-sativene synthase.
AN   Cop4.
CA   (2E,6E)-farnesyl diphosphate = (+)-sativene + diphosphate.
CC   -!- Isolated from the fungus Coprinus cinereus.
CC   -!- The enzyme also forms (+)-delta-cadinene, beta-copaene, beta-
CC       cubebene, and traces of several other sequiterpenoids.
CC   -!- See EC 4.2.3.13 EC 4.2.3.127 and EC 4.2.3.128.
DR   A8NU13, COP4_COPC7 ;
//
ID   4.2.3.130
DE   Tetraprenyl-beta-curcumene synthase.
CA   All-trans-heptaprenyl diphosphate = tetraprenyl-beta-curcumene +
CA   diphosphate.
CC   -!- Isolated from Bacillus subtilis.
CC   -!- This sesquarterpene is present in a number of Bacillus species.
DR   O34707, YTPB_BACSU ;
//
ID   4.2.3.131
DE   Miltiradiene synthase.
CA   (+)-copalyl diphosphate = miltiradiene + diphosphate.
CC   -!- Isolated from the plants Rosmarinus officinalis (rosemary) and Salvia
CC       miltiorrhiza.
CC   -!- The enzyme from the plant Selaginella moellendorffii is
CC       mutifunctional and also catalyzes EC 5.5.1.12.
DR   G9MAN7, TPS4_SELML ;
//
ID   4.2.3.132
DE   Neoabietadiene synthase.
CA   (+)-copalyl diphosphate = neoabietadiene + diphosphate.
CC   -!- Isolated from Abies grandis (grand fir).
CC   -!- This class I enzyme forms about equal proportions of abietadiene,
CC       levopimaradiene and neoabietadiene; see also EC 4.2.3.18 and
CC       EC 4.2.3.32.
CC   -!- An X-ray study of this multifunctional enzyme showed that the class I
CC       activity is in the alpha domain, while EC 5.5.1.12 activity (a class
CC       II activity) is in the beta and gamma domains.
CC   -!- In Pinus taeda (loblolly pine) the major product is levopimaradiene,
CC       with less abietadiene and neoabietadiene.
DR   H8ZM70, LAS_ABIBA  ;  M4HXU6, TPSD1_PINBN;  M4HY05, TPSD1_PINCO;
DR   Q50EK2, TPSD1_PINTA;  M4HYC6, TPSD2_PINCO;  Q38710, TPSDV_ABIGR;
//
ID   4.2.3.133
DE   Alpha-copaene synthase.
CA   (2E,6E)-farnesyl diphosphate = alpha-copaene + diphosphate.
CC   -!- Isolated from Helianthus annuus (sunflower).
CC   -!- The enzyme also produces beta-caryophyllene, delta-cadinene and
CC       traces of other sesquiterpenoids.
CC   -!- See EC 4.2.3.13 and EC 4.2.3.57.
DR   Q4U3F6, CS_HELAN   ;  J7LP58, TPS1_PHYDL ;  B9S9Z3, TPS1_RICCO ;
//
ID   4.2.3.134
DE   5-phosphonooxy-L-lysine phospho-lyase.
AN   5-phosphohydroxy-L-lysine ammoniophospholyase.
CA   (5R)-5-phosphonooxy-L-lysine + H(2)O = (S)-2-amino-6-oxohexanoate + NH(3)
CA   + phosphate.
CF   Pyridoxal 5'-phosphate.
CC   -!- Has no activity with phosphoethanolamine (cf. EC 4.2.3.2).
DR   Q8IUZ5, AT2L2_HUMAN;  Q8R1K4, AT2L2_MOUSE;
//
ID   4.2.3.135
DE   Delta(6)-protoilludene synthase.
AN   6-protoilludene synthase.
CA   (2E,6E)-farnesyl diphosphate = Delta(6)-protoilludene + diphosphate.
CC   -!- Isolated from the fungus Armillaria gallica.
CC   -!- Delta(6)-Protoilludene is the first step in the biosynthesis of the
CC       melleolides.
DR   P0DL13, PRO1_ARMGA ;
//
ID   4.2.3.136
DE   Alpha-isocomene synthase.
CA   (2E,6E)-farnesyl diphosphate = (-)-alpha-isocomene + diphosphate.
CC   -!- Isolated from the roots of the plant Matricaria chamomilla var.
CC       recutita (chamomile).
CC   -!- The enzyme also produced traces of five other sesquiterpenoids.
DR   I6R4V5, TPS2_MATCR ;
//
ID   4.2.3.137
DE   (E)-2-epi-beta-caryophyllene synthase.
AN   2-epi-(E)-beta-caryophyllene synthase.
CA   (2E,6E)-farnesyl diphosphate = (E)-2-epi-beta-caryophyllene +
CA   diphosphate.
CC   -!- Isolated from the plant Selaginella moellendorfii.
CC   -!- The enzyme also gives two other sesquiterpenoids.
DR   J9QS25, MTS26_SELML;
//
ID   4.2.3.138
DE   (+)-epi-alpha-bisabolol synthase.
CA   (2E,6E)-farnesyl diphosphate + H(2)O = (+)-epi-alpha-bisabolol +
CA   diphosphate.
CC   -!- Isolated from the plant Phyla dulcis (Aztec sweet herb).
CC   -!- (+)-epi-alpha-bisabolol is the precursor of the sweetener
CC       hernandulcin.
DR   J7LH11, TPS8_PHYDL ;
//
ID   4.2.3.139
DE   Valerena-4,7(11)-diene synthase.
CA   (2E,6E)-farnesyl diphosphate = valerena-4,7(11)-diene + diphosphate.
CC   -!- Isolated from the plant Valeriana officinalis (valerian).
DR   J9R5V4, TPS2_VALOF ;
//
ID   4.2.3.140
DE   Cis-abienol synthase.
AN   Z-abienol synthase.
CA   (13E)-8-alpha-hydroxylabd-13-en-15-yl diphosphate = cis-abienol +
CA   diphosphate.
CC   -!- Isolated from the plants Abies balsamea (balsam fir) and Nicotiana
CC       tabacum (tobacco).
DR   G3CCC1, CABS_TOBAC ;  H8ZM73, CAS_ABIBA  ;
//
ID   4.2.3.141
DE   Sclareol synthase.
CA   (13E)-8-alpha-hydroxylabd-13-en-15-yl diphosphate + H(2)O = sclareol +
CA   diphosphate.
CF   Mn(2+) or Mg(2+).
CC   -!- Isolated from the plant Salvia sclarea (clary sage).
CC   -!- Originally thought to be synthesized in one step from geranylgeranyl
CC       diphosphate it is now known to require two enzymes, EC 4.2.1.133 and
CC       EC 4.2.3.141.
CC   -!- Sclareol is used in perfumery.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 3.1.7.4.
//
ID   4.2.3.142
DE   7-epizingiberene synthase ((2Z,6Z)-farnesyl diphosphate cyclizing).
CA   (2Z,6Z)-farnesyl diphosphate = 7-epizingiberene + diphosphate.
CC   -!- Isolated from the plant Solanum habrochaites.
CC   -!- 7-epizingiberene is a whitefly repellant.
//
ID   4.2.3.143
DE   Kunzeaol synthase.
CA   (2E,6E)-farnesyl diphosphate + H(2)O = kunzeaol + diphosphate.
CC   -!- Isolated from the root of the plant Thapsia garganica.
CC   -!- The enzyme also produces germacrene D, bicyclogermacrene and traces
CC       of other sesquiterpenoids.
CC   -!- See EC 4.2.3.77 and EC 4.2.3.100.
DR   K4LMW2, STS2_THAGA ;
//
ID   4.2.3.144
DE   Geranyllinalool synthase.
CA   Geranylgeranyl diphosphate + H(2)O = (E,E)-geranyllinalool + diphosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme is a component of the herbivore-induced indirect defense
CC       system.
CC   -!- The product, (E,E)-geranyllinalool, is a precursor to the volatile
CC       compound 4,8,12-trimethyl-1,3,7,11-tridecatetraene (TMTT), which is
CC       released by many plants in response to damage.
DR   Q93YV0, GES_ARATH  ;  Q29VN2, TPS2_MAIZE ;
//
ID   4.2.3.145
DE   Ophiobolin F synthase.
CA   (2E,6E,10E,14E)-geranylfarnesyl diphosphate + H(2)O = ophiobolin F +
CA   diphosphate.
CC   -!- Isolated from the fungus Aspergillus clavatus.
CC   -!- The product is a sesterterpenoid (C(25) terpenoid).
DR   A1C8C3, OPHFS_ASPCL;
//
ID   4.2.3.146
DE   Cyclooctat-9-en-7-ol synthase.
CA   Geranylgeranyl diphosphate + H(2)O = cyclooctat-9-en-7-ol + diphosphate.
CF   Mg(2+).
CC   -!- Isolated from the bacterium Streptomyces melanosporofaciens, where it
CC       is part of the biosynthesis of cyclooctatin, a potent inhibitor of
CC       lysophospholipase.
DR   C9K1X5, COTB2_STRMJ;
//
ID   4.2.3.147
DE   Pimaradiene synthase.
CA   (+)-copalyl diphosphate = pimara-8(14),15-diene + diphosphate.
CC   -!- Isolated from the plants Pinus banksiana (jack pine) and Pinus
CC       contorta (lodgepole pine).
DR   M4HY08, MPIM1_PINBN;  M4HYC8, MPIM1_PINCO;
//
ID   4.2.3.148
DE   Cembrene C synthase.
CA   Geranylgeranyl diphosphate = cembrene C + diphosphate.
CF   Mg(2+).
CC   -!- Isolated from the bacterium Streptomyces sp. SANK 60404.
CC   -!- This bifunctional enzyme also produces (R)-nephthenol (cf.
CC       EC 4.2.3.149).
DR   M1V9Q0, DTCYA_STRSQ;
//
ID   4.2.3.149
DE   Nephthenol synthase.
CA   Geranylgeranyl diphosphate + H(2)O = (R)-nephthenol + diphosphate.
CF   Mg(2+).
CC   -!- Two isozymes with this activity were isolated from the bacterium
CC       Streptomyces sp. SANK 60404.
CC   -!- The enzyme encoded by the DtcycA gene also produces cembrene C (see
CC       4.2.3.148), while the enzyme encoded by the DtcycB gene also produces
CC       (R)-cembrene A and (1S,4E,8E,12E)-2,2,5,9,13-
CC       pentamethylcyclopentadeca-4,8,12-trien-1-ol (cf. EC 4.2.3.150 and
CC       EC 4.2.3.151).
DR   M1V9Q0, DTCYA_STRSQ;  M1VDX3, DTCYB_STRSQ;
//
ID   4.2.3.150
DE   Cembrene A synthase.
CA   Geranylgeranyl diphosphate = (R)-cembrene A + diphosphate.
CF   Iron-sulfur; Mg(2+).
CC   -!- Isolated from the bacterium Streptomyces sp. SANK 60404.
CC   -!- This trifunctional enzyme also produces (R)-nephthenol and
CC       (1S,4E,8E,12E)-2,2,5,9,13-pentamethylcyclopentadeca-4,8,12-trien-1-ol
CC       (cf. EC 4.2.3.149 and EC 4.2.3.151).
DR   M1VDX3, DTCYB_STRSQ;
//
ID   4.2.3.151
DE   Pentamethylcyclopentadecatrienol synthase.
CA   Geranylgeranyl diphosphate + H(2)O = (1S,4E,8E,12E)-2,2,5,9,13-
CA   pentamethylcyclopentadeca-4,8,12-trien-1-ol + diphosphate.
CF   Iron-sulfur; Mg(2+).
CC   -!- Isolated from the bacterium Streptomyces sp. SANK 60404.
CC   -!- This trifunctional enzyme also produces (R)-nephthenol and (R)-
CC       cembrene A (cf. EC 4.2.3.149 and EC 4.2.3.150).
DR   M1VDX3, DTCYB_STRSQ;
//
ID   4.2.3.152
DE   2-epi-5-epi-valiolone synthase.
AN   C(7)-cyclitol synthase.
CA   D-sedoheptulose 7-phosphate = 2-epi-5-epi-valiolone + phosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme is highly specific for alpha-D-sedoheptulopyranose
CC       7-phosphate.
CC   -!- It requires a divalent metal ion (Zn(2+) or Co(2+)) and an NAD(+)
CC       cofactor, which is transiently reduced during the reaction.
CC   -!- The enzyme is involved in the biosynthesis of C(7)N-aminocyclitol
CC       natural products, such as the valienamine moiety of the antidiabetic
CC       drug acarbose and the crop protectant validamycin A.
CC   -!- Cf. EC 4.2.3.154 and EC 4.2.3.155.
DR   Q9ZAE9, ACBC_ACTS5 ;  A1YPR2, CETA_ACTSX ;  E3FKM2, EEVS_STIAD ;
DR   B0B0T7, EEVS_STRGA ;  A8D7K2, SALQ_STRA4 ;  H2K887, VALA_STRHJ ;
//
ID   4.2.3.153
DE   (5-formylfuran-3-yl)methyl phosphate synthase.
AN   2-furaldehyde phosphate synthase.
AN   4-HFC-P synthase.
CA   2 D-glyceraldehyde 3-phosphate = (5-formylfuran-3-yl)methyl phosphate +
CA   phosphate + 2 H(2)O.
CC   -!- The enzyme catalyzes the reaction in the direction of producing
CC       (5-formylfuran-3-yl)methyl phosphate, an intermediate in the
CC       biosynthesis of methanofuran.
CC   -!- The sequence of events starts with the removal of a phosphate group,
CC       followed by aldol condensation and cyclization.
CC   -!- Methanofuran is a carbon-carrier cofactor involved in the first step
CC       of the methanogenic reduction of carbon dioxide by methanogenic
CC       archaea.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 4.1.99.21.
DR   O28087, MFNB_ARCFU ;  A6UU96, MFNB_META3 ;  Q8THS6, MFNB_METAC ;
DR   Q46DH3, MFNB_METBF ;  Q58499, MFNB_METJA ;  Q8TUZ9, MFNB_METKA ;
DR   A4FY92, MFNB_METM5 ;  A9A7Q1, MFNB_METM6 ;  A6VK15, MFNB_METM7 ;
DR   Q8PXV2, MFNB_METMA ;  Q6LZC1, MFNB_METMP ;  A5UNQ5, MFNB_METS3 ;
DR   O26244, MFNB_METTH ;  A6USK6, MFNB_METVS ;  Q9X4H5, Y264_KITAU ;
DR   Q8GEK8, Y264_METEX ;  B1W5S5, Y6403_STRGG;  Q9ZBH3, Y6440_STRCO;
//
ID   4.2.3.154
DE   Demethyl-4-deoxygadusol synthase.
CA   D-sedoheptulose 7-phosphate = demethyl-4-deoxygadusol + phosphate +
CA   H(2)O.
CF   Co(2+) or Zn(2+); NAD(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the cyanobacterium Nostoc punctiforme
CC       PCC 73102, is involved in the biosynthesis of the sunscreen compound
CC       shinorine.
CC   -!- Cf. EC 4.2.3.152 and EC 4.2.3.155.
DR   Q3M6C3, DDGS_ANAVT ;  B2J6X9, DDGS_NOSP7 ;
//
ID   4.2.3.155
DE   2-epi-valiolone synthase.
CA   D-sedoheptulose 7-phosphate = 2-epi-valiolone + phosphate.
CF   Co(2+) or Zn(2+); NAD(+).
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacteria Actinosynnema mirum and
CC       Stigmatella aurantiaca DW4/3-1, produces 2-epi-valiolone, which is
CC       believed to function as a precursor in aminocyclitol biosynthesis.
CC   -!- Cf. EC 4.2.3.152 and EC 4.2.3.154.
DR   C6WFL3, EVS_ACTMD  ;  Q08VU0, EVS_STIAD  ;
//
ID   4.2.3.156
DE   Hydroxysqualene synthase.
CA   Presqualene diphosphate + H(2)O = hydroxysqualene + diphosphate.
CC   -!- This enzyme, isolated from the bacteria Rhodopseudomonas palustris
CC       and Zymomonas mobilis, participates, along with EC 2.5.1.103 and
CC       EC 1.17.18.1, in the conversion of all-trans-farnesyl diphosphate to
CC       squalene.
CC   -!- Eukaryotes achieve the same goal in a single step, catalyzed by
CC       EC 2.5.1.21.
DR   Q6N3F1, HPNC_RHOPA ;  P55351, HPNC_SINFN ;  Q5NP67, HPNC_ZYMMO ;
//
ID   4.2.3.157
DE   (+)-isoafricanol synthase.
CA   (2E,6E)-farnesyl diphosphate + H(2)O = (+)-isoafricanol + diphosphate.
CC   -!- (+)-isoafricanol is a sesquiterpene alcohol.
CC   -!- Its synthesis has been shown to occur in the bacteria Streptomyces
CC       violaceusniger and S.malaysiensis.
//
ID   4.2.3.158
DE   (-)-spiroviolene synthase.
CA   Geranylgeranyl diphosphate = (-)-spiroviolene + diphosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme, which forms the diterpene (-)-spiroviolene, has been
CC       characterized from the bacterium Streptomyces violens.
DR   P0DPK6, SPVIS_STRVB;
//
ID   4.2.3.159
DE   Tsukubadiene synthase.
CA   Geranylgeranyl diphosphate = tsukubadiene + diphosphate.
CC   -!- The synthesis of the diterpene tsukubadiene has been shown to occur
CC       in the Actinobacterium Streptomyces tsukubaensis.
DR   I2N045, TSUKU_STRT9;
//
ID   4.2.3.160
