CA   (2E,6E)-farnesyl diphosphate + H(2)O = (-)-drimenol + diphosphate.
CC   -!- Isolated from the plants Valeriana officinalis (valerian) and
CC       Persicaria hydropiper (water pepper).
CC   -!- The enzyme does not act on farnesol or drimenol diphosphate.
CC   -!- Using 18-oxygen labelled water 18-oxygen was incorporated suggesting
CC       involvement of a stabilized carbocation or an equivalent species.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 3.1.7.7.
//
ID   4.2.3.195
DE   Rhizathalene A synthase.
CA   Geranylgeranyl diphosphate = rhizathalene A + diphosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme was identified in the roots of the plant Arabidopsis
CC       thaliana (thale cress).
CC   -!- The product is a semivolatile diterpene that acts as a local
CC       antifeedant in belowground direct defense against root-feeding
CC       insects.
DR   O65435, TPS08_ARATH;
//
ID   4.2.3.n1
DE   Transferred entry: 4.2.3.38.
//
ID   4.2.3.n2
DE   Delta-selinene synthase.
CA   (1) Farnesyl-diphosphate = delta-selinene + diphosphate.
CA   (2) Farnesyl-diphosphate = (E,E)-germacrene B + diphosphate.
CA   (3) Farnesyl-diphosphate = guaia-6,9-diene + diphosphate.
CA   (4) Farnesyl-diphosphate = germacrene A + diphosphate.
CA   (5) Farnesyl-diphosphate = (+)-delta-cadinene + diphosphate.
CF   Mg(2+).
CC   -!- Has a broad product range.
CC   -!- While delta-selinene is the major product, (E,E)-germacrene B, guaia-
CC       6,9-diene, germacrene A and delta-cadinene are produced in
CC       appreciable amounts and further 29 other minor products can also be
CC       detected.
CC   -!- The enzyme can use geranyl diphosphate as a substrate, producing
CC       mainly limonene, (Z)-ocimene and myrcene as the major products.
//
ID   4.2.3.n3
