ID   4.2.99.22
DE   Tuliposide A-converting enzyme.
AN   6-O-(4 -hydroxy-2 -methylenebutyryl)-D-glucose acyltransferase (lactone-
AN   forming).
AN   Tuliposide-converting enzyme.
CA   6-tuliposide A = tulipalin A + D-glucose.
CC   -!- Isolated from the plant Tulipa gesneriana (tulip).
CC   -!- The reaction is an intramolecular transesterification producing the
CC       lactone.
CC   -!- The enzyme also has a weak activity with 6-tuliposide B and 6-O-
CC       benzoyl-D-glucose.
DR   R4X244, TCAB1_TULGE;  R4X4V6, TCAB2_TULGE;  R4X5P0, TCAB3_TULGE;
DR   R4X247, TCAB4_TULGE;  I4DST8, TCEA1_TULGE;  I4DST9, TCEA2_TULGE;
//
ID   4.2.99.23
DE   Tuliposide B-converting enzyme.
CA   6-tuliposide B = tulipalin B + D-glucose.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from pollen of the plant Tulipa gesneriana
CC       (tulip), catalyzes the intramolecular transesterification of
CC       6-tuliposide B to form the antibiotic aglycon tulipalin B as a sole
CC       product.
CC   -!- It does not catalyze the hydrolysis of 6-tuliposide B to form a
CC       hydroxy acid.
CC   -!- The enzyme has marginal activity with 6-tuliposide A.
CC   -!- Cf. EC 4.2.99.22.
DR   A0A0H5BMX5, TCEB1_TULGE;
