ID   4.3.1.13
DE   Carbamoyl-serine ammonia-lyase.
AN   O-carbamoyl-L-serine deaminase.
CA   O-carbamoyl-L-serine + H(2)O = pyruvate + 2 NH(3) + CO(2).
CF   Pyridoxal 5'-phosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme cleaves a carbon-oxygen bond, releasing CO(2), ammonia,
CC       and an unstable enamine product that tautomerizes to an imine form,
CC       which undergoes a hydrolytic deamination to form pyruvate and a
CC       second ammonia molecule.
CC   -!- The latter reaction, which can occur spontaneously, can also be
CC       catalyzed by EC 3.5.99.10.
