DE   Erythro-3-hydroxy-L-aspartate ammonia-lyase.
AN   3-hydroxyaspartate dehydratase.
AN   Erythro-3-hydroxy-L(s)-aspartate hydro-lyase (deaminating).
AN   Erythro-3-hydroxyaspartate dehydratase.
AN   Erythro-beta-hydroxyaspartate dehydratase.
CA   Erythro-3-hydroxy-L-aspartate = oxaloacetate + NH(3).
CF   Pyridoxal 5'-phosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme, which was characterized from the bacterium Paracoccus
CC       denitrificans NCIMB 8944, is highly specific for the L-isomer of
CC       erythro-3-hydroxyaspartate.
CC   -!- Different from EC 4.3.1.16 and EC 4.3.1.27.
CC   -!- Requires a divalent cation such as Mn(2+), Mg(2+), or Ca(2+).
CC   -!- Formerly EC 4.2.1.38.
//
ID   4.3.1.21
DE   Transferred entry: 4.3.1.9.
//
ID   4.3.1.22
DE   3,4-dihydroxyphenylalanine reductive deaminase.
AN   DOPA-reductive deaminase.
AN   DOPARDA.
AN   Reductive deaminase.
CA   L-dopa + NADH = 3,4-dihydroxyphenylpropanoate + NAD(+) + NH(3).
CC   -!- Forms part of the L-phenylalanine-catabolism pathway in the
CC       anoxygenic phototrophic bacterium Rhodobacter sphaeroides OU5.
CC   -!- NADPH is oxidized more slowly than NADH.
//
ID   4.3.1.23
DE   Tyrosine ammonia-lyase.
AN   L-tyrosine ammonia-lyase.
AN   TAL.
AN   Tyrase.
CA   L-tyrosine = trans-p-hydroxycinnamate + ammonia.
CF   MIO.
CC   -!- Member of the aromatic amino acid lyase family, other members of
CC       which are EC 4.3.1.3, EC 4.3.1.24 and EC 4.3.1.25.
CC   -!- Far more active with tyrosine than with phenylalanine as substrate,
CC       but the substrate specificity can be switched by mutation of a single
CC       amino acid (H89F) in the enzyme from the bacterium Rhodobacter
CC       sphaeroides.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 4.3.1.5.
