CC   -!- Acts on the product of the reaction catalyzed by EC 1.14.17.3, thus
CC       removing a terminal glycine residue and leaving a des-glycine peptide
CC       amide.
DR   P08478, AMDA_XENLA ;  P12890, AMDB_XENLA ;  P83388, AMDL_CAEEL ;
DR   P10731, AMD_BOVIN  ;  P19021, AMD_HUMAN  ;  P97467, AMD_MOUSE  ;
DR   P14925, AMD_RAT    ;  Q9V5E1, PAL1_DROME ;  Q9W1L5, PAL2_DROME ;
DR   P91268, PGAL_CAEEL ;
//
ID   4.3.2.6
DE   Gamma-L-glutamyl-butirosin B gamma-glutamyl cyclotransferase.
CA   Gamma-L-glutamyl-butirosin B = butirosin B + 5-oxoproline.
CC   -!- The enzyme catalyzes the last step in the biosynthesis of the
CC       aminoglycoside antibiotic butirosin B.
CC   -!- The enzyme acts as a cyclotransferase, cleaving the amide bond via
CC       transamidation using the alpha-amine of the terminal gamma-L-
CC       glutamate of the side chain, releasing it as the cyclic 5-oxoproline.
DR   Q4H4F0, BTRG_BACCI ;
//
ID   4.3.2.7
DE   Glutathione-specific gamma-glutamylcyclotransferase.
AN   Gamma-glu-GCG.
CA   Glutathione = L-cysteinylglycine + 5-oxo-L-proline.
CC   -!- The enzyme, found in bacteria, fungi and animals, is specific for
CC       glutathione (cf. EC 4.3.2.9).
CC   -!- The enzyme acts as a cyclotransferase, cleaving the amide bond via
CC       transamidation using the alpha-amine of the L-glutamyl residue,
CC       releasing it as the cyclic 5-oxo-L-proline.
DR   Q5SPB6, CHAC1_DANRE;  Q9BUX1, CHAC1_HUMAN;  Q8R3J5, CHAC1_MOUSE;
DR   B3STU3, CHAC1_RAT  ;  Q0IIH4, CHAC2_BOVIN;  Q5ZI66, CHAC2_CHICK;
DR   Q4KMJ1, CHAC2_DANRE;  Q8WUX2, CHAC2_HUMAN;  Q9CQG1, CHAC2_MOUSE;
DR   Q641Z5, CHAC2_RAT  ;  Q5PPV4, CHAC2_XENLA;  P39163, CHAC_ECOLI ;
DR   P87305, CHAC_SCHPO ;  P32656, CHAC_YEAST ;
//
ID   4.3.2.8
DE   Gamma-glutamylamine cyclotransferase.
CA   Epsilon-(gamma-L-glutamyl)-L-lysine = L-lysine + 5-oxo-L-proline.
CC   -!- The enzyme, found in vertebrates, has no activity toward alpha-
CC       (gamma-L-glutamyl)-L-amino acids (cf. EC 4.3.2.9).
CC   -!- The enzyme acts as a cyclotransferase, cleaving the amide bond via
CC       transamidation using the alpha-amine of the gamma-L-glutamyl residue,
CC       releasing it as the cyclic 5-oxo-L-proline.
DR   A0JMM9, GGACA_DANRE;  Q66I06, GGACB_DANRE;  A3KNL6, GGACC_DANRE;
DR   Q0VFX9, GGACT_BOVIN;  Q9BVM4, GGACT_HUMAN;  Q923B0, GGACT_MOUSE;
DR   Q4KM86, GGACT_RAT  ;  Q66KX0, GGACT_XENLA;
//
ID   4.3.2.9
DE   Gamma-glutamylcyclotransferase.
AN   GGCT.
CA   Alpha-(gamma-L-glutamyl)-L-amino acid = alpha-L-amino acid + 5-oxo-L-
CA   proline.
CC   -!- The enzyme, found in animals and plants, acts on derivatives of
CC       L-glutamate, L-2-aminobutanoate, L-alanine and glycine.
CC   -!- The enzyme acts as a cyclotransferase, cleaving the amide bond via
CC       transamidation using the alpha-amine of the L-glutamyl residue,
CC       releasing it as the cyclic 5-oxo-L-proline.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 2.3.2.4.
DR   Q2UPC2, ACLK_ASPOR ;  Q8GY54, GCT21_ARATH;  Q84MC1, GCT22_ARATH;
DR   Q84QC1, GCT23_ARATH;  Q32LE4, GGCT_BOVIN ;  O75223, GGCT_HUMAN ;
DR   Q9D7X8, GGCT_MOUSE ;  E9R9Y3, GLIK_ASPFU ;  M1W855, TCPK_CLAP2 ;
//
ID   4.3.2.10
DE   Imidazole glycerol-phosphate synthase.
AN   IGP synthase.
CA   5-((5-phospho-1-deoxy-D-ribulos-1-ylamino)methylideneamino)-1-(5-phospho-
CA   beta-D-ribosyl)imidazole-4-carboxamide + L-glutamine = 5-amino-1-
CA   (5-phospho-beta-D-ribosyl)imidazole-4-carboxamide + D-erythro-1-
CA   (imidazol-4-yl)glycerol 3-phosphate + L-glutamate.
CC   -!- The enzyme is involved in histidine biosynthesis, as well as purine
CC       nucleotide biosynthesis.
CC   -!- The enzymes from archaea and bacteria are heterodimeric.
CC   -!- A glutaminase component (cf. EC 3.5.1.2) produces an ammonia molecule
CC       that is transferred by a 25 A tunnel to a cyclase component, which
CC       adds it to the imidazole ring, leading to lysis of the molecule and
CC       cyclization of one of the products.
CC   -!- The glutminase subunit is only active within the dimeric complex.
CC   -!- In fungi and plants the two subunits are combined into a single
CC       polypeptide.
//
ID   4.3.3.1
DE   3-ketovalidoxylamine C-N-lyase.
CA   4-nitrophenyl-3-ketovalidamine = 4-nitroaniline + 5-D-(5/6)-5-
CA   C-(hydroxymethyl)-2,6-dihydroxycyclohex-2-en-1-one.
CF   Ca(2+).
CC   -!- Eliminates 4-nitroaniline from 4-nitrophenyl-3-ketovalidamine or
CC       4-nitrophenol from 4-nitrophenyl-alpha-D-3-dehydroglucoside.
CC   -!- Involved in the degradation of the fungicide validamycin A by
CC       Flavobacterium saccharophilum.
//
ID   4.3.3.2
DE   Strictosidine synthase.
AN   STR.
AN   Strictosidine synthetase.
CA   3-alpha-(S)-strictosidine + H(2)O = tryptamine + secologanin.
CC   -!- Catalyzes a a Pictet-Spengler reaction between the aldehyde group of
CC       secologanin and the amino group of tryptamine.
CC   -!- Involved in the biosynthesis of the monoterpenoid indole alkaloids.
DR   P92976, SSL11_ARATH;  P94111, SSL12_ARATH;  P18417, STSY_CATRO ;
DR   P68174, STSY_RAUMA ;  P68175, STSY_RAUSE ;
//
ID   4.3.3.3
DE   Deacetylisoipecoside synthase.
CA   Deacetylisoipecoside + H(2)O = dopamine + secologanin.
CC   -!- The enzyme from the leaves of Alangium lamarckii differs in
CC       enantiomeric specificity from EC 4.3.3.4.
CC   -!- The product is rapidly converted to demethylisoalangiside.
//
ID   4.3.3.4
DE   Deacetylipecoside synthase.
CA   Deacetylipecoside + H(2)O = dopamine + secologanin.
CC   -!- The enzyme from the leaves of Alangium lamarckii differs in
CC       enantiomeric specificity from EC 4.3.3.3.
CC   -!- The product is rapidly converted to demethylalangiside.
//
ID   4.3.3.5
DE   4'-demethylrebeccamycin synthase.
AN   Arcyriaflavin A N-glycosyltransferase.
CA   4'-O-demethylrebeccamycin + H(2)O = dichloro-arcyriaflavin A + beta-D-
CA   glucose.
CC   -!- This enzyme catalyzes a step in the biosynthesis of rebeccamycin,
CC       an indolocarbazole alkaloid produced by the bacterium Lechevalieria
CC       aerocolonigenes.
CC   -!- The enzyme is a glycosylase, and acts in the reverse direction to
CC       that shown.
CC   -!- It has a wide substrate range, and was shown to glycosylate several
CC       substrates, including the staurosporine aglycone, EJG-III-108A,
CC       J-104303, 6-N-methyl-arcyriaflavin C and indolo-[2,3-a]-carbazole.
DR   Q8KHE4, REBG_NOCAE ;
//
ID   4.3.3.6
DE   Pyridoxal 5'-phosphate synthase (glutamine hydrolyzing).
CA   D-ribose 5-phosphate + D-glyceraldehyde 3-phosphate + L-glutamine =
CA   pyridoxal 5'-phosphate + L-glutamate + 3 H(2)O + phosphate.
CC   -!- The ammonia is provided by the glutaminase subunit and channeled to
CC       the active site of the lyase subunit by a 100 A tunnel.
CC   -!- The enzyme can also use ribulose 5-phosphate and dihydroxyacetone
CC       phosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme complex is found in aerobic bacteria, archeae, fungi and
CC       plants.
