CA   L-cystathionine + H(2)O = L-cysteine + NH(3) + 2-oxobutanoate.
CF   Pyridoxal 5'-phosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme cleaves a carbon-sulfur bond, releasing L-cysteine and an
CC       unstable enamine product that tautomerizes to an imine form, which
CC       undergoes a hydrolytic deamination to form 2-oxobutanoate and
CC       ammonia.
CC   -!- The latter reaction, which can occur spontaneously, can also be
CC       catalyzed by EC 3.5.99.10.
CC   -!- Also catalyzes the conversion of L-homoserine to 2-oxobutanoate and
CC       ammonia, of L-cystine to thiocysteine, pyruvate and ammonia, and of
CC       L-cysteine to pyruvate, hydrogen sulfide and ammonia.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 4.2.1.15.
