ID   4.7.1.1
DE   Alpha-D-ribose 1-methylphosphonate 5-phosphate C-P-lyase.
CA   Alpha-D-ribose 1-methylphosphonate 5-phosphate + S-adenosyl-L-methionine
CA   + reduced electron acceptor = alpha-D-ribose 1,2-cyclic phosphate
CA   5-phosphate + methane + L-methionine + 5'-deoxyadenosine + electron
CA   acceptor.
CF   Iron-sulfur; S-adenosyl-L-methionine.
CC   -!- This radical SAM (AdoMet) enzyme is part of the C-P lyase complex,
CC       which is responsible for processing phophonates into usable
CC       phosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme from the bacterium Escherichia coli can act on additional
CC       alpha-D-ribose phosphonate substrates with different substituents
CC       attached to the phosphonate phosphorus (e.g. alpha-D-ribose-1-
CC       (N-(phosphonomethyl)glycine)-5-phosphate and alpha-D-ribose-1-(2-N-
CC       acetamidomethylphosphonate)-5-phosphate).
