DR   O27448, CFBA_METTH ;
//
ID   4.99.1.4
DE   Sirohydrochlorin ferrochelatase.
CA   Siroheme + 2 H(+) = sirohydrochlorin + Fe(2+).
CC   -!- This enzyme catalyzes the third of three steps leading to the
CC       formation of siroheme from uroporphyrinogen III.
CC   -!- The first step involves the donation of two S-adenosyl-L-methionine-
CC       derived methyl groups to carbons 2 and 7 of uroporphyrinogen III to
CC       form precorrin-2 (EC 2.1.1.107) and the second step involves an
CC       NAD(+)-dependent dehydrogenation to form sirohydrochlorin from
CC       precorrin-2 (EC 1.3.1.76).
CC   -!- In Saccharomyces cerevisiae, the last two steps are carried out by a
CC       single bifunctional enzyme, Met8p.
CC   -!- In some bacteria, steps 1-3 are catalyzed by a single multifunctional
CC       protein called CysG, whereas in Bacillus megaterium, three separate
CC       enzymes carry out each of the steps, with SirB being responsible for
CC       the above reaction.
