//
ID   4.99.1.5
DE   Aliphatic aldoxime dehydratase.
CA   An aliphatic aldoxime = an aliphatic nitrile + H(2)O.
CF   Ca(2+); Heme b.
CC   -!- Exhibits a strong preference for aliphatic aldoximes, such as
CC       butyraldoxime and acetaldoxime, over aromatic aldoximes, such as
CC       pyridine-2-aldoxime, which is a poor substrate.
CC   -!- No activity was found with the aromatic aldoximes benzaldoxime and
CC       pyridine-4-aldoxime.
//
ID   4.99.1.6
DE   Indoleacetaldoxime dehydratase.
AN   3-indoleacetaldoxime hydro-lyase.
AN   Indole-3-acetaldehyde-oxime hydro-lyase.
AN   Indoleacetaldoxime hydro-lyase.
CA   (Indol-3-yl)acetaldehyde oxime = (indol-3-yl)acetonitrile + H(2)O.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 4.2.1.29.
DR   O49342, C71AD_ARATH;
//
ID   4.99.1.7
DE   Phenylacetaldoxime dehydratase.
AN   Arylacetaldoxime dehydratase.
AN   PAOx dehydratase.
CA   (Z)-phenylacetaldehyde oxime = phenylacetonitrile + H(2)O.
CF   Heme.
CC   -!- The enzyme from Bacillus sp. OxB-1 contains protoheme IX, the iron of
CC       which must be in the form Fe(2+) for activity.
CC   -!- (Z)-phenylacetaldoxime binds to ferric heme (the Fe(3+) form) via the
CC       oxygen atom whereas it binds to the active ferrous form via the
CC       nitrogen atom.
CC   -!- In this way, the oxidation state of the heme controls the
CC       coordination stucture of the substrate--heme complex, which regulates
CC       enzyme activity.
CC   -!- The enzyme is active toward several (Z)-arylacetaldoximes and (E/Z)-
CC       alkylaldoximes as well as toward arylalkylaldoximes such as
CC       3-phenylpropionaldoxime and 4-phenylbutyraldoxime.
CC   -!- However, it is inactive with phenylacetaldoximes that have a
CC       substituent group at an alpha-site of an oxime group, for example,
CC       with (E/Z)-2-phenylpropionaldoxime and (E/Z)-mandelaldoxime.
CC   -!- The activity of the enzyme is inhibited completely by the heavy-metal
CC       cations Cu(+), Cu(2+), Ag(+) and Hg(+) whereas Fe(2+) and Sn(2+) have
CC       an activatory effect.
DR   P82604, OXD_BACSX  ;
//
ID   4.99.1.8
DE   Heme ligase.
AN   Hemozoin synthase.
CA   2 ferriprotoporphyrin IX = beta-hematin.
CC   -!- This heme detoxifying enzyme is found in Plasmodium parasites and
CC       converts toxic heme to crystalline hemozoin.
CC   -!- These organisms lack the mammalian heme oxygenase for elimination of
CC       heme.
DR   Q8IL04, HDP_PLAF7  ;
//
ID   4.99.1.9
DE   Coproporphyrin ferrochelatase.
CA   Fe-coproporphyrin III + 2 H(+) = coproporphyrin III + Fe(2+).
CC   -!- The enzyme, present in Gram-positive bacteria, participates in heme
CC       biosynthesis.
CC   -!- It can also catalyze the reaction of EC 4.99.1.1 at a much lower
CC       level.
//
ID   4.99.1.10
DE   Magnesium dechelatase.
AN   Mg-dechelatase.
CA   (1) Chlorophyll a + 2 H(+) = pheophytin a + Mg(2+).
CA   (2) Chlorophylide a + 2 H(+) = pheophorbide a + Mg(2+).
CC   -!- SGR has very low activity with chlorophyllide a and none with
CC       chlorophyll b.
CC   -!- It acts on chlorophyll a both in its free form and in protein
CC       complex.
CC   -!- SGRL, on the other hand, is more active with chlorophyllide a than
CC       with chlorophyll a.
CC   -!- The magnesium formed is scavenged by MCS (metal-chelating substance).
//
ID   4.99.1.11
DE   Sirohydrochlorin nickelchelatase.
CA   Ni-sirohydrochlorin + 2 H(+) = sirohydrochlorin + Ni(2+).
CC   -!- The enzyme, studied from the methanogenic archaeon Methanosarcina
CC       acetivorans, participates in the biosynthesis of the nickel-
CC       containing tetrapyrrole cofactor coenzyme F(430), which is required
CC       by EC 2.8.4.1.
CC   -!- It catalyzes the insertion of the nickel ion into sirohydrochlorin.
DR   A6UWT5, CFBA_META3 ;  Q8TJZ5, CFBA_METAC ;  P61816, CFBA_METBF ;
DR   Q12X56, CFBA_METBU ;  Q58380, CFBA_METJA ;  Q8TY77, CFBA_METKA ;
DR   Q8PZH6, CFBA_METMA ;  P61819, CFBA_METMP ;  O27448, CFBA_METTH ;
//
ID   4.99.1.12
DE   Pyridinium-3,5-bisthiocarboxylic acid mononucleotide nickel chelatase.
AN   P2TMN nickel chelatase.
CA   Ni(II)-pyridinium-3,5-bisthiocarboxylate mononucleotide = pyridinium-3,5-
CA   bisthiocarboxylate mononucleotide + Ni(2+).
CC   -!- This enzyme, found in Lactobacillus plantarum, is involved in the
CC       biosynthesis of a nickel-pincer cofactor.
CC   -!- It catalyzes the insertion of Ni(2+) into the cofactor forming a
CC       covalent bond between a carbon atom and the nickel atom.
DR   B2ULM9, LARC_AKKM8 ;  A6TKJ0, LARC_ALKMQ ;  Q97KZ2, LARC_CLOAB ;
