CC   -!- The first type of this enzyme found proved to be the protein
CC       cyclophilin, which binds the immunosuppressant cyclosporin A.
CC   -!- Other distinct families of the enzyme exist, one being FK-506 binding
CC       proteins (FKBP) and another that includes parvulin from Escherichia
CC       coli.
CC   -!- The three families are structurally unrelated and can be
CC       distinguished by being inhibited by cyclosporin A, FK-506 and
CC       5-hydroxy-1,4-naphthoquinone, respectively.
