DE   2-chloro-4-carboxymethylenebut-2-en-1,4-olide isomerase.
AN   2-chlorocarboxymethylenebutenolide isomerase.
AN   Chlorodienelactone isomerase.
CA   Cis-2-chloro-4-carboxymethylenebut-2-en-1,4-olide = trans-2-chloro-4-
CA   carboxymethylenebut-2-en-1,4-olide.
//
ID   5.2.1.11
DE   Deleted entry.
//
ID   5.2.1.12
DE   Zeta-carotene isomerase.
AN   15-cis-zeta-carotene isomerase.
CA   9,15,9'-tri-cis-zeta-carotene = 9,9'-di-cis-zeta-carotene.
CC   -!- The enzyme catalyzes the cis-trans isomerization of the 15-15'
CC       carbon-carbon double bond in 9,15,9'-tricis-zeta-carotene, which is
CC       required for biosynthesis of all plant carotenoids.
CC   -!- Requires heme b.
DR   Q9SAC0, ZCIS_ARATH ;  B4FHU1, ZCIS_MAIZE ;
//
ID   5.2.1.13
DE   Prolycopene isomerase.
AN   Carotene cis-trans isomerase.
AN   Carotene isomerase.
AN   Carotenoid isomerase.
AN   CRTISO.
CA   7,9,7',9'-tetra-cis-lycopene = all-trans-lycopene.
CF   FADH(2).
CC   -!- The enzyme is involved in carotenoid biosynthesis.
DR   Q52QW3, CRTS1_ONCHC;  Q52QW2, CRTS2_ONCHC;  Q9M9Y8, CRTSO_ARATH;
DR   Q2VEX9, CRTSO_DAUCA;  Q8S4R4, CRTSO_SOLLC;
//
ID   5.2.1.14
DE   Beta-carotene isomerase.
CA   All-trans-beta-carotene = 9-cis-beta-carotene.
CC   -!- The enzyme participates in a pathway leading to biosynthesis of
CC       strigolactones, plant hormones involved in promotion of symbiotic
CC       associations known as arbuscular mycorrhiza.
DR   Q7XA78, D27_ARATH  ;  C7AU21, D27_ORYSJ  ;
//
