ID   5.3.1.5
DE   Xylose isomerase.
AN   D-xylose ketoisomerase.
CA   D-xylopyranose = D-xylulose.
CF   Mg(2+).
CC   -!- The enzyme catalyzes the interconversion of aldose and ketose sugars
CC       with broad substrate specificity.
CC   -!- The enzyme binds the closed form of its sugar substrate (in the case
CC       of glucose, only the alpha anomer) and catalyzes ring opening to
CC       generate a form of open-chain conformation that is coordinated to one
CC       of the metal sites.
CC   -!- Isomerization proceeds via a hydride-shift mechanism.
