ID   5.3.1.14
DE   L-rhamnose isomerase.
AN   Rhamnose isomerase.
CA   L-rhamnopyranose = L-rhamnulose.
CF   Divalent cation.
CC   -!- The enzyme binds the closed ring form of the substrate and catalyzes
CC       ring opening to generate a form of open-chain conformation that is
CC       coordinated to one of the metal sites.
CC   -!- Isomerization proceeds via a hydride-shift mechanism.
CC   -!- While the enzyme from the bacterium Escherichia coli is specific for
CC       L-rhamnose, the enzyme from the bacterium Pseudomonas stutzeri has
CC       broad substrate specificity and catalyzes the interconversion of
CC       L-mannose and L-fructose, L-lyxose and L-xylulose, D-ribose and
CC       D-ribulose, and D-allose and D-psicose.
