DE   6-phospho-3-hexuloisomerase.
AN   3-hexulose-6-phosphate isomerase.
AN   6-phospho-3-hexulose isomerase.
AN   PHI.
AN   Phospho-3-hexuloisomerase.
CA   D-arabino-hex-3-ulose 6-phosphate = D-fructose 6-phosphate.
CC   -!- This enzyme, along with EC 4.1.2.43, plays a key role in the
CC       ribulose-monophosphate cycle of formaldehyde fixation, which is
CC       present in many microorganisms that are capable of utilizing
CC       C1-compounds.
CC   -!- The hyperthermophilic and anaerobic archaeon Pyrococcus horikoshii
CC       OT3 constitutively produces a bifunctional enzyme that sequentially
CC       catalyzes the reactions of EC 4.1.2.43 and this enzyme.
