ID   5.4.2.2
DE   Phosphoglucomutase (alpha-D-glucose-1,6-bisphosphate-dependent).
AN   Glucose phosphomutase.
AN   Phosphoglucose mutase.
CA   Alpha-D-glucose 1-phosphate = alpha-D-glucose 6-phosphate.
CC   -!- Maximum activity is only obtained in the presence of alpha-D-glucose
CC       1,6-bisphosphate.
CC   -!- This bisphosphate is an intermediate in the reaction, being formed by
CC       transfer of a phosphate residue from the enzyme to the substrate,
CC       but the dissociation of bisphosphate from the enzyme complex is much
CC       slower than the overall isomerization.
CC   -!- Also, more slowly, catalyzes the interconversion of 1-phosphate and
CC       6-phosphate isomers of many other alpha-D-hexoses, and the
