CC   -!- In the direction shown, the enzyme is phosphorylated by
CC       3-phosphoglyceroyl phosphate to give phosphoenzyme and
CC       3-phosphoglycerate.
CC   -!- The latter is rephosphorylated by the enzyme to yield 2,3-
CC       diphosphoglycerate, but this reaction is slowed down by dissociation
CC       of 3-phosphoglycerate from the enzyme, which is therefore more active
CC       in the presence of added 3-phosphoglycerate.
CC   -!- Also catalyzes, slowly, the reaction of EC 5.4.2.12.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 2.7.5.4.
