DE   Phosphoglucomutase (glucose-cofactor).
AN   Glucose phosphomutase.
AN   Glucose-1-phosphate phosphotransferase.
CA   Alpha-D-glucose 1-phosphate = alpha-D-glucose 6-phosphate.
CC   -!- Activated by D-glucose, which probably acts as an acceptor for a
CC       phosphate residue from the substrate, thus being itself converted
CC       into the product.
CC   -!- Cf. EC 5.4.2.2.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 2.7.5.5.
//
ID   5.4.2.6
DE   Beta-phosphoglucomutase.
CA   Beta-D-glucose 1-phosphate = beta-D-glucose 6-phosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme is able to autophosphorylate itself with its substrate
CC       beta-D-glucose 1-phosphate.
CC   -!- Although this is a slow reaction, only a single turnover is required
CC       for activation.
CC   -!- Once the phosphorylated enzyme is formed, it generates the reaction
CC       intermediate beta-D-glucose 1,6-bisphosphate, which can be used to
CC       phosphorylate the enzyme in subsequent cycles.
CC   -!- Cf. EC 5.4.2.2.
DR   O06995, PGMB_BACSU ;  P77366, PGMB_ECOLI ;  P71447, PGMB_LACLA ;
