//
ID   6.1.1.24
DE   Glutamate--tRNA(Gln) ligase.
AN   Nondiscriminating glutamyl-tRNA synthetase.
CA   ATP + L-glutamate + tRNA(Glx) = AMP + diphosphate + L-glutamyl-tRNA(Glx).
CC   -!- When this enzyme acts on tRNA(Glu), it catalyzes the same reaction as
CC       EC 6.1.1.17.
CC   -!- It has, however, diminished discrimination, so that it can also form
CC       glutamate-tRNA(Gln).
CC   -!- This relaxation of specificity has been found to result from the
CC       absence of a loop in the tRNA that specifically recognizes the third
CC       position of the anticodon.
CC   -!- This accounts for the ability of this enzyme in, for example,
CC       Bacillus subtilis, to recognize both tRNA(1)(Gln) (UUG anticodon) and
CC       tRNA(Glu) (UUC anticodon) but not tRNA(2)(Gln) (CUG anticodon).
CC   -!- The ability of this enzyme to recognize both tRNA(Glu) and one of the
CC       tRNA(Gln) isoacceptors derives from their sharing a major identity
CC       element, a hypermodified derivative of U34 (5-methylaminomethyl-2-
CC       thiouridine).
CC   -!- The glutamyl-tRNA(Gln) is not used in protein synthesis until it is
CC       converted by EC 6.3.5.7 into glutaminyl-tRNA(Gln).
//
ID   6.1.1.25
DE   Deleted entry.
//
ID   6.1.1.26
DE   Pyrrolysine--tRNA(Pyl) ligase.
AN   PylRS.
AN   Pyrrolysyl-tRNA synthetase.
CA   ATP + L-pyrrolysine + tRNA(Pyl) = AMP + diphosphate + L-pyrrolysyl-
CA   tRNA(Pyl).
CC   -!- In organisms such as Methanosarcina barkeri that incorporate the
CC       modified amino acid pyrrolysine (Pyl) into certain methylamine
CC       methyltransferases, an unusual tRNA(Pyl), with a CUA anticodon,
CC       can be charged directly with pyrrolysine by this class II aminoacyl-
CC       -tRNA ligase.
CC   -!- Specific for pyrrolysine as substrate as it cannot be replaced by
CC       lysine or any of the other natural amino acids.
DR   Q8TUB8, PYLS_METAC ;  Q6WRH6, PYLS_METBA ;  Q46E77, PYLS_METBF ;
DR   Q12UB6, PYLS_METBU ;  Q8PWY1, PYLS_METMA ;  Q1L6A3, PYLS_METTE ;
//
ID   6.1.1.27
DE   O-phosphoserine--tRNA ligase.
AN   O-phosphoseryl-tRNA ligase.
AN   SepRS.
CA   ATP + O-phospho-L-serine + tRNA(Cys) = AMP + diphosphate + O-phospho-L-
CA   seryl-tRNA(Cys).
CC   -!- In organisms like Archaeoglobus fulgidus lacking EC 6.1.1.16 for the
CC       direct Cys-tRNA(Cys) formation, Cys-tRNA(Cys) is produced by an
CC       indirect pathway, in which EC 6.1.1.27 ligates O-phosphoserine to
CC       tRNA(Cys), and EC 2.5.1.73 converts the produced O-phospho-L-seryl-
CC       tRNA(Cys) to Cys-tRNA(Cys).
CC   -!- The SepRS/SepCysS pathway is the sole route for cysteine biosynthesis
CC       in the organism.
CC   -!- Methanosarcina mazei can use both pathways, the direct route using
CC       EC 6.1.1.16 and the indirect pathway with EC 6.1.1.27 and
CC       EC 2.5.1.73.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 6.1.1.n2.
PR   PROSITE; PDOC00363;
DR   O30126, SEPS_ARCFU ;  A6UVW6, SEPS_META3 ;  Q8TUH7, SEPS_METAC ;
DR   Q0W0T4, SEPS_METAR ;  A7I4Y4, SEPS_METB6 ;  Q46D71, SEPS_METBF ;
DR   Q12XG0, SEPS_METBU ;  Q2FSR2, SEPS_METHJ ;  Q59054, SEPS_METJA ;
DR   Q8TY66, SEPS_METKA ;  A2SQV5, SEPS_METLZ ;  A4FYB1, SEPS_METM5 ;
