ID   6.1.2.1
DE   D-alanine--(R)-lactate ligase.
CA   D-alanine + (R)-lactate + ATP = D-alanyl-(R)-lactate + ADP + phosphate.
CC   -!- The product of this enzyme, the depsipeptide D-alanyl-(R)-lactate,
CC       can be incorporated into the peptidoglycan pentapeptide instead of
CC       the usual D-alanyl-D-alanine dipeptide, which is formed by
CC       EC 6.3.2.4.
CC   -!- The resulting peptidoglycan does not bind the glycopeptide
CC       antibiotics vancomycin and teicoplanin, conferring resistance on the
CC       bacteria.
DR   P25051, VANA_ENTFC ;  Q06893, VANB_ENTFA ;
//
ID   6.1.2.2
DE   Nebramycin 5' synthase.
AN   Tobramycin carbamoyltransferase.
CA   (1) Tobramycin + carbamoyl phosphate + ATP + H(2)O = nebramycin 5' +
CA   AMP + diphosphate + phosphate.
CA   (2) Kanamycin A + carbamoyl phosphate + ATP + H(2)O = 6''-O-
CA   carbamoylkanamycin A + AMP + diphosphate + phosphate.
CF   Fe(3+).
CC   -!- The enzyme from the bacterium Streptoalloteichus tenebrarius
CC       catalyzes the activation of carbamoyl phosphate to
CC       O-carbamoyladenylate and the subsequent carbamoylation of kanamycin
CC       and tobramycin.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 2.1.3.13 and EC 2.1.3.14.
DR   Q70IY1, TOBZ_STRSD ;
//
ID   6.1.3.1
DE   Olefin beta-lactone synthetase.
CA   ATP + a (2R,3S)-2-alkyl-3-hydroxyalkanoate = AMP + diphosphate + a cis-3-
CA   alkyl-4-alkyloxetan-2-one.
CC   -!- The enzyme, found in certain bacterial species, participates in a
CC       pathway for the production of olefins.
CC   -!- It forms a beta-lactone.
CC   -!- The alkyl group at C(2) of the substrate ends up as the 3-alkyl group
CC       of the product.
//
ID   6.2.1.1
DE   Acetate--CoA ligase.
AN   Acetate thiokinase.
AN   Acetyl-activating enzyme.
AN   Acetyl-CoA synthase.
AN   Acetyl-CoA synthetase.
AN   Acyl-activating enzyme.
CA   ATP + acetate + CoA = AMP + diphosphate + acetyl-CoA.
CC   -!- Also acts on propanoate and propenoate.
