ID   6.2.1.19
DE   Long-chain-fatty-acid--protein ligase.
AN   Acyl-protein synthetase.
CA   ATP + a long-chain fatty acid + [protein]-L-cysteine = AMP + diphosphate
CA   + a [protein]-S-(long-chain-acyl)-L-cysteine.
CC   -!- Together with a hydrolase component (EC 3.1.2.2/3.1.2.14) and a
CC       reductase component (EC 1.2.1.50), this enzyme forms a multienzyme
CC       fatty acid reductase complex that produces the long-chain aldehyde
CC       substrate of the bacterial luciferase enzyme (EC 1.14.14.3).
CC   -!- The enzyme activates free long-chain fatty acids, generated by the
CC       action of the transferase component, forming a fatty acyl-AMP
CC       intermediate, followed by the transfer of the acyl group to an
CC       internal L-cysteine residue.
CC   -!- It then transfers the acyl group to EC 1.2.1.50.
