ID   6.3.1.9
DE   Trypanothione synthase.
AN   TSR synthetase.
CA   (1) Glutathione + spermidine + ATP = glutathionylspermidine + ADP +
CA   phosphate.
CA   (2) Glutathione + glutathionylspermidine + ATP = N(1),N(8)-
CA   bis(glutathionyl)spermidine + ADP + phosphate.
CF   Mg(2+).
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from several trypanosomatids (e.g.
CC       Trypanosoma cruzi) catalyzes two subsequent reactions, leading to
CC       production of trypanothione from glutathione and spermidine.
CC   -!- Some trypanosomatids (e.g. Crithidia species and some Leishmania
CC       species) also contain an enzyme that only carries out the first
CC       reaction (cf. EC 6.3.1.8).
CC   -!- The enzyme is bifunctional, and also catalyzes the hydrolysis of
CC       glutathionylspermidine and trypanothione (cf. EC 3.5.1.78).
PR   PROSITE; PDOC50975;
DR   O60993, TRYS_CRIFA ;  Q9GT49, TRYS_TRYCC ;
//
ID   6.3.1.10
DE   Adenosylcobinamide-phosphate synthase.
CA   (1) ATP + adenosylcobyric acid + (R)-1-aminopropan-2-yl phosphate = ADP +
CA   phosphate + adenosylcobinamide phosphate.
CA   (2) ATP + adenosylcobyric acid + (R)-1-aminopropan-2-ol = ADP + phosphate
CA   + adenosylcobinamide.
CC   -!- This enzyme forms part of the anaerobic cobalamin biosynthesis
CC       pathway.
CC   -!- One of the substrates for this reaction, (R)-1-aminopropan-2-yl
CC       phosphate, is produced by CobD (EC 4.1.1.81).
