ID   6.3.1.13
DE   L-cysteine:1D-myo-inositol 2-amino-2-deoxy-alpha-D-glucopyranoside
DE   ligase.
AN   MshC ligase.
AN   Mycothiol ligase.
CA   1-O-(2-amino-2-deoxy-alpha-D-glucopyranosyl)-1D-myo-inositol + L-cysteine
CA   + ATP = 1-O-(2-(L-cysteinamido)-2-deoxy-alpha-D-glucopyranosyl)-1D-myo-
CA   inositol + AMP + diphosphate.
CC   -!- This enzyme is a key enzyme in the biosynthesis of mycothiol, a small
CC       molecular weight thiol found in Mycobacteria spp. and other
CC       actinomycetes.
CC   -!- Mycothiol plays a fundamental role in these organisms by helping to
CC       provide protection from the effects of reactive oxygen species and
CC       electrophiles, including many antibiotics.
CC   -!- The enzyme may represent a novel target for new classes of
CC       antituberculars.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 6.1.1.n1.
