//
ID   6.3.2.11
DE   Carnosine synthase.
AN   Carnosine synthetase.
CA   ATP + L-histidine + beta-alanine = ADP + phosphate + carnosine.
CC   -!- This enzyme was thought to form AMP, but studies with highly purified
CC       enzyme proved that it forms ADP.
CC   -!- Carnosine is a dipeptide that is present at high concentrations in
CC       skeletal muscle and the olfactory bulb of vertebrates.
CC   -!- It is also found in the skeletal muscle of some invertebrates.
CC   -!- The enzyme can also catalyze the formation of homocarnosine from
CC       4-aminobutyrate and L-histidine, with much lower activity.
DR   D3KCC4, CRNS1_CHICK;  A5YM72, CRNS1_HUMAN;  Q6ZPS2, CRNS1_MOUSE;
//
ID   6.3.2.12
DE   Dihydrofolate synthase.
AN   7,8-dihydrofolate synthetase.
AN   DHFS.
AN   Dihydrofolate synthetase.
AN   H(2)-folate synthetase.
CA   ATP + 7,8-dihydropteroate + L-glutamate = ADP + phosphate + 7,8-
CA   dihydropteroylglutamate.
CC   -!- In some bacteria, a single protein catalyzes both this activity and
CC       that of EC 6.3.2.17, the combined activity of which leads to the
CC       formation of the coenzyme polyglutamated tetrahydropteroate
CC       (H(4)PteGlu(n)), i.e. various tetrahydrofolates.
CC   -!- In contrast, the activities are located on separate proteins in most
CC       eukaryotes studied to date.
CC   -!- This enzyme is reponsible for attaching the first glutamate residue
CC       to dihydropteroate to form dihydrofolate and is present only in those
CC       organisms that have the ability to synthesize tetrahydrofolate de
CC       novo, e.g. plants, most bacteria, fungi and protozoa.
DR   F4JYE9, DHFS_ARATH ;  Q05865, FOLC_BACSU ;  P57265, FOLC_BUCAI ;
DR   Q8K9X3, FOLC_BUCAP ;  Q89AT2, FOLC_BUCBP ;  P08192, FOLC_ECOLI ;
DR   P43775, FOLC_HAEIN ;  I6Y0R5, FOLC_MYCTU ;  Q9UTD0, FOLD_SCHPO ;
DR   Q12676, FOLD_YEAST ;
//
ID   6.3.2.13
DE   UDP-N-acetylmuramoyl-L-alanyl-D-glutamate--2,6-diaminopimelate ligase.
AN   MurE synthetase.
AN   UDP-N-acetylmuramoyl-L-alanyl-D-glutamate:meso-2,6-diamino-heptanedioate
AN   ligase (ADP-forming).
AN   UDP-N-acetylmuramoyl-L-alanyl-D-glutamyl-meso-2,6-diaminopimelate
AN   synthetase.
AN   UDP-N-acetylmuramoylalanyl-D-glutamate--2,6-diaminopimelate ligase.
AN   UDP-N-acetylmuramyl-tripeptide synthetase.
CA   ATP + UDP-N-acetyl-alpha-D-muramoyl-L-alanyl-D-glutamate + meso-2,6-
CA   diaminoheptanedioate = ADP + phosphate + UDP-N-acetyl-alpha-D-muramoyl-L-
CA   alanyl-D-gamma-glutamyl-meso-2,6-diaminoheptanedioate.
CC   -!- Involved in the synthesis of a cell-wall peptide.
CC   -!- This enzyme adds diaminopimelate in Gram-negative organisms and in
CC       some Gram-positive organisms; in others EC 6.3.2.7 adds lysine
CC       instead.
CC   -!- It is the amino group of the L-center of the diaminopimelate that is
CC       acylated.
