ID   6.3.2.42
DE   N-acetylaspartylglutamylglutamate synthase.
AN   N-acetylaspartylglutamylglutamate synthetase.
AN   NAAG synthetase II.
AN   NAAGS-II.
CA   2 ATP + N-acetyl-L-aspartate + 2 L-glutamate = 2 ADP + 2 phosphate +
CA   N-acetyl-L-aspartyl-L-glutamyl-L-glutamate.
CC   -!- The enzyme, found in mammals, also has the activity of EC 6.3.2.41.
DR   Q8IXN7, RIMKA_HUMAN;  Q6PFX8, RIMKA_MOUSE;
//
ID   6.3.2.43
DE   [Lysine-biosynthesis-protein LysW]--L-2-aminoadipate ligase.
AN   AAA--LysW ligase.
AN   Alpha-aminoadipate-lysW ligase.
CA   ATP + [lysine-biosynthesis-protein LysW]-C-terminal-L-glutamate + L-2-
CA   aminoadipate = ADP + phosphate + [lysine-biosynthesis-protein LysW]-C-
CA   terminal-gamma-(L-2-aminoadip-2-yl)-L-glutamate.
CC   -!- The enzymes from the thermophilic bacterium Thermus thermophilus and
CC       the thermophilic archaea Sulfolobus acidocaldarius and Sulfolobus
CC       tokodaii protect the amino group of L-2-aminoadipate by conjugation
CC       to the carrier protein LysW.
CC   -!- This reaction is part of the lysine biosynthesis pathway in these
CC       organisms.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 6.3.2.n4.
DR   Q4JAP9, LYSX_SULAC ;  Q7SI95, LYSX_SULSO ;  Q976J9, LYSX_SULTO ;
DR   Q5SH23, LYSX_THET8 ;
//
ID   6.3.2.44
DE   Pantoate--beta-alanine ligase (ADP-forming).
AN   Pantoate--beta-alanine ligase.
AN   Pantothenate synthetase.
CA   ATP + (R)-pantoate + beta-alanine = ADP + phosphate + (R)-pantothenate.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the archaeon Methanosarcina mazei,
CC       is involved in the biosynthesis of pantothenate.
CC   -!- It is different from EC 6.3.2.1, the AMP-forming pantoate-beta-
CC       alanine ligase found in bacteria and eukaryota.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 6.3.2.n5.
DR   Q57662, PASYA_METJA;  Q8PUQ1, PASYA_METMA;
//
ID   6.3.2.45
DE   UDP-N-acetylmuramate L-alanyl-gamma-D-glutamyl-meso-2,6-
DE   diaminoheptanedioate ligase.
AN   Murein peptide ligase.
CA   ATP + UDP-N-acetyl-alpha-D-muramate + L-alanyl-gamma-D-glutamyl-meso-2,6-
CA   diaminoheptanedioate = ADP + phosphate + UDP-N-acetylmuramoyl-L-alanyl-
CA   gamma-D-glutamyl-meso-2,6-diaminoheptanedioate.
CF   Mg(2+).
CC   -!- The enzyme catalyzes the reincorporation into peptidoglycan of the
CC       tripeptide L-alanyl-gamma-D-glutamyl-2,6-meso-diaminoheptanedioate
CC       released during the maturation and constant remodeling of this
CC       bacterial cell wall polymer that occur during cell growth and
CC       division.
CC   -!- The enzyme can also use the tetrapeptide L-alanyl-gamma-D-glutamyl-
CC       meso-2,6-diaminoheptanedioyl-D-alanine or the pentapeptide L-alanyl-
CC       gamma-D-glutamyl-meso-2,6-diaminoheptanedioyl-D-alanyl-D-alanine in
CC       vivo and in vitro.
DR   P37773, MPL_ECOLI  ;  P43948, MPL_HAEIN  ;
//
ID   6.3.2.46
DE   Fumarate--(S)-2,3-diaminopropanoate ligase.
CA   ATP + fumarate + (S)-2,3-diaminopropanoate = AMP + diphosphate + N(3)-
CA   fumaroyl-(S)-2,3-diaminopropanoate.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Enterobacter
CC       agglomerans, is involved in biosynthesis of dapdiamide tripeptide
CC       antibiotics, a family of fumaramoyl- and epoxysuccinamoyl-peptides
CC       named for the presence of an L-2,3-diaminopropanoate (DAP) moiety and
CC       two amide linkages in their scaffold.
DR   E2JA32, DDAG_ENTAG ;
//
ID   6.3.2.47
DE   Dapdiamide synthase.
AN   Dapdiamide A synthase.
CA   (1) ATP + 3-((((2R,3R)-3-carboxyoxiran-2-yl)carbonyl)amino)-L-alanine +
CA   L-valine = ADP + phosphate + 3-((((2R,3R)-3-carboxyoxiran-2-
CA   yl)carbonyl)amino)-L-alanyl-L-valine.
CA   (2) ATP + 3-(((2E)-4-amino-4-oxobut-2-enoyl)amino)-L-alanine + L-valine =
CA   ADP + phosphate + 3-(((2E)-4-amino-4-oxobut-2-enoyl)amino)-L-alanyl-L-
CA   valine.
CA   (3) ATP + 3-(((2E)-4-amino-4-oxobut-2-enoyl)amino)-L-alanine +
CA   L-isoleucine = ADP + phosphate + 3-(((2E)-4-amino-4-oxobut-2-
CA   enoyl)amino)-L-alanyl-L-isoleucine.
CA   (4) ATP + 3-(((2E)-4-amino-4-oxobut-2-enoyl)amino)-L-alanine + L-leucine
CA   = ADP + phosphate + 3-(((2E)-4-amino-4-oxobut-2-enoyl)amino)-L-alanyl-L-
CA   leucine.
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Pantoea agglomerans,
CC       is involved in biosynthesis of dapdiamide tripeptide antibiotics,
CC       a family of fumaramoyl- and epoxysuccinamoyl-peptides named for the
CC       presence of an (S)-2,3-diaminopropanoate (DAP) moiety and two amide
CC       linkages in their scaffold.
DR   E2JA31, DDAF_ENTAG ;
//
ID   6.3.2.48
DE   L-arginine-specific L-amino acid ligase.
CA   ATP + L-arginine + an L-amino acid = ADP + phosphate + an L-arginyl-L-
CA   amino acid.
CF   Mn(2+).
CC   -!- The enzyme shows strict substrate specificity toward L-arginine as
CC       the N-terminal amino acid of the product.
CC   -!- The second amino acid could be any standard protein-building amino
CC       acid except for L-proline.
DR   B5UAT8, RIZA_BACIU ;
//
ID   6.3.2.49
DE   L-alanine--L-anticapsin ligase.
AN   Alanine-anticapsin ligase.
AN   L-Ala-L-anticapsin ligase.
CA   ATP + L-alanine + L-anticapsin = ADP + phosphate + bacilysin.
CF   Mn(2+) or Mg(2+).
CC   -!- The enzyme, characterized from the bacterium Bacillus subtilis,
CC       is involved in the biosynthesis of the nonribosomally synthesized
CC       dipeptide antibiotic bacilysin, composed of L-alanine and
CC       L-anticapsin.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 6.3.2.28.
DR   Q8KWS8, BACD_BACAM ;  Q8KWT3, BACD_BACIU ;  P39641, BACD_BACSU ;
//
ID   6.3.2.50
DE   Tenuazonic acid synthetase.
CA   ATP + L-isoleucine + acetoacetyl-CoA = AMP + diphosphate + tenuazonic
CA   acid + CoA.
CC   -!- This fungal enzyme, isolated from Magnaporthe oryzae, is an non-
CC       ribosomal peptide synthetase (NRPS)-polyketide synthase (PKS) hybrid
CC       protein that consists of condensation (C), adenylation (A) and
CC       peptidyl-carrier protein (PCP) domains in the NRPS portion and a
CC       ketosynthase (KS) domain in the PKS portion.
CC   -!- ATP is required for activation of isoleucine, which is then condensed
CC       with acetoacetyl-CoA.
CC   -!- Cyclization and release from the enzyme are catalyzed by the KS
CC       domain.
//
ID   6.3.2.51
DE   Phosphopantothenate--cysteine ligase (ATP).
AN   Phosphopantothenoylcysteine synthetase.
CA   ATP + (R)-4'-phosphopantothenate + L-cysteine = AMP + diphosphate +
CA   N-((R)-4'-phosphopantothenoyl)-L-cysteine.
//
ID   6.3.2.52
DE   Jasmonoyl--L-amino acid synthetase.
CA   ATP + jasmonate + an L-amino acid = AMP + diphosphate + a jasmonoyl-L-
CA   amino acid.
CC   -!- Two jasmonoyl-L-amino acid synthetases have been described from
CC       Nicotiana attenuata and one from Arabidopsis thaliana.
CC   -!- The N.attenuata enzymes generate jasmonoyl-L-isoleucine, jasmonoyl-L-
CC       leucine, and jasmonoyl-L-valine.
CC   -!- The enzyme from A.thaliana could catalyze the addition of many
CC       different amino acids to jasmonate in vitro.
CC   -!- While the abundant form of jasmonate in plants is (-)-jasmonate,
CC       the active form of jasmonoyl-L-isoleucine is (+)-7-iso-jasmonoyl-L-
CC       isoleucine.
