ID   6.3.3.4
DE   (Carboxyethyl)arginine beta-lactam-synthase.
AN   Beta-lactam synthetase.
CA   ATP + L-N(2)-(2-carboxyethyl)arginine = AMP + diphosphate +
CA   deoxyamidinoproclavaminate.
CC   -!- Forms part of the pathway for the biosythesis of the beta-lactamase
CC       inhibitor clavulanate in Streptomyces clavuligerus.
CC   -!- It has been proposed that L-N(2)-(2-carboxyethyl)arginine is first
CC       converted into an acyl-AMP by reaction with ATP and loss of
CC       diphosphate, and that the beta-lactam ring is then formed by the
CC       intramolecular attack of the beta-nitrogen on the activated carboxy
CC       group.
DR   P0DJQ8, BLS_STRC2  ;  P0DJQ7, BLS_STRCL  ;
//
ID   6.3.3.5
DE   O-ureido-D-serine cyclo-ligase.
CA   O-ureido-D-serine + ATP + H(2)O = D-cycloserine + CO(2) + NH(3) + ADP +
CA   phosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme participates in the biosynthetic pathway of D-cycloserine,
CC       an antibiotic substance produced by several Streptomyces species.
DR   D2Z030, DCSG_STRLA ;
//
ID   6.3.3.6
DE   Carbapenam-3-carboxylate synthase.
AN   Carbapenam-3-carboxylate ligase.
CA   ATP + (2S,5S)-5-carboxymethylproline = AMP + diphosphate + (3S,5S)-
CA   carbapenam 3-carboxylate.
CC   -!- The enzyme is involved in the biosynthesis of the carbapenem beta-
CC       lactam antibiotic (5R)-carbapen-2-em-3-carboxylate in the bacterium
CC       Pectobacterium carotovorum.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 6.3.1.16.
DR   Q9XB61, CARA_PECCC ;
//
ID   6.3.3.7
DE   Ni-sirohydrochlorin a,c-diamide reductive cyclase.
CA   ATP + Ni-sirohydrochlorin a,c-diamide + 3 reduced electron acceptor +
CA   H(2)O = ADP + phosphate + 15,17(3)-seco-F(430)-17(3)-acid + 3 electron
CA   acceptor.
CC   -!- The enzyme, studied from the methanogenic archaeon Methanosarcina
CC       acetivorans, participates in the biosynthesis of the nickel-
CC       containing tetrapyrrole cofactor coenzyme F(430), which is required
CC       by EC 2.8.4.1.
DR   Q8TJZ9, CFBC_METAC ;  Q46FL1, CFBC_METBF ;  Q8TJZ8, CFBD_METAC ;
DR   Q46FL2, CFBD_METBF ;  Q58818, CFBD_METJA ;  O27566, CFBD_METTH ;
