ID   6.3.4.2
DE   CTP synthase (glutamine hydrolyzing).
AN   CTP synthetase.
AN   UTP--ammonia ligase.
CA   ATP + UTP + L-glutamine = ADP + phosphate + CTP + L-glutamate.
CC   -!- The enzyme contains three functionally distinct sites: an allosteric
CC       GTP-binding site, a glutaminase site where glutamine hydrolysis
CC       occurs (cf. EC 3.5.1.2), and the active site where CTP synthesis
CC       takes place.
CC   -!- The reaction proceeds via phosphorylation of UTP by ATP to give an
CC       activated intermediate 4-phosphoryl UTP and ADP.
CC   -!- Ammonia then reacts with this intermediate generating CTP and a
CC       phosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme can also use ammonia from the surrounding solution.
PR   PROSITE; PDOC00405;
