ID   6.3.4.14
DE   Biotin carboxylase.
CA   ATP + [biotin carboxyl-carrier protein]-biotin-N(6)-L-lysine +
CA   hydrogencarbonate- = ADP + phosphate + [biotin carboxyl-carrier protein]-
CA   carboxybiotin-N(6)-L-lysine.
CC   -!- This enzyme, part of an acetyl-CoA carboxylase complex, acts on a
CC       biotin carboxyl-carrier protein (BCCP) that has been biotinylated by
CC       EC 6.3.4.15.
CC   -!- In some organisms the enzyme is part of a multi-domain polypeptide
CC       that also includes the carrier protein (e.g. mycobacteria).
CC   -!- Yet in other organisms (e.g. mammals) this activity is included in a
CC       single polypeptide that also catalyzes the transfer of the carboxyl
CC       group from biotin to acetyl-CoA (see EC 6.4.1.2).
