ID   6.3.4.15
DE   Biotin--[biotin carboxyl-carrier protein] ligase.
AN   Acetyl-CoA carboxylase biotin holoenzyme synthetase.
AN   Biotin--[acetyl-CoA carboxylase] synthetase.
AN   Biotin--[acetyl-CoA-carboxylase] ligase.
AN   Biotin--protein ligase.
CA   ATP + biotin + [biotin carboxyl-carrier protein]-L-lysine = AMP +
CA   diphosphate + [biotin carboxyl-carrier protein]-N(6)-biotinyl-L-lysine.
CC   -!- The enzyme biotinylates a biotin carboxyl-carrier protein that is
CC       part of an acetyl-CoA carboxylase complex, enabling its subsequent
CC       carboxylation by EC 6.3.4.14.
CC   -!- The carboxyl group is eventually transferred to acetyl-CoA by
CC       EC 2.1.3.15.
CC   -!- In some organisms the carrier protein is part of EC 6.4.1.2.
DR   Q5F5C8, BICOA_NEIG1;  Q9JWI7, BICOA_NEIMA;  Q9JXF1, BICOA_NEIMB;
