ID   6.3.4.16
DE   Carbamoyl-phosphate synthase (ammonia).
AN   Carbamoyl-phosphate synthetase (ammonia).
AN   Carbamoyl-phosphate synthetase I.
AN   Carbamoylphosphate synthase (ammonia).
AN   Carbamoylphosphate synthetase (ammonia).
AN   Carbon-dioxide--ammonia ligase.
AN   CPS I.
CA   2 ATP + NH(3) + HCO(3)(-) = 2 ADP + phosphate + carbamoyl phosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme catalyzes the first committed step in the urea cycle.
CC   -!- The reaction proceeds via three separate chemical reactions:
CC       phosphorylation of hydrogencarbonate to carboxyphosphate; a
CC       nucleophilic attack of ammonia on carboxyphosphate yielding
CC       carbamate; and the phosphorylation of carbamate forming carbamoyl
CC       phosphate.
CC   -!- Two moles of ATP are utilized for the synthesis of one molecule of
CC       carbamyl phosphate, making the reaction essentially irreversible.
CC   -!- The enzyme requires the allosteric activator N-acetyl-L-glutamate.
CC   -!- Cf. EC 6.3.5.5.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 2.7.2.5.
PR   PROSITE; PDOC00676;
DR   P31327, CPSM_HUMAN ;  Q91293, CPSM_LITCT ;  Q8C196, CPSM_MOUSE ;
DR   P07756, CPSM_RAT   ;
//
ID   6.3.4.17
DE   Formate--dihydrofolate ligase.
AN   Dihydrofolate formyltransferase.
AN   Formyl dihydrofolate synthase.
CA   ATP + formate + dihydrofolate = ADP + phosphate + 10-formyldihydrofolate.
