ID   6.3.4.22
DE   tRNA(Ile)(2)-agmatinylcytidine synthase.
AN   tRNA(Ile)-2-agmatinylcytidine synthetase.
AN   tRNA(Ile)-agm(2)C synthetase.
AN   tRNA(Ile)-agmatidine synthetase.
CA   ATP + agmatine + (tRNA(Ile)(2))-cytidine(34) + H(2)O = (tRNA(Ile)(2))-2-
CA   agmatinylcytidine(34) + AMP + 2 phosphate.
CC   -!- The enzyme from the archaeon Archaeoglobus fulgidus modifies the
CC       wobble base of the CAU anticodon of the archaeal tRNA(Ile)(2) at the
CC       oxo group in position 2 of cytidine(34).
CC   -!- This modification is crucial for accurate decoding of the genetic
CC       code.
CC   -!- In bacteria EC 6.3.4.19, catalyzes the modification of
CC       (tRNA(Ile)(2))-cytidine(34) to (tRNA(Ile)(2))-lysidine(34).
