DE   GMP synthase (glutamine-hydrolyzing).
AN   GMP synthetase (glutamine-hydrolyzing).
CA   ATP + XMP + L-glutamine + H(2)O = AMP + diphosphate + GMP + L-glutamate.
CC   -!- Involved in the de novo biosynthesis of guanosine nucleotides.
CC   -!- An N-terminal glutaminase domain binds L-glutamine and generates
CC       ammonia, which is transferred by a substrate-protective tunnel to the
CC       ATP-pyrophosphatase domain.
CC   -!- The enzyme can catalyze the second reaction alone in the presence of
CC       ammonia.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 6.3.4.1.
