//
ID   6.3.5.8
DE   Transferred entry: 2.6.1.85.
//
ID   6.3.5.9
DE   Hydrogenobyrinic acid a,c-diamide synthase (glutamine-hydrolyzing).
CA   2 ATP + hydrogenobyrinic acid + 2 L-glutamine + 2 H(2)O = 2 ADP +
CA   2 phosphate + hydrogenobyrinic acid a,c-diamide + 2 L-glutamate.
CC   -!- This step in the aerobic biosynthesis of cobalamin generates
CC       hydrogenobyrinic acid a,c-diamide, the substrate required by
CC       EC 6.6.1.2, which adds cobalt to the macrocycle.
DR   Q8UBQ8, COBB_AGRFC ;  Q57CK2, COBB_BRUAB ;  Q8YHU1, COBB_BRUME ;
