ID   7.2.2.3
DE   P-type Na(+) transporter.
AN   Na(+)-exporting ATPase.
AN   Na(+)-transporting ATPase.
AN   Sodium transport ATPase.
AN   Sodium-exporting ATPase.
AN   Sodium-translocating P-type ATPase.
CA   ATP + H(2)O + Na(+)(In) = ADP + phosphate + Na(+)(Out).
CF   Mg(2+).
CC   -!- A P-type ATPase that undergoes covalent phosphorylation during the
CC       transport cycle.
CC   -!- This enzyme from yeast is involved in the efflux of Na(+), with one
CC       ion being exported per ATP hydrolyzed.
CC   -!- Some forms can also export Li(+) ions.
CC   -!- Cf. EC 7.2.2.1 and EC 7.2.2.4.
CC   -!- Formerly EC 3.6.3.7.
PR   PROSITE; PDOC00139;
