ID   7.6.2.3
DE   ABC-type glutathione-S-conjugate transporter.
AN   Glutathione-S-conjugate-translocating ATPase.
AN   Multidrug resistance-associated protein 1.
AN   YBT1 (gene name).
AN   YCF1 (gene name).
CA   ATP + H(2)O + glutathione-S-conjugate(Side 1) = ADP + phosphate +
CA   glutathione-S-conjugate(Side 2).
CC   -!- A eukaryotic ATP-binding cassette (ABC) type transporter that
CC       mediates the transport of glutathione-S-conjugates.
CC   -!- The mammalian enzyme, which also transports some glucuronides,
CC       exports the substrates out of the cell, while plant and fungal
CC       transporters export them into the vacuole.
CC   -!- Over-expression confers resistance to anticancer drugs by their
CC       efficient exportation in glutathione-S-conjugate form.
//
